local E = ns.DB.entries
E["item:agamand-family-axe"] = {t="item",n="Agamand Family Axe",z="tirisfal",s="In northern Tirisfal, the Agamand Family Axe remains among the family's ancestral arms. Once a symbol of the wealthy mill owners, it is now sought by Coleman Farthing to strip the undead Agamands of their remaining dignity.",h="In northern Tirisfal, the Agamand Family Axe remains among the family's ancestral arms.",sec={{t="A Weapon of the Agamands",b="Before the Third War, the Agamand dynasty owned land across Tirisfal Glades' northern hills and kept vast mills and a family crypt. The Agamand Family Axe rested with the ancestral arms, beside the buried patriarchs and warriors. The Scourge overran the estate and slaughtered its inhabitants, but the weapons remained on racks underground.",sp=0},{t="Spiteful Restitution",b="The Scourge raised the fallen Agamands as mindless thralls to the Lich King. Their former servant Coleman Farthing survived in undeath, bitter toward his old masters. Farthing blames the family for his own death and sends Forsaken wanderers into the crypt to take the axe, sword, mace, and dagger from the racks. He wants the last traces of the Agamand heritage erased.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Agamand Family Axe located?",a="The axe rests on a weapon rack inside the Agamand Family Crypt, at the northern edge of Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"axe location","where is the axe","agamand axe place"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Agamand Family Axe?",a="Coleman Farthing, a Forsaken in Brill, seeks the axe along with the family's dagger, mace, and sword. He wants to strip his former masters of their honor.",al={"who needs the axe","coleman farthing quest","who wants agamand heirlooms"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing hate the Agamand family?",a="The Agamands employed Farthing in life, and he blames them for his death. He takes revenge by plundering their crypt while they roam the estate as undead minions.",al={"why does farthing want heirlooms","coleman farthing backstory","farthing grudge"},it="motive"},{q="Is the Agamand Family Axe a usable weapon?",a="No. The axe is an ancestral relic retrieved to prove the family's vault has been desecrated.",al={"can i equip the axe","axe stats"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What is the Agamand Family Axe?",a="The Agamand Family Axe is an heirloom weapon belonging to the prominent Agamand dynasty of Tirisfal Glades. Preserved within their ancestral crypt alongside other cherished armaments, it represents the lineage's martial heritage and legacy from the days before the Scourge swept Lordaeron and turned the living family into mindless undead thralls.",al={"agamand axe","what is agamand family axe","agamand heirloom axe"},it="identity",add="e4f67fe3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, taking the Agamand heirlooms settles a score with Lordaeron's former aristocracy, who also fell to the plague.",["class:Warrior"]="The weapons kept in the crypt show that the Agamand lineage had martial traditions alongside its wealth and grain stores."},kw={"agamand","agamand crypt","agamand family axe","agamand mills","coleman farthing","heirloom","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:1821","npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","item:agamand-family-sword","item:agamand-family-mace","item:agamand-family-dagger","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Agamand Family Axe","Agamand Heirlooms"}}
E["item:agamand-family-dagger"] = {t="item",n="Agamand Family Dagger",z="tirisfal",s="In northern Tirisfal, the Agamand Family Dagger rests among the weapons in the family crypt. Coleman Farthing seeks it and the family’s other arms to strip his former masters of their legacy and honor.",h="In northern Tirisfal, the Agamand Family Dagger rests among the weapons in the family crypt.",sec={{t="A Legacy in the Crypt",b="Before the Third War, the Agamand family held vast estates and grain mills in the rolling meadows of northern Tirisfal Glades. The Scourge destroyed their power, but their weapons endured in the family crypt north of Agamand Mills. Restless undead members of the household and mindless servants of the Lich King guard the dagger. It recalls the martial heritage and standing the family once held above its servants and tenants.",sp=0},{t="A Spiteful Requisition",b="Coleman Farthing resides at Brill, but he once died in the Agamands’ service. He blames the family for his death, and the dagger means resentment to him, not noble lineage. Farthing sends adventurers into the Agamand Family Crypt for the dagger, sword, axe, and mace. By taking these arms from the tomb, he seeks to rob the Scourge patriarchs of their last dignity and extinguish the Agamand name.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Agamand Family Dagger?",a="The wealthy Agamand family of Tirisfal Glades owned this ancestral weapon. It was laid with the family’s other arms in their crypt, now under Scourge control.",al={"agamand dagger","what is the agamand dagger","family dagger tirisfal"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Agamand Family Dagger found?",a="The dagger rests on an Agamand Weapon Rack inside the Agamand Family Crypt, at the northern end of Agamand Mills in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to find agamand dagger","agamand dagger location","dagger weapon rack location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want this dagger?",a="Coleman Farthing served the Agamands in life and blames them for his death. He wants the dagger and the other heirlooms to strip his former masters of their honor and finish their ruin.",al={"why does farthing want the dagger","farthing agamand quest","why rob agamand crypt"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who are the other weapons in this heirloom set?",a="The set also includes the Agamand Family Sword, the Agamand Family Axe, and the Agamand Family Mace. All lie among weapon racks in the family crypt.",al={"other agamand heirlooms","agamand weapons list","what else is in the crypt"},it="item"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know the bitter divide between the Forsaken who survived in Lordaeron and their former masters, now bound to mindless service in the Scourge.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know how slipping past risen dead to take blades from the crypt’s weapon racks can turn burglary into cold vengeance."},kw={"agamand","agamand mills","coleman farthing","crypt","dagger","heirloom","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:1821","npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","item:agamand-family-sword","item:agamand-family-axe","item:agamand-family-mace","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Agamand Family Dagger","Agamand Heirlooms"}}
E["item:agamand-family-mace"] = {t="item",n="Agamand Family Mace",z="tirisfal",s="At Agamand Mills, the Agamand Family Mace remains locked in the family crypt. Once a proud heirloom of northern Lordaeron, it is now sought by their former servant, Coleman Farthing.",h="At Agamand Mills, the Agamand Family Mace remains locked in the family crypt.",sec={{t="A Legacy in Ruin",b="Before the Third War, the Agamand family held vast farmlands and windmills in northern Tirisfal Glades. Like the region’s other aristocrats, they fell to the plague of undeath. The Scourge raised them as mindless thralls in service to the Lich King, and they wander their ruined estate. Their ancient treasures remain locked in the family crypt. Among them rests the Agamand Family Mace, a remnant of a lineage reduced to shambling undead.",sp=0},{t="A Servant's Vengeance",b="Coleman Farthing seeks the mace along with three other martial heirlooms. The former Agamand employee blames the family for his death. Raised among the Forsaken, Farthing wants to strip the mindless Agamands of every trace of dignity and honor. He seeks the ancestral sword, axe, and dagger as well as the mace, hoping to erase the memory and pride of his former masters from the lands they once ruled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Agamand Family Mace located?",a="The mace rests on a weapon rack inside the Agamand Family Crypt, at the far northern end of Agamand Mills in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is the mace","agamand mace location","find agamand mace"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Agamand Family Mace?",a="Coleman Farthing, a Forsaken living in Brill, demands the mace and the other family heirlooms to settle an old score with his former masters.",al={"who needs the mace","who takes the agamand mace","coleman farthing heirloom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want the heirlooms stolen?",a="Farthing served the Agamands in life and blames them for his death. Taking their prized weapons from the crypt is his way of erasing the last traces of their family honor.",al={"why steal the heirlooms","coleman farthing motive","why hate the agamands"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to the Agamand family?",a="The Agamand family ruled the prosperous Agamand Mills in northern Lordaeron until the plague struck. Their reanimated corpses now wander the estate and crypts as mindless thralls of the Scourge.",al={"who were the agamands","what happened to the agamands","agamand lore"},it="history"},{q="What is the Agamand Family Mace?",a="The Agamand Family Mace is an ancestral heirloom belonging to the once-prosperous Agamand family of Tirisfal Glades. Stored away within the family crypt alongside their other martial treasures, this weapon represents a lingering vestige of the lineage's former standing and honor before the family fell to the Scourge.",al={"agamand mace","what is agamand family mace","agamand mace heirloom"},it="identity",add="0ef93592"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The desecration of the Agamand crypts shows how old mortal grievances can drive the Forsaken to settle scores from life."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand family mace","agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","coleman farthing","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:1821","npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","item:agamand-family-sword","item:agamand-family-axe","item:agamand-family-dagger","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Agamand Family Mace","Agamand Heirlooms"}}
E["item:agamand-family-sword"] = {t="item",n="Agamand Family Sword",z="tirisfal",s="In northern Tirisfal, the Agamand Family Sword remains in the family crypt. The tarnished blade once marked the wealth and standing of the mill-owning dynasty, and Coleman Farthing now seeks it to erase their legacy.",h="In northern Tirisfal, the Agamand Family Sword remains in the family crypt.",sec={{t="A Legacy in the Tomb",b="The Agamands once held great wealth and influence through their mills in northern Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, the family met a gruesome end, and their bodies rose as mindless thralls of the Lich King. Their ancestral weapons, including the ceremonial sword, were sealed inside the Agamand Family Crypt at the northern edge of the mills. Taking these blades from their burial racks is an act meant to break the memory and noble standing of the fallen household.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from Beyond the Grave",b="Coleman Farthing, a Forsaken living in Brill, seeks the sword. He served the Agamands in life and blames his former masters for his death. Farthing sends adventurers to claim the sword along with the dynasty's ancestral axe, dagger, and mace. He aims to strip the shambling Agamands of their last shred of honor and extinguish their bloodline's dignity.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Agamand Family Sword?",a="The Agamand Family Sword is an ancestral weapon of the Agamands, a prominent noble family that ran the grain mills in northern Tirisfal Glades before Lordaeron fell.",al={"agamand sword lore","what is agamand family sword"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the sword located?",a="The sword rests on a weapon rack inside the Agamand Family Crypt, at the northern edge of Agamand Mills in Tirisfal Glades. Scourge thralls and risen members of the Agamand bloodline defend the crypt.",al={"where is agamand sword","sword location agamand"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want this sword?",a="Coleman Farthing served the Agamand family in life and blames them for his death. He seeks their heirloom weapons to strip away their remaining honor and erase the memory of their dynasty.",al={"who wants the sword","why does farthing want heirlooms"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happened to the Agamand family?",a="The Agamands were slaughtered during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. Their dead remain trapped in mindless service to the Lich King, haunting their ancestral estate and crypt.",al={"who are the agamands","agamand mills story"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming artifacts from Tirisfal's former nobility means settling scores with a living past that failed to protect them.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see a blade once polished as an emblem of Lordaeron's aristocracy, now neglected in an unhallowed tomb and marked by ruined martial pride."},kw={"agamand","crypt","farthing","heirloom","mills","scourge","sword","tirisfal"},rel={"quest:1821","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","npc:coleman-farthing","item:agamand-family-axe","item:agamand-family-dagger","item:agamand-family-mace","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Agamand Family Sword","Agamand Heirlooms"}}
E["item:blackened-skull"] = {t="item",n="Blackened Skull",z="tirisfal",s="At Agamand Mills, Blackened Skull trophies mark the fight against the Scourge. Deathguard Dillinger in Brill wants them as proof that the Darkeye Bonecasters are being destroyed.",h="At Agamand Mills, Blackened Skull trophies mark the fight against the Scourge.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Bonecasters",b="Darkeye Bonecasters haunt the Agamand Mills. These skeletal spellcasters turn their necromantic malice against the living and the Forsaken, seeking to secure a forward base for the Lich King's armies in northern Tirisfal. Deathguard Dillinger in Brill asks for their ruined skulls as proof that the Scourge's mystical vanguard is being beaten back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do blackened skulls come from?",a="Blackened skulls come from Darkeye Bonecasters, skeletal spellcasters found in the fields and buildings around Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"blackened skull source","who drops blackened skulls","where to get blackened skulls"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger want blackened skulls?",a="Deathguard Dillinger wants blackened skulls and notched ribs as proof that Forsaken defenders are fighting the Scourge. The Forsaken must keep the Lich King's mindless minions from gaining a foothold so close to Brill and the Undercity.",al={"dillinger skulls","why collect skulls","mills overrun skulls"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the skulls blackened?",a="No one in Brill says what blackened the skulls. Deathguard Dillinger wants them as proof that the Darkeye Bonecasters at Agamand Mills are being destroyed.",al={"why is it blackened","blackened skull lore"}},{q="What is the Scourge doing at Agamand Mills?",a="The Scourge is trying to fortify the abandoned Agamand Mills as a forward staging ground for deeper attacks and raids across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"agamand mills scourge","why are scourge at the mills"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Blackened Skull?",a="A Blackened Skull is a grim trophy harvested from the Darkeye Bonecasters haunting Agamand Mills. These dark remains serve as physical proof to the Forsaken Deathguards that another Scourge spellcaster has been put down before it could help establish an enemy base in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what is blackened skull","blackened skull item","blackened skulls lore"},it="identity",add="d39fbd85"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you fight Darkeye Bonecasters to survive and keep your former master from establishing a staging ground on your doorstep.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you know these skulls are the remains of the skeletal spellcasters targeted at Agamand Mills."},kw={"agamand mills","blackened skull","brill","darkeye bonecaster","deathguard dillinger","notched rib","scourge","the mills overrun"},rel={"quest:426","subzone:agamand-mills","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:brill","item:notched-rib","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Blackened Skull","The Mills Overrun (Classic)"}}
E["item:candle-of-beckoning"] = {t="item",n="Candle of Beckoning",z="tirisfal",s="On Brightwater Lake, Gunther Arcanus keeps an enchanted candle for a summons. Light it on a nearby islet, and the restless spirit Lillith Nefara answers.",h="On Brightwater Lake, Gunther Arcanus keeps an enchanted candle for a summons.",sec={{t="A Test of Allegiance",b="Gunther Arcanus keeps the Candle of Beckoning in a crate beside him on his island in Brightwater Lake. The candle is an instrument for a ritual of summoning. Gunther is a fiercely independent undead sorcerer who broke free of the Lich King's command on his own, and he remains wary of both the Scourge and the Forsaken. To show Gunther that you are not loyal to the Lich King, carry one of the candles southwest to a smaller islet. Set it on an old, bloodstained table and light it. The flame pierces the veil between worlds and beckons the dormant, restless shade of Lillith Nefara, a powerful Scourge agent, so she can be destroyed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Candle of Beckoning used for?",a="Light the Candle of Beckoning on the old, bloodstained ritual table on the smaller islet southwest of Gunther Arcanus's camp to summon the shade Lillith Nefara. The candle draws her dormant spirit into the physical realm.",al={"what does candle of beckoning do","use of candle of beckoning","how to use candle of beckoning"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do you get the Candle of Beckoning?",a="You can take a Candle of Beckoning from a crate beside Gunther Arcanus on his island in Brightwater Lake, in eastern Tirisfal Glades, while undertaking his test of allegiance.",al={"where to find candle of beckoning","how to get candle of beckoning","candle crate location"},gp=true},{q="Who is summoned by the candle?",a="Lighting the candle summons Lillith Nefara, a powerful Scourge agent who haunts the bloody altar off the island's southern coast. Defeating her proves that you do not serve the Scourge.",al={"who does it summon","candle summon target","who is lillith nefara"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gunther Arcanus have these candles?",a="Gunther uses the candles in a trial for anyone seeking his alliance. Fiercely protective of his autonomy from the Scourge and suspicious of outsiders, he demands that you face and destroy the restless dead he summons.",al={"why does gunther have candles","gunther ritual candles"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Candle of Beckoning?",a="The Candle of Beckoning is an enchanted ritual taper found on the isolated island retreat of the necromancer Gunther Arcanus in Brightwater Lake. Kept within a crate beside the reclusive mage, the candle carries potent summoning magic tailored to pierce the veil of death. When set upon a bloodied ritual table on a nearby islet and ignited, its flame acts as a supernatural lure, calling forth the dormant shade of Lillith Nefara.",al={"what is candle of beckoning","candle of beckoning lore","what is the beckoning candle"},it="identity",add="63af5e56"},{q="Why would anyone want a Candle of Beckoning?",a="Anyone seeking an audience or alliance with Gunther Arcanus must first prove their loyalty lies away from the Lich King. Gunther demands proof of allegiance before sharing his formidable talents with the Forsaken. By retrieving a Candle of Beckoning, you can draw forth and destroy Lillith Nefara, demonstrating your resolve to oppose the Scourge and earning the hermit necromancer's hard-won respect.",al={"why do i need candle of beckoning","why want candle of beckoning","purpose of candle of beckoning"},it="why_wanted",add="cb4d5793"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken emissaries sent by the Undercity, handling Gunther's ritual candle is a necessary step to convince the fiercely independent necromancer that you are not thralls of the Lich King.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Gunther's mastery of necromantic and conjuration arts in the way he binds spirits to ritual implements like this candle, outside the Kirin Tor's sanctioned teachings."},kw={"brightwater lake","candle of beckoning","gunther arcanus","lillith nefara","proving allegiance","the dormant shade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:410","quest:409","quest:431","npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:brightwater-lake","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Candle of Beckoning","The Dormant Shade"}}
E["item:darkhound-blood"] = {t="item",n="Darkhound Blood",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal's fields and forests, tainted darkhounds yield Darkhound Blood, a bodily fluid. The Royal Apothecary Society gathers it as an early reagent for experiments to engineer a lethal new plague.",h="In Tirisfal's fields and forests, tainted darkhounds yield Darkhound Blood, a bodily fluid.",sec={{t="Fuel for the New Plague",b="Under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Royal Apothecary Society seeks a virulent contagion that can wipe out Arthas and his Scourge. Apothecary Johaan is stationed in Brill. He theorizes that local beasts, corrupted by dark energies and resilient to the surrounding decay, possess unusual biological properties.\n\nBy distilling wild darkhound blood, Johaan hopes to uncover compounds that can resist or spread virulent necrotic strains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darkhound Blood used for?",a="Apothecary Johaan in Brill uses Darkhound Blood as an early reagent in the Royal Apothecary Society's research to concoct a new plague deadlier than anything Azeroth has ever seen.",al={"darkhound blood use","why get darkhound blood","darkhound blood purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Which creatures yield this blood?",a="Darkhound Blood comes from the cursed, ravenous, and decrepit darkhounds wandering Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to get darkhound blood","who drops darkhound blood","darkhound blood source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why are darkhounds targeted for plague research?",a="Apothecary Johaan theorizes that the blood of beasts acclimated to Tirisfal's corrupted lands may hold the biological secrets needed to synthesize an unstoppable contagion.",al={"why darkhounds","apothecary johaan theory","darkhound properties"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Darkhound Blood?",a="Darkhound Blood is the tainted vital fluid harvested from the feral darkhounds prowling Tirisfal Glades. Warped by dark magic and lingering undeath across the glades, these wretched canines possess blood that carries unique, resilient properties. While repulsive and hazardous to ordinary living creatures, alchemists and researchers find it an ideal medium for biological experiments, particularly when investigating virulent compounds or resisting necrotic decay.",al={"what is darkhound blood","darkhound blood lore","explain darkhound blood"},it="identity",add="db825c3d"},{q="Where does Darkhound Blood come from, and who made it?",a="This blood is naturally harvested from the cursed, ravenous, and decrepit darkhounds that stalk the haunted woodlands and ruined farmsteads of Tirisfal Glades. It is not an artificial concoction, but rather the bodily fluid of beasts that have adapted to and absorbed the blight poisoning the region since the Third War.",al={"source of darkhound blood","where does darkhound blood come from","who created darkhound blood"},it="origin",add="93cde5f9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Harvesting reagents like Darkhound Blood is essential work for the Forsaken. It helps Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society forge their ultimate weapon against the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="In Brill, the Royal Apothecary Society pursues dark experiments whose toxic potential few beyond the Forsaken inner circle fully grasp."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","darkhound","darkhound blood","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:367","npc:apothecary-johaan","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","topic:scourge"},src={"Darkhound Blood","A New Plague"}}
E["item:devlin-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Devlin's Remains",z="tirisfal",s="Near Agamand Mills, Devlin Agamand’s bones carry a bitter legacy. The younger son of the wealthy family that owned the mills, he roamed the road by his ruined home as a mindless Scourge thrall. A traveler struck him down and brought his remains to a survivor in Brill, who sought vengeance.",h="Near Agamand Mills, Devlin Agamand’s bones carry a bitter legacy.",sec={{t="A Bitter Legacy",b="Devlin Agamand lived in the shadow of his elder brother Thurman. Thurman was gentle and tall, while Devlin was frail and sharp-tongued. When the Plague of Undeath swept through northern Tirisfal Glades, the Agamand family failed to protect its lands and laborers. Devlin was among the first to fall. The Scourge raised him as a ravenous ghoul, and his mad chattering haunted the roadside leading to Agamand Mills.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance on the Mantle",b="Coleman Farthing lives in Brill and holds a deep grudge against the Agamand bloodline. He blames the family for failing his own when the plague came. Farthing sent travelers to lay Devlin to rest and gather his remains. He wanted Devlin’s bones on his mantle, to savor how his former masters had been reduced to dust and shattered fragments beneath his heel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Devlin Agamand in life?",a="Devlin was the younger son of the wealthy Agamand family, who owned Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades. His mild-tempered, broad-shouldered brother Thurman stood in sharp contrast to Devlin, who was frail, sickly, ill-tempered, and sharp-tongued.",al={"who is devlin","devlin agamand backstory","about devlin"},it="people"},{q="Where were Devlin's remains gathered from?",a="Devlin’s remains came from his Scourge-controlled corpse, south of Agamand Mills beside the road through Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is devlin","where to find devlin","devlin agamand location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want these bones?",a="Coleman Farthing despises the Agamand family and believes they abandoned him and his loved ones during the Plague. He wants Devlin’s bones on his mantelpiece in Brill as a trophy of vengeance and satisfaction.",al={"why farthing wants remains","coleman farthing motive","why collect agamand bones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is Devlin part of the Forsaken?",a="No. The Plague took Devlin’s mind, and the Scourge made him a mindless ghoul. He wandered near the mills, babbling madness until he was destroyed.",al={"is devlin forsaken","was devlin scourge"},it="side"},{q="What are Devlin's Remains?",a="Devlin's Remains are the skeletal bones of Devlin Agamand, the younger son of the prominent Agamand dynasty. After falling to the Plague of Undeath, Devlin was reduced to a mindless Scourge wretch lingering along the road to his family's ruined mills until put down and collected.",al={"what are devlins remains","devlin remains item","who is devlins remains"},it="identity",add="0d9d3e5c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, the Agamands represent Lordaeron’s old privileged nobility. The family’s failures left common folk to perish and rise as monsters, so desecrating Devlin’s remains is an act of class retribution."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","devlin agamand","devlin's remains","the haunted mills","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:362","npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","quest:354","quest:355","quest:408","subzone:brill"},src={"Devlin's Remains","The Haunted Mills (Classic)"}}
E["item:duskbat-wing"] = {t="item",n="Duskbat Wing",z="tirisfal",s="Duskbats circle Deathknell, and local tailors turn their wings into makeshift armor for newly risen soldiers.",h="Duskbats circle Deathknell, and local tailors turn their wings into makeshift armor for newly risen soldiers.",sec={{t="Improvised Protection in Deathknell",b="New Forsaken claw from Deathknell’s soil with little more than rags and brittle bones. With mindless Scourge and hostile wildlife nearby, they must gather what protection they can. Novice Elreth, assistant to Shadow Priest Sarvis, collects Duskbat Wings and wolf paws to piece together and strengthen clothing and armor for freshly raised warriors before they enter the wilderness to fight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Duskbat Wings used for?",a="In Deathknell, Novice Elreth uses Duskbat Wings and scavenger paws to make, mend, and strengthen garments and armor for newly awakened Forsaken recruits.",al={"duskbat wing use","why get duskbat wings","purpose of duskbat wings"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Duskbat Wings come from?",a="Duskbats and Mangy Duskbats in the groves and hills around Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades provide these wings.",al={"where to find duskbat wings","duskbat wing source","who drops duskbat wings"},it="origin"},{q="Who requests these wings in Deathknell?",a="Novice Elreth asks recruits to gather the wings. She tends the wounded and makes gear under Shadow Priest Sarvis’s direction in the Deathknell chapel.",al={"who needs duskbat wings","turn in duskbat wing","duskbat wing quest giver"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken rely on bat parts for armor?",a="Deathknell has almost no supply lines or traditional manufacturing, so local caretakers scavenge hides, fur, and leathery bat wings from Tirisfal’s native predators. They use these materials to make rudimentary protective clothing for recruits heading into combat.",al={"why bat wings for armor","bat leather armor forsaken"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Duskbat Wing?",a="A Duskbat Wing is the leathery wing harvested from duskbats that flutter through the haunted woods of Tirisfal Glades. In Deathknell, where manufactured goods are scarce, these wings serve as a vital raw material. Tailors and caretakers among the Forsaken stitch and cure the bat hide into durable garments and light armor for newly awakened undead before sending them out to face the hazards of the glades.",al={"what is duskbat wing","duskbat wing item","about duskbat wing"},it="identity",add="d5eef861"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a freshly awakened Forsaken, you gather these wings among your first survival duties, helping keep yourself in one piece during your first skirmishes.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Novice Elreth shows how tailors in Tirisfal use tough bat wings as workable substitutes for leather and fabric."},kw={"deathknell","duskbat","duskbat wing","novice elreth","scavenger paw","the damned","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:novice-elreth","quest:376","item:scavenger-paw","subzone:deathknell","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Duskbat Wing","The Damned (Classic)"}}
E["item:embalming-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Embalming Ichor",z="tirisfal",s="In northern Tirisfal, Rot Hide gnolls carry a fluid that preserves their decaying bodies. The Forsaken Apothecaries seek to study it against the Scourge.",h="In northern Tirisfal, Rot Hide gnolls carry a fluid that preserves their decaying bodies.",sec={{t="Unnatural Preservation",b="Rot Hide gnolls at Garren's Haunt and the nearby mass graves are rotting thralls sent by the Scourge to dig up plague victims. Embalming Ichor flows through their decayed veins, preserving their flesh and sustaining their unlife. Magistrate Sevren in Brill wants vials recovered from these grave robbers. The Royal Apothecary Society will use fresh specimens to study the fluid and seek ways to turn it against the Lich King's minions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Embalming Ichor?",a="Embalming Ichor is a preserving fluid found in the animated bodies of Rot Hide gnolls in Tirisfal Glades. It sustains their rotting flesh and keeps them moving for the Scourge.",al={"embalming ichor","what is ichor","gnoll fluid"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants this ichor collected?",a="Magistrate Sevren in Brill orders Forsaken champions to collect ichor from slain Rot Hides for the Royal Apothecary Society to study.",al={"who needs embalming ichor","magistrate sevren ichor","who wants ichor"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Rot Hide gnolls digging up graves?",a="The Scourge sends Rot Hide gnolls to dig up plague victims buried in the northern mass graves near Garren's Haunt, seeking bodies to bolster its ranks.",al={"why are gnolls graverobbing","mass graves tirisfal","gnoll scourge connection"},it="motive"},{q="What do the Forsaken plan to do with the fluid?",a="The Apothecaries in the Undercity study the ichor for ways to counter the Scourge and for new alchemical formulas.",al={"what does sevren do with ichor","apothecary study ichor","use of embalming ichor"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Embalming Ichor come from, and who made it?",a="Embalming Ichor is harvested from the Rot Hide gnolls haunting the Mass Grave and Garren's Haunt in Tirisfal Glades. It is the foul unnatural fluid used by the Scourge to animate and preserve these undead gnoll servants, sustaining the pseudo-life that drives them to unearth corpses for their masters' armies.",al={"embalming ichor origin","who made embalming ichor","where does ichor come from"},it="origin",add="e6b7bf5e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you deny the Scourge fresh cadavers from the mass graves, helping protect Tirisfal and securing raw materials for your own survival.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you may find the preservation fluid inside Rot Hides intriguing as you study dark alchemical methods and the plague's reagents."},kw={"apothecaries","brill","embalming ichor","garren's haunt","graverobber","magistrate sevren","mass graves","rot hide"},rel={"quest:358","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:garren-s-haunt","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Embalming Ichor","Graverobbers (Classic)"}}
E["item:encrypted-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Scroll",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, an Encrypted Scroll calls a newly risen rogue to training. Sealed by David Trias, it directs its bearer to meet him at the inn and begin training among the Forsaken’s covert operatives.",h="In Deathknell, an Encrypted Scroll calls a newly risen rogue to training.",sec={{t="A Covert Summons",b="In Deathknell, a newly awakened Forsaken with a gift for stealth draws notice. The Encrypted Scroll is handed over after a scout proves capable against the mindless Scourge in the nearby graveyard. Sealed by rogue trainer David Trias, it tells the bearer to find him at the local inn. The summons points a fledgling operative toward the discipline needed to serve the Dark Lady, rather than spend a second chance at life as a pickpocket.",sp=0},{t="Eyes of the Shadowstalkers",b="The scroll’s brief message tells the rogue to make contact in Deathknell before traveling deeper into Tirisfal Glades. Trias watches for promising talent on behalf of the Shadowstalkers, the Forsaken’s covert arm. In Lordaeron, the Forsaken rely on silent blades and cunning scouts against the Scarlet Crusade, surviving Alliance enclaves, and the Scourge left behind. Answering the ciphered summons begins the path toward joining that covert network.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Scroll?",a="The Encrypted Scroll summons a newly risen Forsaken rogue to David Trias at the Deathknell inn to begin rogue training.",al={"what does scroll do","why encrypted scroll","scroll purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Encrypted Scroll?",a="The Encrypted Scroll bears the personal seal of David Trias, the rogue trainer in Deathknell who watches for promising recruits.",al={"who wrote scroll","scroll sender","who is the scroll from"},it="origin"},{q="What are the Shadowstalkers mentioned by David Trias?",a="The Shadowstalkers are a covert Forsaken group of rogues, scouts, and assassins operating across Lordaeron. David Trias assesses new talent for their ranks.",al={"who are shadowstalkers","shadowstalkers forsaken","shadowstalker order"},it="people"},{q="Where do I take the Encrypted Scroll after reading it?",a="Take the Encrypted Scroll to David Trias at the inn in Deathknell.",al={"where turn in scroll","who do i bring scroll to","scroll hand in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Encrypted Scroll?",a="The Encrypted Scroll is a discreet, ciphered dispatch delivered to newly awakened rogues in Deathknell. Stamped with the personal seal of the rogue trainer David Trias, it serves as an initial summons and test of confidentiality, directing promising stealth operatives to introduce themselves before taking on deeper reconnaissance for the Forsaken.",al={"what is encrypted scroll","what is this scroll","encrypted scroll info"},it="identity",add="0c548ac5"},{q="Why does David Trias want to contact you with the Encrypted Scroll?",a="David Trias uses the scroll to recruit and assess fresh talent among the newly risen Forsaken. The Shadowstalkers and the fledgling nation need sharp, capable infiltrators rather than clumsy pickpockets. By quietly summoning promising recruits to the Deathknell tavern, he ensures prospective agents receive proper training and stay on the path toward serving the Dark Lady's intelligence network.",al={"why does david trias send the scroll","why is encrypted scroll wanted","why contact me encrypted scroll"},it="why_wanted",add="496fc5eb"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you begin your instruction in stealth, lockpicking, and dirty fighting under the Forsaken rogue cadre’s watch.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the newly risen in Deathknell, you have an early chance to find a purposeful role in Sylvanas’s emerging kingdom."},kw={"david trias","deathknell","encrypted scroll","forsaken rogues","rogue trainer","shadowstalkers","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:3096","npc:david-trias","subzone:deathknell","topic:rogue","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Encrypted Scroll","Encrypted Scroll (quest)"}}
E["item:gloom-weed"] = {t="item",n="Gloom Weed",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, Gloom Weed grows in the fields between Deathknell and Brill. Gordo, a lumbering Forsaken abomination, gathers it by mistake while searching for doom weed.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, Gloom Weed grows in the fields between Deathknell and Brill.",sec={{t="A Mistaken Harvest",b="Gloom Weed grows in the fields west of Brill and east of Solliden Farmstead. The plant is harmless, with none of the alchemical strength sought by the Royal Apothecary Society. Gordo, an abomination, wanders the road pulling weeds with his clumsy hands. He misunderstood his master's orders and keeps gathering Gloom Weed instead. Then he asks travelers to carry it to Master Holland in the Brill graveyard, much to the apothecary's annoyance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Gloom Weed used for?",a="Forsaken alchemists have little use for Gloom Weed. Gordo gathers it because he mistakes it for doom weed, the herb his master requested.",al={"gloom weed use","what does gloom weed do","who needs gloom weed"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Gloom Weed grow?",a="Gloom Weed grows in fields across Tirisfal Glades between Brill and Deathknell. It can be found along the road and in meadows east of Solliden Farmstead.",al={"where to find gloom weed","gloom weed location","gloom weed spots"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gordo and why is he picking it?",a="Gordo is an abomination sent by Master Holland to gather reagents. His hands are clumsy and his mind is simple, so he pulls the wrong plants and asks passersby to help him.",al={"who is gordo","why is gordo picking weeds","gordo abomination"},it="motive"},{q="What did Master Holland actually want?",a="Master Holland needs doom weed for his experiments in the Brill graveyard. When travelers bring him Gloom Weed, he scoffs at the mistake and sends them to gather the herb he needs.",al={"master holland weed","what does holland need","doom weed vs gloom weed"}},{q="What is Gloom Weed?",a="Gloom Weed is an ordinary, sickly-looking wild plant that sprouts in the cursed soil of Tirisfal Glades, primarily found along the roadways and open fields between Brill and Deathknell. It holds no magical potency or valuable alchemical properties. In truth, it is little more than a common roadside weed—the Tirisfal equivalent of a daisy—that happens to flourish despite the blighted conditions of the countryside.",al={"what is gloom weed","gloom weed lore","gloom weed plant"},it="identity",add="bc1ac336"},{q="Why does anyone want Gloom Weed?",a="Virtually no one actually wants Gloom Weed. The only reason anyone gathers it is because Gordo, a dim-witted abomination wandering the fields near Brill, completely misunderstood his instructions. His master, Junior Apothecary Holland, sent him out to harvest valuable doom weed for Forsaken experiments, but Gordo's lumbering mind confused the names and sent unwitting travelers to pick worthless gloom weed instead.",al={"who wants gloom weed","why gather gloom weed","why collect gloom weed"},it="why_wanted",add="defb981c"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a trained herbalist, you can sense Gloom Weed with Find Herbs, making it easier to spot in Tirisfal's shadowy undergrowth.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken newly departed from Deathknell, you can learn from fetching Gloom Weed how poorly abominations work and how sharply Undercity alchemists speak."},kw={"abomination","brill","doom weed","gloom weed","gordo","master holland","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:5481","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:horde"},src={"Gloom Weed","Gordo's Task (Classic)"}}
E["item:glyphic-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Glyphic Scroll",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, the Glyphic Scroll calls newly raised Forsaken magi to the church. Isabella’s seal marks the summons, which invites fledgling spellcasters to begin their arcane training in undeath.",h="In Deathknell, the Glyphic Scroll calls newly raised Forsaken magi to the church.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Church",b="Newly awakened Forsaken mages find a sealed scroll after culling mindless Scourge in Deathknell’s graveyard. Isabella, the settlement’s mage trainer, marks it with her seal and calls them to the ruined parish sanctuary. There, new magi begin learning the arcane under the Forsaken banner. Death has freed them from mortal weakness, but magic’s corrupting temptations remain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Glyphic Scroll?",a="The Glyphic Scroll introduces newly raised Forsaken magi in Deathknell to their arcane training. Sealed by their trainer Isabella, it calls them to meet her inside the town church.",al={"what is this item","glyphic scroll use","what does scroll do"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Glyphic Scroll?",a="Isabella sends the Glyphic Scroll to newly raised undead with an aptitude for the arcane. She is the mage trainer in Deathknell’s ruined church.",al={"who wrote it","who gave me this","scroll sender"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Isabella want to train new Forsaken mages?",a="Isabella trains Forsaken magi who share the pain of dying and the wish to reclaim their homeland and destinies. She teaches them to build the arcane power to destroy those who oppose the Forsaken, while warning them against magical addiction and corruption.",al={"isabella motive","why train mages"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you receive this first formal summons to training. Undeath does not spare you the corrupting pull of arcane magic.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you reclaim arcane knowledge as a weapon to secure your sovereignty against the Scourge and living enemies."},kw={"arcane","deathknell","glyphic scroll","isabella","mage","scroll","tirisfal"},rel={"quest:3098","subzone:deathknell","topic:mage","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Glyphic Scroll","Glyphic Scroll (quest)"}}
E["item:gregor-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Gregor's Remains",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing seeks Gregor's Remains to settle an old score. The bones belonged to Gregor Agamand, once a member of Tirisfal Glades' wealthiest family.",h="Coleman Farthing seeks Gregor's Remains to settle an old score.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Ruin",b="Before the Third War, the Agamands held great wealth and broad lands across northern Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the family patriarchs chose pride over flight. They fortified their mills and urged their loyal laborers to stand against the undead. The defense failed. The estate fell, and those who stood their ground were butchered and raised into undeath. Gregor Agamand became a mindless servant of the Lich King, haunting the mills his family had ruled.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Vengeance",b="Some who escaped the Lich King's control joined the Forsaken, but the memory of that defense still wounds them. Coleman Farthing, a former mill worker now stationed in Brill, blames the Agamands' pride for trapping his soul in eternal rot. Farthing seeks Gregor's remains as personal retribution against the master who led his household into damnation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Gregor Agamand?",a="Gregor Agamand was a prominent member of the Agamand dynasty, Tirisfal Glades' wealthiest land-owning family before the Third War. When the Plague of Undeath arrived, he and his family fortified their estate instead of fleeing. The Scourge slaughtered and raised everyone inside.",al={"gregor lore","who is gregor","gregor agamand"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want Gregor's Remains?",a="Coleman Farthing once worked at the Agamands' mills. He resents the family for persuading their workers to stay and fight the Scourge, a choice that condemned them all to undeath. He seeks Gregor's remains as long-delayed vengeance.",al={"why coleman wants remains","coleman farthing grudge","why collect gregor bones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are Gregor's Remains found?",a="Gregor Agamand's risen form at the Agamand Mills in the northern hills of Tirisfal Glades yields the remains.",al={"where to find gregor","gregor location","agamand mills gregor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are the Agamands part of the Forsaken?",a="No. Gregor Agamand and his kin remain mindless servants bound to the Scourge, unlike the Forsaken who broke free under Queen Sylvanas.",al={"is gregor forsaken","are agamands scourge","who controls gregor"},it="side"},{q="What are Gregor's Remains?",a="They are the physical remnants of Gregor Agamand, one of the heirs of the prominent Agamand dynasty. After falling to the Plague of Undeath, Gregor rose as a mindless minion of the Scourge, haunting the ruins of his family's once-prosperous mills until put down permanently.",al={"what are gregors remains","gregors remains item","what is gregors remains"},it="identity",add="6dd1de2a"},{q="Where do Gregor's Remains come from?",a="These remains are what is left of Gregor Agamand after he is struck down at the Agamand Mills in western Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, his family fortified their estate and urged their workers to stand and fight, only for all of them to be slaughtered and raised into undeath.",al={"gregors remains origin","who made gregors remains","where did gregors remains come from"},it="origin",add="45ae8d93"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Agamand tragedy echoes the fate of many Forsaken: ordinary folk betrayed by noble pride and abandoned to the horrors of the Plague.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the Agamand Mills strikes at Scourge forces still threatening Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"agamand","brill","coleman","deaths in the family","farthing","gregor","mills","remains","scourge"},rel={"quest:354","npc:coleman-farthing","item:thurman-s-remains","item:nissa-s-remains","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Gregor's Remains","Deaths in the Family (Classic)"}}
E["item:gunther-s-spellbook"] = {t="item",n="Gunther's Spellbook",z="tirisfal",s="Bethor's enchantment now marks Gunther's Spellbook in Tirisfal Glades. The tome may show its owner that other mages have escaped the Lich King's control.",h="Bethor's enchantment now marks Gunther's Spellbook in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Token of Old Kinship",b="Gunther Arcanus once studied magic in Dalaran with Bethor Iceshard and Thule Ravenclaw as fellow Kirin Tor members. When the Plague of Undeath swept Lordaeron, Gunther fell and rose again as one of the undead. In time, he broke free of the Scourge's hold on his mind. Believing he stood alone and that the Lich King's agents hunted him, Gunther grew deeply hostile to outsiders. After the tome was recovered, Bethor laid an arcane enchantment across its pages. Its magic bears Bethor's signature, so Gunther can recognize his old companion's presence and learn that another mage has kept his own will.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="Whose spellbook is this?",a="Gunther Arcanus owns the spellbook and lives on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake, in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who owns the book","gunther book owner","spellbook owner"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q358.4"}},{q="Why did Bethor enchant the spellbook?",a="Bethor placed a personal spell on the tome to prove that he survives in Lordaeron and has escaped the Lich King's control. He hopes Gunther will believe him and ally with the Forsaken.",al={"why enchant the book","bethor spell on book","book magic"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Gunther suspicious when the book is returned?",a="Gunther believes anyone who approaches his retreat may be a Scourge agent sent to enslave him again. At first, he thinks you are only the thief who took his tome.",al={"why is gunther mad","gunther angry","gunther hostile"}},{q="How did Gunther and Bethor know each other?",a="Before the Plague took them, Gunther, Bethor Iceshard, and Thule Ravenclaw studied magic together in Dalaran as friends and Kirin Tor apprentices.",al={"bethor and gunther past","kirin tor connection","dalaran friends"},sp=1,it="origin",bt={"q358.4"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you share Dalaran's arcane roots with the Forsaken's magical leaders and with practitioners who roam the wilderness alone.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Forsaken seek powerful undead who have freed themselves from the Lich King's control."},kw={"arcanus","bethor","dalaran","gunther","iceshard","kirin tor","spellbook","tirisfal"},rel={"quest:366","subzone:gunther-s-retreat","quest:446","subzone:dalaran","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:mage"},src={"Gunther's Spellbook","Return the Book"}}
E["item:hallowed-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Scroll",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, the Hallowed Scroll calls newly awakened Forsaken priests to the ruined chapel. Sealed by Dark Cleric Duesten, it begins their training in faith, willpower, and shadow.",h="In Deathknell, the Hallowed Scroll calls newly awakened Forsaken priests to the ruined chapel.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Faithless",b="Newly risen Forsaken priests feel their bond with the world change violently. As Deathknell is reclaimed amid ongoing chaos, the Hallowed Scroll sends them to seek guidance in the settlement’s ruined chapel. Dark Cleric Duesten’s seal marks the parchment. It introduces the new priests to formal instruction and directs them to report for it, beginning their study of the practical beliefs that shape Forsaken priesthood.",sp=0},{t="The Path of Self-Reliance",b="Dark Cleric Duesten tells priests who answer the summons to leave old teachings behind. The Holy Light, ancestral spirits, and demonic pacts cannot be their crutches. Instead, the scroll begins a discipline grounded in each priest’s own will. Its teachings call on them to survive and rule through conviction, making faith a means of self-command and mastery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Scroll?",a="The Hallowed Scroll is a written summons for newly risen Forsaken priests in Deathknell. It directs them to report to Dark Cleric Duesten in the local chapel for formal training.",al={"what is this scroll","hallowed scroll purpose","item hallowed scroll"},it="identity"},{q="Who sent the Hallowed Scroll?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten’s personal seal marks the Hallowed Scroll. He trains priests in Deathknell’s abandoned church.",al={"who wrote hallowed scroll","who sent the scroll","duesten scroll"},it="origin"},{q="What does Dark Cleric Duesten teach when you bring him the scroll?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten teaches undead priests to leave behind reliance on the Holy Light, ancestral spirits, and otherworldly powers. He says the Forsaken survived through personal willpower and urges young priests to build faith in themselves so they can guide and dominate others.",al={"what does duesten say","forsaken priest beliefs","deathknell priest lore"}},{q="Why does Dark Cleric Duesten want you to have the Hallowed Scroll?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten uses the sealed scroll to summon newly risen Forsaken priests to Deathknell's church. Rather than leaving you to cling to the forgotten Light or ancestral spirits, he intends to instruct you in the grim philosophy of the Forsaken priesthood—relying strictly on your own unyielding willpower to wield power and survive in a hostile world.",al={"why hallowed scroll","why duesten hallowed scroll","purpose of hallowed scroll"},it="why_wanted",add="758c1904"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, this parchment marks your break from traditional human faith. It points you toward conviction of your own and the shadowy arts of the Cult of the Forgotten Shadow.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you receive this summons as Deathknell urgently gathers and trains the newly awakened, bringing them into Sylvanas’s forces."},kw={"deathknell","duesten","forsaken","hallowed scroll","light","priest","tirisfal"},rel={"quest:3097","subzone:deathknell","topic:priest","zone:tirisfal","topic:light","topic:scourge"},src={"Hallowed Scroll","Hallowed Scroll (quest)"}}
E["item:johaan-s-special-drink"] = {t="item",n="Johaan's Special Drink",z="tirisfal",s="At Brill, Apothecary Johaan offers a drink with a deadly purpose. Disguised as a common refreshment, it tests the Royal Apothecary Society’s developing plague.",h="At Brill, Apothecary Johaan offers a drink with a deadly purpose.",sec={{t="A Toxic Brew",b="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan prepares a brew from venomous components and local reagents. Though it looks like a tavern drink, the mixture is made to test how virulent the plague is against living beings. Johaan hands it over as if to quench a captive’s thirst. The work serves the Forsaken apothecaries’ effort to create a weapon potent enough to fulfill Sylvanas Windrunner’s designs for Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="The Cellar Trial",b="Beneath the Gallows' End Tavern, the Deathguard keeps stray intruders in a cellar holding cell. A captured dwarven mountaineer, chained there, eagerly drinks what he mistakes for crude ale. The brew kills him at once, showing the Royal Apothecary Society that its latest strain can swiftly extinguish living victims.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Johaan's Special Drink?",a="Apothecary Johaan prepares a deadly drink in Brill to test the Forsaken’s developing plague against living beings.",al={"what is johaans drink","johaan drink","what is this item"},it="identity"},{q="Who is the drink given to?",a="The drink is taken to the cellar beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill and given to a captured mountaineer held by the local Deathguard.",al={"who drinks it","who do i give the drink to","drink target"},it="target"},{q="What happens when someone drinks it?",a="The prisoner drinks the brew, expecting harsh ale, and dies at once.",al={"does the dwarf die","effect of the drink","what does it do"},sp=1},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan make this drink?",a="Apothecary Johaan makes the drink to test the Royal Apothecary Society’s new plague. He gives it to a captured dwarf to see how effectively it kills mortal life.",al={"why did johaan make it","apothecary johaan motive","why test the plague"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Johaan's Special Drink come from, and who made it?",a="The concoction is brewed directly by Apothecary Johaan at Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Working on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, Johaan refines experimental toxins gathered from local creatures to craft this potent, lethal mixture.",al={"who made johaans special drink","where did johaans special drink come from","who brewed the drink"},it="origin",add="7bd04f9d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help the Royal Apothecary Society and advance Lady Sylvanas’s designs against the living.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you face the danger of being captured by the Deathguard near Tirisfal Glades and used as a test subject."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","captured mountaineer","gallows' end tavern","johaan","johaan's special drink","new plague"},rel={"quest:367","npc:captured-mountaineer","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Johaan's Special Drink","A New Plague (4)"}}
E["item:laced-pumpkin"] = {t="item",n="Laced Pumpkin",z="tirisfal",s="At Apothecary Johaan's hand, Laced Pumpkin turns an ordinary gourd into a deadly test of Forsaken alchemy. In Brill, the Royal Apothecary Society seeks weapons against the Scourge and living human forces.",h="At Apothecary Johaan's hand, Laced Pumpkin turns an ordinary gourd into a deadly test of Forsaken alchemy.",sec={{t="A Bitter Harvest",b="In Tirisfal Glades, the pumpkin looks like ordinary produce salvaged from blighted soil. Apothecary Johaan in Brill treats it with experimental toxins meant to realize the full potential of undeath. The Royal Apothecary Society seeks weapons against the Scourge in the north and living human forces advancing from the south. Even a simple harvest can carry infection and chemical death.",sp=0},{t="The Cellar Experiment",b="In the cellar of the Gallows' End Tavern, Forsaken captors hold a famished Captured Scarlet Zealot. The prisoner accepts a tainted offering as sustenance, desperate for nourishment. The laced pumpkin holds Apothecary Johaan's concoction, and eating it triggers a violent transformation. The human zealot becomes a mindless ghoul, stumbling briefly in agony before collapsing dead on the cold stone floor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Laced Pumpkin?",a="Laced Pumpkin is an ordinary field gourd treated with an experimental formula concocted by Apothecary Johaan in Brill. The formula is meant to test the effects of Forsaken alchemy on living subjects.",al={"laced pumpkin","poison pumpkin","johaan pumpkin"},it="identity"},{q="Who eats the Laced Pumpkin?",a="A Captured Scarlet Zealot, imprisoned by Forsaken captors in the cellar beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, eats the tainted offering after being starved.",al={"who eats it","pumpkin target","feed the pumpkin"},it="target"},{q="What happens when someone eats the pumpkin?",a="The pumpkin's concoction triggers a violent transformation: the prisoner becomes a mindless ghoul, stumbles briefly in agony, then collapses dead on the cold stone floor.",al={"pumpkin effect","what happens to zealot","zealot ghoul"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Why did the Forsaken make this?",a="Apothecary Johaan and the Royal Apothecary Society make new biological concoctions to combat the Scourge in the north and living humans advancing from the south. They use captured enemies as test subjects.",al={"why make poisoned pumpkin","forsaken plague testing"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Laced Pumpkin come from, and who made it?",a="Apothecary Johaan prepared this pumpkin in Brill. Seeking weapons to defend the Forsaken against the Scourge to the north and the living humans to the south, he harvested ordinary produce from the Solliden Farmstead and treated it with his experimental blight concoction.",al={"who made laced pumpkin","where did laced pumpkin come from","creator of laced pumpkin"},it="origin",add="242570cd"},{q="Why does anyone want the Laced Pumpkin?",a="Apothecary Johaan needs the pumpkin fed to a living subject to evaluate his latest chemical formula. It is offered to a starving Scarlet Crusade prisoner locked in the cellar beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, serving as a lethal trial for the Royal Apothecary Society's research.",al={"why want laced pumpkin","why use the laced pumpkin","what is the laced pumpkin needed for"},it="why_wanted",add="071bacef"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the Royal Apothecary Society will use any means to secure Tirisfal against zealous living crusaders. Turning ordinary food into a weapon shows their pragmatism.",["faction:Alliance"]="As Alliance, you know a captured zealot faces a grotesque fate in Forsaken territory. His end is a stark reminder of what may await living humans taken alive."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","captured scarlet zealot","gallows' end","laced pumpkin","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:captured-scarlet-zealot","quest:365","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:human","topic:light"},src={"Laced Pumpkin","Fields of Grief (2)"}}
E["item:maggot-eye-s-paw"] = {t="item",n="Maggot Eye's Paw",z="tirisfal",s="At Garren's Haunt, Maggot Eye's Paw proves the gnoll chieftain is dead. The paw is carried to Brill as proof of his execution for stealing corpses for the Scourge.",h="At Garren's Haunt, Maggot Eye's Paw proves the gnoll chieftain is dead.",sec={{t="Proof of Execution",b="Maggot Eye raided graves and pillaged the countryside near Garren's Haunt, supplying corpses to the Lich King's armies. The Forsaken posted a death sentence and bounty in Brill. To collect the bounty and close it, hunters must bring the gnoll's severed paw back to town. Executor Zygand accepts that proof in place of rumors of Maggot Eye's death.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Executor Zygand want Maggot Eye's paw?",a="Executor Zygand wants Maggot Eye's paw as proof that the condemned gnoll has been killed. Brill pays the bounty once the execution is confirmed.",al={"why paw","maggot eye bounty proof","zygand paw"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What crimes did Maggot Eye commit against the Forsaken?",a="Maggot Eye led raids across northern Tirisfal Glades and stole buried corpses from farmsteads such as Garren's Haunt. He supplied them to the Lich King's armies.",al={"maggot eye crimes","why is maggot eye wanted","what did maggot eye do"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Maggot Eye found?",a="Maggot Eye is found at Garren's Haunt, a ruined farmstead north of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He usually lurks inside the ruined farmhouse.",al={"maggot eye location","where to find maggot eye","garrens haunt gnoll"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why are gnolls working with the Lich King's forces?",a="In Tirisfal Glades, rogue gnoll bands have allied with or fallen under the Scourge's sway. They raid human and Forsaken graves to deliver bodies to necromancers.",al={"gnolls and scourge","why do gnolls steal bodies","scourge gnolls"},it="allies"},{q="What is Maggot Eye's Paw?",a="It is the severed paw of the notorious gnoll Maggot Eye. Taking it serves as undeniable, physical proof of the beast's execution for the authorities in Brill.",al={"what is maggot eyes paw","maggot eye paw","what is this paw"},it="identity",add="9017e45e"},{q="Where does Maggot Eye's Paw come from, and who made it?",a="It is not a crafted artifact, but a trophy carved straight from the corpse of Maggot Eye himself, a treacherous gnoll operating around Garren's Haunt in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where did maggot eye paw come from","maggot eye paw origin","who made maggot eyes paw"},it="origin",add="e496e47e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken of Brill, bringing back Maggot Eye's paw strikes at the body thieves who supply the hated Lich King."},kw={"bounty","brill","executor zygand","garren's haunt","gnoll","maggot eye","maggot eye's paw","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:398","subzone:garren-s-haunt","npc:executor-zygand","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:gnoll","topic:lich-king","quest:358"},src={"Maggot Eye's Paw","Wanted: Maggot Eye"}}
E["item:nissa-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Nissa's Remains",z="tirisfal",s="Nissa's remains belong to a noblewoman of the once-wealthy Agamand dynasty in northern Tirisfal Glades. Slain and made mindless servants of the Scourge during the Third War, Nissa and her family are now hunted by former laborers seeking vengeance.",h="Nissa's remains belong to a noblewoman of the once-wealthy Agamand dynasty in northern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Pride",b="Before the Third War, the Agamands were Tirisfal Glades' wealthiest and most influential dynasty. Their prosperous mills stood across the northern hills. When the Plague of Undeath spread through Lordaeron, the family patriarchs refused to flee. They fortified their estates and persuaded their retainers and laborers to stay and fight. Their pride cost them their lives. The Scourge slew the Agamands, then raised them as mindless thralls bound to the Lich King's will.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Retribution",b="In Brill, survivors who later broke free under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner still remember the Agamands' fatal pride. Coleman Farthing, once a laborer in their mills, resents his former masters for luring the workers into undeath. He charges adventurers with putting down the risen Agamands and retrieving their physical remains, including Nissa's. For Farthing and other Forsaken, destroying these relics offers a grim sense of closure and revenge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Nissa Agamand?",a="Nissa Agamand belonged to the noble Agamand family, which owned the sprawling Agamand Mills in Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, she died with her kin and was raised as an undead minion under the Lich King's control.",al={"who is nissa","nissa lore","nissa agamand"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want Nissa's remains?",a="Coleman Farthing worked in the Agamand mills while alive. He resents the family for refusing to flee and persuading their loyal workers to stay behind and die. Gathering the family's remains lets him take revenge on his former masters.",al={"why coleman want remains","why kill agamands","coleman farthing motive"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these remains gathered?",a="Nissa Agamand haunts the ruined Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades. She wanders among the decrepit farmhouses with her reanimated relatives and mindless Scourge thralls.",al={"where do i find nissa","nissa agamand location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did Nissa retain her free will like the Forsaken?",a="No. Nissa and her family remained enslaved to the Scourge as mindless undead, unlike the Forsaken who broke free from the Lich King. They lacked the sentience and freedom of Undercity's citizens.",al={"is nissa forsaken","did nissa have free will","is nissa scourge"}},{q="What are Nissa's Remains?",a="These are the physical remnants of Nissa Agamand, a member of the wealthy Agamand dynasty that once owned the mills in northern Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, the family fortified their estate and convinced their workers to stand fast. Like the rest of her kin, Nissa fell to the Plague and rose as a mindless thrall in the service of the Lich King.",al={"what is nissas remains","nissa remains","who do nissas remains belong to"},it="identity",add="a9aa03e3"},{q="Where do Nissa's Remains come from, and who made them?",a="They are recovered directly from the destroyed corpse of Nissa Agamand at the Agamand Mills. Once a proud aristocrat, she succumbed to the Plague of Undeath and lingered on her ancestral lands as an undead creature. The remains are what you salvage after laying her mindless Scourge form to rest.",al={"where do you get nissas remains","how to get nissas remains","who dropped nissas remains"},it="origin",add="4cb46b58"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Tirisfal means purging their former Scourge oppressors and the wealthy aristocrats whose foolish pride doomed common laborers to undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="Slaying the reanimated Agamands and clearing their mills helps secure northern Tirisfal Glades from Scourge pockets that threaten Brill and the Undercity."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","nissa agamand","nissa's remains","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:354","npc:coleman-farthing","item:gregor-s-remains","item:thurman-s-remains","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Nissa's Remains","Deaths in the Family (Classic)"}}
E["item:nondescript-letter"] = {t="item",n="Nondescript Letter",z="tirisfal",s="Calvin Montague sends a Nondescript Letter east from Deathknell to Innkeeper Renee in Brill. He gives it to newly awakened Forsaken as an excuse to leave the valley and reach the Gallows' End Tavern.",h="Calvin Montague sends a Nondescript Letter east from Deathknell to Innkeeper Renee in Brill.",sec={{t="A Courier's Errand",b="Calvin Montague asks newly arisen Forsaken near Deathknell to carry an unmarked envelope east to Brill. He claims he is tired from fighting zombies and spiders, and says the letter is for an innkeeper named Renee. His promise of rich compensation sounds hollow, and the errand takes travelers out of the valley toward the Gallows' End Tavern.",sp=0},{t="Suspicious Correspondence",b="Innkeeper Renee first pretends the letter brings sweet news from her saintly mother in Deathknell. When she sees the courier is not fooled, her cheerful manner gives way to irritation. She snatches the letter, refuses to say who sent it or what it contains, and orders the bearer away unless they mean to pay for a room.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Nondescript Letter?",a="The Nondescript Letter is a plain, unmarked envelope Calvin Montague gives newly awakened Forsaken in Deathknell to carry to Innkeeper Renee in Brill.",al={"nondescript letter","what is this letter","calvin's letter"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the letter, and who receives it?",a="Calvin Montague gives the letter to couriers in Deathknell. It is addressed to Innkeeper Renee at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill.",al={"who sent the letter","who gets the letter","letter sender"},it="origin"},{q="What does the letter actually say?",a="The letter's contents are never revealed. When you ask, Innkeeper Renee drops her cheerful act and angrily says its origins and contents are none of your business.",al={"what does the letter say","letter contents","can you read the letter"},it="item"},{q="Why does Calvin Montague want it delivered?",a="Calvin claims he is too busy fighting local zombies and spiders to carry the letter himself. The delivery sends travelers out of Deathknell and introduces them to Brill's inns and resting places.",al={"why send the letter","calvin's motive","why brill"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, Calvin Montague's shifty manner and Renee's abrupt change of mood suggest intrigue and coded underworld messages.",["race:Undead"]="As a newly risen Forsaken, carrying this letter gives you an early reason to leave Deathknell and explore the settlements of Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"a rogue's deal","brill","calvin montague","deathknell","innkeeper renee","nondescript letter","renee"},rel={"quest:8","npc:calvin-montague","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:rogue","topic:forsaken","quest:5481"},src={"Nondescript Letter","A Rogue's Deal"}}
E["item:notched-rib"] = {t="item",n="Notched Rib",z="tirisfal",s="At Agamand Mills, Notched Ribs prove the Forsaken are breaking the Scourge's hold on Tirisfal.",h="At Agamand Mills, Notched Ribs prove the Forsaken are breaking the Scourge's hold on Tirisfal.",sec={{t="Grim Proof of Battle",b="Across northern Tirisfal Glades, the Scourge gathers skeletons in ruined armor. Cracked Skull Soldiers and Rattlecage Soldiers attack any living being or creature with free will they meet. Blades leave their brittle bones pitted and scored. Deathguards demand proof that Forsaken scouts and volunteers are killing these mindless intruders. A battle-marked rib shows that another of the Lich King's thralls has been shattered.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Mills",b="Northwest of Brill, the Agamand Mills hold a key position. If the Scourge settles among the ruined farmsteads and windmills, the undead gain a base from which to strike deep into Tirisfal. Deathguard Dillinger watches the northern roads and sends champions to break up the skeleton ranks before they can gather strength. The notched ribs brought back to Brill show that the Forsaken line holds as it wears down the Scourge vanguard bone by bone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Notched Rib?",a="A Notched Rib is a scarred bone taken from an animated Scourge soldier in northern Tirisfal Glades. It gives Deathguard Dillinger proof that an enemy has been destroyed.",al={"notched rib","what is notched rib","notched rib item"},it="identity"},{q="Where do Notched Ribs come from?",a="Notched Ribs come from Cracked Skull Soldiers and Rattlecage Soldiers patrolling the Agamand Mills, northwest of Brill.",al={"where to find notched rib","who drops notched ribs","notched rib source"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants these bones?",a="Deathguard Dillinger collects Notched Ribs and Blackened Skulls along the road outside Brill to confirm the Scourge advance has been repelled.",al={"who takes notched ribs","notched rib turn in","who needs notched rib"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Scourge gathering at Agamand Mills?",a="The mindless undead are trying to establish a base at Agamand Mills, from which they could strike across Tirisfal Glades and threaten Forsaken settlements.",al={"scourge at agamand mills","why are skeletons at the mills","agamand mills scourge threat"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you gather these shattered bones in a war for survival against the Lich King's mindless minions, who would drag you back into servitude."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","cracked skull soldier","deathguard dillinger","notched rib","rattlecage soldier","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:426","item:blackened-skull","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Notched Rib","The Mills Overrun (Classic)"}}
E["item:putrid-claw"] = {t="item",n="Putrid Claw",z="tirisfal",s="Putrid Claws reach Deathguard Dillinger as proof that the Scourge near Brill is being held back. Mindless undead roam the woods west of town, especially by the old bridge.",h="Putrid Claws reach Deathguard Dillinger as proof that the Scourge near Brill is being held back.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Mindless",b="The mindless Scourge keeps crossing into Tirisfal Glades. Rotting dead and ravaged corpses wander the eastern borders, gathering along roads and near the old bridge west of Brill. Deathguards place bounties on these horrors to protect travelers and garrison supply lines. A severed putrid claw proves that one more shambling corpse has been put down for good.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are putrid claws used for?",a="Deathguard Dillinger in Brill collects putrid claws as bounties. They confirm that local Forsaken recruits are thinning out the Scourge wandering Tirisfal Glades.",al={"putrid claw use","why collect putrid claws","who wants putrid claws"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do putrid claws come from?",a="Putrid claws come from the rotting dead and ravaged corpses roaming the haunted woods west of Brill, especially near the old river bridge.",al={"where to get putrid claws","putrid claw drops","rotting dead drops"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the Scourge in Tirisfal Glades?",a="After Lordaeron's devastation, remnants of the Lich King's mindless Scourge keep crossing west into Tirisfal. They menace roads and settlements unless someone culls them.",al={"why are zombies near brill","scourge in tirisfal"},it="threat"},{q="Why don't the Forsaken just let the mindless undead wander?",a="Queen Sylvanas and the Forsaken broke free of the Lich King's reach and regained their will. The mindless Scourge obey dark instincts or his lingering command, attacking any living or free undead on sight.",al={"forsaken vs mindless zombies","why kill other undead"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Putrid Claw?",a="A Putrid Claw is the severed, rotting hand of a mindless zombie belonging to the Scourge. These decaying appendages are taken from the walking corpses haunting Tirisfal Glades as proof of their destruction.",al={"what is putrid claw","putrid claws info","putrid claw lore"},it="identity",add="37750c4d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a fresh Forsaken initiate leaving Deathknell, clearing the mindless Scourge reminds you that liberation means constant defense against the mindless husks you once resembled."},kw={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard dillinger","putrid claw","ravaged corpse","rotting dead","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:404","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Putrid Claw","A Putrid Task (Classic)"}}
E["item:rattlecage-skull"] = {t="item",n="Rattlecage Skull",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, novice Forsaken warlocks gather skulls from mindless undead. Venya Marthand asks for them as a test of their will before teaching them the dark arts of summoning.",h="In Deathknell, novice Forsaken warlocks gather skulls from mindless undead.",sec={{t="A Neophyte's Test",b="In Deathknell, Venya Marthand guides newly raised Forsaken who have a gift for dark magic. She sends them to subdue Rattlecage Skeletons near the ruined smithy and bring back their severed skulls. The trial tests whether a fledgling warlock can bend creatures from beyond this world to their command. It also lays the groundwork for breaching the void and binding a first demonic servant.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Rattlecage Skulls used for?",a="Venya Marthand collects three Rattlecage Skulls in Deathknell. Forsaken warlocks bring them to prove their focus and resolve before she teaches them to summon and bind an imp.",al={"what are rattlecage skulls","rattlecage skull use","who wants rattlecage skulls"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do Rattlecage Skulls come from?",a="Rattlecage Skulls come from Rattlecage Skeletons, mindless undead wandering the overgrown roads and crumbling grounds near Deathknell's abandoned smithy.",al={"where to get rattlecage skulls","who drops rattlecage skulls","rattlecage skull location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Venya Marthand require skeletal skulls for a warlock trial?",a="Venya Marthand believes power eludes the ignorant, and mastery means bending outside forces to one's will. Slaying mindless skeletons and claiming their heads shows an apprentice can command chaotic energies instead of being consumed by them.",al={"why skulls for warlocks","venya marthand test"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What knowledge is granted after gathering these skulls?",a="After the skulls are offered, Venya Marthand teaches the secret ritual to call forth and bind an imp, giving young warlocks their first true demonic minion.",al={"what do you get from rattlecage skulls","piercing the veil reward"},it="next_step"},{q="What is a Rattlecage Skull?",a="A Rattlecage Skull is the severed head of a Rattlecage Skeleton, one of the mindless undead wandering the blighted grounds near Deathknell's abandoned smithy. For aspiring Forsaken warlocks, these grim trophies serve as proof of basic magical resolve and focus, showing that an initiate can confront and overcome the walking dead.",al={"what is rattlecage skull","rattlecage skull lore"},it="identity",add="9627b388"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Forsaken warlock, gathering these skulls is your first milestone in discipline. It proves you have the cold will to enslave your first demon.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, shattering lesser, unthinking skeletons reflects the Forsaken belief in dominion through sheer will. Free-willed undead set themselves apart from mindless thralls."},kw={"deathknell","imp summoning","piercing the veil","rattlecage skeleton","rattlecage skull","tirisfal glades","venya marthand"},rel={"quest:1470","topic:warlock","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Rattlecage Skull","Piercing the Veil"}}
E["item:samuel-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Samuel's Remains",z="tirisfal",s="Near Deathknell, Samuel's Remains are gathered from a Scourge thrall and laid beside Marla.",h="Near Deathknell, Samuel's Remains are gathered from a Scourge thrall and laid beside Marla.",sec={{t="A Tragic Reunion",b="Samuel Fipps and his wife Marla lived peacefully in Tirisfal Glades before the plague of undeath swept across Lordaeron. Samuel succumbed to the contagion and became the Scourge's mindless servant. Marla escaped undeath, but Samuel struck her down. With her dying breath, she asked to be buried beside him once his cursed form was put to rest. Novice Elreth in Deathknell sends newly awoken Forsaken northeast of the settlement to find Samuel's wandering form, recover his bones, and bury them in the front row of the local cemetery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Samuel Fipps?",a="Samuel Fipps was a human who lived in Tirisfal Glades before the Third War. The Scourge plague killed him, then raised him as an undead thrall of the Lich King. Driven by mindless hunger, he eventually slew his wife, Marla.",al={"samuel fipps","who is samuel","samuel backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where are Samuel's remains found?",a="Samuel's remains are recovered from his wandering form among the ruined camp along the road northeast of Deathknell. Putting an end to his mindless existence lets his bones be retrieved.",al={"find samuel remains","where is samuel fipps","samuel location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken bury him beside his wife?",a="Marla's dying wish was to rest beside her beloved husband, even though he killed her. Novice Elreth honors her request to show that the newly liberated Forsaken still have compassion, respect for the dead, and the humanity that separates them from the Scourge.",al={"why bury samuel","marla grave","marlas last wish"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Samuel's Remains come from?",a="These are the mortal physical remains of Samuel Fipps, a former resident of Tirisfal Glades who fell to the plague of undeath and became a mindless pawn of the Scourge. After roaming the wilderness northeast of Deathknell, his undead body is struck down so his remnants can finally be gathered and laid to rest.",al={"samuels remains origin","where do samuels remains come from","who made samuels remains"},it="origin",add="29aac9a9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you learn early that honoring the tragic dead marks the moral divide between free Forsaken and the Scourge's mindless thralls."},kw={"deathknell","marla fipps","marla's grave","marla's last wish","novice elreth","samuel fipps","samuel's remains"},rel={"quest:6395","npc:novice-elreth","subzone:deathknell","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Samuel's Remains","Marla's Last Wish"}}
E["item:scarlet-armband"] = {t="item",n="Scarlet Armband",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Scarlet Armbands mark the zealots pressing into Forsaken territory. Executor Arren demands them as proof that the newly risen have struck back.",h="In Deathknell, Scarlet Armbands mark the zealots pressing into Forsaken territory.",sec={{t="A Badge of Fanaticism",b="Scarlet Armbands mark the Scarlet Crusade's followers, from Initiates to fresh converts. The Crusade's red insignia warns newly risen Forsaken in Deathknell that danger waits close by. Crusaders make no distinction between the Scourge's mindless servants and the free-willed subjects of the Dark Lady. To them, every walking corpse must burn. Executor Arren gathers the armbands to confirm that enemy scouts southeast of Deathknell have died and that new Forsaken can defend their fledgling nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Executor Arren want Scarlet Armbands?",a="Executor Arren wants Scarlet Armbands as proof that the Scarlet Crusade encampment southeast of Deathknell is being culled. The Crusade threatens newly awakened Forsaken, and the tokens show its forward scouts and recruits have been eliminated.",al={"why collect armbands","arren armband quest","scarlet armband purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wears these armbands?",a="Scarlet Initiates, Scarlet Converts, and the messenger Meven Korgal wear these armbands. They are lower-ranking members of the Scarlet Crusade stationed near Deathknell.",al={"who drops scarlet armbands","where to find armbands"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade hate the Forsaken?",a="The Scarlet Crusade hates the Forsaken because its zealots see no difference between the Lich King's mindless Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. They regard all undead as abominations to be eradicated.",al={"why scarlet attack undead","crusade vs forsaken","scarlet zealots"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the camp where these armbands can be found?",a="The camp lies just southeast of Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades, in the hills beyond the settlement's perimeter.",al={"scarlet camp location","deathknell scarlet camp","where are scarlet converts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Scarlet Armband?",a="A Scarlet Armband is a piece of crimson cloth worn by initiates and converts of the Scarlet Crusade. It serves as an identifying insignia for the zealous human order, marking its wearers as pledged crusaders dedicated to eradicating all undead from Lordaeron, regardless of whether those undead serve the Scourge or possess free will like the Forsaken.",al={"what is scarlet armband","scarlet armband meaning","scarlet armband lore"},it="identity",add="365b2391"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly raised Forsaken, gathering Scarlet Armbands brings you face to face with the living world's hatred. Your survival depends on defending yourself against the Crusade."},kw={"deathknell","executor arren","scarlet armband","scarlet convert","scarlet crusade","scarlet initiate","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:381","npc:executor-arren","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","quest:382","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king"},src={"Scarlet Armband","The Scarlet Crusade (quest)"}}
E["item:scarlet-crusade-documents"] = {t="item",n="Scarlet Crusade Documents",z="tirisfal",s="At the Crusade's camp near Deathknell, a messenger carries Scarlet Crusade Documents through Tirisfal. The intercepted orders name field commanders and direct their forces, giving the Forsaken military leadership intelligence on Scarlet positions across the Glades.",h="At the Crusade's camp near Deathknell, a messenger carries Scarlet Crusade Documents through Tirisfal.",sec={{t="Intercepted Orders",b="Meven Korgal carried the documents from the Crusade's encampment southeast of Deathknell. By order of the Highlord, they direct the captains of the Crusade's Tirisfal Regional Command. Captain Perrine must further fortify the southwest tower and gather information on the undead in Brill. Captain Vachon must crush undead movement near the northern tower, while Captain Melrose watches the borders of the Plaguelands. The orders name Scarlet field officers, their posts, and their duties across Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Brill",b="Executor Arren sees that Deathknell's local forces cannot use the full breadth of this intelligence. The captured documents become a newly awakened Forsaken's passport out of Deathknell. Carry them northeast, past Cold Hearth Manor, to Brill, and deliver them to Executor Zygand outside Brill Town Hall. With the orders in hand, Forsaken military leaders plan swift strikes against Scarlet commanders entrenched across the Glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was carrying these documents?",a="Meven Korgal, a Scarlet Crusade courier, carried the documents at the Crusade's encampment southeast of Deathknell.",al={"who dropped these","scarlet messenger","meven korgal"},it="target"},{q="What information is inside the documents?",a="By order of the Highlord, the documents direct the Crusade's Tirisfal Regional Command. Captain Perrine must fortify the southwest tower and gather information on the undead in Brill. Captain Vachon must crush undead movement near the northern tower, and Captain Melrose must watch the borders of the Plaguelands.",al={"what do the papers say","document contents"},it="power"},{q="Who needs to see these documents?",a="You recover the documents for Executor Arren in Deathknell, and he entrusts them to you for delivery to Executor Zygand, who oversees regional military efforts outside Brill Town Hall.",al={"where do i take them","who do i give the documents to"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are these documents important to the Forsaken?",a="The orders reveal where Scarlet officers are deployed across Tirisfal Glades. The Forsaken can use them to eliminate enemy leaders and shatter the zealots' regional morale.",al={"why do forsaken want them","scarlet documents importance"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are the Scarlet Crusade Documents?",a="They are a sheaf of confidential military papers, battle reports, and orders carried by a courier of the Scarlet Crusade. While much of the bundle consists of ordinary scouting accounts and propaganda about skirmishes with the Forsaken, it also contains detailed operational instructions intended for Crusade officers stationed throughout Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what are the documents","scarlet crusade documents info","scarlet documents item"},it="identity",add="b6ac443b"},{q="Where did the Scarlet Crusade Documents come from?",a="They are directives issued by order of the Crusade's Highlord to the captains of its Tirisfal Regional Command. They were entrusted to a courier named Meven Korgal, whom the Forsaken found at the Crusade's camp southeast of Deathknell.",al={"who wrote scarlet crusade documents","scarlet documents source","where did documents come from"},it="origin",add="5f5d9cee"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an awakened Forsaken, carrying these papers takes you from Deathknell's cemetery trials into the wider war effort directed from Brill."},kw={"brill","deathknell","executor arren","executor zygand","meven korgal","scarlet crusade documents","the red messenger","vital intelligence"},rel={"quest:382","quest:383","npc:executor-arren","npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scarlet Crusade Documents","The Red Messenger","Vital Intelligence (Classic)"}}
E["item:scarlet-insignia-ring"] = {t="item",n="Scarlet Insignia Ring",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Insignia Rings mark the Crusade's members. In Brill, the Forsaken collect them as proof that another zealot has fallen.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Insignia Rings mark the Crusade's members.",sec={{t="Tokens of Zealotry",b="Every Scarlet Crusade fighter in Tirisfal Glades carries an insignia ring, from new neophytes and zealous friars to captains Melrache and Perrine. The Crusade's fiery sigil marks each ring, identifying members within an order consumed by paranoia. To outsiders, the rings identify Lordaeron's most fanatical human remnant.",sp=0},{t="Bounty of the Dreadlord",b="Deathguard Burgess in Brill collects the rings under orders from Varimathras, Lady Sylvanas's dreadlord lieutenant. The Forsaken see the Scarlet Crusade as a pestilence across their newly claimed homeland. Recruits bring the rings back to Brill as proof of a Crusader's death and of their loyalty to the throne of the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wears these insignia rings?",a="Nearly every Scarlet Crusade member stationed in Tirisfal Glades wears an insignia ring. Wearers include neophytes, missionaries, zealots and vanguards, as well as field officers Captain Perrine, Captain Melrache and Captain Vachon.",al={"who drops rings","which crusaders have rings","ring owners"},it="people"},{q="Why does Deathguard Burgess want Scarlet Insignia Rings?",a="Deathguard Burgess collects the rings as proof that Scarlet Crusaders are being killed. Acting on orders from Varimathras and the Dark Lady, the Forsaken garrison in Brill uses them to judge recruits' loyalty and success in clearing humans from Lordaeron.",al={"why collect rings","proof of demise reason","burgess rings"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does the insignia on the ring represent?",a="The ring bears the Scarlet Crusade's mark and represents its holy war to eradicate all undeath from Lordaeron. Crusaders wear it with fierce pride as a badge of righteousness, while their obsession drives them to slaughter anyone outside their order.",al={"scarlet symbol","what is the insignia","ring emblem"}},{q="What role does Varimathras have in collecting these rings?",a="Varimathras is Sylvanas Windrunner's chief lieutenant in the Undercity. He oversees military efforts against hostile living humans in Tirisfal Glades, making the Scarlet Crusade a priority for Forsaken commanders such as Executor Zygand and Deathguard Burgess.",al={"varimathras orders","why varimathras want rings","dreadlord involvement"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Scarlet Insignia Ring?",a="A Scarlet Insignia Ring is an identifying band carried by members of the Scarlet Crusade across Tirisfal Glades. Bearing the militant order's emblem, it marks the wearer's allegiance to their fanatical crusade to eradicate undeath. For the Forsaken defending their new borders, these rings serve as indisputable proof that an enemy soldier or officer has been eliminated.",al={"what is scarlet insignia ring","scarlet insignia ring lore","what are these rings"},it="identity",add="d4097e42"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, tearing these rings from dead Crusaders declares Tirisfal belongs to the dead and fulfills the orders of the Dark Lady and Varimathras.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, collecting these rings helps secure a foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms by weakening the fanatical crusaders around the Undercity."},kw={"brill","deathguard burgess","executor zygand","proof of demise","scarlet crusade","scarlet insignia ring","tirisfal glades","varimathras"},rel={"quest:374","npc:deathguard-burgess","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","npc:varimathras","npc:executor-zygand","quest:370","subzone:brill"},src={"Scarlet Insignia Ring","Proof of Demise (quest)"}}
E["item:scavenged-goods"] = {t="item",n="Scavenged Goods",z="tirisfal",s="Around Deathknell, Forsaken gather Scavenged Goods from equipment boxes. Newly risen undead rely on these discarded supplies to arm and clothe the recruits who follow.",h="Around Deathknell, Forsaken gather Scavenged Goods from equipment boxes.",sec={{t="Fending for Themselves",b="New Forsaken rise in Deathknell's graveyard with little more than rotting burial shrouds. Nearby settlements and kingdoms offer the undead no aid, so they must salvage what they need. Deathguard Saltain gathers discarded weapons, tools, and garments from supply crates across the village, then gives them to the next recruits to rise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are scavenged goods used for?",a="Deathguard Saltain gathers Scavenged Goods to outfit fresh Forsaken rising from the cemetery. Without the supplies in nearby crates, they would enter Tirisfal Glades unarmed and unclad.",al={"scavenged goods purpose","why collect scavenged goods","what does saltain do with scavenged goods"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where are these goods found?",a="The goods are found in equipment boxes outside cottages and around ruined buildings across Deathknell.",al={"where to find scavenged goods","scavenged goods location","where are equipment boxes"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who asks for the scavenged goods?",a="Deathguard Saltain, an officer in Deathknell, asks newly awakened Forsaken to gather the supplies. He teaches them self-reliance and prepares for the recruits who follow.",al={"who wants scavenged goods","deathguard saltain quest"},it="wants",gp=true},{q="What are scavenged goods?",a="These are assorted pieces of serviceable equipment, clothing, and gear salvaged from old crates left scattered around Deathknell. Rather than pristine armaments, they are discarded remnants of the town's past life that can still serve a practical purpose for newly awakened Forsaken.",al={"scavenged goods what are they","what is scavenged goods"},it="identity",add="f565021a"},{q="Where do the scavenged goods come from?",a="They come from equipment boxes abandoned among the ruined structures of Deathknell. Once belonging to the living inhabitants of Lordaeron before the kingdom fell to the plague, these supplies remained forgotten in the ruins until the Forsaken began reclaiming the town as their staging ground.",al={"scavenged goods origin","who made scavenged goods","where did scavenged goods come from"},it="origin",add="0b2267aa"},{q="Why does Deathguard Saltain want scavenged goods?",a="The Forsaken are continually awakening newly risen dead from the graveyard, and these fresh recruits enter the world with little to their names. Deathguard Saltain gathers these salvaged items so the emergent undead have basic clothing and equipment rather than stumbling into service unarmed and exposed.",al={"why does saltain want scavenged goods","why collect scavenged goods","why are scavenged goods needed"},it="why_wanted",add="36f8df02"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you need discarded equipment to survive; the living offer you no aid or mercy."},kw={"deathguard saltain","deathknell","equipment boxes","forsaken supplies","scavenged goods","scavenging deathknell"},rel={"quest:3902","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scavenged Goods","Scavenging Deathknell"}}
E["item:scavenger-paw"] = {t="item",n="Scavenger Paw",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Scavenger Paw comes from the young, ragged wolves roaming the hills. Newly awakened Forsaken gather the severed paws for local caretakers to stitch into crude protective gear.",h="In Deathknell, Scavenger Paw comes from the young, ragged wolves roaming the hills.",sec={{t="Cobbled Armor in Deathknell",b="Deathknell's newly returned Forsaken have little to spare. The Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade press against Tirisfal, so every scrap of hide and bone goes to practical use. Novice Elreth assists Shadow Priest Sarvis and gathers paws from scavenger wolves, along with bat wings. She uses them to make serviceable garments and armor for Forsaken who have just risen from their graves, still disoriented by their return.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Scavenger Paws used for?",a="Novice Elreth collects Scavenger Paws in Deathknell and stitches raw animal parts into basic armor and garments for fresh Forsaken.",al={"scavenger paw purpose","use for paws","why collect paws"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Where do you find them?",a="You find them on Young Scavengers and Ragged Scavengers, feral wolves roaming the woods and fields around Deathknell.",al={"paw drop location","where to get paws","which wolves drop paws"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who asks for these paws?",a="Novice Elreth asks for the paws. She assists Shadow Priest Sarvis by treating wounded recruits, tailoring equipment, and outfitting those sent into the field.",al={"who wants scavenger paws","paw quest giver","novice elreth paws"},gp=true},{q="What is a Scavenger Paw?",a="A Scavenger Paw is the severed paw of a scavenger wolf roaming the haunted woods of Tirisfal Glades around Deathknell. While seemingly grim trophies, these durable animal parts serve as raw material for the newly awakened Forsaken, who must utilize every scrap of native wildlife to craft necessities and survive.",al={"scavenger paw identity","what are scavenger paws","what is scavenger paw"},it="identity",add="41bb56d4"},{q="Where does a Scavenger Paw come from?",a="These paws are harvested from the young and ragged scavenger wolves prowling the perimeter of Deathknell. Stalking the withered glades just beyond the village walls, these feral beasts scavenge the blighted countryside for carrion, making them easy prey for fresh Forsaken recruits looking to prove their strength.",al={"scavenger paw source","where to get scavenger paw","scavenger wolf paws"},it="origin",add="366465d3"},{q="Why does anyone want Scavenger Paws?",a="Novice Elreth in Deathknell collects them to tailor armor and sturdy clothing for newly awakened Forsaken soldiers. Resources are desperately scarce for the newborn free undead, and Elreth pieces together pelts, wings, and paws to patch together gear that can protect you from the mindless undead and Scarlet Crusaders threatening the haven.",al={"why collect scavenger paws","who needs scavenger paws","scavenger paws use lore"},it="why_wanted",add="f83538b8"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly awakened Forsaken with decaying flesh and little gear, you can gather parts from local predators to assemble enough armor for Tirisfal's hazards.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see how Novice Elreth stitches wolf paws and bat wings into crude gear for the fledgling Forsaken settlements."},kw={"deathknell","novice elreth","ragged scavenger","scavenger paw","the damned","young scavenger"},rel={"quest:376","item:duskbat-wing","npc:novice-elreth","subzone:deathknell","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},src={"Scavenger Paw","The Damned (Classic)"}}
E["item:thurman-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Thurman's Remains",z="tirisfal",s="At Agamand Mills, Thurman's remains bear witness to the family's failed stand against the Scourge. The once-wealthy mill owner fell to the Plague and now wanders his ruined estate as an undead thrall.",h="At Agamand Mills, Thurman's remains bear witness to the family's failed stand against the Scourge.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Ruin",b="Before the Third War, the Agamands were Tirisfal Glades' wealthiest landowners, with extensive mills and dozens of local workers. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, Thurman Agamand and his kin fortified their estate instead of fleeing. Certain their wealth and strong mills could withstand the attack, they persuaded their loyal workers to take up arms beside them. The defense failed. The Agamands and their workers were slaughtered and made mindless servants of the Lich King. Coleman Farthing, a former worker who rose as Forsaken, now demands the destruction of his former masters. He seeks Thurman's remains as proof that the foolish patriarch paid for dooming his household.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Thurman Agamand?",a="Thurman Agamand belonged to the wealthy Agamand dynasty, which owned Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge struck Lordaeron, his pride led him to persuade the workers to stay and fight. Everyone on the estate was slaughtered and raised again.",al={"thurman agamand","who is thurman","who was thurman"},it="people"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want Thurman's remains?",a="Coleman Farthing was a mill worker who trusted the Agamands and died defending their estate. Now one of the Forsaken, he seeks Thurman's remains in vengeance against the employers who doomed their workers to undeath.",al={"why coleman wants remains","coleman farthing motive","why kill thurman"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Did Thurman have free will when he was destroyed?",a="No. After death, Thurman Agamand remained under the Scourge's mental domination, unlike the Forsaken of the Undercity. He served as an unthinking minion until he was destroyed at the mills.",al={"did thurman have free will","was thurman scourge","is thurman forsaken"}},{q="Who else from the Agamand family is being targeted?",a="Coleman Farthing also seeks the destruction and recovered remains of Gregor Agamand and Nissa Agamand, alongside Thurman, to end the bloodline that once ruled the mills.",al={"other agamands","agamand family members","deaths in the family targets"}},{q="What are Thurman's Remains?",a="These are the physical remnants of Thurman Agamand, recovered after putting down his restless undead form at the Agamand Mills. Once part of the prosperous Agamand dynasty that owned the surrounding mills, Thurman fell victim to the Plague of Undeath and lingered as a mindless thrall of the Scourge until finally struck down.",al={"what is thurmans remains","thurman remains item","who is thurman remains"},it="identity",add="559ae8e6"},{q="Where do Thurman's Remains come from?",a="They are taken directly from the destroyed corpse of Thurman Agamand at the Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge swept through the land, Thurman and his kin fortified their estate and persuaded their workers to make a stand. The defense failed, turning the family into Scourge monstrosities until their bodies were broken.",al={"where do you get thurmans remains","thurmans remains origin","how are thurmans remains made"},it="origin",add="0ea47aa9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you reclaim these remains to settle accounts with aristocratic masters whose hubris led their workers into the Scourge's grasp."},kw={"agamand","agamand mills","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","thurman agamand","thurman's remains","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:354","item:gregor-s-remains","item:nissa-s-remains","npc:coleman-farthing","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","subzone:brill"},src={"Thurman's Remains","Deaths in the Family (Classic)"}}
E["item:tirisfal-pumpkin"] = {t="item",n="Tirisfal Pumpkin",z="tirisfal",s="At Solliden Farmstead, living humans still tend pumpkins in blighted Tirisfal. The Forsaken take them for the Royal Apothecary Society’s mixtures.",h="At Solliden Farmstead, living humans still tend pumpkins in blighted Tirisfal.",sec={{t="Harvest in a Blighted Land",b="West of Brill, crops still grow despite the corruption spreading across Lordaeron. At Solliden Farmstead, living human farmers work the soil and grow large orange pumpkins under the watch of the nearby Scarlet Crusade. The harvest feeds these farmers. To the Forsaken of Brill, the pumpkins are targets for sabotage and raw materials for Apothecary Johaan.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Reagents",b="Deathguard Simmer sends young Forsaken into the contested fields to steal pumpkins from under the farmers’ noses. The vegetables do not feed the dead; they go into the Royal Apothecary Society’s cauldrons. Apothecaries test how natural plants react to plagues and experimental mixtures, using Lordaeron’s remaining crops against the living.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Tirisfal Pumpkins be found?",a="They grow at Solliden Farmstead, west of Brill and just north of Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"pumpkin location","where are the pumpkins","solliden farm pumpkins"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Forsaken want these pumpkins?",a="Deathguard Simmer orders the pumpkins stolen to deny them to the surviving humans and the Scarlet Crusade, and to bring them to Apothecary Johaan in Brill as raw materials for apothecary research.",al={"why steal pumpkins","johaan pumpkin","what are pumpkins for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can players eat or cook with Tirisfal Pumpkins?",a="No. The Royal Apothecary Society gathers them for its mixtures, and adventurers do not use them for cooking.",al={"can you eat tirisfal pumpkins","pumpkin cooking ingredient"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is currently growing them?",a="Living human farmers still tend the soil at Solliden Farmstead, with loose protection from the Scarlet Crusade at a nearby watchtower.",al={"who owns the farm","solliden farmers"},it="origin"},{q="What is a Tirisfal Pumpkin?",a="A Tirisfal Pumpkin is a hardy gourd cultivated by surviving human farmers at the Solliden Farmstead in Tirisfal Glades. In a blighted realm where living vegetation struggles to endure, these gourds represent precious sustenance for the living and vital alchemical reagents for the Forsaken.",al={"what is tirisfal pumpkin","tirisfal pumpkin","what are tirisfal pumpkins"},it="identity",add="dab4ae64"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you raid Solliden Farmstead both to deprive living people of food and to provide Apothecary Johaan with materials for Forsaken research.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the pumpkins at Solliden Farmstead as the surviving people of Lordaeron trying to feed themselves amid Forsaken raids."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","deathguard simmer","fields of grief","pumpkin","reagent","solliden farmstead","tirisfal pumpkin"},rel={"quest:365","subzone:solliden-farmstead","npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:deathguard-simmer","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken"},src={"Tirisfal Pumpkin","Fields of Grief (Classic)"}}
E["item:vicious-night-web-spider-venom"] = {t="item",n="Vicious Night Web Spider Venom",z="tirisfal",s="In eastern Tirisfal, Vicious Night Web Spider Venom carries an old contagion. The Royal Apothecary Society prizes it for holding historical disease strains, and uses it in work on the Forsaken's New Plague.",h="In eastern Tirisfal, Vicious Night Web Spider Venom carries an old contagion.",sec={{t="A Preserved Contagion",b="Apothecary Johaan in Brill studies old texts about a plague that killed thousands. The contagion behind that outbreak endured for centuries inside the venom of local Night Web spiders. Apothecaries hunt the vicious breed in Venomweb Vale, south of the Scarlet Monastery, and draw out the preserved contagion for their alchemical experiments.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="The Forsaken seek a weapon against the Scourge and the living. Johaan adds the venom as the final component of his experimental concoction, hoping its preserved contagion will work with the mixture.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What makes this venom unique compared to regular spider poison?",a="Old texts studied by the Royal Apothecary Society tell of an ancient plague pathogen preserved in the venom glands of the Night Web spider lineage. Their poison holds a reservoir of contagion.",al={"why this venom","night web venom lore","spider venom plague"},it="power"},{q="Where can the spiders carrying this venom be found?",a="Vicious night web spiders live mainly in Venomweb Vale, in eastern Tirisfal Glades south of the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"where to find spider venom","vicious night web spider location","venomweb vale spiders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this venom in Brill?",a="Apothecary Johaan in Brill wants multiple samples to continue his research into a new infectious agent for the Forsaken.",al={"who needs spider venom","apothecary johaan venom","who uses the venom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does the venom fit into the Forsaken's research?",a="Johaan needs the venom as the final component of his experiment. Old texts describe an ancient plague preserved in Night Web Spider venom, and he wants to learn whether its contagion will work with his concoction.",al={"apothecary research venom","new plague component","forsaken spider venom"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Vicious Night Web Spider Venom?",a="This is a potent, lethal toxin harvested directly from the vicious night web spiders that infest eastern Tirisfal Glades. Beyond ordinary predatory poison, it harbors a rare preserving quality, maintaining the virulence of an ancient deadly contagion within the spiders' fangs.",al={"what is vicious night web spider venom","vicious night web venom","spider venom tirisfal"},it="identity",add="901a886f"},{q="Where does Vicious Night Web Spider Venom come from, and who made it?",a="It is naturally produced by the vicious night web spiders dwelling in Tirisfal Glades, notably throughout Venomweb Vale south of the Scarlet Monastery. According to ancient texts uncovered by the Royal Apothecary Society, the spiders absorbed and preserved a virulent contagion that wiped out thousands in bygone ages, carrying that ancient pestilence in their venom to this day.",al={"who made vicious night web venom","where does vicious night web venom come from","origin of night web venom"},it="origin",add="8bf9d73e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, gathering this venom helps Lady Sylvanas pursue her mandate to develop a plague powerful enough to bring down Arthas and his Scourge.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue familiar with natural neurotoxins, you can see how the Royal Apothecary Society turns dangerous wild venoms into engineered bio-weapons."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","new plague","spider venom","tirisfal glades","venomweb vale","vicious night web"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","quest:367","subzone:venomweb-vale","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet"},src={"Vicious Night Web Spider Venom","A New Plague (3)"}}
E["item:vile-fin-scale"] = {t="item",n="Vile Fin Scale",z="tirisfal",s="Vile Fin Scale comes from murloc tribes prowling Tirisfal’s northern coasts and waterways. In Brill, the Royal Apothecary Society studies these samples as it works on a plague meant to strike the living and the Scourge.",h="Vile Fin Scale comes from murloc tribes prowling Tirisfal’s northern coasts and waterways.",sec={{t="Apothecary Reagents",b="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks a blight that can spread through the living and the Scourge. Simple toxins are easy to brew, but an infectious disease needs properties that help it pass from one population to another. In Brill, Apothecary Johaan studies Vile Fin scales for their natural resilience and mucous coatings. He hopes these traits can help stabilize his experimental contagions and carry them onward.",sp=0},{t="The Coastline Menace",b="The Vile Fin tribe inhabits Tirisfal Glades’ northern shores and western shallows, where its members threaten travelers and press into Forsaken territory. Gathering their scales helps keep the feral murloc populations in check and supplies Johaan’s laboratory with fresh organic material for tests in biological warfare.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want these scales?",a="Apothecary Johaan studies Vile Fin scales for the Royal Apothecary Society’s work on a new plague. Ordinary poisons lack the power to spread, so he examines the scales’ natural properties for help carrying his experiments from one population to another.",al={"what does johaan do with scales","why vile fin scales","johaan plague scale"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Vile Fin murlocs be found?",a="Vile Fin murlocs inhabit Tirisfal Glades’ coasts, especially the northern shoreline and western waters beside Brightwater Lake and the sea.",al={"where are vile fin","murloc location tirisfal","where to get scales"},gp=true},{q="What makes the New Plague project important to the Forsaken?",a="The Forsaken seek a weapon against their bitter rivals: the mindless Scourge and the living races who see them as monsters. Johaan’s work in Brill is an early effort toward that kingdom-wide aim.",al={"why new plague","forsaken plague goal","what is apothecary johaan researching"},it="motive"},{q="Which specific creatures carry these scales?",a="Vile Fin Minor Oracles, Muckdwellers, and Puddlejumpers of the Vile Fin tribe in Tirisfal carry these scales.",al={"who drops vile fin scale","which murlocs drop scales"},gp=true},{q="What is a Vile Fin Scale?",a="A Vile Fin Scale is a tough, aquatic scale harvested from the hides of the Vile Fin murloc tribe dwelling along the shores and waterways of Tirisfal Glades. Naturally slick and resistant to northern coastal waters, these scales make an unusually durable biological material.",al={"what are vile fin scales","vile fin scale lore","murloc scale"},it="identity",add="cceccf47"},{q="Where do Vile Fin Scales come from?",a="These scales are biological remnants harvested directly from members of the local Vile Fin murloc tribe, such as puddlejumpers, muckdwellers, and minor oracles prowling the northern and western coastlines of Tirisfal Glades. They are natural growths rather than manufactured goods.",al={"who made vile fin scale","where to get vile fin scales","origin of vile fin scale"},it="origin",add="3252dae7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, each Vile Fin scale you gather aids the Royal Apothecary Society’s duty to develop a weapon for Forsaken survival against the living and the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help secure Tirisfal Glades’ outskirts for messengers and travelers when you clear aggressive coastal murloc settlements."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","murloc","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades","vile fin scale"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","quest:367","subzone:brill","topic:murloc","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Vile Fin Scale","A New Plague (2)"}}
E["npc:apothecary-johaan"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Johaan",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan works to develop a plague for the Forsaken. The Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas have charged him with lethal experiments on local plants and animals.",h="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan works to develop a plague for the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Servant of the Society",b="Apothecary Johaan works openly from Brill in Tirisfal Glades for the newly formed Royal Apothecary Society. Like his colleagues across Lordaeron, he follows direct orders to create biological and alchemical weapons. The Forsaken hope these weapons will secure their fragile future against the living and the Scourge alike.",sp=0},{t="Brewing the New Plague",b="Apothecary Johaan leads early field trials of the Society's New Plague. He uses materials from Tirisfal's corrupted wildlife and blighted farms, including darkhound blood, murloc scales, spider venom and stolen farm pumpkins. He tests the mixtures on living subjects, measures their potency and sends his findings south to Silverpine Forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Apothecary Johaan researches alchemy in Brill for the Royal Apothecary Society. He directs young Forsaken champions to gather vile reagents across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"apothecary johaan","who is johaan","johaan brill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Apothecary Johaan?",a="You can find Apothecary Johaan outside in Brill, near the gallows and alchemical apparatus. The town lies just north of the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"johaan location","where is johaan","find johaan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Johaan working on?",a="Johaan is developing early strains of the New Plague. He tests biological agents and venomous extracts from Tirisfal's blighted fields and beasts.",al={"johaan experiments","what does johaan do","johaan plague"},it="wants"},{q="What does he do with the plague samples?",a="After mixing samples and assessing their lethality, Johaan sends couriers to deliver them to allied apothecaries in Silverpine Forest.",al={"delivery to silverpine","where do plague samples go"},it="purpose"},{q="What organization does Johaan belong to?",a="Johaan belongs to the Royal Apothecary Society, the alchemical guild that serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken in the Undercity.",al={"johaan faction","who does johaan work for"},it="ties"},{q="Why is he interested in the local farms?",a="Human farms such as the Solliden Farmstead and nearby pumpkin patches grow pumpkins that Johaan uses as raw reagents for experimental toxins.",al={"fields of grief johaan","why send me to farms"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Johaan on?",a="Johaan serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken as a member of the Royal Apothecary Society. Operating out of Brill, he labors on behalf of the Undercity to develop chemical weapons and plagues meant to secure their domain against both the Scourge and the living.",al={"johaan faction","who does johaan serve","apothecary johaan loyalty"},it="side",add="c51cf856"},{q="Why is Apothecary Johaan in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Johaan is stationed in Brill to conduct field research and harvest local ingredients across Tirisfal Glades. His proximity to nearby blighted flora, wildlife, and contested human settlements lets him gather testing reagents and experiment directly on subjects away from the Undercity's main chambers.",al={"why is johaan here","why is apothecary johaan in brill","johaan tirisfal purpose"},it="why_here",add="90913b50"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you belong to the Forsaken cause Johaan's research serves. He develops weapons meant to secure a permanent homeland free of the Scourge and living threats.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may see how Johaan's deadly concoctions protect its foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms. Orcs and tauren might balk at alchemical blights."},kw={"apothecary","brill","johaan","plague","royal apothecary society","silverpine","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:brill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:367","quest:365","quest:445","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},src={"Apothecary Johaan"}}
E["npc:aramis-hammerhand"] = {t="npc",n="Aramis Hammerhand",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand trains the newly risen Forsaken in holy combat. The Holy Light can answer their call, but wielding it burns their decayed flesh and demands fierce discipline.",h="In Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand trains the newly risen Forsaken in holy combat.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Deathknell",b="In Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand guides Forsaken who hold fast to their former faith. Before the Scourge swept across the north, many people of Lordaeron answered the Silver Hand's call. Aramis survived the fall of Lordaeron, then rose into undeath. He kept the martial and spiritual teachings of his former life, and now guides others who refuse to surrender their devotion.",sp=0},{t="The Agony of the Holy Light",b="For the Forsaken, channeling the Holy Light demands fierce will. Its power burns necrotic flesh and stirs long-dead nerves into excruciating pain. Aramis teaches new paladins that faith means enduring that torment. He asks them to face the physical and spiritual costs of wielding a force opposed to their undead nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand trains Forsaken paladins in Deathknell's chapel in Tirisfal Glades. He guides the newly risen who seek holy combat.",al={"aramis lore","who is hammerhand","deathknell paladin trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Can the Forsaken actually wield the Holy Light?",a="Yes. The Forsaken can call upon the Holy Light through willpower and conviction. Its radiant power burns and scours their rotting flesh even as it heals or strengthens them.",al={"can undead be paladins","how do undead use light","forsaken light"}},{q="Where can I find Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand stands inside the chapel at Deathknell, the Forsaken's starting settlement in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is aramis","hammerhand location","paladin trainer deathknell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Aramis Hammerhand offer?",a="Aramis offers class-specific training to newly risen paladins, including A Difficult Path, Rediscovering the Light, A Light in the Darkness, Coming to Terms, and Continue Your Training.",al={"aramis quests","deathknell paladin quests"},gp=true},{q="Why is a paladin trainer working for the Forsaken?",a="Before the plague, Lordaeron was the cradle of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Many newly liberated Forsaken remember their oaths and keep to their sacred calling despite their undead state.",al={"why are there forsaken paladins","forsaken silver hand"},it="purpose"},{q="Does using the Light heal the undead in the normal way?",a="The Light can mend undead bodies and grant martial strength, but using it is excruciating. It awakens their senses, forcing them to feel the rot of their own bodies.",al={"does light hurt undead","light healing undead lore"}},{q="Whose side is Aramis Hammerhand on?",a="Aramis Hammerhand stands firmly with the Forsaken. Though he embraces the discipline of a paladin and teaches newly risen undead to wield the Holy Light, his loyalty belongs to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner and the kingdom she is forging in the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"aramis hammerhand allegiance","who does aramis serve","aramis hammerhand faction"},it="side",add="63e97215"},{q="Why is Aramis Hammerhand here in Deathknell?",a="You will find Aramis stationed in the ruined chapel of Deathknell to receive newly awakened Forsaken. He awaits those freshly freed from the Scourge's grasp who carried holy vows in life, guiding them through the agony and discipline required to rekindle their sacred power in undeath.",al={"why is aramis in deathknell","aramis hammerhand deathknell location","what brought aramis here"},it="why_here",add="c81bf44f"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a Forsaken paladin, Aramis is your first mentor. He guides you through the pain and spiritual discipline of wielding the Holy Light in an undead body.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you can see in Aramis that undeath need not sever Lordaeron's heritage of holy warfare, though the path brings great suffering."},kw={"aramis","chapel","deathknell","forsaken","hammerhand","light","paladin","tirisfal","trainer"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:light","quest:98601","quest:90902","quest:98389","quest:91208"},src={"Aramis Hammerhand"}}
E["npc:calvin-montague"] = {t="npc",n="Calvin Montague",z="tirisfal",s="At Deathknell's gate, Calvin Montague preys on newly awakened Forsaken leaving the graveyard, tricking passersby into errands for him.",h="At Deathknell's gate, Calvin Montague preys on newly awakened Forsaken leaving the graveyard, tricking...",sec={{t="A Grifter by the Gate",b="Calvin Montague waits just beyond Deathknell's gates, where the road leads out into Tirisfal Glades. He tries to talk wandering adventurers into carrying his letters, using false pretenses instead of handling his own correspondence or paying a fair courier's fee. Other prominent undead named Montague manage banking interests in the Undercity. Calvin follows a less reputable path, relying on petty schemes and deception.",sp=0},{t="A Rogue's Scheme",b="Calvin Montague offers travelers a sealed message to carry for him. Those with sharp wits or underworld training can quickly see through his words. Newly risen undead may still be searching for purpose in Tirisfal's bleak ruins, but Calvin's offer shows how scarce trust can be in the service of the Dark Lady.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Calvin Montague?",a="Calvin Montague is a Forsaken rogue waiting near Deathknell's exit gate in Tirisfal Glades. He tries to cheat newly risen undead into running an unpaid errand for him.",al={"calvin montague","who is calvin montague","calvin deathknell"},it="identity"},{q="What does Calvin want adventurers to do?",a="Calvin Montague tries to talk passing travelers into carrying a letter for him under false pretenses, hoping to get free courier service through smooth talk.",al={"calvin montague quest","calvin letter","what does calvin want"},it="wants"},{q="Is Calvin Montague related to the Undercity bankers?",a="Calvin shares his surname with prominent Undercity bankers Ophelia, Mortimer, William, and Randolph Montague. No family relationship has been confirmed.",al={"montague family","undercity bankers montague","calvin related to bankers"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Calvin Montague be found?",a="Calvin Montague waits along the road just outside Deathknell's wooden northern gate, where he can intercept adventurers heading into Tirisfal Glades.",al={"calvin location","where is calvin montague","find calvin montague"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Calvin Montague on?",a="Calvin is an independent Forsaken rogue looking out primarily for himself. While he resides within the lands of the Forsaken and interacts with its travelers, his schemes and shady dealings show he serves his own pocket rather than any noble cause or state enterprise.",al={"calvin montague faction","who does calvin montague serve","is calvin montague forsaken"},it="side",add="9e392640"},{q="Why is Calvin Montague stationed outside Deathknell?",a="Calvin positions himself right along the road leading out of Deathknell to prey upon newly awakened undead. Freshly risen Forsaken heading into the wider reaches of Tirisfal Glades make easy marks for an opportunistic rogue looking to trick someone into doing his courier work for free.",al={"why is calvin montague here","calvin montague deathknell location","why is calvin at the deathknell exit"},it="why_here",add="0598d792"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Forsaken rogue, you can recognize Calvin Montague's attempt to manipulate the uninitiated as a cheap hustle by a fellow cutpurse.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the newly risen leaving Deathknell, you may learn early that not all of Sylvanas's subjects seek solidarity."},kw={"a rogue's deal","calvin montague","con artist","deathknell","forsaken rogue","montague","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:8","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Calvin Montague"}}
E["npc:captured-mountaineer"] = {t="npc",n="Captured Mountaineer",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, a captured Ironforge Mountaineer is held beneath the Gallows' End Tavern. The Forsaken keep him bound for the Royal Apothecary Society's experiments.",h="In Brill, a captured Ironforge Mountaineer is held beneath the Gallows' End Tavern.",sec={{t="A Prisoner in the Cellar",b="Beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, an Ironforge Mountaineer is held far from Khaz Modan. While patrons drink above, the Royal Apothecary Society uses him to test its concoctions. Apothecary Johaan and his peers measure their developing plague against living Alliance bodies, testing how swiftly and painfully their toxins kill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Captured Mountaineer?",a="He is an Alliance scout from Ironforge, now held by the Forsaken in the Gallows' End Tavern basement in Brill.",al={"who is this dwarf","dwarf in brill tavern","captive dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Forsaken keeping him alive in the basement?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society keeps him alive as a test subject. Apothecaries such as Johaan give him experimental mixtures to study their effects on living dwarves.",al={"why keep him alive","why is he in the tavern","what are they doing to the dwarf"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens to him during the tests?",a="The apothecaries force him to swallow concoctions as they develop a new plague. The lethal mixture kills him, showing the toxin's progress.",al={"does the dwarf die","what happens in a new plague"},sp=1},{q="Who else interacts with him down here?",a="The Deathguard use the tavern cellar to hold captured mountaineers until they can be dealt with. Apothecaries also come there to conduct experiments.",al={"who talks to the dwarf","renee lauer"}},{q="Whose side is the Captured Mountaineer on?",a="He belongs to Ironforge and the Grand Alliance. Dwarven mountaineers typically patrol the mountain passes of Khaz Modan and contested borders, making him a sworn enemy of the Forsaken and the Horde.",al={"captured mountaineer faction","captured mountaineer alliance or horde","what side is the mountaineer on"},it="side",add="5cefef25"},{q="What does the Captured Mountaineer want?",a="Locked in chains inside a damp cellar, his primary hope is survival and escape. Unfortunately for him, the Royal Apothecary Society views him not as a prisoner of war to ransom, but as raw material for refining their deadly New Plague.",al={"what does the captured mountaineer want","captured mountaineer goal","captured mountaineer desires"},it="wants",add="d7cdb16d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For a dwarf, seeing an Ironforge brother caged beneath a Forsaken tavern and subjected to alchemical trials shows the Forsaken's hostility toward the living.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, living Alliance captives serve the Royal Apothecary Society's effort to perfect a plague against the Scourge and the living."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill basement","captured mountaineer","dwarf prisoner","gallows end tavern","ironforge scout"},rel={"quest:367","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Captured Mountaineer"}}
E["npc:captured-scarlet-zealot"] = {t="npc",n="Captured Scarlet Zealot",z="tirisfal",s="Beneath Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, a Scarlet Zealot is held captive. Forsaken apothecaries use him to test concoctions for the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Beneath Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, a Scarlet Zealot is held captive.",sec={{t="A Bitter Captive in Brill",b="Beneath Gallows' End Tavern, a Scarlet Crusade zealot remains chained and defiant. His unyielding faith reflects his order, and he sees the undead around him as abominations. He calls on the Light to shield him from the foul creatures holding him. The Forsaken did not capture him out of mercy. As a living human, he is valuable test material for Apothecary Johaan, who uses him to measure the lethality of experimental plagues and toxins under development.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a Scarlet Zealot kept alive in Brill?",a="The Forsaken keep him captive beneath Gallows' End Tavern as a living human test subject for poisons and chemical agents the Royal Apothecary Society is developing.",al={"why is scarlet zealot captured","why keep zealot alive","who is the zealot in brill cellar"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can I find this captive?",a="He is held in the cellar beneath Gallows' End Tavern, in the center of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is captured scarlet zealot","scarlet zealot location","zealot in brill"},gp=true},{q="How does he react to the Forsaken around him?",a="He remains fanatically defiant in captivity, calling on the Light to protect him from his undead captors and swearing the Scarlet Crusade will rid Azeroth of them.",al={"what does the zealot say","zealot dialogue","renee lauer and zealot"}},{q="Who is the Captured Scarlet Zealot?",a="He is a captured human soldier belonging to the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. Imprisoned in the dark cellar beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, he serves as an involuntary subject for Forsaken interrogation, taunting, and alchemical trials.",al={"captured scarlet zealot who","who is the zealot in the basement","scarlet prisoner brill"},it="identity",add="e526a97b"},{q="Whose side is the Captured Scarlet Zealot on?",a="He is fiercely loyal to the Scarlet Crusade, an uncompromising order dedicated to eradicating all undead. Even bound and surrounded by Forsaken captors, he refuses to recant his allegiance, spitting defiance and branding the Forsaken as unnatural abominations.",al={"captured scarlet zealot faction","what side is the zealot on","zealot loyalty"},it="side",add="7dde551c"},{q="What does the Captured Scarlet Zealot want?",a="Above all, he seeks the absolute destruction of the Forsaken and the Scourge alike. Held helpless in chains, he wants nothing more than to see the Crusade burn the Undercity and purge what he views as blasphemous monsters from Lordaeron.",al={"zealot goal","what does the prisoner want","captured zealot motive"},it="wants",add="69888ecc"},{q="Who is the Captured Scarlet Zealot tied to?",a="He is bound to the Scarlet Crusade, answering to its commanders who wage war across Tirisfal Glades. Locally, he is under the close watch of Apothecary Johaan and the patrons of the Gallows' End Tavern, who treat him as an enemy captive and an alchemical test subject.",al={"captured zealot connections","who does the zealot answer to","captured zealot ties"},it="ties",add="aafac6db"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="To Brill's Forsaken, this chained fanatic represents the crusaders who seek their extermination. They put him to use as test material for an apothecary.",["class:Priest"]="Scarlet zealots claim the Holy Light for their own, but this prisoner's unwavering faith offers no defense against Forsaken captivity."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","captured scarlet zealot","gallows' end tavern","prisoner","scarlet crusade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","quest:365"},src={"Captured Scarlet Zealot"}}
E["npc:carolai-anise"] = {t="npc",n="Carolai Anise",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Carolai Anise teaches alchemy while her experiments make the guards uneasy.",h="In Brill, Carolai Anise teaches alchemy while her experiments make the guards uneasy.",sec={{t="A Volatile Craft",b="Carolai Anise pursues alchemy in Brill, where she teaches novice alchemists. Many Forsaken researchers work under the Royal Apothecary Society's grim mandate, but Carolai makes her own strange brews inside the settlement. Her unpredictable experiments and smoking retorts are well known. The Deathguards watching Brill openly grumble that she seems bent on blowing up her own house.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Carolai Anise?",a="Carolai Anise is an undead alchemy trainer in Brill, in Tirisfal Glades. She teaches aspiring Forsaken to brew potions, elixirs, and oils.",al={"carolai anise","brill alchemist","who is carolai"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find her?",a="Carolai works with her alchemy supplies inside a building in Brill, the primary Forsaken town in central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is carolai anise","carolai anise location","where is brill alchemy trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Deathguards complain about her?",a="The Deathguards complain that Carolai's unstable experiments could cause an accident. They joke or fret that she may eventually blow up her entire house.",al={"deathguards on carolai","blowing up house","carolai anise danger"},it="fame"},{q="Whose side is Carolai Anise on?",a="She is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Operating openly out of the settlement of Brill, she serves the broader Forsaken community by instructing fellow undead and Horde travelers in the foundational arts of brewing and distillation.",al={"carolai anise faction","is carolai anise forsaken","who does carolai anise serve"},it="side",add="d66f68b4"},{q="What does Carolai Anise want?",a="Carolai is consumed by her alchemical crafts and volatile experimentation. While she passes on her trade to apprentices, she seems intent on pursuing reckless, bubbling concoctions—so much so that the local town guard worries her experiments might level her workshop.",al={"carolai anise motive","what is carolai anise doing","carolai anise goal"},it="wants",add="dbcf2ddc"},{q="Why is Carolai Anise here in Brill?",a="She resides in Brill to teach alchemy to newly awakened Forsaken and Horde travelers stepping forth from Deathknell. Tirisfal Glades offers plenty of peace and raw ingredients for her to pursue her brewing and push her volatile craft to dangerous extremes.",al={"why is carolai anise in brill","carolai anise tirisfal glades why","why is carolai anise here"},it="why_here",add="917b8b51"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly liberated Forsaken learning to handle reagents, you can learn the foundations of alchemy from Carolai in Tirisfal Glades.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a gatherer in Tirisfal, you can bring Carolai peacebloom, silverleaf, and earthroot to refine into potent mixtures."},kw={"alchemy","apothecary","brill","carolai anise","forsaken trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","quest:95314","topic:forsaken"},src={"Carolai Anise"}}
E["npc:coleman-farthing"] = {t="npc",n="Coleman Farthing",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill's Gallows' End Tavern, Coleman Farthing nurses a hatred born in the Agamand Mills. He served the wealthy Agamand dynasty in northern Tirisfal, where he and the other laborers died defending their employers' estate from the Scourge. Now Forsaken, he seeks vengeance on his former masters.",h="In Brill's Gallows' End Tavern, Coleman Farthing nurses a hatred born in the Agamand Mills.",sec={{t="A Bitter Servant",b="Before the Third War, Coleman Farthing worked at the Agamand Mills, Tirisfal Glades' largest milling and agricultural operation. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the aristocratic Agamand family refused to flee their valuable lands. They urged their household and laborers to take up arms, promising they could hold the farmsteads against the undead horde. Coleman and his fellow workers stayed, believing their masters. Every last one of them died.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from the Grave",b="Coleman Farthing broke free into the Forsaken after being raised into undeath, and he still hates the Agamands. He blames his former employers' greed and pride for tricking their staff into an impossible last stand, not only the Scourge. From a tavern in Brill, he sends Horde champions to the blighted mills to kill the risen Agamand kin and plunder heirloom weapons from their family crypt, stripping away the last of their honor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Coleman Farthing be found?",a="Coleman Farthing spends his days in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, in central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"coleman farthing location","where is coleman farthing","coleman farthing brill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Coleman hate the Agamand family so much?",a="When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the Agamand patriarchs persuaded their workers, Coleman among them, to stay and defend the mills instead of fleeing. The entire workforce was slaughtered, and Coleman sees their call to fight as arrogant manipulation that led him to his death.",al={"why does coleman hate agamands","coleman farthing motivation","agamand mills grudge"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to the Agamand Mills?",a="The Scourge overran the sprawling estate. Its wind-driven mills lie ruined and haunted, while Agamand family members and their slain workers wander the blighted fields as mindlessly hostile undead under the Lich King's sway.",al={"what happened to agamand mills","agamand mills lore","who owns agamand mills"},it="history"},{q="What tasks does Coleman give to adventurers?",a="Coleman sends adventurers north to the Agamand Mills to cull the roaming undead, slay risen members of the Agamand lineage and recover their remains for desecration, then plunder ancestral weapons from the Agamand Family Crypt.",al={"coleman farthing quests","agamand quests brill"},gp=true},{q="Why does Coleman want the Agamand heirloom weapons?",a="Coleman sees the Agamands' ancestral weapons as signs of the hollow pride that led his fellow workers to die. He sends warriors to plunder them from the family crypt, stripping the dynasty of its honor and putting the weapons to practical use against their enemies.",al={"agamand heirlooms quest lore","why steal agamand weapons"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is Coleman Farthing related to Bishop Farthing?",a="Coleman Farthing and Bishop Farthing share a surname and roots in the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, but no confirmed record establishes their family ties.",al={"bishop farthing relation","coleman farthing family"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Coleman Farthing?",a="Coleman Farthing is a Forsaken residing in Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. In life, he was a laborer employed by the wealthy Agamand family at their mills in western Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, his masters convinced him and their other workers to stand and fight rather than flee. The mills were overrun, slaughtering everyone present. Now reanimated into free will under the Dark Lady, Coleman is consumed by bitter resentment toward the family that led him to his gruesome death.",al={"who is coleman farthing","coleman farthing lore","who is coleman"},it="identity",add="54a8df22"},{q="Whose side is Coleman Farthing on?",a="Coleman Farthing stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. He dwells among his undead brethren in Brill, safe from the mindless Scourge that plagues the ruins of his former life. While he supports the Forsaken's struggle to secure Tirisfal Glades, his focus remains deeply personal: directing passing adventurers to settle his old grievances against the masters who doomed him.",al={"coleman farthing faction","is coleman horde","who does coleman serve"},it="side",add="3d5d2be6"},{q="What does Coleman Farthing want?",a="Coleman wants absolute vengeance against the Agamand family. He seeks to see the reanimated remains of his former masters—Gregor, Nissa, Thurman, and Devlin—utterly destroyed so he can smash their remains under his heel. Beyond their deaths, he wants their ancestral crypt plundered of its valuable heirloom weapons, stripping the proud dynasty of their dignity, their lineage, and their resting place.",al={"what does coleman want","coleman farthing goal","coleman goals"},it="wants",add="ac8a2a0f"},{q="Why is Coleman Farthing here in Brill?",a="Coleman stays at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill because it serves as the primary gathering place for newly risen undead and Horde travelers journeying north. Lacking the martial strength to assault the overrun Agamand Mills on his own, he bides his time among travelers, recruiting capable warriors and spellcasters to march northwest and enact vengeance on his behalf.",al={"why is coleman in brill","why is coleman at gallows end","coleman farthing brill"},it="why_here",add="3e94941c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Coleman reflects the resentment many commoners hold toward Lordaeron's old nobility, whose arrogance and pride often hastened their subjects' deaths during the plague.",["class:Warrior"]="Coleman points aspiring warriors toward the Agamand Family Crypt to plunder the martial heirlooms of a fallen aristocratic house and arm themselves for the wars ahead."},kw={"agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","gallows' end tavern","lordaeron","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:gallows-end-tavern","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","quest:354","quest:362","quest:1821","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Coleman Farthing"}}
E["npc:dark-cleric-beryl"] = {t="npc",n="Dark Cleric Beryl",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Dark Cleric Beryl guides newly awakened undead priests in the shadows. Stationed in the Gallows' End Tavern, he teaches them shadow magic and helps them adapt to their unholy existence under the Dark Lady.",h="In Brill, Dark Cleric Beryl guides newly awakened undead priests in the shadows.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Shadows",b="Dark Cleric Beryl mentors new Forsaken priests upstairs in Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. He teaches that a priest's power comes from darkness and shadow, yet mastering the dark also requires knowing the light. Newly risen priests turn their focus to shadow and the dark arts under his guidance. Their early trials include crafting their Garments of Darkness and proving their dedication to this new path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dark Cleric Beryl?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl trains Forsaken priests upstairs in Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. He helps newly risen undead priests expand their spellcraft and embrace the shadows.",al={"beryl role","who is beryl","cleric beryl lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dark Cleric Beryl?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, within Tirisfal Glades.",al={"beryl location","where is beryl","find dark cleric beryl"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do Forsaken priests use the title Dark Cleric?",a="Forsaken priests who leave behind the traditional dogmas of the Holy Light, or balance them with darker disciplines, take the title Dark Cleric. Their order teaches that the Forsaken were forged in corruption and that darkness is their home. A priest must learn to use both light and dark with discretion.",al={"what is a dark cleric","forsaken dark clerics","why dark cleric"}},{q="What quests does Beryl offer?",a="Beryl guides early Forsaken priest training, including In Favor of Darkness and Garments of Darkness. These teach young acolytes to aid their allies and wear vestments suited to the shadow.",al={"beryl quests","dark cleric beryl quests"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Dark Cleric Beryl on?",a="Beryl is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. Operating out of Brill, he serves the interests of Undercity and the Horde by instructing newly awakened undead who hear the call of the priesthood, helping them master shadow and discipline in service to their people.",al={"beryl faction","who does beryl serve","beryl allegiance"},it="side",add="4c1b78a6"},{q="Why is Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill?",a="Beryl is stationed in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill to guide young Forsaken priests emerging from Deathknell. As fledglings venture out into Tirisfal Glades, he provides them with the training and robes necessary to survive against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other perils threatening Lordaeron.",al={"why is beryl in brill","why is beryl here","beryl gallows end"},it="why_here",add="fd6d5379"},{q="What does Dark Cleric Beryl want?",a="Beryl seeks to ensure that the Forsaken's fledgling priests are properly equipped and disciplined in their craft. He charges practitioners to understand their dark calling, testing their readiness and outfitting them in the garments suited to channel the powers of shadow and unyielding will.",al={"what is beryl's goal","what does beryl want","beryl motives"},it="wants",add="6191615e"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest in Tirisfal Glades, you can turn to Beryl in Brill for guidance in shadow magic and the harsh passage into unholy power.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see in Beryl how the Forsaken adapt to their cursed condition, leaving behind the blind devotion of Lordaeron's former faiths for practical, shadowy resilience."},kw={"beryl","brill","dark cleric beryl","forsaken priest","gallows' end tavern","priest trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","quest:5650","quest:5651","topic:forsaken"},src={"Dark Cleric Beryl"}}
E["npc:david-trias"] = {t="npc",n="David Trias",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, David Trias trains the newly awakened Forsaken. He teaches stealth and bladecraft so they can serve Queen Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",h="In Deathknell, David Trias trains the newly awakened Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Guide from the Shadows",b="David Trias trains newly risen undead among Deathknell’s tombstones and ruins. He seeks those with a talent for killing unseen. For the fledgling Forsaken, survival calls for more than strength at arms; it calls for precise strikes from the dark. Trias deciphers orders and teaches initiates to wield daggers, hide their movements, and use their reanimated reflexes with lethal precision against the living and the Scourge.",sp=0},{t="A Familiar Name",b="David Trias shares a surname with Elling Trias, a well-known cheese merchant in Stormwind. Elling secretly maintains close ties to master rogues and spymasters. No family connection between David and Elling is confirmed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is David Trias?",a="David Trias trains newly awakened Forsaken rogues in Deathknell, in Tirisfal Glades. He teaches their first combat techniques and gives them their first covert assignments.",al={"david trias","who is david trias","rogue trainer deathknell"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find David Trias?",a="Find David Trias in Deathknell, the Forsaken starting village in Tirisfal Glades. He stands near the settlement’s structures, helping newly risen undead.",al={"david trias location","where is david trias","deathknell rogue trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is David Trias related to Elling Trias in Stormwind?",a="David Trias shares his surname with Elling Trias of Stormwind, but no family connection is confirmed.",al={"elling trias relation","trias family","is he related to elling trias"},it="ties"},{q="What role does he play in Forsaken training?",a="Newly risen rogues from Deathknell’s crypt bring David Trias an encrypted scroll. He deciphers their instructions, teaches their first skills, and guides them toward covert work for the Forsaken.",al={"david trias quests","encrypted scroll","what does he teach"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is David Trias on?",a="David Trias is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. Stationed in Deathknell, he dedicates his undeath to training newly risen rogues, helping them master stealth, cunning, and backstabbing to defend their free will against the Scourge and living threats.",al={"david trias faction","who does david trias serve","david trias loyalties"},it="side",add="e2140548"},{q="Why is David Trias in Deathknell?",a="Deathknell serves as the primary awakening ground for newly raised Forsaken. David Trias remains here to evaluate newcomers who possess a knack for stealth and subtlety, providing them with basic guidance and instruction before they venture further into Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why is david trias here","david trias deathknell","what brings david trias to deathknell"},it="why_here",add="2dca586e"},{q="What does David Trias want?",a="Trias wants newly awakened rogues to adapt quickly to their undead condition and become effective agents for the Dark Lady. He expects you to learn the value of striking from behind and mastering essential roguish arts so you can survive the harsh struggles awaiting the Forsaken.",al={"david trias motives","what does david trias need","david trias goal"},it="wants",add="52093a30"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Forsaken rogue, David Trias is your first mentor. He helps you decipher secret scrolls and teaches you to wield a blade with the cold precision of undeath.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Forsaken’s grim reality: you were once human in Lordaeron, but the plague severed you from your former life and lineage. Now you serve Queen Sylvanas."},kw={"david trias","deathknell","elling trias","encrypted scroll","forsaken","rogue trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:3096","npc:elling-trias","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"David Trias"}}
E["npc:deathguard-bartholomew"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Bartholomew",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Deathguard Bartholomew keeps watch over the town and helps travelers find their way. He helps keep order among the Forsaken defenders of Tirisfal Glades.",h="In Brill, Deathguard Bartholomew keeps watch over the town and helps travelers find their way.",sec={{t="Sentinel of Brill",b="Deathguard Bartholomew keeps watch in Brill, part of the Forsaken guard defending Tirisfal Glades. Like other Deathguards, he protects reclaimed land from the lingering Scourge, fanatical Scarlet Crusaders, and other threats to Lady Sylvanas's domain. He also guides travelers around the town and helps keep order among the newly risen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Bartholomew?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew guards Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He watches over the town and guides travelers to places they need to find.",al={"bartholomew","who is bartholomew","deathguard bartholomew lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the role of the Deathguard?",a="The Deathguard is the Forsaken's main infantry and defense force. They patrol Lordaeron, defend settlements like Brill from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade, and keep order for the Dark Lady.",al={"what are deathguards","deathguard faction","forsaken guards"},it="purpose"},{q="Can Deathguard Bartholomew give directions?",a="Yes. Deathguard Bartholomew can direct travelers to facilities in Brill, including trainers, the inn, and profession vendors.",al={"where is the inn","brill directions","guard directions brill"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Bartholomew on?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew serves the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. As part of the military force defending Tirisfal Glades, he stands loyal to the Horde, protecting the township of Brill against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and trespassing Alliance intruders.",al={"bartholomew faction","bartholomew allegiance","who does bartholomew serve"},it="side",add="73481549"},{q="Why is Deathguard Bartholomew here?",a="Bartholomew is stationed in Brill as part of the local garrison. Following the Forsaken reclamation of the town's ruins, he remains on guard to secure the settlement, maintain military order, and guide travelers and newly awakened undead navigating Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why is bartholomew in brill","bartholomew duty","what is bartholomew doing here"},it="why_here",add="d578d9b4"},{q="What does Deathguard Bartholomew want?",a="Bartholomew's primary duty is keeping Brill safe and orderly for the Forsaken. Beyond keeping watch over the town and offering directions to arriving travelers, he relies on capable adventurers to assist with local threats and military tasks that ensure the township remains fortified.",al={"bartholomew goals","what does bartholomew need","bartholomew motive"},it="wants",add="750c03a9"},{q="Who is Deathguard Bartholomew tied to?",a="Bartholomew is a sworn soldier within the Deathguard, the standing military and town defense of the Forsaken. He answers to the local Forsaken leadership stationed in Brill and ultimately serves the Undercity and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner alongside his fellow sentries.",al={"bartholomew allies","bartholomew connections","who does bartholomew answer to"},it="ties",add="5978a3f3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly liberated Forsaken from Deathknell, you first meet Lady Sylvanas's standing army through guards like Bartholomew in Brill.",["faction:Horde"]="As an ally arriving from Kalimdor, you can ask Bartholomew for directions through Brill's mist-shrouded streets."},kw={"bartholomew","brill","deathguard","forsaken","guard","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:86784","quest:99134"},src={"Deathguard Bartholomew"}}
E["npc:deathguard-burgess"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Burgess",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Deathguard Burgess keeps watch over the town for the Forsaken. He guards the settlement and points travelers toward the services they need.",h="In Brill, Deathguard Burgess keeps watch over the town for the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Watchman in Brill",b="North of the Undercity, Deathguard Burgess guards Brill against the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade. Like other Deathguards in Tirisfal Glades, he guides arriving Forsaken to local tradesfolk, class trainers, and civic services, helping keep the vulnerable outpost running.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Burgess?",a="Deathguard Burgess guards Brill for the Forsaken. He helps keep order and directs visitors to local trainers and points of interest.",al={"burgess brill","who is burgess","deathguard burgess lore"},it="identity"},{q="What role do the Deathguards serve in Brill?",a="In Brill, the Deathguards protect the Forsaken from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade, and keep civil order.",al={"what are deathguards","deathguards role"},it="purpose"},{q="Can Deathguard Burgess provide directions?",a="Yes. Ask Burgess where to find class trainers, the local inn, profession masters, and other essential facilities in Brill.",al={"burgess directions","where to go in brill"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Burgess on?",a="Deathguard Burgess serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken as part of the nascent kingdom based in the Undercity. Standing sentry in Brill, he defends the township against lingering Scourge threats, hostile Scarlet crusaders, and any outside interlopers who dare threaten the Dark Lady's newly claimed realm.",al={"burgess faction","who does deathguard burgess serve","is burgess forsaken"},it="side",add="ff001a75"},{q="What does Deathguard Burgess want?",a="Burgess wants order, vigilance, and safety for the settlement of Brill. As a member of the town guard, his duty is to watch the roads, keep hostile threats from breaching the township's borders, and ensure that newly risen Forsaken and visitors find their bearings across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what is burgess goal","burgess purpose","what does deathguard burgess do"},it="wants",add="e5a62f54"},{q="Why is Deathguard Burgess here?",a="Burgess is stationed in Brill because it serves as the crucial forward settlement north of the Capital City ruins and the Undercity. Guarding the paths through Tirisfal Glades ensures that Forsaken interests remain secure against Scarlet zealots, mindless undead prowling the wilderness, and encroaching beasts.",al={"why is burgess in brill","deathguard burgess location","why is deathguard burgess stationed here"},it="why_here",add="a4fa6528"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly awoken Forsaken leaving Deathknell, you can get your first bearings in Lordaeron from guards like Burgess in Brill.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally visiting from Kalimdor, you can ask Burgess for directions around Brill when you need supplies or a place to rest at the inn."},kw={"brill","burgess","deathguard burgess","forsaken","guard","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:374","quest:99134","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Deathguard Burgess"}}
E["npc:deathguard-dillinger"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Dillinger",z="tirisfal",s="At Brill's edge, Deathguard Dillinger watches the town and guides newly arrived Forsaken. He also sends recruits against the Scourge remnants threatening the nearby farms and mills.",h="At Brill's edge, Deathguard Dillinger watches the town and guides newly arrived Forsaken.",sec={{t="Sentinel of Brill",b="Deathguard Dillinger guards Brill and guides those arriving from Deathknell. At the town entrance, he points newly awakened undead toward the inn, town hall, and local trainers. They must learn their way through a changed life under the Dark Lady's rule.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borderlands",b="Deathguard Dillinger sends capable recruits to clear mindless Scourge from nearby farms and mills. They cull rotting ghouls and reclaim infested facilities, building a safer border around Brill so the fledgling Forsaken settlements can endure the undead threat.",sp=0},{t="Containing Mindless Horrors",b="Ulag the Cleaver remains sealed in a mausoleum north of Brill. When the Scourge swept through Tirisfal, the Forsaken captured Ulag, a Scourge agent with a free mind who remained enthralled to the Lich King. Every attempt to break that hold failed, so Dillinger sends a proven warrior to lift the seal and destroy Ulag.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Deathguard Dillinger?",a="Deathguard Dillinger watches the path into Brill, on the outskirts of the town in central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"dillinger location","where is dillinger","deathguard dillinger coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the role of the Deathguard?",a="The Deathguard is the Forsaken's standing army and constabulary. It guards settlements such as Brill and the Undercity from the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other regional threats.",al={"what is deathguard","who are the deathguards","deathguard purpose"},it="people"},{q="What tasks does Deathguard Dillinger offer?",a="Dillinger sends recruits to slay mindless Scourge in the surrounding fields and mills, reclaim local infrastructure, and face dangerous threats such as Ulag the Cleaver.",al={"dillinger quests","what quests does dillinger have"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Can Deathguard Dillinger provide directions?",a="Yes. Dillinger can direct you to essential services, profession trainers, and class mentors throughout Brill.",al={"dillinger directions","ask dillinger for help"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken fighting other undead near Brill?",a="The mindless undead in Tirisfal remain under the Scourge and the Lich King's control. The Forsaken broke free of that control and must destroy these feral remnants to protect their territory.",al={"why fight scourge","undead fighting undead","brill ghouls"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Ulag the Cleaver?",a="Ulag the Cleaver is a dangerous Scourge horror tied to tombs near Brill. Dillinger sends Forsaken recruits to summon and destroy Ulag, keeping the surrounding area safe.",al={"ulag quest","who is ulag","ulag the cleaver"},it="target"},{q="Who is Deathguard Dillinger?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken soldier stationed to guard the settlement of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Like the rest of the Deathguard, he was once a human of Lordaeron who fell to the plague of undeath before breaking free from the Lich King's iron will under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. Now, he stands vigil on the front lines to defend newly awakened Forsaken and protect the realm from mindless Scourge prowling the outskirts.",al={"who is dillinger","deathguard dillinger lore","dillinger identity"},it="identity",add="9ba09071"},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Dillinger on?",a="Dillinger is fiercely loyal to the Forsaken and the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. As a sworn guardian of the Undercity's outer perimeter, he serves the Horde by holding the line against the lingering remnants of the Scourge and anyone else who threatens the hard-won sovereignty of the free undead in Lordaeron.",al={"dillinger faction","who does dillinger serve","dillinger loyalty"},it="side",add="e6386dfb"},{q="Why is Deathguard Dillinger here?",a="Dillinger is posted outside Brill to maintain order, provide sentry duty, and direct newly arrived Forsaken fresh from the crypts of Deathknell. Tirisfal Glades is crawling with mindless undead, wild beasts, and hostile encroachers, so experienced Deathguards like him are stationed at town crossroads to organize defenses and enlist capable travelers to cull nearby threats.",al={"why is dillinger in brill","what is dillinger doing here","dillinger post"},it="why_here",add="7c69f447"},{q="What does Deathguard Dillinger want?",a="Dillinger wants the lands surrounding Brill cleared of mindless Scourge and dangerous monstrosities. He enlists promising new Forsaken to thin out the rotting ghouls infesting the nearby countryside and eliminate unruly threats, ensuring that Brill remains a secure foothold for Queen Sylvanas's growing nation.",al={"what does dillinger want","dillinger goals","dillinger purpose"},it="wants",add="fe023b9f"},{q="Who is Deathguard Dillinger tied to?",a="Dillinger is tied directly to the Deathguard, the standing military force charged with securing Forsaken settlements. He answers to the commanders of Brill and the magistrates of Undercity, serving as a frontline intermediary between local authorities, like Magistrate Sevren, and arriving adventurers who can carry out the Forsaken's military orders.",al={"dillinger ties","who does dillinger answer to","dillinger leadership"},it="ties",add="394a16a5"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly freed Forsaken arriving from Deathknell, you may meet Dillinger as your first military authority. He directs you toward training and your first duties in Sylvanas's service.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally, you see the Forsaken's struggle to secure a foothold in northern Lordaeron and the mindless Scourge threatening Brill.",["class:Warrior"]="As an aspiring Forsaken warrior, you may work with Dillinger against the ghouls and skeletal horrors prowling Brill's outskirts."},kw={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard","deathguard dillinger","dillinger","the mills overrun","tirisfal glades","ulag the cleaver"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:404","quest:426","quest:1819","quest:1818","subzone:cold-hearth-manor"},src={"Deathguard Dillinger"}}
E["npc:deathguard-linnea"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Linnea",z="tirisfal",s="At a roadside post in southeastern Tirisfal, Deathguard Linnea watches the roads between Brill and the eastern borders. Her unit guards against the Scarlet Crusade and the lingering Scourge, with passing travelers sometimes helping on patrol.",h="At a roadside post in southeastern Tirisfal, Deathguard Linnea watches the roads between Brill and the...",sec={{t="A Vigil on the Roadside",b="Deathguard Linnea guards a fortified post southeast of Brill. The Forsaken defend their young realm against Scarlet Crusade infiltrators and Scourge still prowling the wilderness. Linnea and her fellow guards patrol the road and coordinate reports with Magistrate Sevren in Brill. Their watch keeps the eastern road toward the Bulwark secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Linnea?",a="Linnea serves in the Deathguard, the Forsaken force that defends their territory. She guards a waystation on the road southeast of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"linnea","deathguard linnea lore","who is linnea"}},{q="Why does she need help patrolling?",a="Forsaken forces are spread thin across Tirisfal Glades. Linnea depends on travelers and rising champions to clear nearby threats, so messengers and supply runners can travel safely to and from Brill.",al={"rear guard patrol lore","why help linnea"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken newly risen from Deathknell, you can help Linnea guard the waystation and secure your kingdom's borders.",["faction:Horde"]="As an ally of the Forsaken traveling through Tirisfal Glades, you can help Linnea secure the outlying roads against hostile forces."},kw={"brill","deathguard linnea","forsaken","magistrate sevren","rear guard patrol","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:356","quest:360"},src={"Deathguard Linnea"}}
E["npc:deathguard-simmer"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Simmer",z="tirisfal",s="At Deathknell’s edge, Deathguard Simmer sizes up newly risen Forsaken. He sends them west to raid a human pumpkin farm patrolled by the Scarlet Crusade, gathering reagents Brill’s apothecaries need.",h="At Deathknell’s edge, Deathguard Simmer sizes up newly risen Forsaken.",sec={{t="Guardian Outside Deathknell",b="Deathguard Simmer guards the ground just outside Deathknell, where the Forsaken hold the line between their haven and Tirisfal Glades. Living humans roam the region, including the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, who see all undead as abominations to purge with fire and blade. Simmer tests newly risen Forsaken by sending them west to Solliden Farmstead. Scarlet Crusade soldiers patrol from a nearby tower. The recruits must steal ten pumpkins and carry them to Apothecary Johaan in Brill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Simmer?",a="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken sentry just outside Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. He tests newly risen Forsaken by sending them to steal pumpkins from a human farm patrolled by the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"deathguard simmer","who is simmer","simmer npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Deathguard Simmer located?",a="Deathguard Simmer stands just outside Deathknell in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, beside the road newly risen Forsaken take from the crypts.",al={"deathguard simmer location","where is simmer","find deathguard simmer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats does Deathguard Simmer fight?",a="Deathguard Simmer despises the living humans who still farm Tirisfal and the Scarlet Crusade that patrols near them. He sends newly risen Forsaken to raid Solliden Farmstead for pumpkins, teaching those humans a lesson and supplying Brill’s apothecaries.",al={"simmer enemies","what does simmer fight","scarlet palisade quests"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Simmer on?",a="Deathguard Simmer serves the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. As a sworn member of the Deathguard, the standing military force of the Undercity, he is dedicated to defending Forsaken territory and stamping out all threats to their newborn kingdom.",al={"simmer faction","who does simmer serve","deathguard simmer allegiance"},it="side",add="6ef429fd"},{q="Why is Deathguard Simmer here?",a="Deathguard Simmer is posted just outside Deathknell, watching over the road that newly risen Forsaken take into Tirisfal Glades. With living humans still farming the nearby fields and the Scarlet Crusade patrolling from its tower to the west, he tests fledgling Forsaken by sending them to raid the Solliden Farmstead.",al={"why is deathguard simmer here","simmer calston estate","why is simmer stationed here"},it="why_here",add="2af4e555"},{q="What does Deathguard Simmer want?",a="Simmer wants fledgling Forsaken to prove themselves to the Dark Lady. He sends them to steal pumpkins from the human farm to the west, where the Scarlet Crusade patrols, teaching the living a lesson while supplying Apothecary Johaan in Brill with much-needed reagents.",al={"what does deathguard simmer need","simmer goals","what does simmer want you to do"},it="wants",add="08301829"},{q="Who is Deathguard Simmer tied to?",a="Simmer belongs to the Deathguard, the soldiers who defend Forsaken lands in Tirisfal Glades. He works with Apothecary Johaan in Brill, sending fledgling Forsaken to him with the pumpkins they steal from the nearby human farm.",al={"simmer connections","who does simmer report to","deathguard simmer ties"},it="ties",add="1e4cdda8"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you first face the Scarlet Crusade through Simmer’s missions. He sends you beyond Deathknell’s crypts to defend Lordaeron."},kw={"deathguard","deathguard simmer","deathknell","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:365"},src={"Deathguard Simmer"}}
E["npc:elder-graveborn"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Graveborn",z="tirisfal",s="Near Brill, Elder Graveborn greets travelers during the Lunar Festival. The ancestral spirit honors them and points pilgrims toward other elders in northern Lordaeron.",h="Near Brill, Elder Graveborn greets travelers during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Tirisfal",b="Elder Graveborn greets travelers just southeast of Brill during the Lunar Festival. The spectral elder stands among the haunted woods of Tirisfal Glades, where the Forsaken town lies nearby. Though the kingdom is troubled, Graveborn offers pilgrims peaceful greetings and ancestral wisdom. He also points them toward spirits in the Undercity, the Sepulcher, and across the Plaguelands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Graveborn?",a="Elder Graveborn is an ancestral ghost who appears during the Lunar Festival. In Tirisfal Glades, just southeast of Brill, he offers festival blessings to travelers.",al={"elder graveborn lore","who is graveborn","brill ghost elder"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he in Tirisfal Glades?",a="During the Lunar Festival, ancestral spirits gather across Azeroth to honor past heroes and shared heritage. Elder Graveborn watches over the land outside Brill.",al={"why brill","where is elder graveborn"},it="why_here"},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak to him?",a="Yes. Festival elders welcome travelers of either faction. Alliance travelers should approach with care: Graveborn stands close to the Forsaken town of Brill.",al={"can alliance talk to graveborn","alliance elder brill"},it="side"},{q="What information does he offer travelers?",a="Elder Graveborn points pilgrims toward other local spirits. He names the Undercity, the Sepulcher in Silverpine, Light's Hope Chapel, the Weeping Cave, and Scholomance.",al={"elder graveborn directions","graveborn quotes"}},{q="What does Elder Graveborn want?",a="Elder Graveborn desires to share his ancient blessings and ancestral wisdom with those who travel the lands during the Lunar Festival. As an earthen spirit returned to honor the world's heritage, he asks travelers to pay their respects to the past, bestowing his blessing and directing them toward other honored elders scattered across the continent.",al={"elder graveborn goal","why visit elder graveborn","what does graveborn want"},it="wants",add="a72aed3e"},{q="Who is Elder Graveborn tied to?",a="Graveborn knows where several other ancestral spirits can be found. He directs travelers toward Elder Darkcore in the Undercity, Obsidian near the Sepulcher, Snowcrown at Light's Hope Chapel, Meadowrun at the Weeping Cave, and Moonstrike at Scholomance.",al={"elder graveborn relations","who does elder graveborn know","graveborn connections"},it="ties",add="066af8bb"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can find Graveborn on the road between Brill and the Undercity. His presence recalls Azeroth's ancient past, untouched by the Scourge or the blight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance pilgrim, you must skirt Brill to reach Graveborn without drawing the attention of Forsaken guards and patrols."},kw={"ancestor","brill","earthen","elder graveborn","graveborn","lunar festival","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:8652","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","npc:elder-darkcore","npc:elder-obsidian","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"},src={"Elder Graveborn"}}
E["npc:eleanor-shackleton"] = {t="npc",n="Eleanor Shackleton",z="tirisfal",s="Southwest of Brill, Eleanor Shackleton camps in the woods of Tirisfal Glades. This Forsaken outdoorswoman teaches travelers wilderness survival and field crafts instead of staying in town or the Undercity. Her surname is shared by other Forsaken in the region, a possible link to life before the plague.",h="Southwest of Brill, Eleanor Shackleton camps in the woods of Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Guide to the Glades",b="Eleanor Shackleton camps in the haunted woods southwest of Brill, away from the Undercity. Newly awakened Forsaken often head for those settlements, but she teaches travelers how to live off Tirisfal's blighted land. Her lessons cover setting up campsites, gathering firewood, and keeping trade crafts while roaming far from civilization's fires and kitchens.",sp=0},{t="Ties from a Past Life",b="Eleanor Shackleton shares her surname with Pierce Shackleton and Samantha Shackleton, who live in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. Family names can be the only tether an undead person has to mortal life in the shattered remnants of Lordaeron. Whether Eleanor, Pierce, and Samantha are close kin or share only common ancestry, each serves the Forsaken in a distinct way across the blighted kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Eleanor Shackleton?",a="Eleanor Shackleton camps in the woods southwest of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, away from the main paved road.",al={"eleanor shackleton location","where is eleanor","shackleton spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Eleanor Shackleton teach adventurers?",a="Eleanor Shackleton teaches wilderness survival, including camping, foraging, and practicing professions in the wild.",al={"eleanor quests","what does eleanor do","camping quests tirisfal"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Eleanor related to other Shackletons in Lordaeron?",a="Eleanor Shackleton shares her family name with Pierce Shackleton and Samantha Shackleton of the Undercity, suggesting they may be kin from before the Scourge claimed the kingdom.",al={"pierce shackleton relative","samantha shackleton","shackleton family lore"},it="ties"},{q="Why is she camping outside Brill instead of staying in town?",a="Eleanor Shackleton teaches fieldcraft and wilderness survival. Her camp in the woods lets her meet travelers where those skills are needed.",al={"why camp outside brill","eleanor shackleton camp"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Eleanor Shackleton?",a="Eleanor Shackleton is a Forsaken outdoorswoman who has set up camp in the woods southwest of Brill. Rather than lingering in town, she embraces survival in the wilds of Tirisfal Glades, guiding fledgling undead on the fundamentals of enduring the outdoors and practicing basic trades in the field.",al={"who is eleanor shackleton","eleanor shackleton identity","eleanor shackleton info"},it="identity",add="a3327cab"},{q="Whose side is Eleanor Shackleton on?",a="Eleanor is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady. She operates just outside Brill, helping newly risen members of her people adapt to their unlife by teaching them how to survive, harvest materials, and hone useful crafts across Lordaeron's haunted glades.",al={"eleanor shackleton faction","is eleanor shackleton horde","eleanor shackleton allegiances"},it="side",add="afc076fe"},{q="What does Eleanor Shackleton want?",a="Eleanor wants adventurers to learn essential survival skills and wilderness trades. By sending travelers out to practice professions like herbalism, skinning, and cooking under open skies, she ensures that Forsaken who venture beyond the safety of settlements are properly equipped to sustain themselves.",al={"what does eleanor want","eleanor shackleton goals","eleanor shackleton motives"},it="wants",add="48da77ca"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, learning to survive in the wilderness without familiar comforts matters. Eleanor helps newly risen brethren adapt to life in rough Tirisfal.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn from Eleanor how to make a field campfire and prepare meals away from civilized hearths. Her camp is a useful stop for cooks on the road."},kw={"brill","camping 101","eleanor shackleton","shackleton","sticks and bones","the adventurer","the great outdoors","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:96658","quest:96607","quest:86784","quest:96627"},src={"Eleanor Shackleton"}}
E["npc:executor-arren"] = {t="npc",n="Executor Arren",z="tirisfal",s="At Deathknell, Executor Arren directs the settlement's defense as new undead rise from their graves. He leads efforts against Scourge zombies, wild beasts, and threats to the Forsaken.",h="At Deathknell, Executor Arren directs the settlement's defense as new undead rise from their graves.",sec={{t="Commander of Deathknell",b="Executor Arren directs Deathknell's defense from outside its chapel. While caretakers in the crypts guide newly risen undead through their confusion, Arren turns their attention to survival beyond the graves. Under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's banner, he organizes efforts to clear mindless zombies from the village borders. The Forsaken secure ground here in the shadow of Lordaeron's fall.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borderlands",b="Danger surrounds Deathknell beyond the confused newly risen. Under Arren's orders, scouts and initiates strike at the vicious spiders in Night Web's Hollow and hunt predators along the woodland edges. He calls on every capable hand to act, testing whether new arrivals can defend their second chance and serve the Dark Lady.",sp=0},{t="The Crimson Threat",b="The Scarlet Crusade is Arren's greatest concern. Its zealots seek to destroy all undead and make no distinction between the Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. Arren orders strikes against Scarlet patrols encamped in the Tirisfal wilderness. His forces intercept couriers and study stolen dispatches to protect Deathknell from a purge in holy fire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Executor Arren?",a="Executor Arren commands Deathknell's defense in Tirisfal Glades. He organizes newly risen Forsaken to defend the village and secure the surrounding countryside.",al={"arren role","who is arren","deathknell executor"},it="identity"},{q="What rank is an Executor among the Forsaken?",a="Among the Forsaken, Executors are trusted military and administrative commanders. They govern local garrisons, direct field operations, and enforce Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's will and law.",al={"executor title","what is an executor","forsaken executor rank"}},{q="Why does Arren send recruits against the zombies?",a="Mindless Scourge remnants prowl near Deathknell, left behind after the plague devastated Lordaeron. Arren orders them cleared so they cannot tear apart newly awakened undead as they leave the crypts.",al={"why kill zombies","the damned quest","mindless scourge"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a radical human faction devoted to exterminating all undead. It holds outposts across Lordaeron's ruins and seeks to purge the Forsaken, whom it considers no different from the Scourge.",al={"scarlet crusade tirisfal","why crusade here","crusaders in deathknell"},it="threat"},{q="What is Night Web's Hollow?",a="Night Web's Hollow is a gold mine northwest of Deathknell, overrun by spiders. The Forsaken need its gold, so Arren sends recruits to clear out the arachnids a little at a time.",al={"spider cave deathknell","night webs hollow","arren spider quest"},it="place"},{q="Where does Arren send recruits once they finish his tasks?",a="After Deathknell's immediate threats are dealt with, Arren sends capable recruits to Brill to report to Executor Zygand and aid the wider Forsaken effort across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"next after deathknell","where to go after arren","the executor in the field"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Executor Arren on?",a="Executor Arren is utterly loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. As the local military commander in Deathknell, his duty is to secure the starting grounds for his newly awakened brethren and eliminate any threats to their young nation, whether mindless Scourge zombies, local beasts, or the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"arren allegiance","who does executor arren serve","arren faction"},it="side",add="610ddc26"},{q="What does Executor Arren want?",a="Arren seeks to firmly establish Forsaken control over Deathknell and test the resolve of the newly risen. He wants the mindless undead cleared from the graveyard, the encroaching arachnids purged, and the nearby camps of the Scarlet Crusade crushed so that fresh recruits can safely depart for Brill and join the broader defense of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what does arren want","arren goals","executor arren purpose"},it="wants",add="25e599ca"},{q="Why is Executor Arren in Deathknell?",a="Arren is stationed in Deathknell to command the initial defense where newly freed Forsaken first break from the grave. Without military oversight, confused recruits could easily be overrun by mindless Scourge wandering the hills or fall prey to Scarlet Crusade scouts probing the settlement's perimeter.",al={"why is arren in deathknell","arren location reason","why is executor arren here"},it="why_here",add="3c8717b4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you meet Executor Arren among the first commanders in Tirisfal. He gives you an early taste of duty under the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Arren's commands at Deathknell secure its first foothold in northern Lordaeron amid hostile surroundings."},kw={"deathknell","executor arren","forsaken","night web's hollow","scarlet crusade","sylvanas","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:night-web-s-hollow","quest:96627"},src={"Executor Arren"}}
E["npc:executor-zygand"] = {t="npc",n="Executor Zygand",z="tirisfal",s="At Brill's town hall, Executor Zygand directs Forsaken defenses across central Tirisfal Glades. He reports to the Undercity's high command and coordinates the fight against Scarlet Crusade forces pressing into Forsaken lands.",h="At Brill's town hall, Executor Zygand directs Forsaken defenses across central Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Command in Brill",b="Executor Zygand directs regional defenses from Brill after the Forsaken's awakening in Deathknell. Officers such as Executor Arren and field sentries such as Deathguard Linnea report to him. He gathers scouts' reports and sends able recruits to guard Lordaeron's borders against encroachment.",sp=0},{t="The War on the Crusade",b="The Scarlet Crusade's presence across Tirisfal Glades commands Executor Zygand's attention. He sends agents against Crusader scouts, encampments, and forward bases, keeping the zealots from gathering enough strength to threaten the approaches to the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken officer based in Brill, Tirisfal Glades. He commands local Deathguard garrisons, receives reports from lower-ranking officers, and directs campaigns against local threats.",al={"zygand","who is executor zygand","zygand role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand can be found inside or near Brill's main town hall. Brill is the central Forsaken settlement in Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Undercity.",al={"zygand location","where is zygand","executor zygand map"},gp=true},{q="What is Zygand's main goal in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Executor Zygand's main goal is to direct the regional war against the Scarlet Crusade. He tracks the zealots across Tirisfal and orders their encampments and leadership dismantled before they can march on the Undercity.",al={"zygand quest goal","why fight crusade","zygand purpose"},it="wants"},{q="Who reports to Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Arren and field sentries such as Deathguard Linnea report to Executor Zygand. Arren directs initial recruits in Deathknell, while Linnea patrols Tirisfal Glades' main crossroads.",al={"zygand subordinates","who serves zygand","arren superior"},it="ties"},{q="Does Executor Zygand handle rogue undead threats?",a="Yes. Executor Zygand also issues regional bounties against feral undead and dangerous rogue scavengers that endanger travel through the glades, including the corpse-stealing gnoll Maggot Eye.",al={"maggot eye","zygand bounties","wanted quests"}},{q="What rank does an 'Executor' hold among the Forsaken?",a="Among the Forsaken, an Executor holds authority as a regional governor and military commander. Executors manage settlements, command local Deathguard units, and enforce Queen Sylvanas's rule across Lordaeron's contested regions.",al={"what is an executor","executor rank","forsaken executor"}},{q="Whose side is Executor Zygand on?",a="Executor Zygand is wholly devoted to the Forsaken and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. As a military officer in Brill, he serves the Undercity by coordinating local defenses, directing deathguards, and organizing strategic strikes to secure Tirisfal Glades against the Forsaken's relentless enemies.",al={"zygand faction","who does zygand serve","executor zygand side"},it="side",add="1dc7a0d0"},{q="Why is Executor Zygand stationed in Brill?",a="Zygand is stationed in Brill because the settlement serves as the Forsaken's primary military bastion directly north of the Undercity. From here, he monitors critical threats across Tirisfal Glades, managing frontline patrols and deploying seasoned fighters to keep vital supply lines and borders secure.",al={"why is zygand here","zygand brill purpose","why is executor zygand in brill"},it="why_here",add="673b7cce"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken venturing out of Deathknell, you meet Executor Zygand as a representative of the Undercity's wider military authority, bringing new citizens into active service against their bitterest enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a traveler from Kalimdor in Tirisfal Glades, you can see in Zygand the disciplined military leadership guiding the Forsaken's struggle to secure Lordaeron."},kw={"arren","brill","deathguard","executor","maggot eye","scarlet crusade","tirisfal","zygand"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","quest:370","npc:executor-arren","npc:deathguard-linnea","quest:398","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken"},src={"Executor Zygand"}}
E["npc:gunther-arcanus"] = {t="npc",n="Gunther Arcanus",z="tirisfal",s="On an island in Brightwater Lake, Gunther Arcanus has escaped the Lich King's control and keeps apart from others. He believes every other undead remains a Scourge thrall.",h="On an island in Brightwater Lake, Gunther Arcanus has escaped the Lich King's control and keeps apart from...",sec={{t="Breaking the Shackles",b="During the Third War, the Scourge swept across the north and the Plague of Undeath killed Gunther, raising him into servitude. His arcane mastery and will let him break the Lich King's mental hold alone, without the weakening of the Lich King or Lady Sylvanas's help that others needed. Believing every other walking corpse remained a mindless Scourge thrall, Gunther withdrew to an island in Tirisfal Glades. Shambling guardians surround him, and he cuts off all contact with the living and the dead alike.",sp=0},{t="The Prodigal Lich",b="The Forsaken sought powerful allies against the Scourge, so they sent emissaries to claim Gunther's spellbook. In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard recognized the handwriting as that of his long-lost peer. Bethor enchanted the returned grimoire, and Gunther demanded the destruction of local Scourge commanders. Through this, he learned that others had broken free. Convinced that Sylvanas's faction truly rebels against the Scourge, Gunther has made a pact with his former schoolmate to aid the Forsaken.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}},{t="A Student of Dalaran",b="Before Lordaeron fell, Gunther studied the arcane arts as a promising Kirin Tor apprentice in Dalaran. With close friends Bethor Iceshard and Thule Ravenclaw, he secretly pursued necromancy despite the Kirin Tor's strict ban on dark magic. To mark their brotherhood, the three bound their apprentice wands together as one heirloom.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="Who is Gunther Arcanus?",a="Gunther Arcanus was a Kirin Tor wizard from Dalaran who died during the Third War. Raised into undeath, he broke the Lich King's domination alone and withdrew to an island in Brightwater Lake, in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who is gunther","gunther lore","gunther arcanus story"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gunther look like a regular Forsaken instead of a skeletal lich?",a="Traditional liches place their spirits in phylacteries and take monstrous, floating skeletal forms. Gunther gained lich-like necromantic power while keeping his original reanimated corpse, so he retains his mortal appearance.",al={"why does gunther look human","gunther not a skeleton","why is gunther a lich"}},{q="Why was Gunther living alone on an island?",a="After escaping the Lich King's control, Gunther believed he was the only undead with free will. Thinking all other walking dead were mindless Scourge slaves, he secluded himself and ordered his minions to strike down anyone who approached.",al={"why is gunther alone","gunther island isolation","why does gunther hide"},it="why_here"},{q="How does Gunther know Bethor Iceshard?",a="Gunther and Bethor Iceshard were close friends and classmates at the Kirin Tor in Dalaran, where they studied with Thule Ravenclaw. The three bound their apprentice wands together to honor their friendship.",al={"bethor and gunther","how does gunther know bethor","bethor iceshard history"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"q358.4"}},{q="Does Gunther join the Forsaken?",a="Yes. Gunther pledges himself to Bethor and the Forsaken cause after adventurers return his enchanted spellbook and kill the local Scourge agent Lillith Nefara, proving they oppose the Lich King.",al={"does gunther join horde","gunther faction","is gunther forsaken"},sp=1,it="side"},{q="Who is Lillith Nefara?",a="Lillith Nefara is a Scourge agent stationed in Tirisfal Glades. Gunther demands her death as proof that an adventurer serves an enemy of the Lich King, rather than the Scourge.",al={"lillith nefara","nefara","gunther target"},sp=1},{q="What does Gunther Arcanus want?",a="Above all, Gunther values his independence from the Lich King. Having broken free through sheer willpower, he spent years in isolation guarding against what he presumed were Scourge thralls. He desires solitude from the Scourge and seeks proof before trusting anyone claiming to share his freedom, wanting assurance that you truly oppose the Lich King's dominion.",al={"what does gunther want","gunther arcanus goal","gunther arcanus motivation"},it="wants",add="3744b38d"},{q="Why is Gunther Arcanus famous or feared?",a="Even as a mortal Dalaran mage, Gunther mastered the forbidden art of necromancy. In undeath, he achieved the rare status of a lich while retaining his original mortal form. Most terrifying of all, he shattered the Lich King's psychic control entirely on his own, commanding undead minions under his own absolute will.",al={"is gunther arcanus powerful","why is gunther arcanus feared","gunther arcanus reputation"},it="fame",add="2466094b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, Gunther is an exception among the Forsaken. His freedom shows that arcane training and iron will alone could sometimes break the Lich King's mental hold.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage trained in Dalaran, Gunther reflects Kirin Tor wizards who secretly studied forbidden necromancy before the Scourge invaded Lordaeron.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, Gunther shows how far forbidden study of dark arts and reanimation could reach beyond Dalaran's leaders' watch."},kw={"arcanus","bethor","brightwater","dalaran","gunther","iceshard","kirin tor","lich","necromancer","thule","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:gunther-s-retreat","npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:405","quest:366","quest:409","quest:411","quest:446"},src={"Gunther Arcanus"}}
E["npc:high-executor-derrington"] = {t="npc",n="High Executor Derrington",z="tirisfal",s="At the Bulwark, High Executor Derrington directs the Forsaken vanguard against threats from the Western Plaguelands. A no-nonsense military officer, he sends seasoned champions toward contested ruins such as Andorhal and Scholomance.",h="At the Bulwark, High Executor Derrington directs the Forsaken vanguard against threats from the Western...",sec={{t="Commander at the Threshold",b="At the Bulwark’s barricades, High Executor Derrington gives orders to those crossing from Tirisfal Glades into the Western Plaguelands. He has little patience for political maneuvering in the Undercity and sees the front lines as a crucible of sheer survival. Horde soldiers and sellswords receive direct orders to scout plague-ridden territory and blunt enemy incursions before they reach Tirisfal.",sp=0},{t="A War on Two Fronts",b="The Bulwark faces threats from the Scourge in Andorhal and from the Scarlet Crusade farther north. Scourge forces spread corruption through cauldrons in the countryside, while the Crusade’s zealous fanatics contest northern fortifications and skirmish relentlessly with Forsaken patrols. Derrington coordinates surgical counterattacks, sabotage against Scarlet lines, and systematic disruption of Scourge cauldron fields to protect the eastern border.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Derrington?",a="High Executor Derrington is the senior Forsaken commander stationed at the Bulwark, the military outpost between Tirisfal Glades and the Western Plaguelands. He coordinates the Horde’s eastward push against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"derrington","who is derrington","high executor derrington lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Derrington located?",a="Derrington is stationed at the Bulwark, a fortified choke point at Tirisfal Glades’ eastern edge, along the road into the Western Plaguelands.",al={"where is derrington","derrington location","find high executor derrington"},gp=true},{q="What is Derrington's objective at the Bulwark?",a="Derrington seeks to preserve Forsaken survival with a strong defense against the Scourge and strikes into the Western Plaguelands. He sends adventurers to scout Andorhal, disable plague cauldrons, and neutralize Scarlet Crusade operations.",al={"what does derrington want","bulwark purpose","derrington mission"},it="wants"},{q="Does Derrington care about Undercity politics?",a="No. Derrington disdains court schemers and politicians; on the front lines, survival must be fought for every day.",al={"derrington personality","is derrington political"}},{q="What major threats does Derrington send soldiers against?",a="Derrington sends soldiers against the Scourge holding Andorhal, the dark necromancers inside Scholomance, and nearby Scarlet Crusade garrisons threatening the Horde’s eastern supply routes.",al={"derrington quests","what does derrington fight"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Bulwark so heavily fortified?",a="The Bulwark is the primary chokepoint between Tirisfal Glades and the Plaguelands’ active combat zones. Its forces hold the pass to keep Scourge swarms or Scarlet Crusade forces from sweeping toward the Undercity.",al={"why is the bulwark here","bulwark lore"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is High Executor Derrington on?",a="High Executor Derrington stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. As a high-ranking military commander under the Dark Lady, he is dedicated to defending their realm and securing their place in Lordaeron against all who would see them eradicated.",al={"derrington faction","who does derrington serve","is derrington horde"},it="side",add="895ac470"},{q="Why is High Executor Derrington stationed at the Bulwark?",a="Derrington commands the frontline defense of Tirisfal Glades. Stationed at the border between Tirisfal and the Western Plaguelands, he oversees the fortification that halts Scourge incursions and prepares the Forsaken's advance eastward into the heart of the blighted lands.",al={"why is derrington here","derrington at the bulwark","why is derrington at the border"},it="why_here",add="e8355a95"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers in Tirisfal, Derrington directs forces into the dangerous conflicts of the Western Plaguelands.",["race:Undead"]="Derrington represents the Forsaken military’s martial backbone, guarding their reclaimed lands against the Scourge’s attempt to reclaim them and against Scarlet fanaticism.",["class:Warrior"]="Derrington embodies a front-line soldier’s grim, practical grit, valuing martial competence and battlefield results over court scheming."},kw={"andorhal","bulwark","derrington","forsaken","high executor derrington","scourge","tirisfal glades","western plaguelands"},rel={"subzone:bulwark","zone:tirisfal","subzone:andorhal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:scholomance","subzone:cauldron"},src={"High Executor Derrington"}}
E["npc:magistrate-sevren"] = {t="npc",n="Magistrate Sevren",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren directs the settlement's defense and sends newcomers to steady the lands around the Undercity.",h="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren directs the settlement's defense and sends newcomers to steady the lands around...",sec={{t="Town Magistrate of Brill",b="From Brill's town hall, Magistrate Sevren directs civil and strategic affairs in the lands north of the Undercity. New Forsaken arriving in Tirisfal Glades find local crises waiting. Sevren sends adventurers to restore order, secure ruined places, and suppress threats in the surrounding hills.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Graves",b="The Tirisfal dead and their burial grounds are among Magistrate Sevren's chief concerns. Scourge-aligned Rot Hide gnolls, graverobbers, and rogue undead threaten the graves and Sylvanas Windrunner's growing dominion. Sevren seeks to reclaim ancestral tombs such as the Agamand Family Crypt and keep deserters or uncooperative forces from undermining Forsaken authority.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magistrate Sevren?",a="Magistrate Sevren directs Brill from its town hall and oversees Forsaken affairs in the region. He sends adventurers arriving from Deathknell to help the fledgling realm.",al={"magistrate sevren","who is sevren","brill magistrate"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Magistrate Sevren be found?",a="Magistrate Sevren can be found inside the Town Hall at the center of Brill, in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"sevren location","where is magistrate sevren","find sevren"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats does Magistrate Sevren deal with?",a="Sevren faces threats across Tirisfal Glades, including Scourge-aligned Rot Hide gnolls who rob graves, Scourge remnants that desecrate crypts, and rogue undead who refuse allegiance to Lady Sylvanas.",al={"sevren quests","what does sevren want","brill problems"},it="threat"},{q="What is Magistrate Sevren's allegiance?",a="Magistrate Sevren is loyal to the Forsaken and governs Brill on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Undercity.",al={"sevren faction","who does sevren serve"},it="side"},{q="Why does Sevren send adventurers to the family crypt?",a="Undead and scavengers overrun the Agamand family crypts. Sevren sends adventurers to secure these ancestral resting places and keep enemies from exploiting them.",al={"agamand crypt","sevren crypt quest"},it="motive"},{q="Does Sevren have ties to the Undercity leadership?",a="Yes. Sevren frequently works with agents and officials from the Undercity. Once adventurers prove their competence in Brill, he directs them deeper into the capital.",al={"sevren undercity","sevren raleigh"},it="ties"},{q="What does Magistrate Sevren want?",a="As Brill's chief civil authority, Sevren wants to secure Tirisfal Glades for the Forsaken. He coordinates efforts to root out lingering Scourge, put down grave robbers desecrating Forsaken resting grounds, and maintain clear lines of command and supply heading deeper into the kingdom.",al={"magistrate sevren goals","sevren motives","what does sevren want"},it="wants",add="54ff886a"},{q="Why is Magistrate Sevren in Brill?",a="Sevren presides over Brill's Town Hall to oversee local administration and law just outside the gates of the Undercity. He serves as the primary municipal authority directing freshly awakened and arriving Forsaken into service to protect and organize the realm.",al={"why is sevren in brill","magistrate sevren town hall","sevren location purpose"},it="why_here",add="2465c638"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly liberated Forsaken leaving Deathknell, you meet the civic face of Sylvanas's realm in Magistrate Sevren. He gives you your first major assignments to safeguard your homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="As an ally of the Horde arriving in Tirisfal, you find Sevren coordinating efforts to pacify the region against bandits, Scourge remnants, and rebel factions."},kw={"agamand","brill","forsaken","magistrate","sevren","tirisfal","town hall","undercity"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:355","quest:360","quest:358","quest:408","zone:undercity"},src={"Magistrate Sevren"}}
E["npc:novice-elreth"] = {t="npc",n="Novice Elreth",z="tirisfal",s="Inside Deathknell's chapel, Novice Elreth guides the newly risen Forsaken. She sends them against the mindless Scourge near the graves and helps them face the plague's sorrowful aftermath.",h="Inside Deathknell's chapel, Novice Elreth guides the newly risen Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Church of the Damned",b="Novice Elreth guides newly risen undead inside the desecrated chapel at Deathknell. They struggle to understand their horrific awakening, while the Forsaken must organize quickly to secure their territory. Elreth sends them south to gather paws from wolves and wings from bats. She also points them toward Lordaeron's tragic aftermath, including the sorrow of her friend Marla Fipps, whom her husband Samuel killed after joining the mindless Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Novice Elreth located?",a="Novice Elreth is inside the chapel at Deathknell, a ruined village in Tirisfal Glades where newly created Forsaken awaken.",al={"elreth location","where is elreth","novice elreth church"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Novice Elreth's role in Deathknell?",a="Novice Elreth guides newly arisen Forsaken and gives them their first directives. She teaches them to strike against the mindless Scourge prowling the village cemetery.",al={"what does elreth do","elreth role","novice elreth purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What quests does Novice Elreth offer?",a="Novice Elreth sends adventurers to gather scavenger paws and duskbat wings, and to defeat the mindless Samuel Fipps and bury his remains beside his wife Marla's grave.",al={"novice elreth quests","elreth tasks"},gp=true},{q="Why is she titled 'Novice'?",a="Her title and place in the chapel suggest Novice Elreth is an initiate in the Forsaken's religious or civic ranks. She is learning to manage Tirisfal's freshly raised undead under the Forsaken order.",al={"why novice","novice meaning elreth","is elreth a priest"},it="name"},{q="Who is Novice Elreth?",a="Novice Elreth is an undead attendant stationed inside the desecrated church of Deathknell. As one of the early caretakers assisting freshly awakened Forsaken, she helps guide newly risen souls through the harsh reality of their undeath and integrates them into service under the Dark Lady.",al={"who is novice elreth","novice elreth lore","about novice elreth"},it="identity",add="04e44638"},{q="Whose side is Novice Elreth on?",a="She is entirely loyal to the Forsaken and Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. Operating out of Deathknell, her work directly supports the Undercity's efforts to secure Tirisfal Glades by evaluating and directing the newly risen.",al={"novice elreth faction","who does novice elreth serve","novice elreth loyalty"},it="side",add="36f54bd8"},{q="What does Novice Elreth want?",a="Elreth wants to ensure that newly freed undead understand their state, confront the truth of their graves, and find their purpose within the Forsaken. She tests the resolve of the newly risen and directs capable hands to the local leadership to aid the war effort.",al={"what does elreth want","novice elreth goal","why does elreth give quests"},it="wants",add="d753a6ea"},{q="Why is Novice Elreth here in Deathknell?",a="Deathknell is where the Forsaken uncover and raise new corpses to join their ranks. Elreth remains in the chapel to minister to these disoriented souls immediately upon their awakening, ensuring they do not succumb to despair or turn against their new kin.",al={"why is elreth in deathknell","why is novice elreth in the church"},it="why_here",add="a4872bf3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly risen Forsaken, you can take some of your first practical steps toward survival with Novice Elreth. She directs your cold hatred toward the mindless Scourge.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you meet Novice Elreth in Lordaeron's former holy grounds. Her work shows the grim, practical needs of the undead."},kw={"chapel","church","deathknell","forsaken","marla's last wish","novice elreth","the damned","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","quest:376","quest:6395","topic:forsaken"},src={"Novice Elreth"}}
E["npc:renee-lauer"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Renee",z="tirisfal",s="Travelers find food, drink, and shelter with Innkeeper Renee at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill.",h="Travelers find food, drink, and shelter with Innkeeper Renee at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill.",sec={{t="Keeper of Gallows' End",b="Innkeeper Renee welcomes weary newcomers to the Gallows' End Tavern, Brill's central inn. She sells food, drink, and general goods from behind her counter, and remarks that the Forsaken have huge appetites. Her tavern offers the undead of Tirisfal a cozy place to rest as plague victims make their way in the world.",sp=0},{t="Letters and Captives",b="Newcomers to Brill often stop first at Renee's inn. Calvin Montague of Deathknell sends fresh adventurers to her with a nondescript letter, the word she has eagerly awaited. Beneath the tavern's floorboards, the cellar also holds a captured Scarlet Crusade zealot.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Innkeeper Renee?",a="Innkeeper Renee welcomes travelers at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. She sells food, drink, and general supplies to those passing through Tirisfal Glades.",al={"renee lauer","brill innkeeper","who is the innkeeper in brill"},it="identity"},{q="What is Renee's connection to Calvin Montague?",a="In the task 'A Rogue's Deal', adventurers running errands for Calvin Montague are sent to deliver a letter directly to Renee at the Gallows' End Tavern.",al={"a rogue's deal renee","calvin montague letter"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Renee on?",a="Renee is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde, tending the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill for the undead of Tirisfal and the Horde travelers who pass through.",al={"renee lauer faction","who does renee lauer serve","is renee horde"},it="side",add="63a8965f"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Renee in Brill?",a="Renee manages the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, offering shelter, provisions, and a resting place for Forsaken citizens and travelers crossing Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why is renee lauer here","why is renee in brill","renee lauer gallows end"},it="why_here",add="f2640528"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you can find an old comfort at Renee's tavern: a hearth, a meal, and a place to rest."},kw={"brill","gallows' end tavern","innkeeper renee","renee lauer","scarlet crusade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:8","npc:calvin-montague","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Renee Lauer"}}
E["npc:shadow-priest-sarvis"] = {t="npc",n="Shadow Priest Sarvis",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell's ruined chapel, Shadow Priest Sarvis guides the newly awakened Forsaken. He gives them purpose and directs them against mindless undead and local threats.",h="In Deathknell's ruined chapel, Shadow Priest Sarvis guides the newly awakened Forsaken.",sec={{t="Shepherd of the Newly Awakened",b="Shadow Priest Sarvis guides Forsaken who have just risen from their graves in Deathknell. Their awakening can be jarring and horrific, and some lose their minds to frenzy or despair. Sarvis gives the newly risen a purpose. He sends them to put down the mindless corpses roaming the cemetery and secure Deathknell's borders against the Scourge.",sp=0},{t="Securing Deathknell",b="Shadow Priest Sarvis also directs Deathknell's defenses against threats in Tirisfal Glades. Scourge forces probe the town's perimeter, and Sarvis sends novices to gather vital intelligence and face trials of arms. The Forsaken must hold Deathknell against those forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="Sarvis is a Forsaken shadow priest in Deathknell. He guides the newly awakened undead, gives them their first orders, and helps defend the town against the Scourge.",al={"sarvis","who is sarvis","deathknell priest"}},{q="Where can I find Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis waits inside the ruined church at the center of Deathknell, in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"sarvis location","where is sarvis","find sarvis"}},{q="Why is Sarvis having players kill mindless zombies?",a="Some corpses raised from the grave lose their free will and sanity. The Forsaken see them as a danger to the settlement and destroy them before they can endanger the living dead.",al={"why kill mindless ones","the mindless ones"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you hear Sarvis among the first voices after you wake from the grave. He sets you on the path to serve the Dark Lady.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you see Sarvis use shadow magic as a Forsaken mentor in a chapel stripped of the Holy Light."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken","novice elreth","sarvis","shadow priest sarvis","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Shadow Priest Sarvis"}}
E["npc:shari-stilwell"] = {t="npc",n="Shari Stilwell",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Shari Stilwell trains Forsaken in the paladin's path. She is stationed in Tirisfal Glades, where the undead who endure the Light's pain learn holy and martial discipline.",h="In Brill, Shari Stilwell trains Forsaken in the paladin's path.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Brill",b="In Brill, Shari Stilwell guides Forsaken who seek the path of holy warriors. The Light brings the undead excruciating pain, yet she trains those willing to endure it. She helps newcomers find their footing in Tirisfal Glades, through early training and the adjustments of Forsaken life. Those she guides seek a place within the Forsaken kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Ties of the Stilwell Name",b="Shari bears the same family name as Daphne, Merissa, and Jordan Stilwell, a renowned smith among the living in the southern kingdoms. Whether the fall of Lordaeron tore Shari from these kin, or whether their bond is only distant, remains unknown amid the Scourge's devastation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shari Stilwell?",a="Shari Stilwell is an undead paladin trainer in Brill, Tirisfal Glades. She guides Forsaken paladins through early martial and holy instruction as they learn to survive in Lordaeron.",al={"who is shari stilwell","shari stilwell lore","brill paladin trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Shari Stilwell be found?",a="Shari can be found in the town of Brill, just north of the Capital City ruins and the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"shari stilwell location","where is shari stilwell","find shari stilwell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Shari related to Jordan Stilwell?",a="Shari shares her surname with Jordan Stilwell, a famous human smith, and with Daphne and Merissa Stilwell. Their exact family connection is unknown, though the plague that destroyed Lordaeron may have severed it.",al={"jordan stilwell relation","stilwell family ties","shari stilwell relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Can Forsaken wield the Light as paladins?",a="The Holy Light brings intense pain and burning to the undead. Shari Stilwell guides determined Forsaken in the devotion and mental fortitude needed to wield its power alongside martial skill.",al={"forsaken paladins","how can undead be paladins","undead paladin lore"}},{q="Whose side is Shari Stilwell on?",a="Shari Stilwell stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. Based in the town of Brill, she serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's kingdom by instructing and guiding Forsaken who walk the demanding, paradoxical path of the paladin in undeath.",al={"shari stilwell faction","who does shari serve","is shari stilwell horde"},it="side",add="1254553f"},{q="Why is Shari Stilwell in Brill?",a="Shari Stilwell is stationed in Brill to serve as a paladin trainer for the newly awakened undead of Tirisfal Glades. As fledglings emerge from Deathknell and seek refuge or purpose in a second home, she ensures those drawn to the paladin's calling receive proper discipline and training.",al={"why is shari in brill","shari stilwell purpose","what is shari stilwell doing here"},it="why_here",add="e32993c8"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a Forsaken paladin beginning in Tirisfal Glades, you can find your primary trainer and mentor, Shari Stilwell, in Brill.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you see in Shari Stilwell how the Third War splintered families: she mentors the Forsaken while possible kin live far to the south."},kw={"brill","forsaken","light","paladin","shari","stilwell","tirisfal","trainer"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","npc:jordan-stilwell","npc:daphne-stilwell","npc:merissa-stilwell","quest:91209"},src={"Shari Stilwell"}}
E["npc:shelene-rhobart"] = {t="npc",n="Shelene Rhobart",z="tirisfal",s="Along Tirisfal's road, Shelene Rhobart trains leatherworkers at a Deathguard waystation. She supplies cured hides and leathercraft training for the Forsaken's military and logistical efforts across the blighted lands.",h="Along Tirisfal's road, Shelene Rhobart trains leatherworkers at a Deathguard waystation.",sec={{t="Crafting for the Forsaken",b="At a Deathguard waystation southeast of Brill, Shelene Rhobart works along the main road toward the ruins of Lordaeron. Practical crafts still matter in undeath, for survival and war. She turns pelts from Tirisfal's prowling beasts into tough hides, armor, straps, and field gear for Forsaken patrols facing the Scourge and Scarlet crusaders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Shelene Rhobart?",a="Find Shelene Rhobart at a small Forsaken post southeast of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, along the road to the Undercity.",al={"shelene rhobart location","where is shelene rhobart","shelene rhobart map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Shelene Rhobart serve?",a="Shelene Rhobart trains leatherworkers in curing pelts, stitching garments, and assembling protective leather gear for the Forsaken.",al={"what does shelene rhobart do","shelene rhobart trainer","shelene profession"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does she need beast hides?",a="The Forsaken use animal hides to patch their injured bodies, since undead skin does not heal. Shelene's supplies are running low, and she needs duskbat wing membranes, darkhound hides, and Vile Fin murloc skin; different thicknesses suit different parts of the body.",al={"hides for the forsaken quest","why collect hides tirisfal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Shelene Rhobart?",a="Shelene Rhobart is an undead leatherworker serving the Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades. Like many of her kin, she retained the craft and skills she practiced in life, now offering her expertise to teach budding leatherworkers and craft essential supplies for her people.",al={"shelene rhobart lore","who is shelene","shelene rhobart info"},it="identity",add="383979a9"},{q="Whose side is Shelene Rhobart on?",a="She is staunchly loyal to the Forsaken and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, as well as the broader Horde. She works directly to support Tirisfal's defenders and tradespeople as they secure their homeland.",al={"shelene rhobart faction","who does shelene rhobart serve","shelene rhobart loyalty"},it="side",add="ffb69fef"},{q="What does Shelene Rhobart want?",a="Shelene wants to supply the Forsaken war effort and support travelers across Tirisfal Glades. She seeks sturdy beast hides from local wildlife to craft armor, gear, and supplies essential for survival against the realm's enemies.",al={"what does shelene want","shelene rhobart goal","shelene rhobart purpose"},it="wants",add="d546cfcf"},{q="Why is Shelene Rhobart here?",a="Shelene is stationed at a Deathguard waystation southeast of Brill, to maintain an outpost along the vital road through Tirisfal Glades. From here, she assists patrolling scouts and passes her leatherworking knowledge to travelers passing through the glades.",al={"why is shelene at deaths watch","why is shelene rhobart here"},it="why_here",add="e156f5b6"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how practical crafts help outfit local defenders amid Tirisfal's decay and desolation."},kw={"brill","hides for the forsaken","leatherworking","shelene rhobart","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken","quest:97558"},src={"Shelene Rhobart"}}
E["npc:undertaker-mordo"] = {t="npc",n="Undertaker Mordo",z="tirisfal",s="At Deathknell's crypt, Undertaker Mordo greets newly awakened Forsaken. He tells them they are free of the Lich King's control and sends them toward Queen Sylvanas's cause. Bodies that never stir go to the fire.",h="At Deathknell's crypt, Undertaker Mordo greets newly awakened Forsaken.",sec={{t="The Awakening at Deathknell",b="Undertaker Mordo tends the crypt in Tirisfal Glades as corpses break free of the Scourge. Newly awakened Forsaken find him in a world they no longer recognize. He tests their sanity, tells them what they have become, and directs them toward service under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",sp=0},{t="Those Who Do Not Wake",b="Some bodies brought to the crypt never wake. Mordo soon casts them into the fire. Those who stir meet his dry impatience and little ceremony. If they have kept their wits, he sends them up the steps and down the road to Shadow Priest Sarvis at the chapel, where Sarvis explains their new existence. The mindless zombies overrunning the north of the village are Sarvis's concern. He sends the newly risen to destroy them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Undertaker Mordo?",a="Undertaker Mordo tends the crypt of Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. He greets newly risen Forsaken and directs them into service.",al={"who is mordo","undertaker mordo lore","mordo deathknell"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he standing in a graveyard?",a="Undertaker Mordo keeps watch at Deathknell's crypt, where newly freed undead wake from the Lich King's control. He greets them as they stir.",al={"why is mordo at the graves","what does mordo do","mordo job"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens to the undead who lose their minds upon waking?",a="Bodies that never wake are cast into the fire. Shadow Priest Sarvis sends the newly risen to destroy the mindless zombies overrunning the north of Deathknell, even when those zombies were once their brothers and sisters.",al={"those that couldnt be saved","mad undead deathknell","feral undead deathknell"}},{q="Where does Mordo send newly risen Forsaken?",a="Mordo sends newly awakened Forsaken with their wits intact out of the crypt and down the road to the chapel. There, Shadow Priest Sarvis explains what it means to join the Forsaken.",al={"where do i go after mordo","mordo quest direction","next step after mordo"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Undertaker Mordo on?",a="Undertaker Mordo serves the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Operating on the front line of newly awakened undead in Deathknell, he ensures that freshly raised corpses who retain their sanity are inducted into the ranks of the Forsaken rather than falling sway to the Lich King or mindless frenzy.",al={"mordo faction","who does mordo serve","is mordo forsaken"},it="side",add="a2ca27d8"},{q="What does Undertaker Mordo want?",a="Mordo's immediate concern is managing the grave sites of Deathknell. He wants newly risen Forsaken to regain their bearings, report to local leadership like Shadow Priest Sarvis, and assist in putting down mindless undead that clawed their way from the dirt without their sanity intact.",al={"what is mordo trying to do","mordo goals","mordo purpose"},it="wants",add="b30fe27a"},{q="Who is Undertaker Mordo tied to?",a="Mordo keeps the crypt of Deathknell and works hand in hand with Shadow Priest Sarvis in the chapel below, to whom he sends every newly awakened Forsaken, all in service of Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",al={"mordo allies","who does mordo work with","mordo connections"},it="ties",add="0fa90ad3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, your first meeting is with Undertaker Mordo when you open your eyes in death. He guides your first steps in service to Queen Sylvanas."},kw={"deathknell","rude awakening","shadow grave","tirisfal glades","undertaker mordo"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","subzone:shadow-grave","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:363"},src={"Undertaker Mordo"}}
E["npc:yvette-farthing"] = {t="npc",n="Yvette Farthing",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Yvette Farthing shares the Gallows' End Tavern with her father, Coleman. A Forsaken, she carries the memory of a love cut short by the Scourge.",h="In Brill, Yvette Farthing shares the Gallows' End Tavern with her father, Coleman.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Mills",b="Yvette loved Thurman Agamand, heir to the prosperous Agamand Mills, before the Third War ruined Lordaeron. As the Scourge plague drew near, Yvette and her father, Coleman, begged Thurman to leave the estate with them. He refused, devoted to his family's legacy. Yvette and Thurman both perished and rose into undeath. Yvette found a place among the free-willed Forsaken in Brill, but she did not know Thurman's final fate.",sp=0},{t="A Final Farewell",b="Thurman wrote Yvette an urgent love letter before the mills fell. In it, he described his brother Devlin's treachery and lamented his choice to stay. The Scourge intercepted the letter, and it lay lost among the ruins of Agamand Mills until adventurers recovered it. Reading Thurman's dying confession brings Yvette a brief, genuine despair from her mortal life. She then forces herself back into cold detachment, bitter that past attachments have no place in the grim reality of the Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Yvette Farthing?",a="Yvette Farthing is a Forsaken woman living in Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. She is Coleman Farthing's daughter and lived in the farmlands of Tirisfal Glades before the Third War destroyed the kingdom.",al={"yvette farthing lore","who is yvette","brill yvette"},it="identity"},{q="What is Yvette's connection to Agamand Mills?",a="Yvette loved Thurman Agamand. When the plague threatened the region, she tried to persuade him to flee with her, but he chose to remain and defend his family's estate.",al={"yvette agamand","thurman agamand and yvette","yvette lover"},it="ties"},{q="What happens when you deliver Thurman's letter to her?",a="Reading Thurman's long-lost letter leaves Yvette briefly crushed by sorrow at his final words of love and betrayal. She quickly hardens her manner, saying that she is Forsaken now and mortal sentiment is useless.",al={"a letter undelivered turn in","thurmans letter reward","yvette reaction letter"},sp=1},{q="Who is Yvette's father?",a="Yvette's father is Coleman Farthing, a Forsaken who also lives in Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. They first fled together, but both eventually succumbed to the plague and became Forsaken.",al={"yvette father","coleman and yvette","who is coleman farthing"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Yvette Farthing on?",a="Yvette stands fully with the Forsaken and the Horde. Though the remnants of her mortal life and past loves can still stir up painful memories, she has cast aside those human emotions. She now embraces her identity as one of the free-willed undead serving Lady Sylvanas.",al={"yvette farthing faction","yvette farthing side","who does yvette serve"},it="side",add="71e9f93d"},{q="What does Yvette Farthing want?",a="Yvette seeks closure from the tragedy that consumed her former life. Having fled Agamand Mills during the Scourge invasion while her lover Thurman stayed behind, she harbored unspoken grief. Receiving word of his final moments allows her to finally shut the door on her mortal heart and embrace her cold existence among the Forsaken.",al={"what does yvette want","yvette farthing goal","yvette farthing motives"},sp=1,it="wants",add="99950259"},{q="Why is Yvette Farthing here in Brill?",a="Following the devastation of the Agamand Mills and the fall of Lordaeron to the Plague, Yvette and her father Coleman took refuge in Brill. In undeath, Brill serves as the primary Forsaken town outside the capital, making it a natural sanctuary for survivors reclaiming their former homeland.",al={"why is yvette farthing in brill","yvette farthing location why","why is yvette here"},it="why_here",add="8e2cc8a4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may carry human memories of love even as undeath hardens the heart."},kw={"a letter undelivered","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","gallows' end tavern","thurman agamand","tirisfal glades","yvette farthing"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","quest:361","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Yvette Farthing"}}
E["quest:1470"] = {t="quest",n="Piercing the Veil",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Venya Marthand tests a novice warlock's resolve. The newly risen Forsaken must gather skulls from nearby mindless skeletons to earn the knowledge to summon and bind an imp.",h="In Deathknell, Venya Marthand tests a novice warlock's resolve.",sec={{t="A Novice's First Step",b="In Deathknell, Venya Marthand teaches newly awakened Forsaken warlocks that strength comes from knowledge and mastery of chaotic powers. She sends novices to gather skulls from the Rattlecage Skeletons near Deathknell's abandoned smithy. The trial tests whether they have the focus to command powers beyond this world and subdue nether beings.",sp=0},{t="Subjugating the Nether",b="Venya accepts the skulls as proof that a novice can overcome mindless undead and face the bleak truths of warlock craft. She then teaches the rituals to summon and bind an imp. Though small, the demon brings cunning and fire, making it a dangerous ally.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Piercing the Veil?",a="Venya Marthand, the Forsaken warlock trainer in Deathknell, gives the trial.",al={"who starts piercing the veil","piercing the veil questgiver","venya marthand quest"},gp=true},{q="What must you collect to complete this quest?",a="You collect three Rattlecage Skulls from Rattlecage Skeletons near Deathknell's ruined smithy.",al={"piercing the veil objective","what do i collect for piercing the veil","rattlecage skulls"},gp=true},{q="Why does Venya Marthand want skeleton skulls?",a="Hunting mindless skeletons tests a novice warlock's control, resolve, and basic magical skill before Venya trusts them with more dangerous demonic rituals.",al={"why rattlecage skulls","purpose of skulls quest"},it="motive"},{q="What power or minion do you learn to summon?",a="The lesson prepares a warlock to summon and bind an imp, the first demonic companion they learn to command.",al={"piercing the veil reward spell","what demon do i get","imp summon quest"},it="for_you"},{q="Where are the Rattlecage Skeletons located?",a="Rattlecage Skeletons wander Deathknell's outskirts, especially around the crumbling, abandoned smithy northwest of the main town clearing.",al={"rattlecage skeleton location","where are the skeletons deathknell","abandoned smithy deathknell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is eligible to undertake this quest?",a="Forsaken warlocks with introductory training in Deathknell can undertake this trial.",al={"who can take piercing the veil","can other classes do this","is this warlock only"},gp=true},{q="What is the Rattlecage Skull for?",a="Venya Marthand uses the skulls as a trial to test your emerging command over dark magic. Warlocks believe knowledge and will are their greatest weapons, and proving you can harvest these remains from the restless dead shows you possess enough discipline to summon and bind an imp to your service.",al={"what are rattlecage skulls for","why rattlecage skulls","rattlecage skull purpose"},it="item",add="149b6242"},{q="Who are the Rattlecage Skeletons?",a="Rattlecage Skeletons are mindless Scourge undead lingering around the abandoned smithy in Deathknell. Like much of Tirisfal Glades, the grounds remain haunted by the remnants of the plague and the Lich King's ruined forces, making them convenient fodder for novice Forsaken warlocks looking to test their growing might.",al={"what are rattlecage skeletons","rattlecage skeletons deathknell","why rattlecage skeletons here"},it="target",add="d722d37c"},{q="Why does Venya Marthand send you instead of handling it herself?",a="Venya Marthand is your warlock trainer, not a mercenary contractor. Gathering the skulls is not a chore she needs completed for herself, but an essential lesson for you. To pierce the veil and bend chaotic beings of the void to your will, you must first prove your power and determination on your own.",al={"why me piercing the veil","why does venya make you get skulls","why cant venya marthand get them"},it="why_me",add="d14f3c7d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you take your first true step into demonology and learn that chaotic magic must bend to iron will.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you draw on your detachment from mortality as you study chaotic and dark magic in Deathknell's shadows."},kw={"deathknell","imp","piercing the veil","rattlecage skull","tirisfal glades","venya marthand","warlock"},rel={"zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Venya Marthand",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1470,ri={"Rattlecage Skull"}},src={"Piercing the Veil"}}
E["quest:1818"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Dillinger",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Austil de Mon sends fighters to Deathguard Dillinger for a hazardous mission in service of Lady Sylvanas. The order begins at the Gallows' End Tavern, where the warrior trainer directs able-bodied recruits to the west end of the village.",h="In Brill, Austil de Mon sends fighters to Deathguard Dillinger for a hazardous mission in service of Lady...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Front",b="At the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, warrior trainer Austil de Mon seeks fighters willing to serve the Dark Lady. When the Deathguards need capable hands, he sends untested recruits into the field. Deathguard Dillinger oversees security on Brill's western edge and has requested someone with martial skill for an urgent task.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Faithful",b="The Forsaken must constantly prove their martial dominance on Tirisfal Glades' front line. Near Brill's graveyard, Dillinger manages local incursions. Reporting to him tests your combat skill and loyalty to the newly forged Forsaken nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Austil de Mon, the warrior trainer at Brill's Gallows' End Tavern, identifies potential soldiers and sends them to aid Deathguard Dillinger.",al={"quest giver","austil de mon","who starts speak with dillinger"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Deathguard Dillinger be found?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is stationed at Brill's western edge in Tirisfal Glades, near the graveyard entrance.",al={"dillinger location","where is dillinger","find dillinger"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of reporting to Dillinger?",a="Dillinger needs an able-bodied champion for a combat mission to defend Brill and prove their allegiance to the Forsaken cause.",al={"why speak with dillinger","dillinger purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What assignment does Dillinger have prepared?",a="When you report to Deathguard Dillinger, he gives you the task of hunting down Ulag the Cleaver, a dangerous threat.",al={"what does dillinger want","next quest dillinger"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Do other Horde races receive this order?",a="Any Horde warrior trusted by Undercity officials can take the assignment, though it is mainly designed to assess recruits' combat prowess as they defend Tirisfal Glades.",al={"is this undead only","can orcs do this"},it="for_you"},{q="Why does a warrior trainer send me to Dillinger?",a="Austil de Mon trains warriors at Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. He sends newly capable adventurers to Deathguard commanders who need immediate muscle.",al={"why undercity start","austil de mon role"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Austil de Mon send you to Dillinger?",a="Austil de Mon acts as an intermediary, directing emerging Forsaken who seek greater standing to where their martial talents can serve the realm. By directing capable hands out of Brill's Gallows' End Tavern and into the field under Deathguard Dillinger's command, he ensures that the frontline settlements receive reinforcement while testing whether you possess genuine value and devotion to Lady Sylvanas's cause.",al={"austil de mon motive","why send to dillinger","austil de mon reason"},it="motive",add="277a5d32"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly liberated Forsaken, answering Dillinger's call is a crucial way to prove your dedication to the Dark Lady and the defense of Tirisfal.",["class:Warrior"]="Deathguard commanders prize martial grit, so Dillinger's call tests your combat skill on the front line.",["faction:Horde"]="Answering defense calls from the Undercity strengthens solidarity between the Horde's Kalimdor allies and the newly integrated Forsaken."},kw={"austil de mon","brill","deathguard dillinger","speak with dillinger","tirisfal glades","ulag the cleaver","undercity"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","npc:austil-de-mon","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Austil de Mon",["end"]="Deathguard Dillinger",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1818},src={"Speak with Dillinger"}}
E["quest:1819"] = {t="quest",n="Ulag the Cleaver",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, a captive Scourge warrior tests the resolve of young Forsaken. Deathguard Dillinger sends you to release Ulag the Cleaver beneath a mausoleum north of Brill and face him in combat.",h="In Tirisfal, a captive Scourge warrior tests the resolve of young Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Bound Scourge Thrall",b="After the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the Forsaken captured an unusual undead warrior who called himself Ulag the Cleaver. His mind remained clear, yet the Lich King still held his spirit in psychic thrall. The Forsaken bound him beneath a mausoleum north of Brill with a magical seal. They hoped to learn how the Scourge chained a mind and to break the hold over him.",sp=0},{t="The Executioner's Trial",b="The Forsaken failed to free Ulag from the Lich King's command. Deathguard Dillinger now uses the captive as a test of combat for rising Forsaken warriors. Disturbing the skull stone outside the crypt breaks the wards and frees Ulag from his prison. A warrior must face him with an axe, granting him release through death.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ulag the Cleaver?",a="Ulag the Cleaver was an undead warrior the Forsaken captured during the Scourge's invasion of Tirisfal Glades. He kept his mind and identity, but remained under the Lich King's command.",al={"ulag lore","who is ulag","ulag the cleaver identity"},it="target"},{q="Why was Ulag imprisoned under the mausoleum?",a="The Forsaken imprisoned Ulag beneath a magical seal to study the Lich King's control of his mind. They hoped to sever the psychic bond, but their efforts failed.",al={"why is ulag locked up","mausoleum prisoner tirisfal"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the Deathguards want Ulag killed now?",a="The Forsaken could not break the Lich King's hold on Ulag, and decided death was the only mercy left. Deathguard Dillinger made the execution a test of courage and discipline for aspiring warriors.",al={"why kill ulag","reason to slay ulag"},it="motive"},{q="How is Ulag summoned?",a="Ulag is held beneath a mausoleum just north of Brill. Touching the skull stone near the tomb breaks the magical seal, and Ulag rises to attack.",al={"how to summon ulag","where is ulag","ulag skull stone"},gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to slay Ulag?",a="Deathguard Dillinger guards the western road out of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He sends Forsaken warriors seeking further instruction to face Ulag.",al={"quest giver ulag","who sends me to ulag"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Ulag is defeated?",a="After you confirm Ulag's death, Deathguard Dillinger recognizes your courage and sends you to Coleman Farthing in Brill to continue your training.",al={"after ulag","ulag quest follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger have you face Ulag instead of dealing with him himself?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is testing your mettle. Ulag was no minor servant of the Scourge, and facing him alone proves whether you possess the skill, courage, and resolve demanded of a true warrior in service to Lady Sylvanas. Dillinger guards Brill and oversees your training; sending you into the crypt serves as your trial by combat to show you are worthy of advanced instruction.",al={"why me dillinger","why kill ulag yourself","why send player ulag"},it="why_me",add="6de55395"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Forsaken warrior, you face an early test of courage against a powerful Scourge champion still under the Lich King's control.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, Ulag's fate shows the horror of Scourge control: some Forsaken broke free, while others remain enslaved to the Lich King."},kw={"brill","deathguard dillinger","dillinger","mausoleum","scourge","skull stone","ulag","ulag the cleaver"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","quest:1818","quest:1820","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1819},src={"Ulag the Cleaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:1820"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Coleman",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Deathguard Dillinger sends proven fighters to Coleman Farthing for help. The tavern meeting opens the way to a private matter tied to the old Agamand lands.",h="In Brill, Deathguard Dillinger sends proven fighters to Coleman Farthing for help.",sec={{t="A Word from the Guard",b="After you help contain grave threats near Brill, including Ulag the Cleaver, Deathguard Dillinger trusts your strength. He watches the roads into town and decides which fighters can take on work beyond the usual patrols. When he sees you are ready, he points you toward people who need specialized help.",sp=0},{t="A Private Vendetta",b="Not every fight in Tirisfal Glades comes from orders in the Undercity. The surviving undead of Lordaeron carry grudges over the lands, families, and fortunes they left behind. Coleman Farthing waits in the Gallow's End Tavern, hoping to find a fighter who can strike at threats near former settlements such as the Agamand Mills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Coleman Farthing?",a="Coleman Farthing waits inside the Gallow's End Tavern on Brill's eastern side in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"coleman farthing location","where is coleman farthing","find farthing brill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends you to talk to Coleman?",a="Deathguard Dillinger, who guards the path into Brill, sends you to Coleman after you prove your fighting skill.",al={"who gives speak with coleman","dillinger quest"},it="origin"},{q="What kind of work does Coleman Farthing have?",a="Coleman seeks a capable fighter to take revenge on enemies of the Forsaken, with matters around the old Agamand properties at stake.",al={"what does coleman want","coleman farthing task"},it="purpose"},{q="What prerequisites are needed before receiving this task?",a="Deathguard Dillinger refers you to Coleman after you defeat Ulag the Cleaver and prove your loyalty and combat skill to the Forsaken.",al={"prereqs for speak with coleman","ulag requirement"},gp=true},{q="Does this mission grant substantial rewards directly?",a="Speaking with Farthing in the tavern connects you with his personal requests; this meeting brings no substantial gear or coin on its own.",al={"speak with coleman rewards","is it worth doing"},gp=true},{q="What is the Gallow's End Tavern?",a="The Gallow's End Tavern is Brill's central inn, a place for the local undead to gather and rest, and an informal meeting place for private contracts.",al={"brill tavern","gallows end tavern"},it="place"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger want me to speak with Coleman?",a="Deathguard Dillinger recognizes that you have proven your strength and loyalty to the Dark Lady by handling threats in Brill. Coleman Farthing has personal grievances and needs an able combatant to exact vengeance on enemies of the Forsaken. By directing you to him, Dillinger ensures capable champions assist fellow citizens while furthering the realm's wider security.",al={"why send to coleman","dillinger motive speak with coleman","why see coleman farthing"},it="motive",add="75bd5c35"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger send me instead of handling Coleman's request himself?",a="Dillinger is a Deathguard stationed to guard Brill's town perimeter against immediate threats like the Scourge. He cannot abandon his post to resolve the personal vendettas or private concerns of local townsfolk. You have demonstrated your combat prowess and independence, making you the ideal agent to assist Coleman Farthing directly.",al={"why me coleman","why not dillinger","why dillinger sends you"},it="why_me",add="5d6ae549"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Many Forsaken carry personal grudges alongside their loyalty to the Dark Lady. Coleman Farthing's requests show how personal loss and the defense of Tirisfal are bound together.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler helping secure Lordaeron, you gain a foothold for work across Tirisfal Glades by meeting Brill's townsfolk."},kw={"agamand","brill","coleman farthing","deathguard dillinger","forsaken","gallow's end tavern","horde","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","npc:coleman-farthing","quest:1821","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",["end"]="Coleman Farthing",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1820},src={"Speak with Coleman"}}
E["quest:1821"] = {t="quest",n="Agamand Heirlooms",z="tirisfal",s="At Agamand Mills, Coleman Farthing seeks the family's heirlooms from their crypt. He blames the Agamands for his death and wants their ancestral weapons taken from them.",h="At Agamand Mills, Coleman Farthing seeks the family's heirlooms from their crypt.",sec={{t="A Servant's Bitter Grudge",b="Coleman Farthing served the wealthy Agamand family at their mills in Tirisfal Glades before the Third War devastated Lordaeron. Whatever happened as the estate fell, Farthing blames his former lords for his death. Raised into undeath among the Forsaken, he takes spiteful satisfaction in the Agamands' downfall. The once-proud family has become mindless minions enslaved to the Lich King.",sp=0},{t="Desecrating the Crypt",b="Farthing sends you into the Agamand Family Crypt beneath the northern bluffs of the mills. Restless dead and lingering Scourge wander its stone halls. He wants you to take four relics: the Agamand family sword, axe, dagger, and mace. Their loss would strip the bloodline of its remaining honor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Coleman Farthing in life?",a="Coleman Farthing served the wealthy Agamand family at Agamand Mills before the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. He died during the calamity and blames his former masters, carrying that resentment into undeath.",al={"who is coleman farthing","coleman backstory","farthing history"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want the heirlooms?",a="Farthing wants vengeance on his former masters. He seeks their ancestral sword, axe, dagger, and mace to strip the fallen family of its last honor and memory.",al={"why steal heirlooms","coleman motive","why take weapons"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to the Agamand family?",a="The Agamand family perished when the Scourge swept across Tirisfal Glades. They were raised as mindless undead thralls bound to the Lich King, wandering their ruined mills and crypt.",al={"agamand fate","are agamands alive","what are agamands now"},it="history"},{q="Where is the Agamand Family Crypt located?",a="The Agamand Family Crypt lies at the northern edge of Agamand Mills, in rocky cliffs overlooking the blighted farmsteads of northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"crypt location","where is crypt","agamand crypt map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What weapons are kept within the crypt?",a="The crypt holds four ancestral weapons: the Agamand Family Sword, the Agamand Family Axe, the Agamand Family Dagger, and the Agamand Family Mace.",al={"which heirlooms","four heirlooms","agamand weapons"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking the Agamands if both are undead?",a="The Forsaken have free will and fight for their own survival. The undead Agamands remain mindless Scourge slaves, serving the Lich King whom the Forsaken despise.",al={"undead vs undead","why fight agamands","forsaken scourge conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="What will Coleman Farthing do with the Agamand heirlooms?",a="To Coleman Farthing, the four weapons—the Agamand family sword, axe, dagger, and mace—represent the final remnants of his former masters' pride and lineage. By desecrating their tomb and taking them, he strips away the last vestiges of honor and memory left to the cursed Agamand lands, and declares that the family truly is no more.",al={"agamand heirlooms use","what are the heirlooms for","agamand family weapons purpose"},sp=1,it="item",add="c3afbf3e"},{q="Who guards the Agamand family crypt?",a="The crypt and the surrounding mills are infested with mindless Scourge minions, including the reanimated remains of the Agamand family itself. Bound to the will of the Lich King rather than free-willed Forsaken, these undead lurk in the dark tombs of their ancestors, fiercely guarding the family relics against any intruders.",al={"agamand crypt enemies","who protects the heirlooms","agamand family crypt monsters"},it="target",add="c1f9d064"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know how grudges from mortal life can linger after death among the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help weaken the Scourge's hold over northern Tirisfal Glades and make the realm safer for travelers.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know how to slip past lurking ghouls and take ancient weapons from guarded burial vaults."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","coleman farthing","heirloom weapon","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","quest:1820"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",level="11",faction="Horde",id=1821,ri={"Agamand Family Axe","Agamand Family Dagger","Agamand Family Mace","Agamand Family Sword"}},src={"Agamand Heirlooms"}}
E["quest:3096"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Scroll",z="tirisfal",s="At Deathknell, a sealed message sends a newly awakened Forsaken rogue to David Trias. Shadow Priest Sarvis passes it on once the recruit has proved ready.",h="At Deathknell, a sealed message sends a newly awakened Forsaken rogue to David Trias.",sec={{t="A Quiet Summons",b="Newly raised Forsaken fight mindless zombies in the cemetery as Deathknell's leaders watch for those drawn to stealth and subterfuge. Once you have proved your readiness, Shadow Priest Sarvis gives promising scouts a sealed parchment. David Trias's discreet seal marks it as an early link to the covert network beneath Forsaken leadership.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="David Trias watches Deathknell's crossroads and inn for prospects in future covert operations. The Forsaken need disciplined agents, not common thieves or reckless cutpurses, to serve their fledgling kingdom. Trias says capable rogues may draw the notice of the Shadowstalkers, a Forsaken cadre that prizes cunning, precision, and absolute loyalty to the Dark Lady.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Scroll?",a="The scroll privately invites a newly awakened Forsaken rogue to meet David Trias for specialized training. Shadow Priest Sarvis gives it to you once you have proved capable.",al={"what is encrypted scroll","what does the scroll do","why encrypted scroll"}},{q="Who is David Trias?",a="David Trias is the rogue mentor at Deathknell's inn. He assesses fresh recruits and scouts prospects for larger Forsaken intelligence operations.",al={"david trias","who is trias","rogue trainer deathknell"}},{q="Who are the Shadowstalkers mentioned by Trias?",a="The Shadowstalkers are Forsaken stealth operatives and assassins. They seek talented, disciplined agents, not clumsy pickpockets.",al={"who are the shadowstalkers","shadowstalkers forsaken","shadowstalkers"}},{q="Why is the message encrypted?",a="Encryption shields sensitive messages from careless eyes in vulnerable Deathknell. For Forsaken rogues, it protects their communications and supports operational security.",al={"why encrypted","why cipher"}},{q="Where do you find Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis oversees the intake of newly awakened Forsaken in Deathknell's central crypt and chapel complex, in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is sarvis","sarvis location","find shadow priest sarvis"}},{q="Where is David Trias located?",a="David Trias is inside Deathknell's damaged inn, just down the path from the central chapel.",al={"where is trias","david trias location","deathknell inn trainer"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you receive a private summons into the Forsaken's covert network, from your first steps as one of the newly risen to the prospect of covert service.",["race:Undead"]="As a newly formed Forsaken, you help secure Tirisfal Glades against the Scourge and living remnants. Scouts and covert agents are vital to the Dark Lady's survival strategy."},kw={"david trias","deathknell","encrypted scroll","forsaken rogue","shadow priest sarvis","shadowstalkers","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:david-trias","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Shadow Priest Sarvis",["end"]="David Trias",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3096},src={"Encrypted Scroll (quest)"}}
E["quest:3097"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Scroll",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, the Hallowed Scroll calls newly risen Forsaken priests to the chapel. Shadow Priest Sarvis gives the summons, sending each novice to Dark Cleric Duesten to learn how the Forsaken wield faith after death.",h="In Deathknell, the Hallowed Scroll calls newly risen Forsaken priests to the chapel.",sec={{t="A Summons in Deathknell",b="Newly awakened undead stagger from Deathknell’s graves, their minds reeling from plague, death, and freedom from the Lich King's grip. For those who followed the Holy Light in life, death leaves deep confusion. As fledgling undead fight the mindless Scourge at the settlement’s edge, Shadow Priest Sarvis receives messages. A summons marked by Dark Cleric Duesten calls newly risen priests away from their wandering and into the desecrated town chapel.",sp=0},{t="Faith Redefined",b="At the chapel, Dark Cleric Duesten teaches a harsh faith. He says the Holy Light abandoned the Forsaken in death, ancestral spirits are hollow tales, and demons have no care for their plight. Forsaken clergy teach that willpower and self-reliance are their only sources of salvation. Under Duesten’s guidance, newly risen priests learn to wield divine discipline and shadow through conviction in their own survival, not devotion to distant gods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Scroll?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis gives newly risen Forsaken priests in Deathknell a sealed document. It sends them to Dark Cleric Duesten in the town chapel for priestly training.",al={"hallowed scroll","scroll item","priest scroll"}},{q="Who sends the scroll to the player?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten marks the scroll with his seal, and Shadow Priest Sarvis hands it to you in Deathknell.",al={"who sent scroll","duesten scroll","sarvis letter"}},{q="Can Forsaken still wield the Holy Light?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten tells new priests that the Holy Light no longer concerns them. Forsaken priests turn from traditional devotion to the Light and rely on themselves and their command of Shadow.",al={"undead use light","forsaken holy light","can undead cast light"}},{q="Where is Dark Cleric Duesten located?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten is inside the ruined church at the center of Deathknell in western Tirisfal Glades, near other Forsaken trainers.",al={"find duesten","duesten location","where is cleric duesten"}},{q="Why does Duesten dismiss ancestors and demons?",a="Duesten wants newly raised undead to cast aside their illusions. He says the Light no longer concerns them, their forefathers’ spirits are fairy tales, and creatures of the Nether do not want them; the Forsaken survived through will alone.",al={"duesten speech","fairy tales","nether dont want you"}},{q="What happens after reading the scroll?",a="You read the parchment and present yourself to Dark Cleric Duesten in the Deathknell chapel. He becomes your trainer there and teaches your first priest abilities.",al={"hallowed scroll objective","turning in scroll"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you enter the Forsaken faith through self-reliance, suffering, and shadow magic rather than traditional piety.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Forsaken have severed ties to their old human faiths and survive through iron will and mutual need."},kw={"dark cleric duesten","deathknell","forsaken priest","hallowed scroll","priest quest","shadow priest sarvis","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:light","topic:scourge"},m={start="Shadow Priest Sarvis",["end"]="Dark Cleric Duesten",level="3",faction="Horde",id=3097},src={"Hallowed Scroll (quest)"}}
E["quest:3098"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Scroll",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Isabella summons newly awakened Forsaken mages to her in the ruined church. Her sealed scroll calls them to hone their volatile arcane powers.",h="In Deathknell, Isabella summons newly awakened Forsaken mages to her in the ruined church.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Arcane",b="Isabella calls newly awakened Forsaken mages to the ruined church in Deathknell. After you show an affinity for arcane magic while fighting the mindless Scourge nearby, the scroll bearing her arcane sigil bids you to report to her. Isabella trains local mages, and she knows that untrained magic can endanger the Forsaken as much as their enemies.",sp=0},{t="Wielding Magic in Undeath",b="In Deathknell’s ruined chapel, Isabella teaches new Forsaken mages that undeath has not ended the dangers of arcane magic. Their bodies have lost the frailties of life, but magic remains volatile and corrupting. For the Forsaken, mastering the arcane is more than study. It can help them survive, seek vengeance, reclaim their destiny, and destroy those who threaten their fragile return to Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Glyphic Scroll?",a="The Glyphic Scroll bears Isabella’s personal seal and calls newly awakened Forsaken mages to report to her in Deathknell’s ruined church to advance their arcane studies.",al={"glyphic scroll quest","what is this scroll","deathknell scroll"}},{q="Who sends the Glyphic Scroll to you?",a="Isabella, the mage trainer in Deathknell, sends the scroll to you after you deal with the nearby mindless Scourge.",al={"who sent the scroll","who wrote glyphic scroll","sender of glyphic scroll"}},{q="Where is Isabella located?",a="Isabella is inside the ruined village church in the center of Deathknell, alongside other trainers who guide newly risen Forsaken.",al={"where is isabella","find isabella","deathknell mage trainer location"}},{q="Why does Isabella warn you about magical corruption?",a="Isabella warns you that arcane magic remains volatile and can corrupt or consume the Forsaken. Mastering it takes discipline and will.",al={"magic corruption undead","arcane corruption lore","why is magic dangerous to undead"}},{q="Why is arcane magic important to the Forsaken in Deathknell?",a="Forsaken mages use arcane power to reclaim Lordaeron and defend their freedom from the mindless Scourge, hostile living mortals, and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"why do forsaken use magic","undead mages lore"}},{q="Can any Forsaken class receive this scroll?",a="No. Only Forsaken mages receive the Glyphic Scroll, which summons them to their trainer in Deathknell.",al={"is glyphic scroll mage only","can warlocks get glyphic scroll","who gets glyphic scroll"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you receive this scroll as your summons to Isabella. Your magic serves the survival and resurgence of your newly freed people.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you wield the arcane to help reclaim your stolen homeland. For the Forsaken, magic is a weapon, not a scholarly game of Dalaran."},kw={"arcane","deathknell","forsaken mage","glyphic scroll","isabella","mage trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={level="3",faction="Horde",id=3098},src={"Glyphic Scroll (quest)"}}
E["quest:354"] = {t="quest",n="Deaths in the Family",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing, once a mill worker, seeks vengeance from Brill against the Agamand family. During the Third War, he stayed to defend their estate with his fellow workers, and they died beside their stubborn masters. The Agamands rose again as mindless thralls of the Lich King.",h="Coleman Farthing, once a mill worker, seeks vengeance from Brill against the Agamand family.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Pride",b="Before the Third War, the Agamands were Tirisfal Glades' wealthiest and most influential farming family. Their mills and fertile pastures yielded grain through the labor of dozens of tenant farmers and millers. When the Plague of Undeath crossed Lordaeron, the family refused to flee or abandon its ancestral lands. They believed their stone walls and loyal workers could hold back the horrors advancing from the east.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Loyalty",b="Coleman Farthing and the other workers trusted their lords' assurances and stayed to defend the estate. The Scourge overwhelmed them. The Agamands and their workers were slaughtered, then raised into undeath where they fell. Farthing eventually broke free through Sylvanas Windrunner's liberation. The Agamand patriarchs and heirs remained under the Lich King's mental grip, wandering the ruined mills as mindless Scourge sentries.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Retribution",b="Coleman Farthing now lives in Brill, still bitter toward the masters whose pride cost him his mortal life. Seeking vengeance and closure, he sends Forsaken champions to Agamand Mills to destroy Gregor, Nissa, and Thurman Agamand. He hopes his former masters kept enough awareness behind their rotting faces to feel terror as their unlife came to an end.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was the Agamand family?",a="Before Lordaeron fell, the Agamands were Tirisfal Glades' wealthiest and most prosperous landowners. They owned and ran Agamand Mills, where they employed numerous local farmers and millers.",al={"who are the agamands","agamand backstory","agamand mills history"},it="people"},{q="Why is Coleman Farthing so angry at them?",a="Coleman Farthing worked at their mills. When the Scourge came, the Agamands persuaded their workers to stay and defend the estate instead of fleeing. Farthing blames their aristocratic pride for the deaths and undeath of him and his fellow workers.",al={"coleman farthing grudge","why does farthing hate the agamands","farthing motive"},it="motive"},{q="Did the Agamands join the Forsaken?",a="No. Coleman Farthing and other Forsaken broke free, but the Agamands remained under the Lich King's control. They still haunt the ruined family mills as mindless Scourge minions.",al={"are agamands forsaken","why are the agamands scourge","who controls the agamands"},it="threat"},{q="Which Agamand family members must be destroyed?",a="You are sent to hunt Gregor Agamand, Nissa Agamand, and Thurman Agamand, then collect their remains from the family estate to confirm their destruction.",al={"who do you kill","agamand targets","which agamands"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where are Agamand Mills located?",a="Agamand Mills lies in northern Tirisfal Glades, northwest of Brill. Ruined windmills and farmhouses fill the once-fertile estate, now infested with Scourge.",al={"where is agamand mills","agamand location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Coleman Farthing do with their remains?",a="Coleman asks for their remains to confirm their destruction. They offer closure for his mortal grudges and proof that the lords who doomed him have been extinguished.",al={"why collect remains","farthing remains"},it="item"},{q="Who are you sent to destroy at the mills?",a="You are sent to destroy the undead remnants of the Agamand family: Gregor, Nissa, and Thurman. In life, they owned the expansive Agamand Mills and convinced their laborers to stay and defend the estate against the Scourge. Their stand failed, and the family members were raised as mindless thralls of the Lich King, haunting the grounds where their workers perished.",al={"who are the targets","who are the agamands","agamand targets"},it="target",add="5fad58e7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you carry the personal grudges many Forsaken bear from mortal life. Lordaeron's fall left deep wounds and bitterness toward those who led them to ruin.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help remove dangerous Scourge commanders close to Brill and the Undercity's northern approaches."},kw={"agamand","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","gregor agamand","nissa agamand","scourge","thurman agamand","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",level="11",faction="Horde",id=354,ri={"Gregor's Remains","Nissa's Remains","Thurman's Remains"}},src={"Deaths in the Family (Classic)"}}
E["quest:355"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Sevren",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren calls you north after Coleman Farthing's reckoning at Agamand Mills. The undead there threaten the settlement's northern border.",h="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren calls you north after Coleman Farthing's reckoning at Agamand Mills.",sec={{t="From Vengeance to Civic Duty",b="Coleman Farthing wanted revenge on his former neighbors, the Agamands, and sent travelers north to kill the undead around their flour mills. After you delivered the remains, Coleman saw that his private grudge touched a wider danger. The Agamand estate still crawls with aggressive Scourge minions, close to Brill.",sp=0},{t="The Magistrate's Call",b="Magistrate Sevren oversees Brill's civic and military security for the Dark Lady. Reports say you survived deep incursions into the haunted farmlands, and Sevren now directs you toward the source of the infestation: the ancient Agamand family crypt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Coleman Farthing send me to Magistrate Sevren?",a="Coleman settled his vengeance against the resurrected Agamand family, but the undead at the mills threaten all of Brill. He told Magistrate Sevren of your skill in battle, and Sevren directs Brill's defense.",al={"why go to sevren","coleman farthing referral","who is magistrate sevren"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Magistrate Sevren be found?",a="Magistrate Sevren is in Brill, Tirisfal Glades, inside Brill Town Hall, where he directs local affairs for the Forsaken.",al={"sevren location","where is magistrate sevren","find sevren"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threat do the Agamand Mills pose?",a="Agamand Mills lies just north of Brill and remains infested by mindless Scourge. The dead and restless spirits in the fields could overrun the town if left unchecked.",al={"agamand mills danger","why are mills a threat"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after speaking with Magistrate Sevren?",a="Magistrate Sevren sends you into the Agamand Family Crypt to strike at the deeper Scourge threat anchoring the undead to the mills.",al={"next quest after sevren","what does sevren want"},it="next_step"},{q="Does this quest require returning to the mills immediately?",a="You report to Sevren in Brill to conclude Coleman's lead before taking on the next mission into the crypt.",al={"do i go back to the mills","is this quest just talking"},gp=true},{q="Why does Brill care about the Agamand family?",a="The Agamands were wealthy mill owners and prominent neighbors in Tirisfal. In death, their estate is a fortified staging ground for mindless Scourge.",al={"agamand importance","who are the agamands to brill"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, proving yourself against the mindless Scourge earns recognition in Brill and brings you from odd jobs into direct civic defense under Magistrate Sevren.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help defend Brill, the first line before the Undercity. Securing the farmland from the Scourge protects the Horde's hold on northern Lordaeron."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","magistrate sevren","sevren","the family crypt","the haunted mills","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:coleman-farthing","quest:362","quest:408","subzone:brill","subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="10",faction="Horde",id=355},src={"Speak with Sevren (Classic)"}}
E["quest:356"] = {t="quest",n="Rear Guard Patrol",z="tirisfal",s="At the Bulwark, Deathguard Linnea sends you to guard Tirisfal's eastern flank. Scourge horrors and lingering spirits haunt Balnir Farmstead, where they threaten the road and the supply lines that keep the front supplied.",h="At the Bulwark, Deathguard Linnea sends you to guard Tirisfal's eastern flank.",sec={{t="Securing the Bulwark's Flank",b="The Bulwark holds back the pestilence and armies of the Western Plaguelands from Tirisfal Glades. Deathguard Linnea oversees security behind the frontier. The defenders cannot spare troops to guard against attacks from the rear. Any undead that slip past the choke point must be destroyed before they can cut the supply lines feeding the front.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Balnir Farmstead",b="Balnir Farmstead was once a working farm in eastern Tirisfal, but it fell to ruin during the Third War. Blight covers its fields, and its crumbling stables shelter Bleeding Horrors and restless Wandering Spirits. Clearing the farmstead denies the Lich King a place to gather forces inside Tirisfal and keeps the road open for Horde reinforcements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this patrol important for the Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark holds the narrow pass between Tirisfal and the Western Plaguelands. If Scourge wander behind the fortification, defenders could face attacks from both sides and lose the supply lines to Brill and the Undercity.",al={"why do rear guard patrol","bulwark importance","why secure balnir"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders this mission?",a="Deathguard Linnea, stationed near the road east into the Plaguelands, orders the patrol and sends reports of success to Executor Zygand.",al={"who gives rear guard patrol","deathguard linnea"},it="identity"},{q="What creatures haunt the Balnir Farmstead?",a="Bleeding Horrors, corpses reanimated and stitched together by necromancy, and Wandering Spirits haunt Balnir Farmstead. The spirits belonged to former inhabitants who died during the Scourge's initial conquest.",al={"balnir farmstead mobs","what monsters are at balnir","bleeding horror"},it="target"},{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken Deathguard commander based in Brill. He is Deathguard Linnea's superior.",al={"executor zygand lore","who is zygand"},it="leader"},{q="Why don't the Forsaken just abandon the eastern border?",a="If the Forsaken abandon the Bulwark, the Scourge's endless hordes from the Plaguelands could reach all of Tirisfal Glades and the gates of the Undercity.",al={"why defend the bulwark","why fight at the border"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Deathguard Linnea need an adventurer instead of handling the patrol herself?",a="The defenders stationed at the Bulwark are stretched thin holding the eastern frontier against constant assaults from the Plaguelands. Linnea and the garrison cannot afford to abandon their fortified posts to sweep the rear without weakening the main line. Turning to capable travelers allows the Forsaken to clear out infiltrators behind them while maintaining an unbroken wall of defense against the Scourge.",al={"why me linnea","why send an adventurer rear guard patrol","why doesnt linnea do it"},it="why_me",add="a47e493a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you depend on the Bulwark's rear defenses for survival. Clearing Scourge from Balnir Farmstead helps keep the Lich King's renewed grasp from reaching your homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help hold Tirisfal's eastern perimeter and protect the Horde's tenuous foothold in the northern Eastern Kingdoms from the undead legions."},kw={"balnir","bleeding horror","bulwark","linnea","scourge","tirisfal","wandering spirit","zygand"},rel={"npc:deathguard-linnea","subzone:balnir-farmstead","subzone:bulwark","npc:executor-zygand","quest:1882","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Linnea",level="11",faction="Horde",id=356},src={"Rear Guard Patrol"}}
E["quest:358"] = {t="quest",n="Graverobbers",z="tirisfal",s="At the Mass Grave southwest of Garren's Haunt, Rot Hide gnolls dig up the dead. Magistrate Sevren sends you to stop them and recover their embalming ichor for the Royal Apothecary Society's research.",h="At the Mass Grave southwest of Garren's Haunt, Rot Hide gnolls dig up the dead.",sec={{t="Desecration of the Mass Graves",b="The Plague of Undeath overwhelmed Tirisfal Glades, and the dead outnumbered those who could bury them. Immense mass graves were dug across the north to hold the countless victims. For a time, the buried escaped resurrection. Now the Scourge sends Rot Hide gnolls to the trenches southwest of Garren's Haunt. They exhume the decayed remains to swell the Lich King's armies.",sp=0},{t="Turning Scourge Alchemy Inward",b="Embalming ichor preserves and animates the Rot Hides' rotting frames. Magistrate Sevren sends you to slay the graverobbers and recover the fluid. This stops the Scourge from harvesting bodies and gives Brill's apothecaries valuable specimens. They hope to turn the Lich King's own alchemy against him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scourge digging up the Mass Grave?",a="The Scourge digs up the Mass Grave's victims from the Plague's first arrival in Tirisfal to raise new soldiers and swell its armies against the Forsaken.",al={"why are gnolls digging corpses","what does the scourge want with bodies","mass grave purpose"},it="threat"},{q="What are the Rot Hide gnolls?",a="Rot Hide gnolls are undead gnolls enslaved by the Scourge. Embalming ichor animates and preserves them, and they serve as scavengers and shock troops around Garren's Haunt and the neighboring graves.",al={"rot hide lore","undead gnolls tirisfal","what are rot hides"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Mass Grave located?",a="The Mass Grave lies southwest of Garren's Haunt, in the northern hills of Tirisfal Glades, just north of Brill.",al={"where are graverobbers","mass grave location","garren's haunt mass grave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do the Forsaken want with the Embalming Ichor?",a="Magistrate Sevren gives the collected ichor to Forsaken apothecaries. They study how the Scourge animates and maintains its lesser thralls, seeking weaknesses to exploit in the ongoing war.",al={"why collect embalming ichor","what is ichor for","ichor lore"},it="item"},{q="Who orders the death of the Graverobbers?",a="Magistrate Sevren, Brill's Forsaken overseer, orders the graverobbers killed to defend Tirisfal's borders and secure useful reagents for the Apothecaries.",al={"who gives graverobbers","magistrate sevren role"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why do the Forsaken care if dead plague victims are raised?",a="The Scourge turns every corpse it claims into an enemy soldier under the Lich King's will, threatening the newly liberated Forsaken kingdom.",al={"why do forsaken protect graves","why care about dead bodies"},it="motive"},{q="Who are you being sent against at the Mass Grave?",a="You are sent to destroy the Rot Hide gnolls—specifically the graverobbers and mongrels—haunting Garren's Haunt and the nearby mass grave. These undead beasts act as vile thralls for the Scourge, tasked with exhuming the countless victims of the original plague to bolster the ranks of the Lich King's armies right on Brill's doorstep.",al={"who are the enemies","what are rot hides doing","target of graverobbers"},it="target",add="9e6ccf32"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help keep the Scourge from raising Tirisfal's former citizens and condemning your fallen countrymen to mindless servitude.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help halt the Scourge's resupply efforts and secure northern Lordaeron, strengthening the Horde's foothold against the Lich King's remaining forces."},kw={"brill","embalming ichor","garren's haunt","graverobbers","magistrate sevren","mass grave","rot hide","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:garren-s-haunt","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",level="8",faction="Horde",id=358,ri={"Embalming Ichor"}},src={"Graverobbers (Classic)"}}
E["quest:360"] = {t="quest",n="Return to the Magistrate",z="tirisfal",s="At Brill, Magistrate Sevren receives a warning from the eastern frontier. Deathguard Linnea sends word that the Lich King's mindless servants still test the Forsaken borders.",h="At Brill, Magistrate Sevren receives a warning from the eastern frontier.",sec={{t="Frontier Reports",b="East of Tirisfal Glades, the road reaches the blighted ruins of the Western Plaguelands, where the Scourge holds sway. The Forsaken built the Bulwark to keep the undead from entering their homeland. Deathguard Linnea watches from a waystation behind the line, gathering reports from the eastern gate. She sends messengers west along the King's Road to Brill before enemy infiltrators can exploit gaps in the defenses.",sp=0},{t="Sevren's Vow",b="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren hears that Scourge scouts are finding paths around or through the frontline. Each creeping ghoul and mindless skeleton recalls the Forsaken's enslavement, broken when Lordaeron fell. Sevren vows that no matter how ceaseless the Lich King's assault, the free undead will not surrender their new autonomy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this report come from?",a="Deathguard Linnea sends the report from her waystation east of Brill, on the road to the Bulwark. She gathers word from the barricades between Tirisfal and the Scourge-held Western Plaguelands.",al={"quest origin","who sent this report","where is linnea"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Magistrate Sevren concerned about this news?",a="The dispatch warns Sevren that Scourge forces have slipped past the Bulwark's fortifications. Their incursions threaten the Forsaken's young towns and recall the Lich King's effort to reclaim them.",al={"why is sevren worried","what does the report say","scourge threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Magistrate Sevren?",a="Magistrate Sevren administers Brill from its town hall. He oversees local defenses, infrastructure, and the mustering of newly raised Forsaken across central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"sevren lore","who is the magistrate"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark is a fortified outpost on the main road between Tirisfal Glades and the Western Plaguelands. It bars Scourge incursions into Forsaken lands.",al={"bulwark lore","eastern border tirisfal"},it="place"},{q="Why do the Forsaken hate the Scourge so much?",a="The Forsaken were once the Scourge's mindless thralls, slain in life and raised to butcher their own kin. Now free-willed, they hate the Lich King and fear falling under his control again.",al={"forsaken vs scourge","why hate lich king"},it="conflict"},{q="What path does this message travel?",a="Messengers carry the message west from Deathguard Linnea's waystation along the main road, through central Tirisfal Glades, to Brill's town center.",al={"route from bulwark to brill","road to brill"}},{q="Why does Deathguard Linnea want this done?",a="Deathguard Linnea is stationed at a Deathguard waystation east of Brill, on the road toward the Bulwark. When Scourge forces breach these eastern defenses and infiltrate Tirisfal Glades, Brill's leadership must know immediately. Linnea needs Magistrate Sevren warned without delay so local authorities can prepare for incursions and mobilize defenders against the Lich King's relentless minions.",al={"why linnea report","why send report to sevren","deathguard linnea motive"},it="motive",add="8343d5ab"},{q="Why does Deathguard Linnea need you to deliver the message?",a="Linnea and her fellow Deathguards keep watch at a waystation east of Brill, monitoring Scourge activity that slips past the Bulwark. She asks a passing adventurer to carry her report back to Magistrate Sevren so the town can prepare while the waystation maintains its watch.",al={"why not send a deathguard","why linnea needs me","why deliver message to sevren"},it="why_me",add="0dd03a94"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know how fragile Forsaken freedom remains: the master you escaped still presses against your new home.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Tirisfal Glades anchors your foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms. The Bulwark guards it from the horrors of the Plaguelands."},kw={"brill","bulwark","forsaken duties","linnea","scourge","sevren","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:bulwark","npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:deathguard-linnea","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Linnea",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="9",faction="Horde",id=360},src={"Return to the Magistrate (Classic)"}}
E["quest:361"] = {t="quest",n="A Letter Undelivered",z="tirisfal",s="A faded, bloodstained letter to Yvette Farthing lies among the skeletal ruins of Agamand Mills. It recalls two lovers parted as the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, and what the Forsaken left behind when they traded life for undeath.",h="A faded, bloodstained letter to Yvette Farthing lies among the skeletal ruins of Agamand Mills.",sec={{t="A Message Lost in the Fall",b="Thurman Agamand, eldest son of patriarch Gregor Agamand, wrote the message that never reached Yvette Farthing. When the Plague of Undeath consumed Tirisfal Glades, Thurman refused to leave his ancestral home or his kin. As the Scourge struck, he took up his quill to write to Yvette, whom he had loved before the kingdom turned to ash.",sp=0},{t="The Severed Bond",b="When Yvette Farthing receives the letter at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, a painful memory returns. She recalls begging Thurman to flee Agamand Mills with her and her father, and says his brother Brand bore him ill will. The warmth soon passes. Yvette steels her heart, casts aside mortal remorse, and declares that love has no place in her new existence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote this letter?",a="Thurman Agamand, eldest son of Gregor Agamand, wrote the letter. He perished defending his family's mills against the Scourge alongside the rest of his cursed household.",al={"author","thurman agamand","who is thurman"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Yvette Farthing?",a="Yvette Farthing is a Forsaken woman living inside the tavern in Brill. In life, she begged her lover Thurman Agamand to leave Agamand Mills with her and her father, but he stayed with his family.",al={"yvette","who is yvette","recipient"},it="people"},{q="Where did the letter come from?",a="The letter is found among walking skeletons prowling the devastated grounds and fields of Agamand Mills in western Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to find letter","letter drop","letter location"},it="origin"},{q="What happened between Thurman and Yvette?",a="Thurman and Yvette were lovers before the Third War. She begged him to leave his family's mills and escape with her, but he stayed with his kin to face the Plague.",al={"thurman and yvette","yvette backstory","what happened to them"},it="history"},{q="What does Yvette do when she reads the letter?",a="Yvette briefly grieves for Thurman and curses both the Scourge and his brother Brand, then quickly suppresses her feelings. She says regrets are for the weak and romance has no place in her Forsaken existence.",al={"yvette reaction","what does yvette say"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Brand Agamand?",a="Brand was Thurman Agamand's brother. Yvette says Brand harbored deep resentment and ill intent toward Thurman even before the estate fell to the Plague.",al={"brand","brand agamand","who is brand"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The letter shows the painful divide between a Forsaken's mortal memories and the cold, purpose-driven existence they lead under the Banshee Queen.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers in Brill, this recovered parchment shows the emotional detachment that defines the Forsaken people."},kw={"agamand","brill","farthing","letter","scourge","tavern","thurman","undelivered","yvette"},rel={"npc:yvette-farthing","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","npc:farthing"},m={start="A Letter to Yvette",["end"]="Yvette Farthing",level="7",faction="Horde",id=361},src={"A Letter Undelivered"}}
E["quest:362"] = {t="quest",n="The Haunted Mills",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing of Brill seeks vengeance on the Agamands, his former landowners. He sends you north to Agamand Mills to destroy their restless remains, beginning with Devlin, the family’s sharp-tongued younger son. Farthing’s hatred reaches back to the family’s failure to protect Tirisfal’s common folk from the Plague.",h="Coleman Farthing of Brill seeks vengeance on the Agamands, his former landowners.",sec={{t="A Bitter Harvest",b="Before the Third War, Agamand Mills fed northern Tirisfal under the rule of a wealthy landed family. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, common folk turned to the nobles for safety and found no shelter. Coleman Farthing survived as undead, but hatred for the family he served still consumes him. He wants their bones gathered, not to end their torment, but to desecrate them beneath his heel.",sp=0},{t="The Younger Brother",b="Devlin Agamand was Thurman Agamand’s younger brother. People remembered Devlin as weak, spiteful, and sharp-tongued, unlike his gentle elder brother. When the Plague of Undeath reached the mill estate, Devlin quickly fell to its corruption. Now his mindless corpse chatters without cease along the northern road into the family mills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want Devlin's remains?",a="Coleman Farthing blames the Agamands for abandoning him and his relatives when the Scourge overran Lordaeron. In undeath, he seeks revenge by gathering their bones to display on his mantle and grind into dust.",al={"why coleman want bones","coleman farthing motive","why kill devlin"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Devlin Agamand be found?",a="Devlin wanders near the road just south of Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades, gibbering among the undead that prowl the estate’s outskirts.",al={"devlin location","find devlin agamand","where is devlin"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What was Devlin like before the Plague?",a="Coleman Farthing describes Devlin as the smaller, weaker, sharp-tongued younger son of the Agamands, unlike his tall, mild-mannered older brother Thurman.",al={"who was devlin","devlin agamand lore","devlin agamand in life"},it="identity"},{q="Is Devlin part of the Scourge or Forsaken?",a="Devlin is a mindless thrall of the Scourge. He never broke free of the Lich King’s grip as the Forsaken of the Undercity did, and now stalks his family’s ruined lands.",al={"is devlin scourge","devlin faction"},it="side"},{q="What other quests take place at Agamand Mills?",a="Deaths in the Family also sends Forsaken adventurers to Agamand Mills to eliminate the rest of the Agamand household, so you can pursue both at once.",al={"agamand mills quests","quests near devlin"},gp=true},{q="What happens after turning in Devlin's remains?",a="After accepting the bones, Coleman Farthing sends you to speak with Sevren in Brill. That leads deeper into the Agamand family crypt.",al={"quest continuation","next quest after haunted mills"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What does Coleman Farthing do with Devlin's Remains?",a="Coleman intends to mount Devlin's bones right on his mantle, keeping them as a grim trophy of vengeance. He harbors deep, bitter hatred toward the Agamand family for failing him and his relatives when the Scourge swept through Tirisfal. Rather than granting the remains a proper burial or study, Coleman seeks the petty satisfaction of gloating over what is left of the weak, sharp-tongued younger brother, ultimately swearing to grind the Agamand bones under his heel.",al={"devlins remains use","why keep devlins remains","what happens to devlins bones"},it="item",add="6ae9875b"},{q="Who is Devlin Agamand?",a="Devlin was the younger son of the prominent Agamand dynasty, known in life as weak and viciously sharp-tongued in contrast to his gentle older brother, Thurman. When the Plague of Undeath engulfed Agamand Mills, Devlin was among the quickest to succumb. Now risen as a mindless undead monster under the Scourge's thrall, he wanders the road just south of his family's ruined mills, chattering madly to himself in the Tirisfal gloom.",al={"who is devlin agamand","who is devlin","devlin agamand lore"},it="target",add="67792824"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see how the fall of Lordaeron left mortal grudges alive. The landed nobles failed to protect the common folk from the Plague, and resentment remains.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help the Forsaken purge dangerous Scourge from the borders of Brill and Undercity."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","devlin agamand","haunted mills","plague","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-mills","quest:354","quest:355","quest:408","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",level="10",faction="Horde",id=362,ri={"Devlin's Remains"}},src={"The Haunted Mills (Classic)"}}
E["quest:363"] = {t="quest",n="Rude Awakening",z="tirisfal",s="Newly awakened Forsaken leave Deathknell's crypts to face an unfamiliar life. Freed from the Lich King's grip, you are sent down the hill, away from the incinerators, to learn what comes next from Shadow Priest Sarvis.",h="Newly awakened Forsaken leave Deathknell's crypts to face an unfamiliar life.",sec={{t="A Grave Beginning",b="In Deathknell's damp, subterranean crypt, the chill greets you as you open your eyes to undeath. Undertaker Mordo watches over the newly buried, sorting those who regain free will from those bound for the burning pits. Many rise to find rot, cold stone, and confusion. By chance, they have slipped the Scourge's grasp.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Grip of the Frozen Throne",b="Before reaching the chapel, you must face a grim truth: you were once a mindless tool of the Lich King. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner broke that psychic enslavement, freeing remnants of your former humanity to reclaim independent thought. Leaving the tomb and heading down into Deathknell begins your life in a world where both the living and the Scourge see you as an abomination to be destroyed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was I in a crypt?",a="You died during the Third War, from plague or violence, and were buried in Tirisfal Glades. In Deathknell, the newly risen are watched to see whether they regain their minds or sink into mindless rot.",al={"why in crypt","where did i wake up","deathknell tomb"},it="arrival"},{q="Who is Undertaker Mordo?",a="Undertaker Mordo cares for Deathknell's crypt. He watches over the newly awakened, sends those who keep their sanity to the town chapel, and disposes of those who fail to awaken with their minds intact.",al={"undertaker mordo","who is mordo","gravekeeper"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Mordo mention throwing people into the fire?",a="Not every corpse raised from the grave regains free will or steady thoughts. Those who awaken mad or purely feral cannot join Forsaken society, so they are destroyed and burned to prevent rampages.",al={"burn bodies","toss into fire","cremation"},it="history"},{q="Who freed me from the Lich King?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, known as the Banshee Queen, broke free of the Lich King's psychic domination as his power waned. She gathered other free-willed undead beneath her banner and founded the Forsaken to fight their former master and hostile living remnants.",al={"who freed me","sylvanas freed undead","why am i free"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Shadow Priest Sarvis located?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis is inside the damaged chapel at the base of the hill in Deathknell. Leave the crypt and follow the cobblestone path downhill to the chapel entrance.",al={"find sarvis","sarvis location","where is the chapel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the Forsaken fighting against?",a="The Forsaken wage a two-front war for survival. They fight the Scourge, which seeks to reclaim or destroy them, and human zealots and surviving settlements that see no difference between them and mindless monsters.",al={"forsaken enemies","who do we fight","undead enemies"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Undertaker Mordo send me to Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="Undertaker Mordo's duty is merely to tend the crypts and sort the salvageable undead from the truly lost. He is no statesman or spiritual guide. Newly awakened Forsaken are disoriented, traumatized, and dangerously unaware of the war around them. By sending you immediately down the hill to Shadow Priest Sarvis in the chapel, Mordo ensures you are educated, integrated into Lady Sylvanas's cause, and trained for survival before you wander off or fall into the hands of enemies.",al={"why visit sarvis","mordo motive","why send me to church"},it="motive",add="e742af5a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you have shed the Scourge's shackles and begin a spiteful, free life among the Forsaken.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you meet the Forsaken priesthood through Shadow Priest Sarvis, where spiritual devotion takes new meaning after undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you enter a fragile alliance formed from sheer necessity against mutual extinction."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken","lich king","mordo","rude awakening","sarvis","scourge","shadow priest sarvis","sylvanas","tirisfal glades","undertaker mordo"},rel={"npc:undertaker-mordo","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","subzone:deathknell","quest:364","zone:tirisfal","topic:lich-king","topic:scourge"},m={start="Undertaker Mordo",["end"]="Shadow Priest Sarvis",level="1",faction="Horde",id=363},src={"Rude Awakening"}}
E["quest:364"] = {t="quest",n="The Mindless Ones",z="tirisfal",s="Newly risen Forsaken face the Mindless Ones on Deathknell's northern edge. Shadow Priest Sarvis sends them to cull Mindless Zombies and Wretched Zombies, Scourge thralls bound to the Lich King's command.",h="Newly risen Forsaken face the Mindless Ones on Deathknell's northern edge.",sec={{t="Slaves to the Frozen Throne",b="Many who rise from Lordaeron's dirt never recover their minds. The Forsaken broke free of Ner'zhul's domination as his power waned, but countless corpses remain chained to his will. In northern Deathknell, Mindless Zombies and Wretched Zombies wander, driven to violence. For you, newly risen among the undead, putting them down is the first hard trial. You prove your freedom by ending the thrall of those who never escaped.",sp=0},{t="Mercy Through Destruction",b="Shadow Priest Sarvis grieves that these legions of dead cannot strengthen the Forsaken's desperate struggle. There is no cure for them. Their minds are broken, and they remain instruments of slaughter. If left to roam, they bring chaos to Deathknell's doorstep and give the Lich King easy fodder. Destroying them is necessary for the settlement and brings a grim end to some of Lordaeron's fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't the mindless zombies be recruited into the Forsaken?",a="The zombies cannot choose to join Lady Sylvanas because their minds are broken and bound to the Lich King. Shadow Priest Sarvis says their numbers would be invaluable, but they remain dangerous Scourge thralls.",al={"recruit mindless zombies","why kill them","can mindless zombies be cured","free the zombies"}},{q="Who are these zombies originally?",a="The zombies were human inhabitants of Lordaeron who fell to the plague of undeath during the Third War. Unlike you, they never regained their memories, personalities, or freedom of choice when the Lich King's grip slipped.",al={"who were the mindless ones","identity of mindless zombies","deathknell corpses"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Shadow Priest Sarvis commanding the defense here?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis oversees the first days of newly risen undead in Deathknell. He judges whether they have the grit and clear mind to survive their new existence.",al={"who is sarvis","sarvis deathknell role","priest sarvis"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the difference between Forsaken and Scourge zombies?",a="Forsaken have free will, while Scourge zombies do not. Forsaken escaped the Lich King's telepathic control and kept their intelligence and emotions; he directly puppeteers the empty vessels of the Scourge.",al={"scourge vs forsaken","difference between forsaken and mindless","why are some zombies mindless"},it="identity"},{q="Are the mindless zombies a threat to Deathknell?",a="Yes. These zombies wander just north of Deathknell, threatening new arrivals from the graves and the Forsaken priests trying to organize the settlement.",al={"deathknell danger","why clear northern deathknell","zombie threat"},it="danger"},{q="Where does this task lead next?",a="Your success against the mindless dead leads to more duties securing Deathknell, including culling skeletal Scourge in Rattling the Rattlecages and beginning training with your class mentor.",al={"next quest after mindless ones","mindless ones followup","what comes next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Sarvis want the zombies destroyed?",a="Deathknell is surrounded and under constant pressure from the Lich King's minions. Sarvis sees the overrun northern side of the village as an immediate danger to the Forsaken foothold here. The Scourge cannot be reasoned with or swayed to your cause, so destroying them is the only way to secure the area and ensure the survival of your newly awakened people.",al={"sarvis motive","why kill mindless zombies","why destroy mindless ones"},it="motive",add="b9d2809d"},{q="Who are the Mindless Zombies wandering northern Deathknell?",a="They are slain residents of Lordaeron raised by the Scourge who never regained their free will. Trapped as feral thralls to the Lich King's will, these mindless and wretched corpses now shamble through the ruins of northern Deathknell, attacking anyone who crosses their path.",al={"who are the mindless zombies","wretched zombies","what are mindless ones"},it="target",add="40675fbd"},{q="Why does Sarvis send you to kill the zombies instead of the guards?",a="Sarvis is testing your resolve and capability in this new existence. Deathknell's established guardians must maintain their posts around the chapel and perimeter. Proving that you can destroy even mindless former kin demonstrates you possess the stomach and martial strength needed to serve the Dark Lady.",al={"why me","why send me to kill zombies","why sarvis asks you"},it="why_me",add="58c1d115"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may see a former neighbor, kin, or friend among the zombies roaming the village outskirts. They remind you what you were spared and what could happen if the Forsaken fall.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you serve under Shadow Priest Sarvis and meet the Forsaken's pragmatic, shadow-tinged way of life, adopted in place of the Holy Light that abandoned them.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see why the Horde once viewed the Forsaken with deep suspicion before admitting them to the faction."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken","lich king","mindless ones","mindless zombie","scourge","shadow priest sarvis","wretched zombie"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","quest:363","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Shadow Priest Sarvis",level="2",faction="Horde",id=364},src={"The Mindless Ones"}}
E["quest:365"] = {t="quest",n="Fields of Grief",z="tirisfal",s="Pumpkins are taken from a human farmstead north of Deathknell for the Royal Apothecary Society in Brill. Deathguard Simmer sends newly risen Forsaken to gather them.",h="Pumpkins are taken from a human farmstead north of Deathknell for the Royal Apothecary Society in Brill.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Survival",b="Deathguard Simmer sends you from the crypts of Deathknell into a hostile land. He serves Sylvanas Windrunner's forces, where survival means taking what the living possess and putting it to use for the Undercity's darker aims.",sp=0},{t="Raiding the Living",b="The farm lies west of the road, north of Deathknell, where mortal human peasants work blighted soil. Simmer says they infest the realm like mold on a corpse. The farmers hold their homesteads under the uneasy protection of nearby Scarlet Crusade towers. Taking their crops strikes at their supplies and provides produce for the Royal Apothecary Society's research.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Society",b="Apothecary Johaan conducts experimental research in Brill, where the stolen pumpkins are delivered. The Royal Apothecary Society frequently uses local produce and flora as bases for alchemical brews, poisons, and plague research. Its work aims to secure the Forsaken's precarious foothold in northern Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Fields of Grief?",a="Deathguard Simmer gives you the assignment. He guards the road in southern Tirisfal Glades, just north of the path out of Deathknell.",al={"quest giver","fields of grief quest starter","who starts fields of grief"},gp=true},{q="Where do I take the Tirisfal Pumpkins?",a="Take the ten Tirisfal Pumpkins to Apothecary Johaan in Brill, east in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to turn in pumpkins","pumpkin turn in","fields of grief hand in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are there living humans farming in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The human peasants are remnants of Lordaeron's original population who survived the Third War and the Scourge plague. They cling to their homesteads near Scarlet Crusade guard posts and resist Forsaken dominion.",al={"why humans here","living humans tirisfal","why are humans in undead zone"},it="people"},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want pumpkins?",a="Apothecary Johaan wants pumpkins for the Royal Apothecary Society's research. The Society uses plants, blighted crops, and biological matter as testing agents and base components for alchemical mixtures, poisons, and experimental plagues.",al={"why pumpkins","what are pumpkins for","apothecary johaan pumpkins"},it="item"},{q="Who patrols near the farmstead?",a="Scarlet Crusade zealots patrol down from a nearby watchtower. They defend the human settlement and try to purge undead who approach the fields.",al={"scarlet crusade near farm","who protects the farm"},it="threat"},{q="What comes after Fields of Grief?",a="After you deliver the pumpkins, Apothecary Johaan gives you another assignment of the same name. He hands you a pumpkin laced with his latest formula to take to a captured Scarlet Zealot in the cellar of the Gallows' End Tavern.",al={"next quest","fields of grief followup","what is after fields of grief"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Deathguard Simmer want this done?",a="Deathguard Simmer sees surviving humans farming the glades as mold on a rotting corpse—an intolerable infestation on land that now belongs to the Forsaken. Stealing their crops strikes at their meager livelihood while simultaneously aiding the Royal Apothecary Society with fresh reagents, proving whether newly awakened Forsaken have the grit to serve the Dark Lady.",al={"why simmer pumpkins","deathguard simmer motive","fields of grief reason"},it="motive",add="39021143"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, this is your first military assignment outside Deathknell. You strip your former mortal kin of their livelihood to advance the Royal Apothecary Society.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Tirisfal Glades by breaking the lingering human presence and dismantling Scarlet Crusade influence along the southern roads.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know apothecaries rely on Tirisfal's twisted flora for deadly concoctions. Every local root and crop can become a reagent of war."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","deathguard simmer","deathknell","fields of grief","royal apothecary society","scarlet crusade","tirisfal pumpkin"},rel={"npc:deathguard-simmer","npc:apothecary-johaan","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={start="Deathguard Simmer",["end"]="Apothecary Johaan",level="7",faction="Horde",id=365,ri={"Tirisfal Pumpkin"}},src={"Fields of Grief (Classic)"}}
E["quest:366"] = {t="quest",n="Return the Book",z="tirisfal",s="Bethor Iceshard sends his enchanted message back to Gunther Arcanus on Brightwater Lake. The stolen spellbook may bring his old Kirin Tor companion into the Forsaken fold.",h="Bethor Iceshard sends his enchanted message back to Gunther Arcanus on Brightwater Lake.",sec={{t="A Message in Arcane Ink",b="Bethor Iceshard sends an arcane message to Gunther Arcanus through a stolen spellbook. Once Bethor learns the necromancer on Brightwater Lake is his old companion, he enchants the tome's pages. The spell leaves Bethor's own magical mark, showing he is active in Lordaeron and free of the Lich King's control.",sp=0},{t="The Old Circle of Dalaran",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw studied and became friends in the Kirin Tor of Dalaran. When the Lich King rose, Thule betrayed his companions and joined the Scourge willingly. Bethor and Gunther fell to the Plague. Bethor later broke free alongside Queen Sylvanas. Believing Gunther dead or enslaved, Bethor now learns his old friend has also won his own freedom and seeks to bring him to the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="Mistrust on the Island",b="Gunther Arcanus meets an intruder on his island with fury. He suspects a Scourge agent has come to enslave him again, or that the thief who stole his magic has returned. Then he sees his grimoire and feels Bethor's familiar magic in it. The sign of someone from his mortal past forces the solitary mage to question his isolation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why did Bethor enchant Gunther's spellbook?",a="Bethor Iceshard enchants the stolen spellbook with his magical signature to show Gunther he is free of the Lich King. A plain messenger might be rejected or destroyed by Gunther, who fears the Scourge.",al={"why enchant the book","gunthers book spell","what did bethor do to the book"},it="item"},{q="Who was Gunther Arcanus before he died?",a="Before his death, Gunther Arcanus was a human mage and Kirin Tor scholar in Dalaran. He studied with Bethor Iceshard and Thule Ravenclaw before the Third War, then fell to the Scourge's Plague of Undeath.",al={"who is gunther arcanus","gunther backstory","gunther lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gunther hiding on Brightwater Lake?",a="After breaking free of the Lich King's control, Gunther believed he was alone in his freedom. He hid on an island in Brightwater Lake to escape the Scourge and living enemies who might hunt or kill him.",al={"why is gunther on the island","gunthers retreat lore","why did gunther leave"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw was a fellow Kirin Tor student of Bethor Iceshard and Gunther Arcanus in Dalaran. Unlike them, Thule willingly serves the Scourge as a loyal necromancer in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is thule","thule ravenclaw lore","third friend"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gunther think the player is a thief?",a="Bethor earlier sent Forsaken adventurers into Gunther's sanctum to steal his spellbook and learn who was practicing necromancy on the lake. Gunther recognizes the returning adventurer as the one who robbed him.",al={"why does gunther call me a thief","did i steal gunthers book","stolen book"},it="hostile"},{q="Does Gunther immediately join the Forsaken?",a="No. Gunther is stunned to learn Bethor lives and is free, but remains wary of the Forsaken. He asks you to prove you oppose the Scourge by summoning and destroying its agent Lillith Nefara at an old altar off the island's southern coast.",al={"does gunther join sylvanas","gunther allegience","what happens next with gunther"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want to recruit Gunther?",a="Bethor and Gunther were close friends and fellow mages within Dalaran's Kirin Tor before both succumbed to the Plague. Having learned that Gunther managed to break free from the Lich King's grasp on his own, Bethor desperately wants to bring his powerful former colleague into the Forsaken. By returning Gunther's enchanted spellbook, Bethor hopes to prove that other undead have reclaimed their free will and convince the reclusive necromancer that he no longer needs to stand alone.",al={"why does bethor want gunther","bethor iceshard motives","why recruit gunther"},it="motive",add="3bda1a56"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you share Gunther's struggle: waking from mindless service to face a hostile, lonely world.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know how former Kirin Tor magi can recognize one another's magic across undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help strengthen Undercity's arcane ranks when independent undead sorcerers like Gunther join the cause against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","dalaran","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","gunther's spellbook","kirin tor","return the book","thule ravenclaw","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:357","quest:409","subzone:gunther-s-retreat","quest:446","subzone:dalaran","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Bethor Iceshard",["end"]="Gunther Arcanus",level="8",faction="Horde",id=366},src={"Return the Book"}}
E["quest:367"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, A New Plague begins with blood taken from darkhounds. Apothecary Johaan gathers the samples for the Royal Apothecary Society, acting on Lady Sylvanas Windrunner’s command.",h="In Brill, A New Plague begins with blood taken from darkhounds.",sec={{t="A Royal Mandate",b="Apothecary Johaan works in Brill for the Royal Apothecary Society, under orders from the Dark Lady. Sylvanas Windrunner has charged her alchemists with making a disease unlike any Azeroth has known. The original Plague of Undeath served the Lich King, slaughtering humanity and binding their souls. This new plague is meant to annihilate Arthas Menethil and lay waste to his Scourge legions.",sp=0},{t="Raw Ingredients",b="Johaan needs grim experiments to develop a weapon against the undead. He believes the blood of native beasts may hold useful chemical properties, beginning with darkhounds roaming Tirisfal Glades. You gather vials of their tainted blood so Johaan can isolate elements and test whether the beasts' resilience and predatory nature can help create a lethal contagion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of the new plague?",a="Lady Sylvanas tasked the Royal Apothecary Society with brewing a disease deadlier than any other on Azeroth. Its aim is the destruction of Arthas and his Scourge army.",al={"why make a new plague","purpose of new plague","what does the plague do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Johaan is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Brill. He conducts early field experiments, testing compounds gathered from Tirisfal's local beasts.",al={"who is johaan","apothecary johaan lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Johaan need darkhound blood?",a="Johaan believes native beasts' blood may provide a foundation for his alchemical formulas. He needs darkhound blood to test his early theories in the laboratory.",al={"why darkhound blood","what is the blood for"},it="item"},{q="How does this plague differ from the Scourge's plague?",a="The original Plague of Undeath was made by the Lich King to slaughter the living and bind their souls. Sylvanas's new plague is meant to bring ruin to Arthas's undead legions.",al={"difference between plagues","scourge plague vs forsaken plague"}},{q="Who ordered the creation of this plague?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner directly ordered the Royal Apothecary Society to create the plague. She believes Forsaken alchemy combined with newfound magic can defeat Arthas.",al={"who started the plague research","who wants the plague"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after gathering the blood?",a="Gathering darkhound blood begins a series of experiments. Johaan uses the samples to refine the pathogen through further field tests across the Glades.",al={"what is the next step","does the plague work"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want this done?",a="Lady Sylvanas herself called upon the Royal Apothecary Society to create a weapon deadlier than any affliction on Azeroth, engineered to bring Arthas and his Scourge army to ruin. As an apothecary of the Society stationed in Brill, Johaan is striving to answer the Dark Lady's mandate by testing his theories on indigenous beast reagents.",al={"johaan motive","why does johaan want a new plague","why help johaan"},it="motive",add="399e4c7c"},{q="What are darkhounds and why hunt them here?",a="Darkhounds are fierce, corrupted predatory beasts that roam the blighted woods and pathways of Tirisfal Glades. Their blood has absorbed the corruptive energies seeping into the land, making them prime biological specimens for the Royal Apothecary Society's toxicological experiments.",al={"what are darkhounds","darkhounds tirisfal","why darkhounds"},it="target",add="762eb481"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you make your first direct contribution to the Royal Apothecary Society's project: creating the weapon Sylvanas plans to wield against Arthas.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you stand beside the Forsaken, whose alchemical work in Tirisfal focuses on a grim weapon aimed at Northrend."},kw={"apothecary","arthas","brill","darkhound","johaan","plague","scourge","sylvanas","tirisfal"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",level="6",faction="Horde",id=367,ri={"Darkhound Blood"}},src={"A New Plague"}}
E["quest:368"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan gathers scales from the Vile Fin murlocs along Tirisfal's coast. The errand supports the Royal Apothecary Society's work on a contagion meant to spread beyond isolated victims and reach larger populations.",h="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan gathers scales from the Vile Fin murlocs along Tirisfal's coast.",sec={{t="Scaling Up the Contagion",b="Apothecary Johaan's research in Brill needs more than a poison that harms one target. He is working on a disease that can spread on its own and endure in the wild. For those studies, he looks to the shoreline wildlife of Tirisfal Glades. The resilient biology of the coastal Vile Fin murlocs offers promising material for his work.",sp=0},{t="The Vile Fin Reagents",b="Aggressive Vile Fin murloc tribes trouble the northern and western shores of Tirisfal Glades. Their scales contain organic compounds adapted to damp, harsh conditions. Johaan wants to add those slick, resilient scales to his developing brew, hoping they will strengthen the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague and help it endure in the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of Apothecary Johaan's research?",a="Apothecary Johaan is developing a new plague for the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas. He aims to make a contagion that can spread across entire populations and lands, targeting both the living and the Scourge.",al={"why make a new plague","johaan plague goal","what is johaan doing"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Johaan need murloc scales specifically?",a="Johaan needs Vile Fin scales because they contain biological compounds that may help his contagion survive in the wild and pass between hosts. His early brewing showed him that simple poisons lack the complexity needed to spread effectively.",al={"why murloc scales","vile fin scale purpose","why scales for plague"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the Vile Fin murlocs be found?",a="The Vile Fin murlocs live along the coasts of Tirisfal Glades, especially on the northern beaches by the Great Sea and along the western coast.",al={"where are murlocs tirisfal","vile fin location","murloc spots"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who does Apothecary Johaan answer to?",a="Apothecary Johaan is an operative of the Royal Apothecary Society, an alchemical guild headquartered in the Undercity that answers directly to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who leads the apothecaries","johaan boss","royal apothecary society leader"},it="leader"},{q="What is the next step in this quest chain?",a="After you bring the Vile Fin scales to Johaan, he continues refining the formula. He needs more biological components and eventually plans to test the newly brewed strain.",al={"what comes next","after vile fin scales","next plague quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Are the Forsaken concerned about using murloc parts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is pragmatic and amoral about its experiments. It harvests from local flora, fauna, or beasts whenever they yield the biochemical traits it needs.",al={"murloc alchemy dangerous","why harvest murlocs"}},{q="What is the Vile Fin Scale for?",a="Apothecary Johaan requires Vile Fin Scales as a vital reagent for formulating the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague. While simple poisons can easily fell an isolated victim, Johaan realizes that engineering a virulent disease capable of spreading across an entire world requires far more complex biological ingredients to ensure proper contagion.",al={"vile fin scale purpose","why vile fin scales","what are the murloc scales for"},it="item",add="2300af12"},{q="Who are the Vile Fin murlocs?",a="The Vile Fin are a tribe of primitive murlocs dwelling along the northern coast and western waters of Tirisfal Glades. Like most of their kind, they aggressively defend their seaside settlements and scavenging grounds against any outsiders who wander near their shores.",al={"vile fin murlocs","who are vile fins","tirisfal murlocs"},it="target",add="0dd4c7ec"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help Apothecary Johaan work on a deadly plague meant to protect your sovereign realm and destroy your foes.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you share a war with the Scourge, and the Forsaken pursue their new plague as a weapon against them."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","murloc","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades","vile fin scale"},rel={"quest:367","npc:apothecary-johaan","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:murloc"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",level="9",faction="Horde",id=368,ri={"Vile Fin Scale"}},src={"A New Plague (2)"}}
E["quest:369"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan studies how an ancient plague survived in spider venom. He seeks a potent new biological agent for the Forsaken.",h="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan studies how an ancient plague survived in spider venom.",sec={{t="Unearthing Ancient Contagions",b="Apothecary Johaan studies old texts in Brill for the Royal Apothecary Society. He finds records of an ancient pestilence that killed thousands. The texts say the pathogen survived across generations in the venom of Tirisfal Glades' local spiders. Johaan needs that venom as a biological reagent.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Venomweb Vale",b="Apothecary Johaan sends agents to eastern Tirisfal Glades for a viable sample. Venomweb Vale lies south of the Scarlet Monastery, where vicious night web spiders infest the hollow. Harvesters must enter their dens and gather fresh venom glands for Johaan's experimental brew.",sp=0},{t="Brewing the Final Formulation",b="Apothecary Johaan adds the harvested venom to a simmering cauldron with reagents gathered earlier. As the mixture boils down, the spiders' contagious element completes the compound. The Royal Apothecary Society moves closer to practical field trials.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want spider venom?",a="An ancient text Johaan found says a plague that killed thousands survived in the venom of Tirisfal's night web spiders. He means to use that contagious element in his concoction.",al={"why spider venom","apothecary johaan spiders","spider venom use"},it="item"},{q="Where do the vicious night web spiders live?",a="Vicious night web spiders live in Venomweb Vale in eastern Tirisfal Glades, south of the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"where are night web spiders","night web spider location","venomweb vale location"},gp=true},{q="What is the goal of the Royal Apothecary Society's research here?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks to create a lethal new strain that can exterminate both the Scourge and the living, securing the Forsaken's survival and independence in Lordaeron.",al={"why make a new plague","forsaken plague goals","royal apothecary society plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Apothecary Johaan is a Forsaken researcher in Brill who works for the Royal Apothecary Society. He oversees local chemical and biological experiments, combining dark alchemy with reagents gathered in Tirisfal.",al={"who is johaan","apothecary johaan lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after this venom is gathered?",a="After boiling the venom into his brew, Johaan prepares to test the compound and see if the resulting toxic agent has the lethality he wants.",al={"what happens next","new plague quest sequel","after a new plague 3"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this the same plague that created the Scourge?",a="No. The Scourge spread the Plague of Undeath, created by the Lich King. The Forsaken's apothecaries are making a distinct biological weapon of their own.",al={"is this scourge plague","plague of undeath difference"}},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan need this venom right now?",a="While consulting his tomes, Apothecary Johaan discovered that an ancient plague which slew thousands of innocents was preserved within the venom of Night Web spiders. He needs this final reagent to test whether its contagious properties can make his concoction truly lethal and infectious.",al={"johaan motive","why does johaan want this done","why gather spider venom"},it="motive",add="25fc540a"},{q="What are Vicious Night Web Spiders and why are they targeted?",a="Vicious Night Web Spiders are deadly arachnids lurking in the eastern reaches of Tirisfal Glades, particularly around Venomweb Vale. Johaan targets them because ancient texts record their venom as naturally carrying and preserving the lethal, virulent properties of a forgotten historical plague.",al={"why vicious night web spiders","what are night web spiders","who are we sent against"},it="target",add="3c54dfe3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you seek an original weapon for lasting security against Scourge remnants and Scarlet crusaders at your doorstep.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may help Forsaken researchers as an orc or tauren ally. Their biological experiments often unsettle the wider Horde."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","night web spider","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades","venom","venomweb vale"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","subzone:brill","subzone:venomweb-vale","zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","quest:367"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",level="11",faction="Horde",id=369,ri={"Vicious Night Web Spider Venom"}},src={"A New Plague (3)"}}
E["quest:370"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, the Forsaken strike at Scarlet Crusade forces threatening their borders. Executor Zygand sends champions after Captain Perrine and his garrison at a ruined tower southwest of Brill, using intelligence taken in Deathknell.",h="In Tirisfal, the Forsaken strike at Scarlet Crusade forces threatening their borders.",sec={{t="Intelligence Put to Use",b="Executor Arren recovered documents from the Scarlet Crusade in Deathknell, revealing troop movements across Tirisfal Glades. Rather than wait for the fanatics to attack newly fortified Brill, Executor Zygand uses the captured intelligence to strike their field commanders first.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at the Ruined Tower",b="Captain Perrine commands Scarlet Zealots and Missionaries from a ruined watchtower southwest of Brill. From there, the Crusade watches Forsaken movements and reaches farther into Tirisfal. Perrine's death matters to the defense of the Dark Lady's young kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Perrine?",a="Captain Perrine is a Scarlet Crusade officer at a ruined watchtower southwest of Brill, where he commands a detachment of Zealots and Missionaries pressing into Tirisfal Glades.",al={"captain perrine","perrine","who is perrine"},it="target"},{q="Where did the Forsaken get information on Captain Perrine?",a="Executor Arren recovered documents from the Crusade during the defense of Deathknell. They detail troop assignments and outpost locations, including Perrine's post.",al={"strategic documents zygand","arren's documents","scarlet documents deathknell"},it="origin"},{q="Why are Scarlet Missionaries and Zealots in Tirisfal?",a="The Scarlet Crusade sees all undead as abominations to be exterminated, whether they serve the Scourge or the Forsaken. Its missionaries and zealots push into Tirisfal to wage holy war and reclaim Lordaeron for the living.",al={"why is scarlet crusade in tirisfal","scarlet missionaries tirisfal","scarlet zealots"},it="why_here"},{q="How does this quest fit into the campaign against the Crusade?",a="This is the second step in the Tirisfal campaign against the Crusade. Perrine's death breaks up a local scouting post before Executor Zygand escalates operations against larger encampments across the glades.",al={"at war with the scarlet crusade chain","what comes next after perrine"},it="conflict"},{q="Can this quest be done together with anything else nearby?",a="Yes. Proof of Demise pairs with it: Deathguard Burgess asks for Scarlet Insignia Rings taken from the same crusaders, as proof of loyalty to Varimathras and the Dark Lady.",al={"proof of demise pairing","quest pairing perrine","brill tower quests"},gp=true},{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is the primary military commander stationed in Brill. He secures Tirisfal Glades and directs strategic offensives for Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"zygand","executor zygand brill"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want Captain Perrine killed?",a="Executor Zygand intends to purge the lands around Brill of what he views as a human infestation. Having analyzed intercepted strategic Crusade documents, he knows Captain Perrine commands a fortified brigade at the ruined tower southwest of town. Striking Perrine and his retinue breaks the Crusade's local command and directly serves the Dark Lady's conquest of Tirisfal.",al={"why kill perrine","zygand motives","why target the scarlet brigade"},it="motive",add="6b0cf47a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, eliminating the Scarlet Crusade is necessary for their survival. The zealots make no distinction between free-willed undead and the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms depends on the Forsaken securing Tirisfal Glades against hostile human zealots."},kw={"brill","captain perrine","executor arren","executor zygand","proof of demise","ruined tower","scarlet crusade","scarlet missionary","scarlet zealot","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:374","subzone:brill","npc:executor-arren","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="9",faction="Horde",id=370},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (2)"}}
E["quest:371"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Zygand sends Forsaken fighters against the Scarlet Crusade near Balnir Farmstead. Their strike targets Captain Vachon and his friars in southeastern Tirisfal Glades, where Crusader raids threaten the Dark Lady's lands.",h="Executor Zygand sends Forsaken fighters against the Scarlet Crusade near Balnir Farmstead.",sec={{t="A Looming Encroachment",b="The Forsaken guard Brill and the Undercity while the Scarlet Crusade holds fortified sites across the countryside. Executor Arren reports active Crusader incursions from a crumbling guard tower in southeastern Tirisfal Glades. The tower stands close to the abandoned Balnir Farmstead.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Chain of Command",b="Executor Zygand targets the Crusade's field leaders, knowing coordinated squads pose a greater danger than scattered zealots. You strike at Captain Vachon and the Scarlet Friars who strengthen his men with holy magic. Without their leadership and support, the cell may lose its cohesion and its raids into Forsaken lands may falter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders this strike?",a="Executor Zygand, stationed in Brill, orders the strike. Executor Arren gathered and delivered the frontline reports on Crusade movements near Balnir Farmstead.",al={"quest giver","who gives this quest","who is zygand"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Captain Vachon located?",a="Captain Vachon and his Scarlet Friars are based in a ruined watchtower in southeastern Tirisfal Glades, just east of Balnir Farmstead.",al={"vachon location","where is vachon","where are scarlet friars"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Executor Zygand target Scarlet Friars specifically?",a="Scarlet Friars give the zealots magical and spiritual support. Defeating these spellcasters takes away defensive wards and healing, crippling the squad's field operations.",al={"why kill friars","scarlet friars"}},{q="What threat does the ruined tower pose to Brill?",a="The ruined tower gives the Scarlet Crusade high ground and a fortified place to launch attacks. Its patrols can ambush Forsaken travelers and disrupt supply roads running east from Brill.",al={"tower threat","why attack tower","balnir tower"},it="threat"},{q="How does this fit into the broader conflict with the Crusade?",a="This strike is the third phase of Executor Zygand's campaign against Scarlet Crusade strongholds in Tirisfal Glades. He aims to drive the zealots back before they can lay siege to the Undercity.",al={"scarlet war chain","war with the scarlet crusade lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Captain Vachon is slain?",a="Captain Vachon's defeat slows Crusader advances in southeastern Tirisfal. Executor Zygand then turns his attention to larger Scarlet Crusade fortifications elsewhere in the region.",al={"next quest","what after vachon","vachon aftermath"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want Captain Vachon and the friars dead?",a="Executor Arren sent word that Scarlet Crusaders have entrenched themselves in the ruined tower near the Balnir Farmstead and are actively staging raids across southeastern Tirisfal. The Scarlet Crusade continues to grow stronger on the glades' borders, threatening Brill and the Dark Lady's broader campaign. By cutting down Captain Vachon and his accompanying friars, Zygand intends to blunt their offensive momentum and deliver a crippling blow to their local command structure before they can push any deeper into Forsaken lands.",al={"why kill captain vachon","zygand motives","why target scarlet tower"},it="motive",add="bf2ccde1"},{q="Who are you being sent against?",a="You are sent to eliminate Captain Vachon and five Scarlet Friars occupying the ruined watchtower overlooking southeastern Tirisfal. Vachon commands this forward raiding force for the Scarlet Crusade, relying on zealot friars for holy support and field leadership. Their presence so close to the Balnir Farmstead grants them an fortified staging ground to disrupt Forsaken travel and harry the Dark Lady's subjects throughout the countryside.",al={"who is captain vachon","who are the scarlet friars","who do i kill"},it="target",add="6cf92196"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you help secure your newborn nation's borders with every Crusader post cleared in Tirisfal Glades. You protect Lady Sylvanas's realm from living purifiers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep the approach to the Undercity open and communication routes through northern Lordaeron secure.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you face Scarlet Friars whose dogmatic faith in holy power clashes with your mastery of the Shadow and distorted Holy power."},kw={"arren","balnir","brill","crusader","friar","tirisfal","tower","vachon","zygand"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:balnir-farmstead","subzone:brill","npc:executor-arren","quest:370","quest:1882","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="10",faction="Horde",id=371},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (3)"}}
E["quest:372"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, Executor Zygand sends Forsaken agents from Brill against the Scarlet Crusade. Captain Melrache and his personal vanguard hold a ruined watchtower past Faol's Rest.",h="In Tirisfal, Executor Zygand sends Forsaken agents from Brill against the Scarlet Crusade.",sec={{t="A Strike at the Vanguard",b="The Forsaken are securing the ruins of Lordaeron while Scarlet Crusade forces keep probing Tirisfal's borders. From a watchtower in northern Tirisfal, past Faol's Rest, crusaders lead raids against Forsaken patrols and lands. Executor Zygand chooses to strike at the officers directing those raids instead of waiting for another attack.",sp=0},{t="Captain Melrache's Hold",b="Captain Melrache commands the northern camp, with two sworn bodyguards always at his side. From the tower, the Scarlet Crusade can watch the coastal roads and nearby woods. Killing Melrache breaks the raiders' coordination near Brill, removes a direct threat to Lady Sylvanas's young kingdom, and drives the zealots back toward their stronger fortifications farther east.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Melrache?",a="Captain Melrache commands a Scarlet Crusade raiding camp at a ruined tower in northern Tirisfal Glades, beyond Faol's Rest. He leads raids into Forsaken lands with his personal bodyguards.",al={"melrache","captain melrache lore","who is the scarlet captain"},it="target"},{q="Where is the ruined tower located?",a="The ruined tower stands in northern Tirisfal Glades, just past the graveyard of Faol's Rest, overlooking the northern coast.",al={"melrache location","where is the tower","faol's rest tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want Melrache dead?",a="Melrache's forces raid from their tower, harassing Forsaken troops and threatening Brill and the Undercity. Zygand orders his death to break the Scarlet Crusade's local offensive.",al={"why kill melrache","zygand's motive"},it="motive"},{q="How does this fight connect to the wider war against Arthas?",a="Executor Zygand sees the Scarlet Crusade as a dangerous distraction. Removing its aggressive officers lets the Forsaken strengthen their hold on Tirisfal and preserve strength for vengeance against the Lich King.",al={"arthas connection","why mention arthas"},it="conflict"},{q="Does slaying Melrache clear the Scarlet Crusade from Tirisfal?",a="No. Melrache's death ends an immediate raiding cell and eases pressure on Brill, but the Scarlet Crusade still holds nearby strongholds, including the Scarlet Monastery to the east.",al={"is scarlet crusade defeated","do they leave tirisfal"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Faol's Rest?",a="Faol's Rest is a secluded burial site in northern Tirisfal. Melrache's tower stands in the rugged hills just beyond it.",al={"faols rest","faol resting place"},it="place"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand send an adventurer rather than his own guards?",a="Brill's standing garrison is already stretched thin guarding the town and maintaining patrols against constant incursions. Striking deep into the northern wilderness past Faol's Rest to breach an enemy-held ruined tower requires surgical assassination rather than a clumsy troop deployment. Zygand relies on capable, independent champions who have already proven their ruthlessness to cut off the enemy command quietly.",al={"why send me","why not use guards","why not royal dreadguard"},it="why_me",add="515f522a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, every crusader you slay is one less fanatic denying your right to live in the homeland where you lived before.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect its vulnerable foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms by securing Tirisfal's perimeter.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you strike behind enemy lines to separate a commander from the forces around him, as Deathstalkers do."},kw={"brill","captain melrache","executor zygand","faol's rest","scarlet bodyguard","scarlet crusade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","subzone:brill","subzone:faol-s-rest","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal","quest:370"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="12",faction="Horde",id=372},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (4)"}}
E["quest:374"] = {t="quest",n="Proof of Demise",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Proof of Demise sends soldiers against the Scarlet Crusade across Tirisfal Glades. Varimathras, Sylvanas Windrunner's dreadlord lieutenant, orders the campaign to thin their ranks and test loyalty to the Forsaken cause. Recruits must take signet rings from fallen crusaders as proof.",h="In Brill, Proof of Demise sends soldiers against the Scarlet Crusade across Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Mandate from the Dreadlord",b="Across northern Tirisfal Glades, the Forsaken wage a coordinated war against the living. Varimathras surrendered and pledged his blade to Sylvanas Windrunner. He oversees many of the Forsaken's aggressive military maneuvers.\n\nHis orders pass to commanders such as Executor Zygand, then to frontline officers like Deathguard Burgess. Burgess makes the order plain: humans are vermin to be purged from Lordaeron, and nearby crusaders are the immediate target.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Slaughter",b="In Brill, words alone do not satisfy the commanders. Soldiers must take Scarlet Insignia Rings from the fingers of slain zealots to prove obedience to the Dark Lady and her lieutenant. The rings bear the Scarlet Crusade's mark, identifying their bearers as sworn enemies of the Forsaken.\n\nBring back these trophies, and the dead crusaders are proved. The rings also show a soldier's allegiance to the Forsaken leadership.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns the task to collect these rings?",a="Deathguard Burgess, a Forsaken guard in Brill, gives the order. He acts on reports from Executor Zygand and follows the military goals set by Varimathras.",al={"who gives proof of demise","quest giver","deathguard burgess quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Burgess demand Scarlet Insignia Rings specifically?",a="Scarlet Insignia Rings provide physical proof that a crusader has been slain. The zealots carry them as personal tokens, making them clear trophies that confirm a soldier's loyalty to Forsaken leadership.",al={"why rings","scarlet rings purpose","what are insignia rings"},it="item"},{q="Who is Varimathras and why is he mentioned?",a="Varimathras is a dreadlord who allied with Queen Sylvanas Windrunner after the Forsaken broke free from the Lich King. He is now her chief lieutenant in the Undercity and directs military strategy against the remaining human enclaves in Lordaeron, including the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"who is varimathras","dreadlord in undercity","why varimathras"},it="leader"},{q="Where are the Scarlet Crusaders located for this task?",a="Scarlet zealots hold several armed camps across Tirisfal Glades. They gather around watchtowers, garrisons, and outposts in the northern and eastern woods.",al={"where to find scarlet crusade","scarlet crusader locations","crusader camps tirisfal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does this connect to Executor Zygand's orders?",a="Executor Zygand oversees the wider campaign against the Scarlet Crusade from Brill. He directs recruits against the crusaders' field presence, while Burgess demands personal trophies as proof of obedience to Varimathras and the Dark Lady.",al={"executor zygand connection","at war with the scarlet crusade link"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Forsaken leadership so hostile to the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade calls all undead abominations destined for holy fire, making no distinction between the mindless Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. Its members hunt the Forsaken along their borders, so Sylvanas and her officers see the crusaders as a dangerous threat that must be annihilated.",al={"why fight scarlet crusade","forsaken vs scarlet crusade","why do forsaken hate humans"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Deathguard Burgess want the Scarlet Crusade killed?",a="Deathguard Burgess serves Varimathras and the Dark Lady directly on the front lines of Brill. In Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Crusade poses an immediate, fanatical threat right on the Undercity's doorstep. Burgess wants their presence eradicated to secure the territory and demands tangible tokens of their defeat to measure your loyalty to the Forsaken cause.",al={"burgess motive","why kill scarlet crusade burgess","why proof of demise"},it="motive",add="ad9b8a55"},{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusaders targeted in this mission?",a="You are sent against the zealous members of the Scarlet Crusade occupying encampments throughout Tirisfal Glades. These fanatical humans view all undead as abominations requiring total eradication, actively waging a campaign to reclaim Lordaeron and wipe out the Forsaken.",al={"who are scarlet crusade target","proof of demise target","who do i kill proof of demise"},it="target",add="a6764d6a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, each crusader ring brought to Brill means one fewer fanatic sworn to cleanse Lordaeron of free-willed undead.",["faction:Horde"]="This task reveals the ruthless, total-war spirit of Sylvanas's northern regime, directed in part by the dreadlord Varimathras."},kw={"brill","dark lady","deathguard burgess","executor zygand","proof of demise","scarlet crusade","scarlet insignia ring","tirisfal glades","varimathras"},rel={"npc:deathguard-burgess","quest:370","npc:executor-zygand","npc:varimathras","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Burgess",level="7",faction="Horde",id=374,ri={"Scarlet Insignia Ring"}},src={"Proof of Demise (quest)"}}
E["quest:375"] = {t="quest",n="The Chill of Death",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, The Chill of Death weighs on Gretchen Dedmar as she fights the cold of undeath. The Forsaken tailor fears losing her mind and her service to Lady Sylvanas, so she asks for materials to sew a warm blanket.",h="In Brill, The Chill of Death weighs on Gretchen Dedmar as she fights the cold of undeath.",sec={{t="A Creeping Frost",b="Gretchen Dedmar feels the Plague of Undeath like an icy serpent moving through her body. The chill drains warmth from her limbs and threatens to leave her mindless, like the wandering corpses in Tirisfal Glades. Her shaking hands make even ordinary work difficult.",sp=0},{t="Service to the Dark Lady",b="Gretchen will not abandon her duty to the Forsaken kingdom. When Sylvanas Windrunner first rallied the liberated dead, Gretchen sewed burial shrouds and body bags for fallen soldiers. Sturdy duskbat pelts and coarse thread can help her make a blanket. Its warmth may steady her hands enough to keep serving the Forsaken cause.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gretchen Dedmar?",a="Gretchen Dedmar is a Forsaken tailor who lives in Brill. She once sewed body bags for Lady Sylvanas's fallen troops.",al={"gretchen dedmar","who is gretchen","brill tailor questgiver"}},{q="What is the 'Mindless State' Gretchen fears?",a="The mindless state is the mental and physical decay that overtakes some undead when their will and necrotic energies fail. They become feral, shambling creatures like those wandering outside Brill and Deathknell.",al={"what is mindless state","why is gretchen losing her mind","forsaken becoming mindless"}},{q="Why does Gretchen feel cold if she is dead?",a="Gretchen feels the plague in her veins as a freezing chill. It stiffens her joints and leaves her hands shaking, though she is undead.",al={"can undead feel cold","why are undead cold","chill of death meaning"}},{q="Why does she need duskbat pelts and thread?",a="Gretchen needs five duskbat pelts and coarse thread to sew a thick blanket. She hopes its warmth will steady her hands so she can keep working.",al={"why duskbat pelts","what is the blanket for"}},{q="Where can duskbats be found?",a="Duskbats roost in the woods and open glades around Brill and northern Tirisfal.",al={"where are duskbats","duskbat pelt location"}},{q="Does this quest connect to any other duties in Brill?",a="Gretchen's need for aid is a concern of her own among Brill's residents. It shows the quiet, personal struggles of the newly liberated Forsaken.",al={"chill of death follow up","gretchen dedmar chain"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, Gretchen's struggle reminds you that freedom from the Lich King does not stop physical rot or the threat of mindlessness.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see how Gretchen's needlework has changed from sewing body bags for Sylvanas's army to making a blanket from pelts."},kw={"brill","chill of death","coarse thread","duskbat pelt","gretchen dedmar","mindless state","plague of undeath","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:plague-of-undeath"},m={level="8",id=375},src={"In-game quest text: The Chill of Death","The Chill of Death (Classic)"},fv=true}
E["quest:376"] = {t="quest",n="The Damned",z="tirisfal",s="New Forsaken in Deathknell turn to Novice Elreth for clothing and battlefield wraps. She trades salvaged armor for the materials needed to make them.",h="New Forsaken in Deathknell turn to Novice Elreth for clothing and battlefield wraps.",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Trade",b="Novice Elreth tends the newly risen Forsaken in Deathknell. She assists Shadow Priest Sarvis, cares for battered soldiers, and mends their garments. Supplies run short, so she sends you into the surrounding glades to hunt duskbats and scavenger wolves. Their pelts, wings, and sinew help keep the camp supplied, and Elreth offers salvaged armor in return.",sp=0},{t="Inherited Protection",b="Elreth's armor has already belonged to Forsaken who did not survive their awakening. She hopes it serves you better than its previous owner. In Tirisfal Glades, every piece of leather and rusted chain is put to use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Novice Elreth?",a="Novice Elreth is an acolyte in Deathknell's chapel and an aide to Shadow Priest Sarvis. She tends wounded Forsaken, mends garments, and equips new arrivals.",al={"novice elreth","who gives the damned quest","elreth"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Elreth need scavenger paws and duskbat wings?",a="Elreth needs scavenger paws and duskbat wings to gather materials for repairs and wraps. Deathknell has little to spare, so she turns to the wildlife in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why bat wings","why scavenger paws","elreth materials"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the armor reward come from?",a="The armor came from Forsaken who did not survive their awakening. Elreth salvages usable gear to protect new arrivals.",al={"where does armor come from","elreth armor origin"},it="item"},{q="Where are the creatures found?",a="Young Scavengers and Duskbats live just south of Deathknell. Tougher ones roam east toward the Scarlet Crusade outpost.",al={"where to find scavengers","where are duskbats","duskbat locations"},gp=true},{q="How does this task fit into the defence of Deathknell?",a="Elreth helps prepare newly risen Forsaken to face nearby threats, including mindless undead and the Scarlet Crusade. Shadow Priest Sarvis expects them to be ready for danger.",al={"why do this quest","deathknell defense"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after helping Novice Elreth?",a="After helping Elreth, you can take on other work around Deathknell: honoring Marla's last wish, dealing with the spiders at Night Web's Hollow, and recovering supplies across the settlement.",al={"next quests after the damned","what comes after the damned"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Novice Elreth need Scavenger Paws and Duskbat Wings?",a="Novice Elreth is tasked with tailoring armor and clothes for Deathknell's defenders, alongside attending to the wounded and aiding Shadow Priest Sarvis. Natural materials like the leather and hides harvested from scavenger paws and duskbat wings serve as essential raw crafting stock. Without fresh supplies, Elreth cannot properly reinforce the ragged garments worn by newly risen Forsaken heading into battle.",al={"what are the scavenger paws for","duskbat wings use","why paws and wings"},it="item",add="9d3a6da0"},{q="Why does Novice Elreth ask you instead of the Deathknell guards?",a="Novice Elreth already carries an overwhelming burden caring for battered soldiers, tailoring supplies, and assisting Shadow Priest Sarvis. Deathknell's established guards cannot abandon their posts while the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade press in. As a newly risen Forsaken facing immediate deployment against the Mindless Ones, gathering your own protective materials serves both the settlement's needs and your own survival.",al={"why me elreth","why doesnt elreth get the paws himself","why not send guards"},it="why_me",add="1b3259f3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For a fresh Forsaken, this shows the hard practicality of survival: fallen predecessors leave gear behind, and the blighted land provides what else is needed.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you see how Forsaken make do in Lordaeron, using wing membranes and scavenged pelts where clean cloth is scarce."},kw={"deathknell","duskbat wing","forsaken","novice elreth","scavenger paw","shadow priest sarvis","the damned","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:novice-elreth","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","subzone:deathknell","quest:363","quest:364","quest:380","quest:3902","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Novice Elreth",level="2",faction="Horde",id=376,ri={"Duskbat Wing","Scavenger Paw"}},src={"The Damned (Classic)"}}
E["quest:380"] = {t="quest",n="Night Web's Hollow",z="tirisfal",s="Northwest of Deathknell, spiders infest a gold mine the Forsaken need. Executor Arren sends newly risen recruits into the cavern to cull the spiders piece by piece. Raw materials are scarce, and the mine's wealth could sustain the Forsaken settlement and war effort.",h="Northwest of Deathknell, spiders infest a gold mine the Forsaken need.",sec={{t="A Nation in Need of Coin",b="Executor Arren oversees operations in Deathknell, where the newly risen Forsaken struggle to survive. They face the Scourge and Scarlet crusaders, but defending themselves is only part of the work. A fledgling society also needs raw materials. Precious metals such as gold were scarce in northern Lordaeron even when the Alliance was strong. Arren knows the Forsaken need wealth to arm and equip themselves and establish their society.",sp=0},{t="The Infested Mine",b="A natural cavern called Night Web's Hollow lies northwest of Deathknell's cemetery, with a gold vein running through it. Monstrous spiders have overrun its tunnels, leaving thick webs and deadly venom in their depths. Arren has too few seasoned troops for a full purge, so fresh recruits thin the young and adult spiders. Once the danger is reduced, mining crews can burn away the webs and extract the ore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the undead need a gold mine?",a="The Forsaken need gold to fund their war effort, buy supplies, and rebuild settlements across Tirisfal Glades. Lordaeron has always lacked natural resources, and a new realm independent of both the Alliance and the Scourge needs valuable currency to trade and procure equipment.",al={"why do forsaken need gold","why gold in deathknell","undead gold mine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Executor Arren?",a="Executor Arren is Deathknell's ranking military authority. He organizes the newly risen undead and secures the immediate perimeter, directing recruits to hunt Scourge remnants, gather supplies, and open local resources.",al={"executor arren lore","who gives night webs hollow","arren role"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Night Web's Hollow located?",a="Night Web's Hollow lies northwest of Deathknell's main settlement and graveyard, among rocky bluffs in a secluded valley in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is night webs hollow","spider cave deathknell","night web mine location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are the Forsaken able to mine the gold immediately after this quest?",a="Not right away. Arren says eradicating the spiders will take weeks or months of sustained effort. Then crews must use torches to burn away the pervasive webs before miners can safely excavate the veins.",al={"is the mine cleared","do they get the gold","what happens to the spiders"},it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't Arren send a full detachment of soldiers to clear the cave?",a="Deathknell's garrison is stretched thin guarding against mindless Scourge prowling the outskirts and watching for Scarlet Crusade scouts. Arren lacks spare manpower to assign a regular squad to pest control, so newly risen recruits clear the mine bit by bit.",al={"why send recruits","why not use deathknell guards","arren lack of manpower"},it="why_me"},{q="Can spider venom harm the undead?",a="Caustic spider venom can burn preserved flesh and weaken reanimated limbs, even though the Forsaken do not bleed or breathe like the living. Arren warns recruits to watch for a sharp burning sensation and seek treatment if afflicted.",al={"does venom hurt undead","forsaken spider poison","are forsaken immune to poison"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Executor Arren want Night Web's Hollow cleared?",a="Deathknell and the nascent Forsaken war effort desperately need natural resources to survive and fortify their lands. Gold was scarce in Tirisfal Glades even at the height of the old Alliance's reign, making the local mine in the hollow an indispensable asset. However, the spiders nesting within make excavation impossible. Arren wants the infestation culled so the Forsaken can eventually secure and harvest the precious metal.",al={"why does arren want this done","why clear night webs hollow","executor arren motive"},it="motive",add="9452aa4f"},{q="What are the Night Web spiders infesting the mine?",a="The target of your mission is the brood of Night Web spiders and their young that have overrun the old gold mine. In the wake of Lordaeron's fall and the plague's blight, predatory wildlife expanded aggressively into abandoned mortal settlements and subterranean caves. The spiders have aggressively nested in the mine tunnels, stringing webs and driving out any miners seeking to tap into the vein.",al={"what are night web spiders","who are we sent against","why are spiders in night webs hollow"},it="target",add="a97ddab4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you face a harsh reality in reclaimed Lordaeron: survival means securing ordinary needs like metal and coin, not just seeking vengeance against the living and the Scourge.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know thick webs and predatory spiders make prospecting perilous in this cavern, one of Deathknell's few nearby sources of gold ore.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know secured resources in Tirisfal Glades help establish the Forsaken as a reliable northern stronghold."},kw={"deathknell","executor arren","forsaken","gold mine","night web spider","night web's hollow","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","npc:executor-arren","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance"},m={start="Executor Arren",level="4",faction="Horde",id=380},src={"Night Web's Hollow (Classic)"}}
E["quest:381"] = {t="quest",n="The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, Deathknell faces a Scarlet Crusade camp southeast of the settlement. Executor Arren sends the newly awakened Forsaken to ambush its zealots, one of their most fanatical and persistent enemies.",h="In Tirisfal, Deathknell faces a Scarlet Crusade camp southeast of the settlement.",sec={{t="A Fanatical Threat",b="After the Night Web spiders are dealt with, Executor Arren turns Deathknell toward a threat drawing near. A detachment of the Scarlet Crusade has made a foothold just southeast of the settlement. Its zealots see no difference between mindless Scourge and free-willed Forsaken. Their presence on Deathknell's border threatens the newly risen dead.",sp=0},{t="Preemptive Retaliation",b="Executor Arren orders a strike before the camp can grow into an organized attack on Deathknell. You cut down Scarlet Converts and Scarlet Initiates, then bring back their crimson armbands as proof. The holy fanatics see all dead flesh as an abomination, leaving the Forsaken to claim survival by force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a religious movement bent on exterminating the undead. Grief and religious zeal after Lordaeron's fall drove its members mad. They see no difference between mindless Scourge and self-aware Forsaken, and seek to purge both.",al={"scarlet crusade lore","what is the scarlet crusade","scarlet zealots"},it="people"},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade camping near Deathknell?",a="Deathknell is where new Forsaken are raised and gathered. The Scarlet Crusade has set up a small outpost to survey the area, catch newly risen undead unawares, and gather forces against the young settlement.",al={"why are scarlets in deathknell","scarlet camp deathknell"},it="why_here"},{q="Why do the Forsaken strike first rather than talk?",a="Executor Arren says the Crusaders are blinded by zeal and see all undead as abominations to be wiped out. They will not reason or negotiate with the dead, so the Forsaken strike first to defend themselves.",al={"can forsaken negotiate with scarlet crusade","why attack scarlets"},it="conflict"},{q="What rank are the Crusaders found in this camp?",a="The camp is staffed largely by recruits and trainees: Scarlet Converts and Scarlet Initiates. Though low in the Crusade's ranks, their fervor makes them dangerous to newly risen Forsaken.",al={"who is in the camp","scarlet converts initiates"},it="target"},{q="What does completing this mission lead to?",a="Executor Arren's superiors in Brill report that a Crusade messenger has come from the Scarlet Monastery to the camp. Arren sends you to intercept The Red Messenger and uncover their battle plans.",al={"what quest comes after","quest chain after scarlet crusade"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Executor Arren?",a="Executor Arren commands Deathknell's military and oversees its defense. He directs freshly awakened Forsaken against threats nearby.",al={"arren role","who gives the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Executor Arren want the Scarlet Crusade camp eliminated?",a="Deathknell is the fragile cradle of the newly awakened Forsaken, and having a hostile human outpost right on its doorstep poses an immediate survival threat. The Scarlet Crusade refuses to distinguish between the mind-controlled Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken, sworn to obliterate any undead they encounter. With the mine recently secured, Executor Arren insists on striking preemptively before this detachment can gather strength or launch an assault on the settlement.",al={"arren motive","why kill scarlet crusade","why attack scarlet camp"},it="motive",add="e81ecc24"},{q="What is the Scarlet Armband for?",a="The Scarlet Armbands serve as undeniable physical proof that you routed the camp and decimated their ranks. Each armlet is stripped from the fallen zealots—Converts and Initiates who wear their vibrant red colors with blinding fanaticism. Bringing twelve of them back confirms to Executor Arren that the immediate encroachment near Deathknell has been crushed.",al={"scarlet armband use","why collect armbands","scarlet armband"},it="item",add="d772c2c9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly arisen Forsaken, you learn early that the living see you as a monster to be exterminated, whatever your free will.",["faction:Horde"]="The Scarlet Crusade's relentless aggression helps explain why the Forsaken sought the Horde's mutual defense and protection.",["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you face how the Holy Light you once revered in Lordaeron has been twisted into fanatical hatred."},kw={"deathknell","executor arren","scarlet armbands","scarlet converts","scarlet crusade","scarlet initiates","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:executor-arren","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:deathknell","quest:382","quest:380","quest:383","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Executor Arren",level="4",faction="Horde",id=381,ri={"Scarlet Armband"}},src={"The Scarlet Crusade (quest)"}}
E["quest:382"] = {t="quest",n="The Red Messenger",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Arren sends you after a courier bound for the camp outside Deathknell. Dispatched from the Scarlet Monastery, the courier carries word from the crusade to its camp. Intercepting him secures intelligence before the zealots can strengthen their hold in the valley. This is among the Forsaken's first offensive efforts to secure their fledgling sanctuary.",h="Executor Arren sends you after a courier bound for the camp outside Deathknell.",sec={{t="Eyes in the East",b="Word of the Scarlet courier reaches Executor Arren through his superiors in Brill. The Scarlet Crusade sent an emissary west from its stronghold at the Scarlet Monastery to Deathknell. Crusaders press across Lordaeron, and a courier sent to the edge of the Forsaken's waking grounds signals an organized effort to destroy the newly risen before they can prepare a defense.",sp=0},{t="Intercepting the Courier",b="Meven Korgal, the courier, blended into the small Scarlet camp east of Deathknell without distinctive heraldry. Executor Arren orders a targeted strike to kill Korgal and seize his dispatch. Taking the missives cuts off the local zealots from further tactical coordination with their eastern headquarters.",sp=0},{t="Vital Dispatches",b="The recovered Scarlet Crusade Documents contain propaganda, scouting notes, and direct orders for the zealots to expand their camp near the ruined capital. They also hold a strategic map marking field commanders and agents throughout the glades. The map is valuable enough to warrant immediate delivery to higher authorities in Brill.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Red Messenger?",a="Meven Korgal is a human courier serving the Scarlet Crusade. He was sent from the Scarlet Monastery to carry strategic orders to the zealots near Deathknell.",al={"meven korgal","who is meven korgal","who is the messenger","scarlet messenger identity"},it="target"},{q="Where did the messenger come from?",a="The messenger came from the Scarlet Monastery, the Scarlet Crusade's massive fortified headquarters in northeastern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where did korgal come from","messenger origin","scarlet courier source"},it="origin"},{q="What information was found in the documents?",a="The dispatches hold scouting summaries, orders to build up Crusader fortifications near Lordaeron's ruined city, and a strategic map showing the positions of Crusade field commanders and agents.",al={"scarlet documents contents","what are the orders","what was korgal carrying"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Where does this intelligence go next?",a="Executor Arren immediately forwards the map and gathered intelligence to his superiors in Brill. It gives the wider Forsaken military actionable targets across Tirisfal.",al={"what happens to the documents","where to deliver scarlet papers","vital intelligence quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade encroaching so close to Deathknell?",a="The Scarlet Crusade seeks to eradicate all undead abominations without distinction. Deathknell is where newly freed undead first rise from their graves, making it a target for zealots trying to destroy the Forsaken before they organize.",al={"why are scarlets in deathknell","crusade in deathknell","why are zealots here"},it="conflict"},{q="Who gave Executor Arren the tip about the messenger?",a="Forsaken command in Brill intercepted news of the courier's departure from the monastery and passed it to Arren, so his local forces could intercept him.",al={"who warned arren","who sent report to arren","how did forsaken know"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Executor Arren want this done?",a="Deathknell is the Forsaken's fledgling sanctuary, and the Scarlet Crusade has brazenly pitched camp right at its threshold. Word from Arren's superiors in Brill warned that an enemy courier slipped in directly from the Scarlet Monastery with critical correspondence. Intercepting those dispatches allows the Forsaken to anticipate Crusade movements, blunting the zealots' assault before their foothold can choke Deathknell completely.",al={"arren motive","why kill the messenger","why does arren want scarlet documents"},it="motive",add="266afb7b"},{q="Why does Executor Arren send you instead of his guards?",a="Deathknell's garrison is stretched thin simply holding the line against Scourge remnants, prowling beasts, and aggressive Scarlet patrols surrounding the haven. Having already proved your mettle by thinning the crusaders at their camp, Executor Arren considers you the most capable operative at hand to slip past their perimeter and strike down the courier.",al={"why send me red messenger","why not use deathknell guards","why me arren"},it="why_me",add="f56377a4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Intercepting the messenger strikes at zealots who seek to kill you again before you have found your footing in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a new Horde recruit, you help break Scarlet operations along the northern perimeter of the Horde's newly established foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Rogue"]="As a newly awakened rogue, you take on covert work by infiltrating the Crusade's camp, killing Meven Korgal, and stealing his dispatches."},kw={"brill","deathknell","executor arren","meven korgal","red messenger","scarlet crusade","scarlet documents","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:381","quest:383","quest:380","npc:executor-arren","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Arren",level="5",faction="Horde",id=382,ri={"Scarlet Crusade Documents"}},src={"The Red Messenger"}}
E["quest:383"] = {t="quest",n="Vital Intelligence",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, a new Forsaken carries captured Scarlet Crusade documents from Deathknell to Brill. Executor Zygand awaits the courier there.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, a new Forsaken carries captured Scarlet Crusade documents from Deathknell to Brill.",sec={{t="Leaving Deathknell",b="Executor Arren sends you from Deathknell with captured Scarlet Crusade documents. You have dealt with local threats and intercepted a Scarlet Crusade courier, and are ready for wider service. Leave through Deathknell's sheltered canyon and follow the road east toward Brill, passing Cold Hearth Manor.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Strike",b="In Brill, Executor Zygand studies the captured correspondence. It names active Scarlet Crusade commanders across Tirisfal Glades and lists their assignments. Zygand plans targeted killings to break the zealots' leadership and morale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What information is inside the Scarlet Crusade Documents?",a="The captured documents name Scarlet Crusade officers stationed across Tirisfal Glades and list their assignments. Executor Zygand plans swift strikes to eliminate the local leadership and demoralize the Crusade.",al={"what are the scarlet documents","scarlet crusade documents contents","what intelligence was gathered"},it="item"},{q="Where is Executor Zygand located?",a="Executor Zygand is in Brill, just outside Brill Town Hall beside the town's main square.",al={"where is zygand","find executor zygand","executor zygand location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do I get to Brill from Deathknell?",a="Follow the road north out of Deathknell. At the fork into greater Tirisfal Glades, take the eastern path past Cold Hearth Manor, then cross the covered bridge into Brill.",al={"path to brill","how to get to brill","directions to brill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does this quest signal the end of Deathknell?",a="Deathknell is the first proving ground for newly awakened Forsaken. After you help secure the hamlet and gather useful intelligence on the Scarlet Crusade, Executor Arren sends you to higher-ranking commanders in Brill.",al={"done with deathknell","why leave deathknell","is this the last deathknell quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Executor Arren?",a="Executor Arren is the Forsaken officer who oversees operations, security, and the first integration of newly risen undead in Deathknell.",al={"who is arren","arren lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after turning in these documents?",a="Delivering the documents brings you into the wider Forsaken military effort based in Brill. From there, assignments across Tirisfal Glades target local Scarlet Crusade encampments and Scourge remnants.",al={"what comes next","next quest after vital intelligence"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Executor Arren want the documents delivered to Brill?",a="Executor Arren knows that the recovered documents contain crucial intelligence on Scarlet Crusade leadership in Tirisfal Glades. Deathknell is merely a staging ground for the newly risen, so tactical decisions on a regional scale fall to his superior, Executor Zygand in Brill. Arren wants the papers in Zygand's hands immediately so the Forsaken military command can coordinate a decisive, morale-shattering strike against the zealots.",al={"why deliver documents to zygand","executor arren motive","why send documents to brill"},it="motive",add="f3a0a7d2"},{q="Why does Executor Arren send you instead of his own deathguards?",a="Deathknell is constantly besieged by Mindless Ones, Scourge remnants, and Scarlet zealots, leaving Executor Arren unable to spare his deathguards from their defense posts. You, on the other hand, have already proven your competence by intercepting the Scarlet messenger and securing the intelligence. Arren recognizes that you have outgrown the sheltered valley of Deathknell and sees this mission as both an essential courier run and an introduction to the wider Forsaken war effort under Executor Zygand.",al={"why send me to zygand","why not use guards to deliver documents","why does arren trust me"},it="why_me",add="5664ce4f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, carrying these intercepted plans marks your passage from Deathknell into the wider war for Lordaeron. You have proven yourself after rising from the grave.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help the Forsaken strengthen their hold on Tirisfal Glades and guard the northern gateway to the Undercity from Scarlet Crusade incursions."},kw={"brill","cold hearth manor","deathknell","documents","executor arren","executor zygand","scarlet crusade","tirisfal glades","vital intelligence"},rel={"quest:382","npc:executor-arren","npc:executor-zygand","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:cold-hearth-manor","quest:5481"},m={start="Executor Arren",["end"]="Executor Zygand",level="5",faction="Horde",id=383},src={"Vital Intelligence (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3901"] = {t="quest",n="Rattling the Rattlecages",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, newly awakened Forsaken face a test against the Rattlecage Skeletons. Shadow Priest Sarvis sends them to destroy twelve skeletons and prove they can defend their hard-won freedom.",h="In Deathknell, newly awakened Forsaken face a test against the Rattlecage Skeletons.",sec={{t="A Test of Resolve",b="Newly risen Forsaken face a harder trial after culling the mindless zombies in Deathknell. Shadow Priest Sarvis sends recruits against the Rattlecage Skeletons roaming the settlement’s outskirts. The animated bones have no sapience or self-control, yet strike harder and fight more fiercely than the nearby decaying corpses. Surviving their clattering ambushes shows Sarvis that a recruit can withstand immediate pressure.",sp=0},{t="Defending Newly Won Freedom",b="Destroying the skeletons protects Deathknell from the lingering grip of the Lich King and tests which recruits can endure the fight. Those who fail or hesitate risk becoming like the mindless wretches wandering the woods. Overcoming the Rattlecages proves to Sarvis that you have the mettle to face a world that despises your existence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Rattlecage Skeletons?",a="Rattlecage Skeletons are mindless undead still held by the Lich King. Stripped of flesh and cognitive will, they roam Deathknell’s edges and attack anyone who crosses their path.",al={"rattlecages","what are rattlecage skeletons","who are the skeletons"},it="target"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Sarvis want the skeletons destroyed?",a="Sarvis tests newly awakened Forsaken for combat skill and willpower under pressure. Thinning the aggressive skeletons also helps keep Deathknell from being overwhelmed by the Scourge.",al={"why kill skeletons","sarvis purpose","reason for rattling rattlecages"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Rattlecage Skeletons found?",a="Rattlecage Skeletons roam the northern and northeastern borders of the Deathknell valley, just beyond the village where mindless zombies wander.",al={"rattlecage location","where to find rattlecage skeletons","skeleton spawns deathknell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Sarvis considers your initial training complete and declares you have proven worthy of your freedom. He sends you to other leaders in Deathknell to aid the Forsaken’s broader operations.",al={"next quest after rattling rattlecages","what to do after","sarvis next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are some undead free while these skeletons remain mindless?",a="After the Lich King’s telepathic hold wavered following the Third War, some undead broke free, reclaimed their sentience, and formed the Forsaken. Constructs and simple animated bones like the Rattlecages kept no personality or will and remained bound to the Scourge.",al={"why are skeletons mindless","forsaken vs scourge free will","how did forsaken wake up"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis oversees the Forsaken in Deathknell’s chapel. He evaluates newly raised undead, guides them through their awakening, and makes sure they are strong enough to survive as free beings.",al={"who is sarvis","sarvis lore","shadow priest sarvis role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Sarvis send you instead of the Deathknell guards?",a="Sarvis is testing your mettle and fitness to serve Lady Sylvanas. Deathknell's established protectors are already occupied guarding the settlement's perimeter against the relentless Scourge. As a newly awakened Forsaken, you must prove you possess the focus and martial resolve to handle dangerous foes before you are granted leave to venture into the wider kingdom.",al={"why me sarvis","why not use the guards","why does sarvis test you"},it="why_me",add="421a2867"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, the Rattlecages show what awaits if your mind slips. Their mindless servitude stands against your hard-won autonomy.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help temper new Forsaken soldiers into fighters who can defend their fledgling faction and secure Tirisfal Glades.",["class:Priest"]="As a newly risen Priest, working for Shadow Priest Sarvis gives you an early glimpse of the ruthless pragmatism that shapes the Forsaken’s spiritual path."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken","rattlecage","sarvis","scourge","skeletons","tirisfal","undead"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","quest:364","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Shadow Priest Sarvis",level="3",faction="Horde",id=3901},src={"Rattling the Rattlecages"}}
E["quest:3902"] = {t="quest",n="Scavenging Deathknell",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, newly awakened Forsaken gather supplies for the recruits rising from nearby graves. Deathguard Saltain sends them to search the blighted settlement for abandoned boxes and crates, where the Forsaken must find what they need to survive.",h="In Deathknell, newly awakened Forsaken gather supplies for the recruits rising from nearby graves.",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Resurrection",b="Newly raised Forsaken wake in Deathknell with little to call their own. Deathguard Saltain sends them to gather what the recruits still climbing from their graves need: clothing and arms. The Forsaken must salvage supplies to outfit those newly risen, with every usable piece put to work.",sp=0},{t="Scraping by in Tirisfal",b="Deathknell holds remnants of its former human inhabitants and supplies abandoned during the kingdom’s fall to the Scourge. Deathguards send newly awakened Forsaken to recover usable goods from boxes and crates scattered through the town. The Forsaken expect no charity from the living and must depend on their own effort to survive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Deathguard Saltain need scavenged goods?",a="Deathguard Saltain gathers equipment for newly awakened Forsaken rising in the nearby cemetery. Scavenged clothing, boots, and tools help keep fresh recruits from wandering the blighted hills unarmed and defenseless.",al={"why scavenge goods","saltain purpose","why look for boxes"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the scavenged goods found?",a="The goods lie in stacks of boxes and crates throughout Deathknell, near abandoned buildings and quiet corners of the settlement.",al={"where are boxes","scavenged goods locations","deathknell boxes"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Deathguard Saltain?",a="Saltain is a Deathguard stationed in Deathknell who evaluates fresh undead recruits and puts them to work. He enforces order and survival through harsh discipline.",al={"who is saltain","deathguard saltain lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why don't the Forsaken have standard military supplies here?",a="The Forsaken are a young, beleaguered people facing hostile living enemies and mind-controlled Scourge. With resources stretched thin in Deathknell, they reclaim and reuse what was left in the ruins.",al={"why no gear","forsaken supply shortage","deathknell equipment"},it="history"},{q="What happens after completing this task?",a="Saltain gives the recruit a piece of salvaged armor from the communal stockpile. It marks the recruit’s passage from an unproven corpse to a functional soldier of the Dark Lady.",al={"next quest","scavenging reward"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are so many new undead rising in Deathknell right now?",a="As the Lich King’s grip on his servants weakens, some of Lordaeron’s dead break free with their minds intact. Confused, they rise from their graves and need immediate guidance.",al={"why rising","new recruits deathknell","why fresh undead"},it="threat"},{q="What are the Scavenged Goods used for?",a="The scavenged goods are recovered equipment and supplies meant to outfit newly awakened Forsaken recruits rising in Deathknell. With supplies scarce and no outside aid, the Forsaken must salvage whatever discarded gear they can find to ensure new soldiers are clothed and armed.",al={"what are scavenged goods for","scavenged goods use","why gather scavenged goods"},it="item",add="e568b68b"},{q="Why does Deathguard Saltain need recruits to scavenge instead of doing it himself?",a="Deathguard Saltain and the other seasoned guards are tasked with holding Deathknell's perimeter and managing the flow of newly risen undead. Scavenging the ruined settlement is low-risk labor, serving both as a practical way to gather supplies and a test to see if fresh recruits are capable of following orders.",al={"why does saltain need me","why send recruits to scavenge","why not have deathguards scavenge"},it="why_me",add="aa140ef7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you learn the hard terms of your new life: no one in Azeroth offers pity or charity, so the Forsaken must salvage their future from the dirt.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken are allied with the Horde across the sea, yet outposts like Deathknell must meet daily needs through desperate local scavenging rather than foreign aid."},kw={"deathguard saltain","deathknell","forsaken supplies","scavenged goods","scavenging deathknell","tirisfal glades","undead starter quest"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Deathguard Saltain",level="3",faction="Horde",id=3902,ri={"Scavenged Goods"}},src={"Scavenging Deathknell"}}
E["quest:398"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted: Maggot Eye",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, the Forsaken leadership has posted a death bounty for Maggot Eye. The notorious gnoll robs nearby graveyards and farms, supplying bodies to the Lich King's Scourge. Executor Zygand demands proof of the kill to secure the lands around Garren's Haunt.",h="In Brill, the Forsaken leadership has posted a death bounty for Maggot Eye.",sec={{t="A Grave Crime",b="In Tirisfal Glades, the dead do not rest in peace. Maggot Eye faces a severe death sentence for aiding the Lich King. Gnolls are usually seen as savage brutes driven by hunger, but Maggot Eye digs up corpses and gathers remains to strengthen the Scourge army.",sp=0},{t="Justice in Brill",b="The Forsaken fight to break free of the Lich King's control, so feeding their dead kin to the Scourge is among the gravest offenses. Executor Zygand oversees local military enforcement in Brill and ordered the bounty to end the grave robberies near Garren's Haunt. To claim the prize, you need Maggot Eye's paw as proof that the beast can trouble Tirisfal no longer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Maggot Eye?",a="Maggot Eye is an infamous gnoll prowling northern Tirisfal Glades. He raids farms near Garren's Haunt and gathers corpses for the Scourge, making him vile even among his kind.",al={"maggot eye lore","who is maggot eye","maggot eye gnoll"},it="target"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want him dead?",a="The Forsaken sentenced Maggot Eye to death for supplying looted corpses to the Lich King's Scourge army. Keeping soldiers and resources from the Scourge is vital to Forsaken survival.",al={"why kill maggot eye","maggot eye crimes","why bounty maggot eye"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Maggot Eye usually found?",a="Maggot Eye lurks in an old ruined hut at Garren's Haunt, a ruined farmstead north of Brill.",al={"maggot eye location","where is maggot eye","find maggot eye"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who pays the reward for the bounty?",a="Executor Zygand, in the center of Brill, accepts proof of the kill and pays the town's reward on behalf of the Forsaken military authority.",al={"who turns in maggot eye","maggot eye quest turn in","brill bounty rewarder"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want his paw?",a="Executor Zygand wants Maggot Eye's paw as unmistakable proof of death before the bounty is paid.",al={"why maggot eye paw","paw proof","maggot eyes paw"},it="item"},{q="Are gnolls allied with the Scourge?",a="Gnolls generally act on their own out of hunger and greed, but Maggot Eye supplies dead bodies to the Scourge, making him a dangerous collaborator.",al={"gnolls and scourge","do gnolls work for lich king","scourge gnolls"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Brill need an adventurer to deal with Maggot Eye?",a="The Forsaken in Brill have their hands full maintaining order and defending against active Scourge incursions and Scarlet Crusade threats across Tirisfal Glades. Rather than stretching their town guard thin by sending soldiers out to track down rogue scavengers, Executor Zygand and the town leadership post public bounties. Calling upon capable travelers and rising champions allows Brill to eliminate regional threats without weakening its local garrison.",al={"why me maggot eye","why don't guards kill maggot eye","why hire adventurer maggot eye"},it="why_me",add="aae6cd91"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know every corpse Maggot Eye steals is a fallen sibling enslaved again by the Lich King. Stopping him defends the Forsaken and answers a personal wrong.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you need Tirisfal's northern borders secure to hold Lordaeron against Scourge remnants."},kw={"bounty","brill","executor zygand","garren's haunt","gnoll","graverobber","lich king","maggot eye","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:garren-s-haunt","npc:executor-zygand","subzone:brill","quest:358","topic:gnoll","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Wanted!",["end"]="Executor Zygand",level="10",faction="Horde",id=398,ri={"Maggot Eye's Paw"}},src={"Wanted: Maggot Eye"}}
E["quest:404"] = {t="quest",n="A Putrid Task",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Dillinger sends you west from Brill to hold the old bridge against the Scourge. Bring back proof that the dead are destroyed, and Tirisfal's defenders can keep the road clear.",h="Deathguard Dillinger sends you west from Brill to hold the old bridge against the Scourge.",sec={{t="Holding the Bridge",b="Brill guards a crossroads in eastern Tirisfal Glades, where an enemy approach threatens the Forsaken stronghold. Scourge wander west across the waterways and gather around the broken old stone bridge. Without patrols to drive them back, the shambling dead could block travel between Brill and the western farmsteads.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Against the Mindless",b="For the Forsaken, Scourge on their borders are more than a threat to defend against. Each mindless ghoul and rotting corpse recalls the servitude and torment they escaped under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Deathguards like Dillinger take grim satisfaction in crushing their former captors. They demand severed claws as proof that the mindless dead have been put to rest for good.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Deathguard Dillinger, an officer of the Forsaken guard, gives the order from Brill's western exit in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"quest giver","where to get putrid task","deathguard dillinger quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger want putrid claws?",a="The claws prove the wandering Scourge have been destroyed, not merely driven away from the main road.",al={"why putrid claws","claws reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the rotting dead found?",a="The rotting dead wander the overgrown fields and riverbanks just west of Brill, gathering around the old stone bridge.",al={"rotting dead location","where are the ghouls","old bridge location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there Scourge in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Forsaken took Lordaeron's capital and the surrounding glades from the Scourge, but Scourge have trickled into Tirisfal Glades and infested the land west of Brill near the old bridge.",al={"why scourge here","scourge in tirisfal"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after completing this task?",a="Once the bridge is clear, trouble on nearby farmsteads sends you farther west to inspect the overrun mills.",al={"next quest","what follows putrid task"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are the Forsaken and the Scourge not the same thing?",a="No. The Forsaken are free-willed undead who broke the Lich King's telepathic control and fight to protect their freedom. The Scourge remain mindless thralls bound to the Iron Will of the Frozen Throne.",al={"difference between forsaken and scourge","aren't they all undead"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger want this done?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is charged with defending Brill and securing the surrounding approaches for the Forsaken. Mindless Scourge have trickled into Tirisfal Glades and gathered around the old bridge just west of town. Left unchecked, these shambling corpses threaten travelers along the road and test the settlement's outer perimeters, making their destruction an urgent matter of regional defense.",al={"dillinger motive","why kill rotting dead","why clear the scourge near brill"},it="motive",add="63865879"},{q="Who are you sent against at the old bridge?",a="You are sent against the rotting dead and ravaged corpses infesting the area near the old bridge west of Brill. Unlike the Forsaken, who broke free from the Lich King's grasp to reclaim their free will, these creatures are mindless remnants of the Scourge plague wandering the glades and attacking anyone who crosses their path.",al={"rotting dead target","ravaged corpses old bridge","who are the scourge near brill"},it="target",add="53a3556c"},{q="Why does Dillinger need you instead of the town guard?",a="The Deathguards stationed in Brill are bound to their watch posts, guarding the village gates, outbuildings, and supply lines against sudden incursions. With Scourge roaming the western roads and hostile forces pressing elsewhere, Dillinger cannot abandon his post to patrol the bridge, requiring able-bodied recruits to hunt down the invaders in the field.",al={"why send me dillinger","why dont guards kill the scourge","why cant dillinger do it"},it="why_me",add="c7fe240d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, destroying the Scourge is personal vengeance against the force that once held your mind captive.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Brill and protect its foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms from the Scourge."},kw={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard dillinger","putrid claw","ravaged corpse","rotting dead","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",level="6",faction="Horde",id=404,ri={"Putrid Claw"}},src={"A Putrid Task (Classic)"}}
E["quest:407"] = {t="quest",n="Fields of Grief",z="tirisfal",s="Apothecary Johaan tests his pumpkin weapon in Brill. He has laced pumpkins from Solliden Farmstead with his latest alchemical concoction and sends you to feed one to a captive Scarlet Crusader.",h="Apothecary Johaan tests his pumpkin weapon in Brill.",sec={{t="A Weapon of Ingenuity",b="Apothecary Johaan believes the Forsaken must use every advantage against the Scourge to the north and human incursions to the south. The Royal Apothecary Society looks beyond blades and dark sorcery, seeking weapons in the ordinary produce of the land. Johaan has tainted pumpkins gathered from the mortal farmers at Solliden Farmstead. He means to prove common crops can be made deadly in service of the Dark Lady.",sp=0},{t="The Cellar Test",b="Beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, a captive Scarlet Zealot waits in chains. Starvation has weakened the prisoner, but the zealot still defies the Forsaken and calls on the Holy Light to purge the undead. When offered a pumpkin, the captive mistakes it for food and devours it. Johaan's formula quickly warps the zealot into a rotting ghoul, who collapses lifeless in the dirt.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan use a pumpkin for his poison?",a="Johaan wants to prove ordinary crops can become weapons against the living. The Royal Apothecary Society laces produce from nearby human farms with alchemical mixtures, turning mortal foes' need for food against them.",al={"why a pumpkin","why poison pumpkin","laced pumpkin lore"},it="item"},{q="Who is the prisoner in the tavern cellar?",a="The prisoner is a Captured Scarlet Zealot, a Scarlet Crusade fanatic taken by Forsaken forces in Tirisfal Glades. Starvation and isolation have weakened the zealot, but religious fervor remains until food appears.",al={"who is captured zealot","zealot in gallows end","brill cellar prisoner"},it="target"},{q="What happens to the Scarlet Zealot after eating the pumpkin?",a="Johaan's formula takes hold almost at once, deforming the starving zealot into a rotting ghoul who collapses lifeless in the dirt.",al={"what happens to zealot","zealot transformation","does zealot turn into ghoul"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is the Gallows' End Tavern cellar?",a="The cellar lies beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. A ramp behind the front counter leads to the holding area where Forsaken guards keep prisoners.",al={"how to find cellar","where is zealot located","gallows end cellar entrance"},gp=true},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to achieve here?",a="Under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Royal Apothecary Society develops biological and alchemical agents to destroy the Scourge and mortal threats such as the Scarlet Crusade. Its small experiments on captives in Brill test these concoctions.",al={"apothecary society goal","why test plague","royal apothecary society tirisfal"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade active in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Scarlet Crusade sees all undead as abominations to be exterminated, whether mindless Scourge or free-willed Forsaken. Its camps and garrisons across the former kingdom of Lordaeron seek to reclaim the land by holy fire.",al={"scarlet crusade tirisfal","why are scarlets here","crusade presence brill"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want this done?",a="Apothecary Johaan views the Forsaken's condition of undeath as a potent weapon against their enemies. Caught between the Scourge marching from the north and human forces encroaching from the south, the Forsaken need ruthless methods to survive. By delivering a lethal, chemically altered pumpkin to a captured enemy, Johaan aims to field-test his latest concoction and prove that even mundane farm produce can be weaponized in service of the Dark Lady.",al={"johaan motive","why does johaan want the pumpkin delivered","why test the pumpkin"},it="motive",add="5c6a869b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you as Forsaken, this experiment shows the ruthless measures your people take to survive, with mortal zealots to the south and the Lich King's armies to the north.",["faction:Horde"]="For you in the Horde, the Royal Apothecary Society's biochemical research can unsettle the Forsaken's new allies, yet it remains central to securing Tirisfal Glades for the Horde."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","captured scarlet zealot","fields of grief","gallows end tavern","laced pumpkin","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:captured-scarlet-zealot","quest:365","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:light"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",["end"]="Captured Scarlet Zealot",level="7",faction="Horde",id=407},src={"Fields of Grief (2)"}}
E["quest:408"] = {t="quest",n="The Family Crypt",z="tirisfal",s="Scourge forces at the Agamand Mills threaten the Forsaken's hold on Tirisfal. From Brill, Magistrate Sevren sends agents against the undead in the family crypt.",h="Scourge forces at the Agamand Mills threaten the Forsaken's hold on Tirisfal.",sec={{t="A Foxtrot in Tirisfal",b="The Forsaken hold Tirisfal Glades, but the Scourge still grips much of its countryside. The Agamand Mills once produced flour for Lordaeron; now they are a Scourge stronghold. In Brill, Magistrate Sevren watches the enemy gather with grave concern. Every stretch of land lost to the undead weakens the Forsaken's independence.",sp=0},{t="Defiling the Tomb",b="Captain Dargol, a skeletal commander, has made the Agamand Family Crypt his headquarters. Through necromancy, he raises generations of the Agamand dead as Rotting and Wailing Ancestors to swell his ranks. Magistrate Sevren sends Forsaken agents to purge the crypt, lay the disturbed dead to rest, and sever Dargol's head to disrupt Scourge forces in northern Tirisfal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Dargol?",a="Captain Dargol is a skeletal Scourge officer based in the Agamand Family Crypt. He commands local Scourge forces and uses necromancy to raise Agamand ancestors against the Forsaken.",al={"captain dargol","who is dargol","dargol lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren care about the Agamand Mills?",a="The Agamand Mills are a major Scourge foothold close to Brill and the Undercity. Captain Dargol's growing force of raised ancestors threatens the Forsaken settlements.",al={"why brill cares","sevren agamand","agamand importance"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Wailing and Rotting Ancestors?",a="The Wailing and Rotting Ancestors are dead forebears of the wealthy Agamand family. Captain Dargol's necromancy has corrupted them and bound them to the Scourge.",al={"wailing ancestors","rotting ancestors","agamand ancestors"},it="target"},{q="What happens after Dargol is killed?",a="Returning Captain Dargol's skull to Magistrate Sevren breaks the Scourge's central leadership at the mills. Sevren hails the victory as a critical strike for the Forsaken and an early step toward purging the Lich King's influence from Lordaeron.",al={"crypt aftermath","end of agamand chain","dargol defeated"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren want Dargol's skull?",a="Magistrate Sevren demands Captain Dargol's skull as undeniable proof that the Scourge commander has been eliminated. The Agamand Family Crypt serves as the Scourge's primary stronghold in western Tirisfal Glades, and Sevren cannot afford mere rumors of Dargol's defeat. Bringing his severed skull back to Brill confirms that the necromancer's leadership has been shattered and his ritual raising of the Agamand ancestors halted.",al={"dargols skull purpose","why take dargols skull","what is dargols skull for"},it="item",add="6458ecfa"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Captain Dargol embodies the enslavement to the Lich King's will they fought to escape. Putting down the raised ancestors protects their people and helps break the Scourge's hold on their homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, securing Tirisfal Glades helps anchor its presence in the Eastern Kingdoms and removes immediate threats to its northern stronghold."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand mills","brill","captain dargol","magistrate sevren","rotting ancestor","scourge","the family crypt","tirisfal glades","wailing ancestor"},rel={"subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","npc:magistrate-sevren","quest:355","quest:362","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="13",faction="Horde",id=408,ri={"Dargol's Skull"}},src={"The Family Crypt (Classic)"}}
E["quest:409"] = {t="quest",n="Proving Allegiance",z="tirisfal",s="Gunther Arcanus tests whether you serve the free-willed Forsaken or the Lich King. To earn his trust, you are sent to summon and destroy Lillith Nefara, a Scourge operative near his island.",h="Gunther Arcanus tests whether you serve the free-willed Forsaken or the Lich King.",sec={{t="A Recluse's Suspicions",b="Gunther Arcanus has kept to an island in Brightwater Lake since rising into undeath. He fiercely guards his freedom. Bethor Iceshard's enchantments on Gunther's spellbook showed that the emissary carries no Scourge taint. Still, words and charms cannot quiet the hermit's suspicions. An outsider must prove hostility toward the Lich King's minions through decisive violence before Gunther will trust them.",sp=0},{t="The Slaying of Lillith Nefara",b="South of Gunther's refuge, a bloodstained ritual altar marks the place where Lillith Nefara operates in the Tirisfal Glades. She is a formidable agent of the Scourge. A Candle of Beckoning awakens her from the shadows, bringing her into open combat. Her defeat breaks Gunther's long-held belief that he alone among the undead had escaped the Lich King's control.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Gunther Arcanus need proof?",a="Gunther has survived as an independent undead by trusting no one. With the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other threats around him in Tirisfal, he suspects any undead visitor may be the Lich King's agent until they shed Scourge blood.",al={"why does gunther doubt me","gunther trust"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Lillith Nefara?",a="Lillith Nefara is a powerful Scourge agent active along Brightwater Lake's southern shores. She serves the Lich King from an ancient, bloody altar near Gunther's island.",al={"who is lillith","lillith nefara lore"},it="target"},{q="What is the Candle of Beckoning?",a="The Candle of Beckoning is a ritual item taken from a crate on Gunther's island. Place and light it on the bloody altar to summon Lillith Nefara from her resting place and face her in battle.",al={"candle of beckoning","how to summon lillith"},it="item"},{q="What realization does Gunther come to upon Lillith's defeat?",a="Lillith's defeat makes Gunther accept that he is not unique. Until then, he believed he was the only undead in Lordaeron to break free from the Lich King's telepathic domination.",al={"gunther reaction","gunther epiphany"},sp=1},{q="Where does this confrontation take place?",a="The confrontation takes place at an altar on the lakeshore just off the southern coast of Gunther's island in Brightwater Lake, in eastern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is the altar","lillith location"},it="place"},{q="What happens after proving your allegiance?",a="Once Gunther's doubts are settled, he agrees to hear the Undercity's emissaries and reconsider his solitary exile, opening the way to his formal recruitment into Lady Sylvanas's Forsaken.",al={"what next after proving allegiance","after lillith dies"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gunther need you to destroy Lillith instead of doing it himself?",a="Gunther Arcanus is not merely asking for a pest to be removed; he is testing your loyalty. He has lived in isolation believing himself to be the sole undead soul who broke free from the Lich King's iron grip. While you claim that you and the Forsaken share that independence, words and magical wards alone do not satisfy him. Sending you to summon and destroy an active Scourge commander forces you to demonstrate that you truly stand against the Lich King before he lowers his guard.",al={"why me gunther","why doesn't gunther kill lillith","why send me proving allegiance"},it="why_me",add="74408c95"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you as Forsaken, breaking Gunther's isolation is personal. It shows a brother in undeath that none of you need face the Scourge or the living alone.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the arcane and necromantic talents of Bethor Iceshard and Gunther Arcanus. Showing your own skill earns the respect of a powerful fellow caster."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","candle of beckoning","gunther arcanus","lillith nefara","proving allegiance","scourge altar","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:411","quest:366","quest:431","npc:gunther-arcanus","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Gunther Arcanus",level="12",faction="Horde",id=409},src={"Proving Allegiance"}}
E["quest:410"] = {t="quest",n="The Dormant Shade",z="tirisfal",s="A dark rite waits at Gunther's Retreat on Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades. Set a mystic candle on an old, blood-soaked table to summon Lillith Nefara, a Scourge agent, and prove to Gunther Arcanus that you oppose the Lich King.",h="A dark rite waits at Gunther's Retreat on Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Altar",b="On Gunther's Retreat, an island in Brightwater Lake, a battered dinner table lies stained with blood. The table is no ordinary abandoned piece of furniture. It is the focus of a dark conjuration, a rough slab where dried gore marks the place death and dark magic gather.",sp=0},{t="The Candle of Beckoning",b="Place the Candle of Beckoning on the bloodied table and light it, and Lillith Nefara's spirit answers from beyond death. The flame calls the Scourge agent out of her rest, bringing her into a test for those who seek to prove their allegiance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of lighting the candle on the table?",a="Lighting the Candle of Beckoning on the battered, bloody table summons Lillith Nefara, a dangerous shade you must defeat.",al={"why light candle","dormant shade objective","table ritual"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is summoned by this ritual?",a="The ritual summons Lillith Nefara, an undead spirit and Scourge agent who haunts Gunther's Retreat on Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who spawns","dormant shade ghost","who is the shade"},it="target"},{q="How does this relate to proving allegiance to the Forsaken?",a="Summoning and defeating Lillith Nefara proves to the reclusive Gunther Arcanus that you oppose the Scourge and serve no purpose to the Lich King.",al={"proving allegiance connection","why kill lillith","forsaken test"},it="ties"},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The ritual takes place at Gunther's Retreat, Gunther Arcanus's island in Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades. A battered dinner table stained with dried blood sits just off the island's southern coast.",al={"table location","where is the table","lilliths dinner table"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can anyone light the candle?",a="Anyone with the Candle of Beckoning who undertakes the Forsaken's trials of allegiance can light it on the altar.",al={"who can do the ritual","class requirements","candle ritual"},gp=true},{q="Is the table naturally haunted?",a="The table is an old, bloody altar used by the Scourge agent Lillith Nefara. Lighting the Candle of Beckoning there wakes her from her rest.",al={"is the table magical","why the bloody table"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Candle of Beckoning used for?",a="The Candle of Beckoning is an enchanted item crafted specifically to bridge the veil and summon the dormant spirit lingering around Gunther's Retreat on Brightwater Lake. When placed atop the bloodied dinner table and lit, its dark flame acts as a beacon, calling forth the restless shade of Lillith Nefara into the physical world so you can confront her.",al={"candle of beckoning use","what does candle of beckoning do","beckoning candle purpose"},it="item",add="7957b0ef"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you perform a grim rite over a bloodied altar in Tirisfal, where death and dark magic mark your new existence and loyalty to the Dark Lady.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know the power of binding spirits to blood-drenched altars. This rite tests your hold over the boundary between life and death.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you recognize the candle's shadowed call, drawing a lingering soul back into conflict."},kw={"bloody table","candle of beckoning","dormant shade","forsaken ritual","lillith nefara","proving allegiance","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:409","zone:tirisfal","topic:light"},m={start="Lillith's Dinner Table",level="10",faction="Horde",id=410,ri={"Candle of Beckoning"}},src={"The Dormant Shade"}}
E["quest:426"] = {t="quest",n="The Mills Overrun",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, the Scourge gather at Agamand Mills, close to Forsaken settlements. Deathguard Dillinger sends soldiers from Brill to break their ranks before the ruined mills become a base for attacks deeper into the glades.",h="In Tirisfal, the Scourge gather at Agamand Mills, close to Forsaken settlements.",sec={{t="A Looming Threat on the Mills",b="The Agamand Mills once anchored Tirisfal Glades' agriculture. Since the Third War, their windmills overlook Scourge forces massing on the grounds under the Lich King's thrall. These mindless undead threaten the fledgling Forsaken holdings. If they secure the mills, they will have a base from which to push deeper into Tirisfal and strike at those settlements.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Destruction",b="Deathguard Dillinger, who helps fortify Brill and patrols the territory, sends recruits against the Scourge. They hunt Rattlecage and Cracked Skull Soldiers, along with Darkeye Bonecasters. Dillinger asks for notched ribs and blackened skulls as proof that the skeletal ranks have been broken apart and driven back toward the Plaguelands before their offensive begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Scourge gathering at Agamand Mills?",a="The Scourge gather to establish a staging ground in western Tirisfal. From Agamand Mills, they can launch raids deeper into the glades and threaten nearby Forsaken settlements such as Brill.",al={"why agamand mills","scourge at the mills","why the mills"},it="target"},{q="Who is Deathguard Dillinger?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Brill. He coordinates strikes against dangers in Tirisfal Glades, including the Scourge and hostile gnoll packs threatening the road.",al={"deathguard dillinger lore","who is dillinger","dillinger brill"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Agamand Mills located?",a="Agamand Mills lies north of the main western highway in Tirisfal Glades. From Brill, cross the river bridge to the west and follow the north fork to the ruined windmills.",al={"where is agamand mills","mills location","how to get to the mills"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Dillinger want ribs and skulls?",a="Dillinger asks for ribs and skulls as proof that the Scourge front line has been broken. The notched ribs come from skeletal infantry, and the blackened skulls from bonecasters.",al={"notched ribs blackened skulls","why ribs and skulls"},it="item"},{q="What is the relationship between the Forsaken and the Scourge here?",a="The Forsaken are undead who broke free of the Lich King's mental domination. The Scourge remain mindless slaves to his will, seeking to wipe out the Forsaken and reclaim Lordaeron for their master.",al={"forsaken vs scourge","why fight other undead"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after clearing these Scourge?",a="Clearing the foot soldiers is only an opening blow against the Scourge at Agamand Mills. Dillinger and the Deathguards keep pushing deeper into the mills against the commanders and dark forces entrenched there.",al={"what comes next","after the mills overrun"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger want this done?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is tasked with defending Brill and securing Tirisfal Glades for the Forsaken. The Scourge are attempting to establish a forward base of operations at Agamand Mills, which would allow the Lich King's mindless minions to stage deeper incursions into Tirisfal and threaten the Undercity's perimeter. Crushing them before they solidify their foothold is vital to holding the region.",al={"why clear agamand mills","dillinger motive","why destroy the scourge at the mills"},it="motive",add="e729259a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you as Forsaken, driving the Scourge from Agamand Mills protects your new lands and strikes at the mindless slaves of the Lich King who once held you in thrall.",["faction:Horde"]="For you in the Horde, holding Tirisfal Glades helps secure the Horde's only foothold in northern Lordaeron. Destroying Scourge staging grounds is a tactical priority.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face armored skeletons at Agamand Mills, relentless foes who feel no pain and give no quarter."},kw={"agamand mills","blackened skulls","brill","darkeye bonecaster","deathguard dillinger","notched ribs","scourge","the mills overrun","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:agamand-mills","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:brill","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",level="8",faction="Horde",id=426,ri={"Blackened Skull","Notched Rib"}},src={"The Mills Overrun (Classic)"}}
E["quest:427"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, Executor Zygand directs the Forsaken campaign against the Scarlet Crusade. With intelligence recovered by Executor Arren, you are sent to strike Scarlet Warriors at a guard tower west of the Solliden Farmstead. The attack opens the Forsaken military effort to drive the crusaders from their borders.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, Executor Zygand directs the Forsaken campaign against the Scarlet Crusade.",sec={{t="A Two-Front War",b="The Forsaken state under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner faces threats on several fronts. The Deathguard watches the growing armies of the Lich King, while the Scarlet Crusade contests Forsaken dominance over their former homeland. The Crusade condemns all undead as abominations to be purged with fire and blade. Its zealots fail to see that the Forsaken have broken free of the Scourge’s control.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Western Outpost",b="Executor Arren secured intelligence documents at Deathknell, giving Executor Zygand the locations of Scarlet encampments and outposts across Tirisfal Glades. With Deathguard garrisons occupied containing the Scourge, independent Forsaken champions are sent to strike the zealots directly. The first target is a guard tower west of Solliden Farmstead, where Scarlet Warriors gather and threaten the western approaches to Brill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile toward the Forsaken?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is an extremist human order devoted to eradicating the undead. Its members make no distinction between the mindless Scourge under the Lich King and the free-willed Forsaken loyal to Lady Sylvanas. They see every undead being as a plague-ridden monster that must be burned.",al={"why scarlet hate undead","scarlet crusade motivation","why are they attacking"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is the senior military officer of the Forsaken Deathguard stationed in Brill. He directs tactical deployments, defends the roads around the capital’s approaches, and oversees offensive strikes against nearby Scarlet and Scourge forces.",al={"who is zygand","brill quest giver executor","zygand lore"},it="identity"},{q="How did the Forsaken get intelligence on Scarlet positions?",a="Recruits serving Executor Arren recovered tactical documents in Deathknell. The papers detailed Scarlet patrol routes, outposts, and encampments throughout Tirisfal, giving Executor Zygand the information to plan targeted counter-attacks.",al={"scarlet documents","arren intelligence","how did they find the tower"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the Scarlet Warriors located?",a="Scarlet Warriors hold a defensive tower west of the Solliden Farmstead, in the western countryside of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"scarlet warrior location","where is the tower","solliden farmstead tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't the Deathguard handle the Crusade directly?",a="The Deathguard’s formal ranks are stretched thin watching the Scourge, whose forces grow in number each night under the Lich King’s reach. Unable to spare regular soldiers from containment, Zygand relies on ambitious, unassigned champions to cull the Crusaders.",al={"why send players","where is the deathguard","why help zygand"},it="why_me"},{q="Does this mission end the Scarlet presence in Tirisfal?",a="No. The attack on the western watchtower is the first strike in a four-part campaign directed by Executor Zygand to dismantle Scarlet command and outposts across the region.",al={"is this the last scarlet quest","scarlet crusade quest chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want the Scarlet Warriors killed?",a="With recovered intelligence revealing Scarlet Crusade camps across Tirisfal Glades, Executor Zygand sees a vital opening to strike back against these zealots. The Crusade seeks to eradicate all undead, making them a lethal threat to Brill and the Forsaken's borders if left unchecked.",al={"why kill scarlet warriors","zygand motive","why attack scarlet crusade"},it="motive",add="3cb6349f"},{q="Who are the Scarlet Warriors at the tower?",a="They are militant zealots of the Scarlet Crusade garrisoned at the watchtower west of the Solliden Farmstead. Driven by fanatical hatred, they view all Forsaken as mindless Scourge monsters deserving of eradication and wage relentless war to reclaim Lordaeron from the undead.",al={"who are scarlet warriors","scarlet warriors tirisfal","who am i killing"},it="target",add="82f56bdf"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you face living former countrymen who call you monsters and seek your eradication instead of mourning Lordaeron’s tragic fall.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you need a secure border around Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity to give the Horde a permanent foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"brill","deathguard","scarlet crusade","scarlet warriors","solliden farmstead","sylvanas","tirisfal glades","zygand"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:solliden-farmstead","npc:executor-arren","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="8",faction="Horde",id=427},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:431"] = {t="quest",n="Candles of Beckoning",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, candles from Gunther's island are bound for a grim test. A crate on Gunther's Retreat holds the ritual tapers Gunther Arcanus uses to test allegiance.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, candles from Gunther's island are bound for a grim test.",sec={{t="Tallow and Dark Rites",b="Gunther asks you to take a candle from the crate on Gunther's Retreat to the old, bloody altar off the island's southern coast. Light it there, and face Lillith Nefara, the Scourge agent.",sp=0},{t="A Reclaimed Relic",b="A crate of candles rests on Gunther's Retreat, the island in Brightwater Lake where Gunther Arcanus dwells. For his test in Proving Allegiance, one candle is enough. Lit on the old, bloody altar off the island's southern coast, it awakens Lillith Nefara, the Scourge agent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Candles of Beckoning?",a="Light a Candle of Beckoning on the bloody altar near Gunther's Retreat to awaken Lillith Nefara for Gunther's test of allegiance.",al={"what are candles of beckoning","purpose of candles","what do candles do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are these candles found?",a="The candles are kept in a Crate of Candles on Gunther's Retreat, Gunther Arcanus's island in Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to find candles of beckoning","candle crate location","crate of candles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who crafted these candles?",a="No maker is named. Gunther keeps a crate of candles on his island for the test he sets in Proving Allegiance.",al={"who made candles of beckoning","candle creator","who made the crate"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Horde or Forsaken want them?",a="Gunther Arcanus needs a candle for his test in Proving Allegiance. Lit on the bloody altar off his island's southern coast, it awakens Lillith Nefara, the Scourge agent. Destroying her proves you are the Lich King's foe.",al={"why forsaken need candles","why retrieve candles","why horde candles"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can just anyone use the candle?",a="Gunther's test calls for placing the Candle of Beckoning on Lillith's bloody dinner table and lighting it to summon her.",al={"can i light it","how to use candle","use candle of beckoning"},it="power"},{q="Are the candles linked to the Scourge?",a="A Candle of Beckoning awakens Lillith Nefara, a powerful Scourge agent. Gunther asks you to destroy her to prove you are the Lich King's enemy.",al={"is this scourge magic","are candles scourge","scourge cult candles"},it="ties"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you salvage occult implements in Tirisfal for survival and study, keeping dangerous artifacts from hostile hands.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you recognize the tallow and magical resonance used in ritual beckoning.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you understand the care needed with items made to invoke lingering spirits and call unseen presences."},kw={"candles of beckoning","crate of candles","forsaken","occult","ritual taper","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Crate of Candles",level="10",faction="Horde",id=431},src={"Candles of Beckoning"}}
E["quest:492"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, A New Plague reaches its first test on a captive dwarf. Apothecary Johaan sends you to Gallows' End Tavern cellar with the brew he has made from reagents gathered across Tirisfal Glades.",h="In Brill, A New Plague reaches its first test on a captive dwarf.",sec={{t="A Deadly Concoction",b="Apothecary Johaan has brought his research to a dangerous trial. The Royal Apothecary Society works for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, seeking a plague that kills the living while bypassing undead bodies. Johaan has brewed what he calls a “special drink” and sends you to give it to an imprisoned enemy of the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Gallows' End Cellar",b="The Deathguard holds captives in a damp cellar beneath Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, where they await interrogation or disposal. One prisoner is a Dwarven Mountaineer, an Ironforge scout caught trespassing in Tirisfal Glades. Defiant and thirsty, he eagerly accepts the drink, unaware of what Johaan has mixed into it.",sp=0},{t="A Chilling Demonstration",b="The captured mountaineer drinks the flask and wistfully compares it to Rhapsody Malt. He boasts that dwarven steam tanks are coming to save him. The poison kills him almost at once. Johaan's final words make clear that this deadly brew is only a taste of what the Dark Lady envisions for the rest of Azeroth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Apothecary Johaan is a Royal Apothecary Society member stationed in Brill, Tirisfal Glades. He directs early work on a plague for Forsaken warfare and has adventurers gather lethal reagents from the surrounding wilderness.",al={"apothecary johaan","who gives a new plague","johaan brilliance"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a dwarf captured in Brill?",a="Ironforge Mountaineers scout the northern kingdoms to watch Forsaken movements and investigate the plaguelands. The Deathguard caught this scout in Tirisfal and locked him in the tavern cellar until the apothecaries found a use for him.",al={"dwarf in cellar","captured mountaineer","why is dwarf in tirisfal"},it="target"},{q="What happens when you give the prisoner the drink?",a="The dwarf gladly takes the flagon, thirsty after his capture. The toxic brew kills him moments after he drinks it, showing the force of Johaan's latest plague formulation.",al={"does the dwarf die","drink result","mountaineer death"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the purpose of the New Plague research?",a="The Forsaken seek a new plague under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's orders. They aim to make a weapon that can destroy both the mindless Scourge and the living races that threaten their territory.",al={"why make new plague","royal apothecary society goal","dark lady plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Captured Mountaineer located?",a="The Captured Mountaineer is held in the cellar downstairs at Gallows' End Tavern, in the center of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"find captive dwarf","gallows end cellar","where is mountaineer"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest chain continue beyond this dwarf?",a="Johaan's four-part assignment ends with the mountaineer's death. Research into the New Plague continues across Lordaeron, with further testing in the Undercity and the Sepulcher.",al={"next quest","a new plague followup","after mountaineer dies"},gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want to poison the mountaineer?",a="Apothecary Johaan is conducting practical trials for the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague. Having refined his concoctions using local venom and blood, he needs a live living subject to observe its lethality firsthand. A captured enemy of the Dark Lady sitting helpless in the tavern cellar presents the perfect opportunity to test whether his brew can swiftly eradicate mortal foes.",al={"why does johaan want this done","johaan motive captured mountaineer","why test poison on dwarf"},it="motive",add="38956767"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the Forsaken's uncompromising struggle to survive and the lethal work of the Royal Apothecary Society.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see how far Ironforge Mountaineers range to watch Tirisfal Glades, risking death and covert interrogation.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the ruthlessness the Forsaken show toward Alliance intruders found in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde member, you see the Forsaken pursue victory through cold alchemical warfare, even against friend or foe."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","captured mountaineer","gallows end","plague","poison","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:captured-mountaineer","quest:367","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",["end"]="Captured Mountaineer",level="11",faction="Horde",id=492},src={"A New Plague (4)"}}
E["quest:5481"] = {t="quest",n="Gordo's Task",z="tirisfal",s="Along the road to Brill, Gordo gathers plants for the Royal Apothecary Society. The wandering abomination cannot manage delicate work, so he asks travelers to pick Gloom Weed and bring it to Junior Apothecary Holland.",h="Along the road to Brill, Gordo gathers plants for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sec={{t="A Clumsy Laborer",b="Between Deathknell and Brill, Gordo trudges through the countryside on the Royal Apothecary Society's behalf. Abominations can fight with brute strength and haul heavy loads, but their huge, stitched hands make delicate work difficult. Sent into the meadows to gather ingredients, Gordo finds that his blunt fingers crush more stems than they pluck. He turns to passersby, bullying or bribing them to do the careful work for him.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Frustrations",b="Junior Apothecary Holland waits for the delivery in the graveyard behind Brill's town hall. Gordo has misunderstood his orders: Holland needs volatile Doom Weed for alchemical research, but Gordo sent travelers to gather harmless Gloom Weed. Holland is thoroughly exasperated by the stitched giant's mistake and takes it as proof that Gordo is useless. He immediately sends you to correct the error.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gordo?",a="Gordo is an abomination bound to the Royal Apothecary Society. He patrols the meadows west of Brill, trying to carry out labor assigned by his master, Junior Apothecary Holland.",al={"who is gordo","gordo tirisfal","gordo npc","what is gordo"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gordo need help gathering weeds?",a="Gordo needs help because his enormous, stitched hands lack the dexterity to pick delicate plants without ruining them. He recruits traveling Forsaken to gather the flora.",al={"why does gordo need weeds","why can't gordo pick weeds","gordo hands"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Master Holland?",a="Junior Apothecary Holland is an alchemist with the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed in the Brill graveyard. He oversees Gordo and researches local flora and blighted soil to aid the Forsaken war effort.",al={"master holland","who is holland","apothecary holland"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Holland upset when the Gloom Weed is delivered?",a="Holland is upset because he needs volatile Doom Weed for alchemical research, but Gordo sent you to gather harmless Gloom Weed.",al={"why is holland mad","gloom weed mistake","wrong weed"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Where can Gloom Weed be found?",a="Gloom Weed grows close to the ground in the fields between Deathknell and Brill, especially in the open meadows east of Solliden Farmstead.",al={"where to find gloom weed","gloom weed locations","finding gloom weed"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing Gordo's Task?",a="Afterward, Holland offers you another assignment, Doom Weed, in Brill's graveyard.",al={"what comes next","gordo's task follow up","next quest after gordo"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gordo want gloom weed collected?",a="Gordo says Master Holland wants weeds and asks for help gathering Gloom Weed. His large hands make picking difficult, so he sends travelers to deliver the plants to Holland in Brill's graveyard.",al={"why does gordo want weeds","gordo motive","why collect gloom weed"},it="motive",add="2383074c"},{q="What is Gloom Weed used for?",a="As far as Master Holland is concerned, gloom weed is utterly useless. It is simply a common, harmless wild weed that grows throughout Tirisfal Glades. Holland has no interest in picking daisies and needs Doom Weed for his concoctions instead.",al={"what is gloom weed for","gloom weed purpose","use of gloom weed"},sp=1,it="item",add="a763e1e7"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a trained herbalist, you can easily find Gloom Weed patches among the blighted grass.",["race:Undead"]="As a newly risen Forsaken leaving Deathknell, you meet the clumsy realities of abomination labor and the Royal Apothecary Society's sharp temper."},kw={"abomination","apothecary","brill","doom weed","gloom weed","gordo","holland","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","subzone:deathknell","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:horde"},m={level="5",faction="Horde",id=5481,ri={"Gloom Weed"}},src={"Gordo's Task (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5482"] = {t="quest",n="Doom Weed",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Junior Apothecary Holland seeks doom weed for his research. The plant grows near Tirisfal's northern mass graves, where Rot Hide gnolls prowl.",h="In Brill, Junior Apothecary Holland seeks doom weed for his research.",sec={{t="Apothecary Ambitions",b="Junior Apothecary Holland researches for the Royal Apothecary Society from Brill. He wants doom weed to advance his experiments, but Gordo cannot tell the right plants from the wrong ones. Holland turns to more capable hands to gather what he needs.",sp=0},{t="The Mass Grave Harvest",b="Doom weed grows thick around the mass gravesite just north of the Brill graveyard, where death and plague have tainted the soil. Rot Hide gnolls prowl the burial mounds, scavenging among the remains and guarding the overgrown trenches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Junior Apothecary Holland need doom weed?",a="Junior Apothecary Holland needs doom weed for his alchemical work with the Royal Apothecary Society. He says this work aids Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, though his eagerness also points to ambition within the society.",al={"holland doom weed","why doom weed","doom weed purpose"}},{q="Why doesn't Gordo gather the weeds himself?",a="Gordo is an abomination sent to gather herbs around Brill, but he cannot identify particular plants. After Gordo brings back the wrong weeds, Holland turns to capable adventurers.",al={"why not gordo","gordo task fail","who is gordo"}},{q="Where does doom weed grow?",a="Doom weed grows around the mass gravesite just north of the graveyard outside Brill. It spreads through soil tainted by burial trenches and lingering plague.",al={"doom weed location","where is doom weed","mass grave weeds"}},{q="What dangers lurk near the doom weed patches?",a="Rot Hide gnolls prowl the grounds around the mass gravesite. These feral, disease-ridden scavengers attack anyone who comes near while gathering the weeds.",al={"doom weed monsters","mass grave enemies","gnolls near brill"}},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society's interest in Tirisfal flora?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society studies plants, poisons, and blight-altered fungi across Tirisfal Glades. It gathers reagents like doom weed to refine toxins, seek alchemical cures, and develop weapons for the Forsaken against their enemies.",al={"apothecary interest","royal apothecary society tirisfal","forsaken herb gathering"}},{q="Who is 'the Lady' mentioned by Holland?",a="“The Lady” means Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen and ruler of the Forsaken. Apothecaries in Undercity and Brill invoke her name, saying their alchemical work follows her command.",al={"who is the lady","holland lady sylvanas","the lady undercity"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you may serve junior members of the Royal Apothecary Society as you establish your usefulness to Sylvanas's realm.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know the glades hold ordinary plants as well as corrupted growths like doom weed, shaped by the Scourge's plague.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see in Brill's unsettling alchemy how the Forsaken differ from their shamanic and nomadic allies in Kalimdor."},kw={"brill","doom weed","gordo","junior apothecary holland","mass grave","rot hide gnolls","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:5481","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:gnoll","topic:horde"},m={level="6",id=5482},src={"In-game quest text: Doom Weed","Doom Weed (Classic)"},fv=true}
E["quest:5650"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of Darkness",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Dark Cleric Beryl tests fledgling Forsaken priests before they delve deeper into shadow. The trial shows whether they can heal and fortify an injured Deathguard, for the priesthood calls for more than afflicting enemies.",h="In Brill, Dark Cleric Beryl tests fledgling Forsaken priests before they delve deeper into shadow.",sec={{t="A Balance of Dark and Light",b="Forsaken priests draw renown and a distinct identity from shadow and darkness. Dark Cleric Beryl also teaches that understanding darkness means learning light and restoration. Those who seek only ruin are urged to study arcane magic instead. A priest's calling includes strengthening and preserving comrades as well as afflicting enemies.",sp=0},{t="A Duty in the Graveyard",b="North of Brill's cemetery, Deathguard Kel holds the line against prowling gnoll packs and has been wounded. Beryl sends you to bind his wounds with healing spells and bolster his stamina with protective enchantments. In this way, you show you can maintain Tirisfal Glades' defenders. Beryl grants you his vestment and accepts you into the priesthood's higher mysteries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do Forsaken priests use healing magic if their power comes from darkness?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl teaches that Forsaken priests draw exceptional strength from shadow, but healing remains essential. Before mastering darkness, an acolyte must learn supportive and restorative magic to keep Forsaken defenders standing on the battlefield.",al={"why do undead heal","forsaken priest healing lore","shadow vs light undead"},it="power"},{q="Who is Deathguard Kel?",a="Deathguard Kel is a Forsaken sentry stationed north of Brill's cemetery. He defends local settlements against aggressive gnoll packs wandering the woods and needs aid when wounded in the line of duty.",al={"deathguard kel lore","who is deathguard kel","wounded deathguard"},it="target"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl, the priest trainer in Brill, offers it after you complete In Favor of Darkness.",al={"who starts garments of darkness","garments of darkness quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What vestments are granted upon finishing the trial?",a="Beryl awards a tailored robe as a badge of station and accomplishment. It marks the priest's mastery of fundamental duties and recognition by their peers.",al={"what robe do you get","garments reward priest"},it="item"},{q="What threats was Deathguard Kel fighting?",a="Kel was wounded fighting local gnolls that infest the wilderness of Tirisfal Glades north of Brill's cemetery.",al={"what attacked kel","kel gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="What darker powers does Dark Cleric Beryl hint at?",a="Beryl hints at shadow techniques unique to the Forsaken priesthood, including distinctive manifestations of shadow magic and mental affliction not practiced by priests of other races.",al={"forsaken priest unique spells","darker powers hint"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dark Cleric Beryl want this done?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl seeks to test your discipline and readiness within the Forsaken priesthood. While Forsaken priests draw profound strength from darkness and shadow, Beryl believes a priest cannot truly master the dark without first understanding the light and its restorative arts. By directing you to mend and fortify the injured Deathguard Kel, he tests your practical grasp of essential healing before welcoming you deeper into the priesthood's darker teachings.",al={"beryl motive","why does beryl send you","why heal kel beryl"},it="motive",add="933f71c0"},{q="Why does Dark Cleric Beryl send you instead of tending to Deathguard Kel himself?",a="This task serves specifically as a rite of passage for you as an initiate. Beryl already possesses these abilities, but evaluating your growth requires you to venture out into the field and apply your training directly. Mending and fortifying an active defender like Deathguard Kel proves to Beryl and your peers that you are capable of supporting the Forsaken in battle.",al={"why send me to heal kel","why not beryl herself","why does beryl need me"},it="why_me",add="a6afe368"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you balance shadow's grim utility with the duty to fortify and heal allies.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you use healing magic to sustain front-line soldiers like Deathguard Kel against gnolls and Scourge remnants."},kw={"brill","dark cleric beryl","deathguard kel","fortitude","garments of darkness","lesser heal","priest","shadow","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:5651","npc:dark-cleric-beryl","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:light","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Dark Cleric Beryl",level="4",faction="Horde",id=5650},src={"Garments of Darkness"}}
E["quest:5651"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Darkness",z="tirisfal",s="Dark Cleric Duesten sends you from Deathknell to Brill in In Favor of Darkness. There, you continue your training with Dark Cleric Beryl and study the Holy Light and Shadow.",h="Dark Cleric Duesten sends you from Deathknell to Brill in In Favor of Darkness.",sec={{t="A Path Carved in Rot",b="Dark Cleric Duesten teaches that the Forsaken were forged in corruption and discarded like carrion. Their survival demands that they understand both Light and Shadow without sentimentality. In Tirisfal Glades, you leave Deathknell's graveyard and face the wider world beyond its walls.",sp=0},{t="Instruction in Brill",b="You follow the road northeast from Deathknell, cross a wooden covered bridge, and reach the ruined hamlet of Brill. Dark Cleric Beryl waits in the upper quarters of the local inn to test your resolve. He values ambition and cold practicality over blind devotion, and expects a Forsaken priest to wield divine power as a weapon and a tool, not a moral crutch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This rite of passage sends Forsaken priests from Deathknell to continue their training. Dark Cleric Duesten sends you to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill for your next priestly challenge.",al={"what does this quest do","why in favor of darkness","in favor of darkness purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do Forsaken priests use the Light if they embrace darkness?",a="Forsaken clerics study both Light and Shadow because they see the world as governed by their balance. The Holy Light causes excruciating pain to undead flesh, and Forsaken origins lie in rot and darkness, so they study both forces out of practicality and necessity.",al={"why do undead priests use light","forsaken priest lore","light and shadow undead"}},{q="Where do I find Dark Cleric Beryl?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl is in Brill, northeast of Deathknell. He resides on the second floor of the Gallows' End Tavern on the settlement's eastern side.",al={"where is dark cleric beryl","beryl location","find beryl"},gp=true},{q="What does this quest lead into?",a="Speaking with Dark Cleric Beryl completes your training here and opens Garments of Darkness. There, he tests your ability to mend and sustain allies using your newfound disciplines.",al={"what comes next","next quest after in favor of darkness","in favor of darkness followup"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Dark Cleric Duesten?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten is the priest trainer in Deathknell. He helps newly awakened Forsaken priests understand their painful existence and use their spiritual powers.",al={"who gives this quest","duesten lore","dark cleric duesten"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Beryl mention ambition over faith?",a="Forsaken priests view traditional pious faith as insufficient after the powers they worshipped in life abandoned them. Dark Cleric Beryl expects disciples to rely on personal ambition, urgency, and practical strength to survive.",al={"beryl dialogue meaning","why ambition not faith","forsaken faith"}},{q="Why does Dark Cleric Duesten send you to Brill?",a="Duesten has taught you the foundational truth of Forsaken priesthood: that while you may wield both the Light and the dark with discretion, your existence was forged in rot and darkness. Now that you have grasped these fundamentals in Deathknell, he sends you onward to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill to advance your training in service of the Forsaken.",al={"why does duesten send me away","duesten motive in favor of darkness","why go to dark cleric beryl"},it="motive",add="066c2d01"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you learn the Forsaken way: wield both Holy Light and Shadow with cold discretion rather than religious reverence.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you travel from Deathknell to Brill on a standard first excursion into the broader Forsaken realm. The journey shows initiates how their people rebuild in the ruins of Lordaeron."},kw={"beryl","brill","deathknell","duesten","light","priest","shadow","tirisfal"},rel={"quest:5650","npc:dark-cleric-beryl","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:light"},m={start="Dark Cleric Duesten",["end"]="Dark Cleric Beryl",level="4",faction="Horde",id=5651},src={"In Favor of Darkness"}}
E["quest:590"] = {t="quest",n="A Rogue's Deal",z="tirisfal",s="Calvin Montague offers newly awakened Forsaken work in Deathknell. He promises wealth for delivering a letter, but you do not know whether he will honor the bargain.",h="Calvin Montague offers newly awakened Forsaken work in Deathknell.",sec={{t="A Dishonorable Promise",b="In Deathknell, Calvin Montague offers newly risen Forsaken work for good coin. He asks them to deliver a letter, but when they return, he pretends no bargain was made and denies owing them anything.",sp=0},{t="Paying the Price",b="When you demand the promised silver, Calvin Montague draws his weapons instead. He expects an inexperienced Forsaken to be easy to cut down. Defeated, he gives you some coin and admits he lied about the payout because he thought he could get away with it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Calvin Montague attack when asked for payment?",a="Calvin Montague is an unscrupulous rogue who never meant to share his coin. When you confront him over the broken promise, he tries to silence you rather than pay, assuming a newly raised Forsaken will be an easy mark.",al={"why calvin fight","calvin montague hostile","why rogue attacks"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Where does this confrontation take place?",a="The confrontation takes place in Deathknell, the ruined village in southwestern Tirisfal Glades where newly risen Forsaken first awaken.",al={"where is calvin montague","calvin montague location","where is rogue's deal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Calvin Montague actually pay what he promised?",a="No. After you beat him, Calvin Montague surrenders and hands over some coin, far less than he originally offered. He admits he lied about the full amount from the start.",al={"calvin reward","does calvin pay","did he lie about coin"},sp=1},{q="How is this second task unlocked?",a="After you complete Calvin Montague's initial letter delivery, return and demand the promised coin. When you challenge his deceit, the fight begins.",al={"how to get part 2","unlock rogue deal fight","secret rogue quest"},gp=true},{q="Does Calvin Montague die when defeated?",a="No. Calvin Montague yields before taking a fatal blow, compliments your fighting skill, and begrudgingly opens his coin pouch to save his own skin.",al={"did i kill calvin","is calvin dead","calvin surrender"},sp=1},{q="What lesson does this encounter offer to new Forsaken?",a="For new Forsaken, the encounter offers a practical lesson in harsh realities: honor is scarce among the undead, words are cheap, and respect is earned only through martial strength.",al={"what is the point of rogue deal","lore behind rogue's deal"}},{q="Why do you have to fight Calvin Montague?",a="Calvin Montague is a rogue through and through. After luring you into doing his dirty work with false promises of wealth, he feigns ignorance when you return to collect your coin. Rather than parting with his silver, he decides it is cheaper and easier to simply attack you, hoping you will be easy prey. To earn your rightful due, you have to beat respect—and your payment—out of him.",al={"why fight calvin montague","who is calvin montague target","why attack calvin"},it="target",add="80d08ba4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a young rogue, dealing with Calvin Montague teaches you to trust no one, watch your purse, and never let another scoundrel walk away with your cut.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, waking in Deathknell quickly shows you that death does not strip away humanity's pettiest vices. Forsaken cutpurses swindle their own kin as readily as living bandits."},kw={"a rogue's deal","brawl","calvin montague","deathknell","forsaken rogue","swindle","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:calvin-montague","quest:8","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Calvin Montague",level="5",faction="Horde",id=590},src={"A Rogue's Deal (2)"}}
E["quest:6395"] = {t="quest",n="Marla's Last Wish",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Marla's Last Wish calls you to bring a husband and wife together in death. Novice Elreth asks you to find Samuel Fipps, still bound to the Scourge, so he can be buried beside his wife, Marla. The Forsaken seek to honor the ties they had in life and to set themselves apart from the Scourge.",h="In Deathknell, Marla's Last Wish calls you to bring a husband and wife together in death.",sec={{t="A Tragic Reunion",b="Marla and Samuel Fipps were husband and wife in Lordaeron before the Third War devastated their home. When the plague swept through their lands, Samuel succumbed and rose as a mindless thrall of the Scourge. Marla escaped undeath, but not her husband. In his frenzy, Samuel killed her. Even then, Marla bore him no hatred. Novice Elreth remembers her final wish: to rest beside Samuel in the Deathknell graveyard.",sp=0},{t="Respecting the Dead",b="Novice Elreth sends you northeast of Deathknell to find Samuel Fipps, who still wanders among a ruined campsite. Ending his torment would remove a Scourge minion from the valley and let his remains be carried back to Marla's resting place. Elreth believes that honoring the dead and their final wishes sets the newly freed Forsaken apart from the Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Marla Fipps?",a="Marla Fipps lived in Lordaeron and survived the plague, but her husband Samuel killed her after he became a mindless Scourge thrall. She wished to be laid to rest beside him.",al={"marla fipps lore","who is marla","marla background"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Samuel Fipps?",a="Samuel Fipps was Marla's husband before the plague. He fell to the Scourge and lost his mind, then killed Marla. He wanders a ruined campsite northeast of Deathknell until Forsaken adventurers put an end to his torment.",al={"samuel fipps lore","who is samuel fipps","where is samuel fipps"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Novice Elreth care about burying them together?",a="Novice Elreth was Marla's friend in life. Elreth believes honoring the dead and treating their remains with dignity shows that the Forsaken retain their humanity and morality, unlike the mindless Scourge.",al={"why help marla","novice elreth motive","why bury samuel"},it="motive"},{q="Did Marla rise as Forsaken?",a="No. Novice Elreth says Marla was spared undeath. Samuel killed her while she was still mortal, and she was buried in the Deathknell graveyard.",al={"is marla undead","did marla become forsaken","marla fipps undead"}},{q="Where is Marla's grave located?",a="Marla's grave is in the first row of the cemetery just outside Deathknell's main chapel.",al={"marla's grave location","where is marla buried","where do i bury samuel"},gp=true},{q="Where can Samuel Fipps be found?",a="Samuel Fipps wanders around a ruined campsite along the road northeast of Deathknell.",al={"samuel fipps location","find samuel fipps","where is samuel"},gp=true},{q="What are Samuel's Remains for?",a="You collect Samuel's earthly remains so they can finally be laid to rest alongside his wife, Marla. Even though Samuel was turned into a mindless scourge and took her life, Marla's dying wish was for them to share an eternal resting place in the Deathknell graveyard.",al={"samuels remains","why gather samuels remains","samuel remains purpose"},it="item",add="e919b4a2"},{q="Who is Samuel Fipps and why must you defeat him?",a="Samuel Fipps was once a living resident of Tirisfal Glades who succumbed to the plague of undeath and became an unthinking servant of the Scourge. After killing his own wife in his mindless state, he now roams the ruined camp northeast of Deathknell as a wandering ghoul, unable to find rest until destroyed.",al={"why kill samuel fipps","who do i fight in marlas last wish","samuel fipps lore"},it="target",add="74d32be4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly risen Forsaken, fulfilling Marla's wish can anchor you to your former human life and show that compassion and honor survived Lordaeron's fall.",["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, Novice Elreth's insistence on proper burial rites speaks to your spiritual duty amid mortality, grief, and the desecration of Lordaeron's dead."},kw={"deathknell","grave","marla fipps","marla's last wish","novice elreth","remains","samuel fipps","scourge"},rel={"npc:novice-elreth","subzone:deathknell","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Novice Elreth",level="5",faction="Horde",id=6395,ri={"Samuel's Remains"}},src={"Marla's Last Wish"}}
E["quest:8"] = {t="quest",n="A Rogue's Deal",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Calvin Montague asks you to carry an unmarked message to Brill. He calls it a simple delivery and promises generous coin.",h="In Deathknell, Calvin Montague asks you to carry an unmarked message to Brill.",sec={{t="A Friendly Courier",b="Calvin Montague lounges among Deathknell's graves and ruined chapels. He says Scourge zombies and creeping spiders have worn him down, then asks you to carry an unmarked letter to Brill. He promises generous coin. For a newly awakened Forsaken, it seems a simple way to reach the region's main town.",sp=0},{t="The Gallows' End Tavern",b="The road east crosses Tirisfal Glades and passes Cold Hearth Manor before reaching Brill. At the Gallows' End Tavern, Innkeeper Renee greets newcomers warmly and fusses over their comfort. But when she receives Montague's letter, her manner breaks. She pretends it brings news from a beloved mother, then scolds you for prying and demands you buy something or leave.\n\nWhen you return to Calvin, he challenges you to a duel instead of peacefully paying what he promised.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Calvin Montague?",a="Calvin Montague is a rogue in Deathknell who asks newly awakened travelers to carry a letter to Innkeeper Renee in Brill. He calls it a simple favor and promises generous pay.",al={"calvin montague","who gives a rogues deal","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What is inside the Nondescript Letter?",a="The letter's exact contents are not recorded. Calvin gives you an unmarked message for Innkeeper Renee in Brill.",al={"nondescript letter contents","what is in the letter","calvins letter"},it="item"},{q="Why does Innkeeper Renee act so strange?",a="Innkeeper Renee runs the tavern in Brill and insists that her correspondence is private. You see her response when you bring her Montague's letter.",al={"innkeeper renee attitude","why is renee fake","renee mother excuse"}},{q="Does Calvin Montague actually pay for the delivery?",a="Calvin Montague promises generous pay for the delivery. Renee offers food or water when the letter reaches her. Return to Calvin afterward to continue dealing with him over the promised payment.",al={"did calvin scam me","where is my money","montague reward"},it="for_you"},{q="Where is Brill located?",a="Brill lies northeast of Deathknell. Follow the main road east out of the starter valley, veer right past Cold Hearth Manor, and cross a covered bridge into town.",al={"how to get to brill","road to brill","brill directions"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after giving the letter to Renee?",a="After giving Renee the letter, return to Calvin Montague in Deathknell to continue dealing with him.",al={"next quest","a rogues deal follow up","what to do after renee"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Calvin Montague want the letter delivered?",a="Calvin Montague claims he has fought more than his fair share of mindless zombies and spiders around Deathknell and simply needs someone to run an errand for him. Rather than trek up the road to Brill himself, he offers to pay you handsomely to deliver his sealed, nondescript letter directly to Innkeeper Renee.",al={"calvin montague motive","why send letter to renee","why does calvin want this done"},it="motive",add="df83fdd9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly risen Forsaken, you make your first journey away from Deathknell's graveyard and head for Brill, the region's busy hub.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you glimpse the informal dealings around Deathknell and Brill through Calvin Montague's private courier errand.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel to Brill, a regional center of Forsaken administration and a place of respite in Tirisfal."},kw={"brill","calvin montague","deathknell","gallows end","innkeeper renee","nondescript letter","rogue","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:calvin-montague","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","quest:5481","subzone:cold-hearth-manor","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Calvin Montague",["end"]="Innkeeper Renee",level="5",faction="Horde",id=8},src={"A Rogue's Deal"}}
E["quest:8652"] = {t="quest",n="Graveborn the Elder",z="tirisfal",s="During the Lunar Festival, Graveborn the Elder waits near Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Travelers seek him among the blighted groves to honor Azeroth’s ancient forebears, and receive his blessing and a holiday token.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Graveborn the Elder waits near Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Ghostly Vigil in Brill",b="In Tirisfal Glades, the Forsaken live among ruined manors and grave sites. During the Lunar Festival, a spirit from ancient times appears just outside Brill. Elder Graveborn welcomes pilgrims who pause to honor the old ways, even in a land shattered by the Scourge and reclaimed by the undead.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Olden Races",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits from long-past eras return with wisdom and gratitude. When you approach Elder Graveborn, he says it heartens him that Tirisfal’s people still honor their ancestors despite the land’s decay. He gives a Coin of Ancestry to those who greet him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Graveborn located?",a="Elder Graveborn waits near the roadside outside Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"elder graveborn location","where is graveborn","graveborn coords"}},{q="What happens when you speak to Elder Graveborn?",a="When you greet Elder Graveborn, he praises you for honoring Azeroth’s ancient peoples and gives you a Coin of Ancestry for the Lunar Festival.",al={"graveborn reward","lunar festival graveborn","what does he give you"}},{q="Why is an ancient elder standing in Tirisfal Glades?",a="During the Lunar Festival, ancient ancestral spirits appear across Azeroth, from kaldorei forests to lands scarred by war and plague. Elder Graveborn watches over northern Lordaeron, where death threatens to eclipse the region’s history.",al={"why is he in tirisfal","graveborn lore","who is elder graveborn"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Graveborn?",a="Elder Graveborn is a neutral spirit who speaks with both Alliance and Horde members. Since he waits just outside the Forsaken town of Brill, Alliance adventurers must beware the local guards.",al={"can alliance talk to graveborn","alliance graveborn the elder","graveborn hostile"}},{q="What is the Coin of Ancestry used for?",a="During the Lunar Festival, you can trade Coins of Ancestry gathered from elders like Graveborn in Moonglade for festive garments, firework recipes, and other celebratory tokens.",al={"coin of ancestry use","what are lunar coins for"}},{q="Is Elder Graveborn one of the Forsaken?",a="No. Elder Graveborn is an ancient spirit honored during the Lunar Festival, not one of the Forsaken. His ghostly form and name near Brill belong to Azeroth’s lineage of elders, not Sylvanas’s Forsaken.",al={"is graveborn undead","is elder graveborn forsaken"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken living in Brill, you see the ancient ancestral spirits arrive as a reminder of Azeroth’s deeper history beyond the Scourge’s recent tragedies.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you must tread carefully through Tirisfal Glades to find Elder Graveborn, since Brill is a heavily fortified Forsaken haven.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you revere the Lunar Festival elders as links to the ancient world before the Sundering, beyond the faction boundaries around them."},kw={"brill","coin of ancestry","elder graveborn","graveborn","lunar festival","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:elder-graveborn","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Elder Graveborn",id=8652},src={"Graveborn the Elder"}}
E["quest:86784"] = {t="quest",n="Sticks and Bones",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Bartholomew asks travelers in Tirisfal Glades to gather dry branches for Eleanor Shackleton. The experienced survivalist camps in the western hills, far from the settlements.",h="Deathguard Bartholomew asks travelers in Tirisfal Glades to gather dry branches for Eleanor Shackleton.",sec={{t="A Friendly Gesture",b="Deathguard Bartholomew pauses between patrols to help an acquaintance in Tirisfal Glades. Deathguards guard against the Scourge and Scarlet crusaders, but Bartholomew also looks out for Eleanor Shackleton. She spends her unlife in the harsh elements, so he asks you to gather dry branches for her campfire.",sp=0},{t="Life in the Wilds",b="Eleanor Shackleton survives alone in Tirisfal's blighted wilderness. Though undead, the Forsaken still feel the damp, bitter chill rolling off the northern moors. Eleanor's rule for gathering wood is simple: when you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more. Grateful for the extra timber, she lets you keep Bartholomew's basket and shares the warmth of her fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Sticks and Bones?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew in Tirisfal Glades asks passing travelers to help his associate Eleanor Shackleton.",al={"who gives sticks and bones","sticks and bones quest starter"},gp=true},{q="Where is Eleanor Shackleton camped?",a="Eleanor Shackleton keeps a small camp in the hills to the west in Tirisfal Glades, where she survives the elements away from the settlements.",al={"eleanor shackleton location","where is eleanor","where to turn in sticks and bones"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken need firewood if they are undead?",a="The Forsaken do not freeze to death like the living, but they still feel Tirisfal's damp, bitter cold. A campfire comforts them, warms their stiff joints, and helps keep a camp livable in the wilds.",al={"do undead get cold","why firewood for undead","forsaken cold"}},{q="What advice does Eleanor give about gathering wood?",a="Eleanor's rule is to gather five times more firewood than you think you need.",al={"eleanor firewood rule","eleanor advice"}},{q="What item do you use to collect the branches?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew gives you a basket for carrying the six dry branches found across the glades. Eleanor lets you keep it after the delivery.",al={"basket for dry branch","how to gather branches"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Does this quest lead to further survival training?",a="Eleanor welcomes you to her camp and shares advice for traveling the wilds. She also offers a friendly contact point in the Tirisfal wilderness.",al={"sticks and bones followup","what does eleanor do next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Deathguard Bartholomew want firewood brought to Eleanor?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew looks out for his associate Eleanor Shackleton, an experienced survivalist braving the dangerous hills to the west. Remembering her personal motto about always stocking up on ample firewood, he suggests you bring her extra fuel both to assist her vigil and to introduce yourself to a seasoned traveler who can teach you the ways of wilderness survival.",al={"why help eleanor","bartholomew motive","why sticks and bones"},it="motive",add="e518ee9d"},{q="What are the Dry Branches for?",a="The dry branches serve as essential fuel for Eleanor Shackleton's campfire out in the wilderness. Despite the walking dead lacking living breath, Eleanor relies on a warm fire to ward off the biting chill of the Tirisfal nights while camped alone amid the hills.",al={"dry branch use","what is dry branch for","firewood for eleanor"},it="item",add="8ea276ef"},{q="Why does Bartholomew ask you instead of gathering the wood himself?",a="As a Deathguard stationed in Tirisfal Glades, Bartholomew's primary duty is maintaining watch and guarding the roads. He cannot abandon his post to forage for fuel, making an independent traveler like you the ideal courier to carry firewood out to Eleanor's wilderness camp.",al={"why me sticks and bones","why does bartholomew need me","why doesn't bartholomew do it"},it="why_me",add="faf72368"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Even in Lordaeron's blighted woods, Forsaken travelers like Eleanor Shackleton must adapt old survival habits to their new unlife.",["faction:Horde"]="Outlying campers like Eleanor offer friendly stopping points for young Horde adventurers setting out across Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"collecting basket","deathguard bartholomew","dry branch","eleanor shackleton","firewood","sticks and bones","survival","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:deathguard-bartholomew","npc:eleanor-shackleton","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Bartholomew",["end"]="Eleanor Shackleton",level="7",faction="Horde",id=86784,ri={"Dry Branch"}},src={"Sticks and Bones (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:90902"] = {t="quest",n="Rediscovering the Light",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, newly raised Forsaken paladins face the pain of calling on the Holy Light. Aramis Hammerhand teaches them to heal wounded Deathguards through the burning agony.",h="In Deathknell, newly raised Forsaken paladins face the pain of calling on the Holy Light.",sec={{t="A Painful Reunion",b="Newly risen Forsaken paladins must face a hard truth: the Holy Light still answers them, but burns their withered bodies. Many were champions of the Silver Hand or knights of Lordaeron before they fell. Aramis Hammerhand teaches them that powers once used without thought now bring fierce pain. The Light clashes with the foul magic that sustains undeath, so calling on it takes resolve and endurance.",sp=0},{t="Purification Through Suffering",b="Deathguards in Deathknell suffer grievous wounds fighting mindless zombies, and Forsaken paladins are called to heal them. Aramis teaches that pushing through the burning pain is like exercising an atrophied muscle. The paladins treat that agony as a badge of honor and proof that the Light has not forsaken them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does using the Light hurt Forsaken paladins?",a="The Holy Light opposes the necrotic energies that sustain undeath. A Forsaken's will and conviction let them channel it, but sacred energy moving through dead flesh brings burning pain.",al={"why does light hurt undead","holy light burning undead","why pain when healing"},it="power"},{q="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand is an undead paladin trainer in Deathknell. He guides newly risen Forsaken paladins as they rebuild their connection to the Holy Light.",al={"who is aramis hammerhand","aramis hammerhand lore","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Deathguards in Deathknell injured?",a="Deathguard soldiers are wounded while defending Deathknell from mindless undead, feral Scourge remnants, and hostile wildlife around the settlement, as the newly risen awaken from their graves.",al={"why are deathguards hurt","injured deathguard lore","deathknell defenders"},it="danger"},{q="Can undead naturally wield the Holy Light?",a="Yes. Undead can wield the Holy Light if they retain faith, willpower, and the memory of their former vows. The Light answers genuine conviction, though it exacts a brutal physical toll on dead bodies.",al={"can forsaken be paladins","undead using the light","forsaken paladin lore"},it="power"},{q="What does Aramis mean when he calls pain a badge of honor?",a="Aramis sees the burning agony as proof that the Light still listens, not as a curse. Forsaken paladins endure the searing heat of their spells to show their loyalty and purpose.",al={"pain purifying property","badge of honor meaning","aramis speech"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="It takes place entirely in Deathknell, the secluded haven in southwestern Tirisfal Glades where newly raised Forsaken first emerge into undeath.",al={"where is this quest","quest location","deathknell quest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Aramis Hammerhand want this done?",a="Aramis aims to train newly risen Forsaken paladins to reconnect with the Holy Light. Because channeling the Light in undeath causes immense physical pain, he knows your abilities have atrophied. The only way to restore your mastery and return to full function is to push through the agony and exercise those spiritual muscles by mending the wounded soldiers defending Deathknell.",al={"why does aramis want this done","aramis hammerhand motive","why heal injured deathguards"},it="motive",add="8eaa6c3c"},{q="Why does Aramis need you to heal the Deathguards?",a="This task serves as your trial and discipline as a newly awakened paladin. While established healers or Aramis himself could attend to the wounded, only by personally channeling the burning agony of the Light can you rebuild your own endurance and reclaim your former powers in undeath.",al={"why me rediscovering the light","why does aramis need me to heal deathguards","why can't aramis heal them"},it="why_me",add="1e0efd99"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For an undead paladin, reconnecting with the Light tests faith and endurance. Holy vows can survive death, though the Light brings blistering agony.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you show the Forsaken's fierce resilience, turning the Light's searing torment into a disciplined weapon for survival."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","deathguard","deathknell","forsaken paladin","holy light","rediscovering the light","tirisfal glades","undead paladin"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","subzone:deathknell","topic:light","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",level="2",faction="Horde",id=90902,ri={"Injured Deathguard"}},src={"Rediscovering the Light"},fv=true}
E["quest:91208"] = {t="quest",n="Coming to Terms",z="tirisfal",s="A frightened former paladin has fled into the hills west of the chapel. Aramis Hammerhand asks a newly risen knight to reach her with compassion.",h="A frightened former paladin has fled into the hills west of the chapel.",sec={{t="A Bitter Resurrection",b="The Silver Hand's former paladins wake among the Forsaken in shock. In life, they served the Holy Light and fought the undead. Now their souls are bound to decomposing flesh. Aramis Hammerhand guides some through this change, while others flee into the Tirisfal wilderness, unable to face their new existence.",sp=0},{t="A Merciful Release",b="A panicked paladin hides in the hills west of the chapel. Aramis Hammerhand hopes a fellow knight can reach her with compassion. The weight of her transformation overwhelms her. When approached, she strikes in fear and fury, leaving no choice but to strike her down. For a Forsaken whose mind shatters upon the grave, a swift end is the only mercy left.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the frightened paladin?",a="She is a recently risen Forsaken who served as a paladin in life. Horrified to wake undead, she fled Deathknell into the nearby western hills.",al={"frightened paladin","who is the paladin in the hills","who do i find in coming to terms"},it="target"},{q="Why does the frightened paladin attack?",a="She fears becoming the kind of creature she once fought and cannot accept her new existence. Aramis warns that some newly risen paladins become violent and asks you to approach her with compassion.",al={"why does she turn hostile","why attack","can you save the frightened paladin"},sp=1,it="hostile"},{q="Who gives the quest Coming to Terms?",a="Aramis Hammerhand, a paladin mentor at the church in Deathknell, offers this guidance to newly risen knights so they can understand the fragile state of their peers.",al={"quest giver coming to terms","aramis hammerhand quest","where to start coming to terms"},it="identity"},{q="Can Forsaken still wield the Light?",a="Yes. Risen paladins like Aramis Hammerhand still serve the Light, and he hopes to guide newly risen paladins back to it.",al={"undead paladins light","do forsaken paladins use the light","undead use light"},it="power"},{q="Where is the frightened paladin located?",a="She fled west from the church in Deathknell and hid among the wooded hills overlooking the settlement.",al={"frightened paladin location","where is she","where in deathknell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing Coming to Terms?",a="You return to Aramis Hammerhand to report on your attempt to help the frightened paladin. He then sends you to further training to hone your discipline as a Forsaken paladin.",al={"next quest coming to terms","after coming to terms"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Aramis Hammerhand send you on this quest?",a="Aramis Hammerhand understands how harrowing it is for fallen holy warriors to awaken as undead. Paladins spent their mortal lives battling the Scourge, making the reality of their own resurrection nearly impossible to reconcile. Aramis hopes to save a newly risen sister with compassion, extending a sympathetic ear to guide her back to the Light before despair and madness consume her entirely.",al={"aramis hammerhand motive","why help frightened paladin","why does aramis want this done"},it="motive",add="ea9eba60"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face the horror of undeath and the struggle to accept what you have become.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see how the shock of awakening in Tirisfal can overwhelm the newly risen. Helping those in panic is part of early Forsaken life."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","coming to terms","deathknell","frightened paladin","holy light","paladin","tirisfal glades","undead paladin"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","quest:91209","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","topic:light","zone:tirisfal","quest:6381"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",level="4",faction="Horde",id=91208},src={"Coming to Terms (quest)"},fv=true}
E["quest:91209"] = {t="quest",n="Continue Your Training",z="tirisfal",s="Newly risen Forsaken paladins leave Deathknell for instruction in Brill. Aramis Hammerhand sends them east into Tirisfal Glades, where dangers and distrust await those who wield the Holy Light.",h="Newly risen Forsaken paladins leave Deathknell for instruction in Brill.",sec={{t="Leaving Deathknell",b="After learning martial combat and channeling holy power in Deathknell's graveyard, you are sent east into Tirisfal Glades. Your destination is Brill, the regional outpost and administrative hub for central Tirisfal. There, Shari Stilwell oversees the training of those who follow the path of the paladin in undeath.",sp=0},{t="A Precarious Calling",b="Aramis offers parting advice about the peril of being an undead paladin. Lordaeron still needs defenders against threats from beyond, yet wielding the Holy Light under Sylvanas Windrunner's banner draws suspicion. Many Forsaken suffered agony or death at the hands of holy zealots, and the Light's presence breeds distrust among their undead kin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where do I find them?",a="Aramis Hammerhand, the paladin trainer in Deathknell, gives it to you.",al={"quest giver","where to start","aramis hammerhand location"},gp=true},{q="Where do I turn in Continue Your Training?",a="You bring it to Shari Stilwell, the paladin trainer in Brill, east along the main road from Deathknell.",al={"where to turn in","shari stilwell location","turn in spot"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken distrust paladins?",a="Many Forsaken resent the Holy Light for the agony it causes undead bodies and for persecution by holy orders such as the Scarlet Crusade. A paladin walks close to forces many undead fear or despise.",al={"why do undead hate paladins","forsaken paladin prejudice","proximity to light"},it="hostile"},{q="Can any Forsaken class take this quest?",a="No. It is for Forsaken paladins leaving Deathknell for Brill and the wider world.",al={"is this quest paladin only","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="What is Brill?",a="Brill is a town in central Tirisfal Glades and a hub for Forsaken travelers, guards, and tradesfolk, just north of the Undercity ruins.",al={"what is brill","brill town lore"},it="place"},{q="What threats does Lordaeron face according to Aramis?",a="Aramis warns that Lordaeron faces rampaging Scourge remnants, hostile wildlife, and vengeful living factions such as the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"threats to lordaeron","why protect lordaeron"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Aramis Hammerhand want me to go to Brill?",a="Aramis recognizes that Deathknell can teach you no more. Though Lordaeron has fallen to ruin, the Forsaken must defend their reclaimed home against countless perils, and that requires fully prepared champions. To temper your holy discipline and survive in a kingdom where your brethren view your wielded Light with deep suspicion, you must continue your instruction under Shari Stilwell in Brill.",al={"why send to brill","aramis hammerhand motive","why continue your training"},it="motive",add="1d15ea77"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As an undead paladin, you may find that wielding holy power leaves you an outsider among your fellow Forsaken.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you live with tensions between loyalty to Lordaeron's soil and the lingering trauma of the Holy Light."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","brill","continue your training","deathknell","forsaken paladin","holy light","shari stilwell","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","npc:shari-stilwell","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:light","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",["end"]="Shari Stilwell",level="4",faction="Horde",id=91209},src={"Continue Your Training"},fv=true}
E["quest:95314"] = {t="quest",n="That Shadowvale Green Elixir",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Carolai Anise seeks bottles of Shadowvale's green elixir. The secluded village once distilled Whispering Elixir from local herbs, and buyers still prize the banned brew.",h="In Brill, Carolai Anise seeks bottles of Shadowvale's green elixir.",sec={{t="A Banned Brew",b="Before the Scourge came, Shadowvale's secluded villagers brewed Whispering Elixir from rare herbs found only in Tirisfal Glades. The draught became known across northern Lordaeron. Though the Capital City outlawed it, mystics, poisoners, and apothecaries still sought its unusual properties, even at the risk of defying royal decrees.",sp=0},{t="Ruins in the Whispering Forest",b="Shadowvale lies deep in the Whispering Forest of western Tirisfal. Its people were insular and distrustful, and rarely welcomed outsiders. The Scourge invasion left the settlement in ruins, but forgotten stores of aged green elixir remain among the wreckage. Carolai Anise works from Brill, where she answers the underworld's lasting demand by paying adventurers willing to brave the forest's unsettling silence.",sp=0},{t="The Whispering Curse",b="Carolai Anise dismisses the rumors as superstition, but the Whispering Forest has a dark reputation. Local lore says an ancient curse taints the soil and roots, and seeps into the plants Shadowvale's brewers harvested. Whatever malevolence lingers around the abandoned hamlet, distant buyers still hunger for its bottled remnants.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Shadowvale?",a="Shadowvale was a secluded village deep in the Whispering Forest of western Tirisfal Glades. Its secretive people distilled rare brews from local herbs before the Scourge overran the region.",al={"where is shadowvale","who lived in shadowvale","shadowvale village"},it="place"},{q="What is Whispering Elixir?",a="Whispering Elixir is a potent green draught brewed from herbs found only in Tirisfal. Mystics, poisoners, and apothecaries sought it, though the Capital City outlawed it before Lordaeron fell.",al={"what does the elixir do","shadowvale green elixir lore","whispering elixir"},it="item"},{q="Who is Carolai Anise?",a="Carolai Anise is a Forsaken resident of Brill. She brokers valuable banned curios, including Shadowvale's elixir, for buyers across the realm.",al={"carolai anise","who gives that shadowvale green elixir quest","brill quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the elixir banned in the Capital City?",a="No reason for the ban is given. Carolai says only that the elixir was outlawed in the city, though apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners sought it. Some blame a curse in the Whispering Forest and its roots, but Carolai dismisses that as superstition and never links it to the ban.",al={"why was whispering elixir illegal","is the elixir poison"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Whispering Forest considered dangerous?",a="The secluded woods west of Deathknell are considered eerie and cursed. Those who venture there speak of deep malevolence and strange woodland phenomena, and rumors say the forest's soil tainted its herbs.",al={"is whispering forest cursed","whispering forest lore"},it="danger"},{q="Who are the buyers wanting this elixir?",a="Carolai Anise says several buyers seek surviving bottles from before the war, but she does not name them.",al={"who buys the elixir","carolai anise buyers"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Carolai Anise want the Whispering Elixir collected?",a="Carolai Anise operates as a procurer of rare goods in Brill, and demand for the illicit brew has never truly died out. With numerous eager buyers pressing her for shipments, there is considerable profit to be made from whatever bottles remain intact among the ruins.",al={"why does carolai want the elixir","carolai anise motive","why collect whispering elixir"},it="motive",add="4d019fa8"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you among the Forsaken, recovering Lordaeron's forgotten brews can bring profit and fuel apothecary experiments in the fledgling Undercity.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know Whispering Elixir was prized by poisoners and scoundrels who worked beyond the notice of Lordaeron's former magistrates.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know the elixir draws its potency from rare herbs that grow only beneath the Whispering Forest's eerie canopy."},kw={"apothecary","brill","carolai anise","poison","shadowvale","tirisfal","whispering elixir","whispering forest"},rel={"npc:carolai-anise","subzone:whispering-forest","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Carolai Anise",level="10",faction="Horde",id=95314,ri={"Bottle of Whispering Elixir"}},src={"That Shadowvale Green Elixir"},fv=true}
E["quest:96656"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="tirisfal",s="Near Deathknell, The Adventurer is sent to investigate a stranger by the road to Brill. Scarlet Crusaders threaten the region, but the stranger is Eleanor Shackleton, a Forsaken traveler with wilderness skills to share.",h="Near Deathknell, The Adventurer is sent to investigate a stranger by the road to Brill.",sec={{t="A Suspicious Watch",b="Executor Arren watches Deathknell and the roads around it. Scarlet Crusaders spy on the region and infiltrate northern Lordaeron, so an unfamiliar figure near Brill draws suspicion. You have proved your dedication by striking at Crusader threats along the border. Now Arren asks you to investigate the stranger quietly and learn whether she threatens the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="A Traveler in the Woods",b="You find Eleanor Shackleton by the roadside near Brill. She is a Forsaken traveler, pausing before another journey into the wilds, with no Crusader plot or Scourge necromancy in mind. Eleanor sees a fellow adventurer in those sent to check on her. She offers to teach you how to survive in open country and make camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Executor Arren want Eleanor investigated?",a="Scarlet Crusade infiltrators and hostile spies threaten Deathknell and Brill. Arren treats anyone unfamiliar on the high road with suspicion until their purpose is clear.",al={"why investigate eleanor","who sent me to eleanor","arren eleanor task"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Eleanor Shackleton?",a="Eleanor Shackleton is a Forsaken adventurer camping by the road near Brill. She explores the wilderness and offers fellow travelers practical survival skills.",al={"who is eleanor","eleanor shackleton lore","who is the adventurer npc"},it="target"},{q="Is Eleanor connected to the Scarlet Crusade?",a="No. Eleanor has no ties to the Scarlet Crusade, whose zealots threaten Tirisfal Glades.",al={"is eleanor scarlet crusade","eleanor enemy","is eleanor a spy"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest lead?",a="Speaking with Eleanor leads to The Great Outdoors, where she begins teaching you wilderness survival and how to make camp.",al={"what comes after the adventurer","next quest after adventurer","eleanor shackleton follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Where can Eleanor Shackleton be found?",a="Eleanor camps just off the main road east toward Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"eleanor location","where is eleanor shackleton","eleanor camp tirisfal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why did Executor Arren choose you for this mission?",a="You earned Arren's trust by rooting out Scarlet Crusade agents and messengers near Deathknell. That work showed you could handle sensitive reconnaissance.",al={"why pick me","arren trust","why executor arren sends you"},it="why_me"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For a new Forsaken near Deathknell, meeting Eleanor, a fellow adventurer, shows that a stranger near Brill may be no Scarlet spy.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can gain practical survival skills by speaking with wandering travelers while Executor Arren guards the Forsaken realm's young borders."},kw={"brill","camping","deathknell","eleanor shackleton","executor arren","scarlet crusade","the adventurer","the great outdoors","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:eleanor-shackleton","npc:executor-arren","quest:96607","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={start="Executor Arren",["end"]="Eleanor Shackleton",level="6",faction="Horde",id=96656},src={"The Adventurer (Tirisfal Glades)"},fv=true}
E["quest:97558"] = {t="quest",n="Hides for the Forsaken",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, the Forsaken gather animal skins to mend their ruined flesh. Shelene Rhobart asks you to bring darkhound hides, duskbat wing membranes, and murloc skin.",h="In Tirisfal, the Forsaken gather animal skins to mend their ruined flesh.",sec={{t="The Price of Undeath",b="Forsaken flesh cannot heal on its own. A wound leaves a rotting gap, and the body cannot close it through natural means. To keep their forms intact, the Forsaken stitch living tissue over their injuries and keep their corpses working.",sp=0},{t="Specialized Materials",b="Different materials mend different parts of the body. Thick darkhound hide suits broad repairs that need to hold firm. Duskbat wing membranes are thin and pliable, covering faces and fingers without making them stiff. Vile Fin murloc skin lines inner membranes and sensitive places such as cheeks and mouths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Forsaken need animal skins?",a="Forsaken skin cannot heal or grow back after an injury. They harvest skins and membranes from living creatures to cover wounds and slow the decay.",al={"why forsaken need hides","undead healing lore","do undead heal"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Shelene Rhobart?",a="Shelene Rhobart is a Forsaken leatherworker in Tirisfal Glades. She gathers hides and other materials so the wounded can mend their rotting forms.",al={"shelene rhobart","who is shelene"},it="identity"},{q="Why are duskbat wing membranes specifically needed?",a="Duskbat wing membranes are thin and supple. They cover delicate places such as faces and fingers without making the skin too thick or stiff.",al={"duskbat wings use","why duskbat membrane"},it="item"},{q="What is murloc skin used for?",a="Vile Fin murloc skin lines inner membranes and delicate surfaces, including the inside of cheeks and mouths.",al={"why murloc skin","murloc skin undead"},it="item"},{q="Where are these materials found?",a="Darkhounds, duskbats, and Vile Fin murlocs roam Tirisfal Glades. Darkhounds and duskbats haunt the woods and roadsides, while Vile Fin murlocs gather along the northern coast and inland waterways.",al={"where to get hides","tirisfal beasts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is using animal hides common for the Forsaken?",a="Yes. The Forsaken rely on animal tissue and scavenged remains to keep going. Without replacement flesh and hides, wounds can leave bones, organs, and muscles exposed.",al={"do all forsaken use hides","forsaken fleshcraft"}},{q="What is the Darkhound Hide used for?",a="Undead flesh does not naturally heal from injury, forcing the Forsaken to patch their bodies with harvested beast hides. While delicate tissues require thin membranes, thicker and hardier pelts like darkhound hide serve as durable grafts for broad, heavy-wear surfaces across the body that require tough, resilient replacement skin.",al={"darkhound hide use","why darkhound hide","darkhound hide forsaken"},it="item",add="84f1a52c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you face the burdens of the Forsaken condition: keeping your body intact takes constant work and scavenged grafts, not natural healing.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can use your stitching to bind beast membranes to decaying bodies as well as to make garments."},kw={"darkhound hide","duskbat wing","hides for the forsaken","shelene rhobart","tirisfal glades","undead graft","vile fin murloc"},rel={"npc:shelene-rhobart","zone:tirisfal","item:duskbat-wing","topic:murloc"},m={start="Shelene Rhobart",level="11",faction="Horde",id=97558,ri={"Darkhound Hide","Duskbat Wing Membrane","Vile Fin Murloc Skin"}},src={"Hides for the Forsaken"},fv=true}
E["quest:97957"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal, Eleanor Shackleton sends new herbalists to Faruza in Brill to learn a useful craft. Incense Candles give spellcasters help as they rest at camps in the wild.",h="In Tirisfal, Eleanor Shackleton sends new herbalists to Faruza in Brill to learn a useful craft.",sec={{t="Flora for the Camp",b="Herbalism gives alchemists their first materials, but travelers also depend on gathered roots and blossoms. Regional master herbalists teach aspiring foragers to prepare Incense Candles. In Tirisfal Glades, Eleanor Shackleton points promising foragers toward Faruza in Brill once they show basic skill.",sp=0},{t="Sustenance for the Mind",b="Long travel wears on spellcasters and spiritualists. Incense Candles release restorative fragrances to lift spirits and soothe tired minds. Gatherers infuse dried plants into the candles, helping healers and mages whose magical reserves falter on the road.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Herbalists build their skill so a trainer can teach them to make Incense Candles. The candles help spellcasters while they rest in wilderness camps.",al={"why do camping herbalism","what does camping 101 give","camping 101 herbalism objective"}},{q="Who offers this quest in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Eleanor Shackleton guides herbalists in Tirisfal Glades and points them toward Faruza in Brill.",al={"who gives camping 101 herbalism tirisfal","eleanor shackleton quest"}},{q="What does an Incense Candle do?",a="Incense Candles lift spirits and help healers and magic users recover their mental focus while resting in the field.",al={"incense candle effect","what are incense candles for"}},{q="Who teaches the Incense Candle recipe?",a="Local herbalism trainers teach the recipe to qualified herbalists. In Tirisfal Glades, Faruza teaches in Brill; Jandi teaches in Orgrimmar, Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge, and Malorne Bladeleaf in Dolanaar.",al={"who teaches camping herbalism","where to turn in camping 101 herbalism"}},{q="Can members of other factions and races take this quest?",a="Yes. Other guides and trainers give herbalists across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms the same instruction as Eleanor Shackleton and Faruza give travelers in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"is camping 101 horde only","alliance camping 101 herbalism"}},{q="What skill requirement is needed to complete the training?",a="Herbalists need a skill of twenty before a trainer will teach them the candle recipe.",al={"how much herbalism needed","camping 101 skill level"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists can aid traveling groups by making fragrant Incense Candles for their camps, alongside brewing potions and gathering stalks.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken travelers from Deathknell and Brill, you can learn from Faruza to make practical use of Tirisfal's withered plants.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you value herbalists who make Incense Candles. Their soothing smoke helps restore focus and spirits far from taverns."},kw={"brill","camping","eleanor shackleton","faruza","herbalism","incense candle","tirisfal"},rel={"npc:eleanor-shackleton","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","zone:orgrimmar","zone:thunderbluff","zone:ironforge","subzone:dolanaar"},m={level="6",id=97957},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism","Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97960"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, new skinners learn how to make a chair for camp from harvested hides. The lesson points them toward craftsmen who teach the trade across Azeroth.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, new skinners learn how to make a chair for camp from harvested hides.",sec={{t="Comfort in the Wilds",b="A sharp blade is not enough to last in the wilds; you also need to know how to save your strength between trials. Adventurers can build basic skill in the field and use treated skins to make camp chairs. Those comforts give weary travelers a place to rest and recover before facing danger again.",sp=0},{t="Mastering the Craft",b="Young Forsaken skinners in Tirisfal Glades who reach their first measure of skill are sent to Rand Rhobart. He works along the road between Brill and the Capital ruins of the Undercity. Rhobart teaches practical ways to turn rough leather into a seat for camp. Skinning masters across the lands of the Horde and Alliance teach the same craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The lesson sends new skinners to a skilled trade mentor, who teaches them to make a camp chair from harvested animal pelts.",al={"what does camping 101 skinning do","why do camping 101 skinning","camping 101 reward"}},{q="Who offers this training in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Eleanor Shackleton gives the lesson in Tirisfal Glades and points new skinners toward Rand Rhobart, along the road between Brill and the Undercity.",al={"who gives quest tirisfal","eleanor shackleton quest"}},{q="What skill level is required to complete this task?",a="You need a skinning skill of at least twenty before a trainer will teach you to make equipment for camp.",al={"what skinning level do i need","camping 101 skinning requirements","skinning skill required"}},{q="Where can Rand Rhobart be found?",a="Rand Rhobart works along the main road south from Brill toward the entrance to the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"rand rhobart location","where is rand rhobart","rand rhobart tirisfal"}},{q="Can members of other factions learn this technique?",a="Yes. Forsaken learn from Rand Rhobart, while other instructors teach skinners in Goldshire, Ironforge, Dolanaar, Orgrimmar, Bloodhoof Village, and Shen'dar Village.",al={"is this horde only","can alliance do camping 101 skinning","alliance skinning camp chair"}},{q="Why is crafting a camp chair useful?",a="A camp chair gives you a comfortable place to sit and regain your strength in the wilds, helping you stay rested and alert for battles ahead.",al={"what does a camp chair do","why make camp chair"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may be free from mortal exhaustion, but a working camp remains useful while you hunt the plagued beasts of Tirisfal.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can make use of every part of a slain beast, leaving nothing to waste along the hard road."},kw={"brill","camp chair","camping","eleanor shackleton","rand rhobart","skinning","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"npc:eleanor-shackleton","subzone:brill","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal","subzone:goldshire","subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:orgrimmar","zone:ironforge"},m={level="6",id=97960},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning","Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:98389"] = {t="quest",n="A Light in the Darkness",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, Aramis Hammerhand asks you to save newly raised Forsaken from Night's Web Hollow. Your aid can show that wielders of the Holy Light remain loyal to Sylvanas and their people.",h="In Deathknell, Aramis Hammerhand asks you to save newly raised Forsaken from Night's Web Hollow.",sec={{t="A Precarious Faith",b="Some Forsaken still wield the Holy Light they knew in life, though its power brings pain to the undead. In Deathknell, Aramis Hammerhand and others seek to prove their faith has not turned them against their own people. They use their gifts to protect the Forsaken and ease fears that holy wielders see their kin as monsters.",sp=0},{t="Night's Web Hollow",b="Northwest of Deathknell, Night's Web Hollow is a dank cavern crawling with vicious spiders. Newly raised Forsaken often stumble inside, disoriented and unable to defend themselves, and become trapped in sticky webbing. Saving them brings new recruits to the Dark Lady and may convince Executor Arren that wielders of the Light serve the Forsaken faithfully.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Light in the Darkness?",a="Aramis Hammerhand, a holy practitioner in Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades, asks you to help.",al={"quest giver","who starts a light in the darkness","aramis hammerhand quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Night's Web Hollow located?",a="Night's Web Hollow lies northwest of Deathknell in the hills of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"nights web hollow location","where are the webbed victims","where is the cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken distrust wielders of the Light?",a="The Holy Light sears undead flesh, and many Forsaken fear its wielders see them as abominations to destroy instead of kin.",al={"why fear the light","why do forsaken hate paladins","forsaken holy fear"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the victims trapped in the webs?",a="The victims are newly awakened Forsaken adventurers who wandered into the spider caves before finding their bearings.",al={"who is webbed","what is inside the webs","trapped victims"},it="target"},{q="Who is Executor Arren, and why does Aramis want to impress him?",a="Executor Arren oversees military and civic order in Deathknell. Aramis seeks his trust so holy wielders can integrate smoothly into the Forsaken forces.",al={"who is executor arren","why arren matters"}},{q="Can the undead really wield the Holy Light?",a="Yes. Some undead retain their bond with the Light through great will and devotion, though wielding it causes immense discomfort and earns suspicion from their own people.",al={"can forsaken use light","undead light lore"},it="power"},{q="Why does Aramis Hammerhand want the webbed victims freed?",a="Aramis wants to prove to his fellow Forsaken that undead who wield the Holy Light are not a threat to their own kind. Many in Deathknell, including Executor Arren, fear or suspect that Light-wielders will turn their powers upon other undead as monstrosities. By rescuing freshly raised Forsaken from the spiders of Night's Web Hollow, Aramis hopes to demonstrate that their power exists to protect the Forsaken and serve the Dark Lady's vision.",al={"aramis hammerhand motive","why free the webbed victims","why does aramis want this done"},it="motive",add="f946e0be"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see the inner struggles of your people, where the newly risen may face prejudice from their own kin.",["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you walk a difficult path between the faith you held in life and the harsh reality of undeath."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","deathknell","executor arren","forsaken","holy light","night's web hollow","tirisfal glades","webbed victims"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","subzone:deathknell","npc:executor-arren","topic:light","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",level="4",faction="Horde",id=98389,ri={"Webbed Forsaken"}},src={"A Light in the Darkness (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:98601"] = {t="quest",n="A Difficult Path",z="tirisfal",s="In Deathknell, a newly awakened Forsaken paladin begins training with the Light. After facing the undead outside the crypt, you are sent to the village church to meet Aramis Hammerhand and learn what holy power demands of the Forsaken.",h="In Deathknell, a newly awakened Forsaken paladin begins training with the Light.",sec={{t="A Reeking Scroll",b="After you clear feral undead from outside the crypt, Shadow Priest Sarvis gives you an unexpected delivery. The Consecrated Scroll shines with holy energy, and Sarvis recoils before asking you to step aside. For one devoted to shadow and decay, the Holy Light burns like an open flame.",sp=0},{t="The Crucible of Holy Fire",b="Aramis Hammerhand waits inside Deathknell’s desecrated church to train Forsaken paladins. Other races may wield the Light with ease and joy, but the undead endure searing agony when they call upon it. Aramis speaks plainly: channeling holy power through a rotting body is torment. He expects his disciples to face that pain instead of shrinking from it, and let it temper their resolve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Shadow Priest Sarvis dislike the scroll?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis serves shadow magic, and the Consecrated Scroll radiates holy energy that is hostile to undead flesh. Its presence unsettles those devoted to the Shadow.",al={"sarvis holy scroll","why is sarvis uneasy","shadow priest reacts to scroll"}},{q="Can Forsaken truly wield the Holy Light without dying?",a="Yes. Forsaken can wield the Light through willpower and faith, but channeling it causes intense pain, especially when healing themselves or others. It takes great mental endurance.",al={"forsaken paladins lore","undead using the light","does the light hurt forsaken"}},{q="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand trains paladins in Deathknell. He teaches newly risen Forsaken to endure the pain of wielding the Light in undeath and make it an effective weapon.",al={"who is aramis hammerhand","deathknell paladin trainer","aramis role"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You meet Shadow Priest Sarvis in Deathknell’s central clearing, then go a short distance to the village’s ruined chapel, where Aramis Hammerhand lives.",al={"where is a difficult path","quest location","where is deathknell church"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do I have to read the Consecrated Scroll to complete the quest?",a="No. You can speak to Aramis Hammerhand inside the church without reading the Consecrated Scroll, and your training advances.",al={"read consecrated scroll","is scroll reading required","skip reading scroll"},gp=true},{q="Why is the path called 'difficult'?",a="The name reflects the hardship of being a Forsaken paladin. Other warriors of the Light find comfort in their faith, while an undead paladin endures holy fire burning through dead flesh with every blessing or strike.",al={"why difficult path","meaning of quest name"}},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Sarvis want this done?",a="Sarvis merely wants the Holy Light out of his sight. The consecrated scroll arrived for you while you were culling the mindless Scourge, and its radiant magic naturally offends his shadow-touched senses. Rather than lingering around its presence or dealing with a budding paladin, he directs you to report to your own trainer, Aramis Hammerhand, so you can begin learning how to hone your painful discipline.",al={"why does sarvis send me to aramis","sarvis motive difficult path","why give me the scroll sarvis"},it="motive",add="6833d98f"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a first trial that makes holy power an agony to endure, demanding discipline and resolve.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can call upon the Light through devotion and discipline, though its power burns the dead flesh that channels it."},kw={"a difficult path","aramis hammerhand","consecrated scroll","deathknell","forsaken paladin","holy light","shadow priest sarvis","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:light","topic:scourge"},m={start="Shadow Priest Sarvis",["end"]="Aramis Hammerhand",level="1",faction="Horde",id=98601},src={"A Difficult Path (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:99134"] = {t="quest",n="Discipline",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Zygand turns to outsiders in Tirisfal Glades to keep his Deathguard sentries alert. He has little faith in the garrison and orders physical punishment for those who slacken.",h="Executor Zygand turns to outsiders in Tirisfal Glades to keep his Deathguard sentries alert.",sec={{t="Enforcing Order in Undeath",b="The Deathguard guard the Forsaken across Lordaeron. Freedom from the Lich King's control has brought its own troubles: apathy, fatigue, and neglect. Executor Zygand has little patience for sentries who let their discipline slip. The Scarlet Crusade and Scourge prowl Tirisfal's borders, and the garrison must stay ready. Its officers use force and close oversight to keep the troops alert.",sp=0},{t="The Executor's Ledger",b="Executor Zygand chooses outsiders to punish negligent Deathguards instead of using soldiers from his own garrison. With the Executor's Motivator, you remind sentries that service to the Dark Lady demands constant vigilance. Even in undeath, they cannot escape the consequences of neglecting their duties.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Discipline quest?",a="Executor Zygand gives the order in Tirisfal Glades, where he oversees the region's defenses and demands obedience from his troops.",al={"discipline quest giver","who starts discipline","executor zygand quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want the Deathguard punished?",a="Zygand considers his Deathguards incompetent and lacking drive. He believes their complacency endangers the Forsaken in Tirisfal, so he uses harsh punishment to rouse the sentries.",al={"why hit deathguards","why motivate deathguard","zygand deathguard reason"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Zygand use an adventurer instead of another soldier?",a="Zygand says you have not yet joined the Deathguard, so you have not had the chance to disappoint him.",al={"why me discipline","why use outsiders zygand"},it="why_me"},{q="What is the Executor's Motivator?",a="The Executor's Motivator is a disciplinary tool Zygand gives you to punish idle Deathguards stationed across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"executors motivator","what is the motivator zygand"},it="item"},{q="What happens if you refuse Zygand's order?",a="Zygand warns that if you hesitate or refuse, he will enter your name in his ledger and send someone else to discipline you.",al={"zygand threats","ledger threat zygand"},gp=true},{q="How do the Forsaken view pain?",a="Zygand counts pain among the few pleasures still open to him in death. His delight in punishment reflects his harsh nature.",al={"do undead feel pain","forsaken pain lore"}},{q="Who are the Deathguards you are punishing?",a="The Deathguard are the standing military and sentinels of the Forsaken, tasked with defending Tirisfal Glades and enforcing the Dark Lady's rule. Executor Zygand views those stationed around Brill and the outlying posts as lazy and incompetent, demanding that they be reminded through physical chastisement of their sworn duty to protect Forsaken lands.",al={"who are the deathguards","deathguard targets discipline","who do i discipline"},it="target",add="ae86ed1b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, discipline means survival. Sentries who give in to apathy put all of Tirisfal Glades at risk.",["faction:Horde"]="Forsaken commanders use grim methods, reflecting the harsh rule of the Horde's northern lands."},kw={"dark lady","deathguard","discipline","executor zygand","forsaken","motivator","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="6",faction="Horde",id=99134,ri={"Deathguards"}},src={"Discipline (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:99141"] = {t="quest",n="Patience",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, Executor Zygand waits for overdue field reports. He sends you to gather updates from Deathguards near Brill and a sentry by Stillwater Pond.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, Executor Zygand waits for overdue field reports.",sec={{t="Enforcing the Dark Lady's Will",b="Executor Zygand commands local security in Tirisfal Glades and allows no lapse in vigilance. Serving Lady Sylvanas, he expects every duty done without fail. When scheduled field reports do not reach his post, he treats the delay as a breach of duty. He stays at his post and sends Forsaken agents to find the tardy subordinates and keep the borders secure.",sp=0},{t="Sentinels of the Glades",b="Sentries at key points around Brill owe Zygand their reports. Deathguard Dillinger watches the graveyard west of town, where rogue undead and Scourge remnants stir. East of Brill, Deathguard Kristof guards a waystation on the approaches to the Capital City and the eastern roads. Gordo is the strangest sentry: a hulking abomination who wanders near Stillwater Pond, where military record-keeping seems a poor fit for his simple mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand commands security around Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He serves in the Forsaken command hierarchy under Lady Sylvanas and demands flawless work from the troops under his watch.",al={"zygand","who is zygand","executor zygand role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Zygand send an adventurer to collect reports?",a="Several field sentries have missed their scheduled reports. Zygand stays at his central post and sends newly proven Forsaken to collect the overdue dispatches across the countryside.",al={"why do patience","why fetch reports"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Gordo and why does he have a report?",a="Gordo is an abomination who wanders near Stillwater Pond. Zygand expected a report from him like those of the other sentries, then saw the folly of expecting written intelligence from an abomination.",al={"gordo","why does an abomination have a report","who is gordo"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Where is Deathguard Dillinger located?",a="Deathguard Dillinger watches near the graveyard west of Brill, where he monitors Scourge activity and newly risen corpses.",al={"dillinger location","find dillinger","where is dillinger"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where is Deathguard Kristof stationed?",a="Deathguard Kristof guards a waystation on the road east of Brill, watching the approaches and road traffic.",al={"kristof location","find kristof","where is kristof"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens when Gordo's report is turned in?",a="Zygand admits that expecting a coherent written report from an abomination was foolish. He accepts the outcome quietly and asks you to keep the embarrassing mistake between you and him.",al={"gordo report outcome","gordo writing"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want these reports collected?",a="Executor Zygand is tasked with upholding the Dark Lady's will and maintaining strict oversight of Brill's defenses. When sentinels and scouts fail to submit their status dispatches on schedule, it compromises the Forsaken's readiness and risks incurring Sylvanas's displeasure. Zygand demands swift compliance to maintain ironclad discipline.",al={"zygand motive","why does zygand want reports","why patience quest"},it="motive",add="e0ff4089"},{q="What is Deathguard Dillinger's Report for?",a="Dillinger's Report conveys the current security situation around the Brill cemetery just west of town. Stationed near the graveyard to watch for threats and disturbances, Deathguard Dillinger is expected to keep Executor Zygand informed about local unrest and perimeter stability.",al={"dillinger's report","what is dillingers report","dillinger report purpose"},it="item",add="cb8b3e87"},{q="What is Deathguard Kristof's Report for?",a="Kristof's Report details patrol activity and roadway conditions around the eastern waystation. Deathguard Kristof watches the passage leading east through Tirisfal Glades, and his dispatch provides Executor Zygand with critical intelligence on traffic and approaching dangers.",al={"kristof's report","what is kristofs report","kristof report purpose"},it="item",add="744f946d"},{q="What is Gordo's Report for?",a="Gordo's Report is supposed to offer an accounting of the area around Stillwater Pond to the west, where the abomination lumbers on patrol. Though Executor Zygand expects written reconnaissance, the simple-minded brute struggles with the concept of military dispatches.",al={"gordo's report","what is gordos report","gordo report purpose"},it="item",add="79b1ee7a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly liberated Forsaken, carrying out Zygand's orders shows the harsh terms of survival in Lordaeron: devotion to the Dark Lady and no tolerance for failure.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally, you see the grim discipline Sylvanas Windrunner's officers enforce throughout Tirisfal."},kw={"brill","dark lady","deathguard","dillinger","gordo","kristof","patience","stillwater pond","tirisfal glades","zygand"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:stillwater-pond","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="6",faction="Horde",id=99141,ri={"Dillinger's Report","Gordo's Report","Kristof's Report"}},src={"Patience (quest)"},fv=true}
E["quest:99142"] = {t="quest",n="Tomb Weed",z="tirisfal",s="At Balnir Farmstead, Holland's altered doom weed now draws the Scourge. The crop has become a new specimen called tomb weed, and Holland wants it for his experiments.",h="At Balnir Farmstead, Holland's altered doom weed now draws the Scourge.",sec={{t="Holland's Cultivation",b="Junior Apothecary Holland wants more than a place among the Royal Apothecary Society. He gathers doom weed, makes small alchemical changes, and replants it in the soil of Balnir Farmstead. There, he has cultivated a new strain he calls tomb weed. Holland sees the hybrid as the heart of his work and a sign of the future he seeks for himself.",sp=0},{t="Unintended Attraction",b="Holland expected his altered plants to gain alchemical potency, but the Scourge wandering Balnir Farmstead have taken an unexpected interest in them. He now depends on travelers to push past the undead and gather the mature crop, so his experiments can continue.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is tomb weed?",a="Tomb weed is a strain of doom weed that Junior Apothecary Holland has altered through alchemy. He plants the treated herb in the blighted soil of Balnir Farmstead.",al={"what is tomb weed","tomb weed lore","tomb weed plant"}},{q="Who is Junior Apothecary Holland?",a="Junior Apothecary Holland belongs to the Royal Apothecary Society and works in Tirisfal Glades. Ambitious and often frustrated by assistants such as the abomination Gordo, he pursues private plant and alchemical experiments to advance his standing.",al={"who is holland","junior apothecary holland","apothecary holland"}},{q="Where is tomb weed grown?",a="Holland grows his altered crops at Balnir Farmstead, an abandoned estate in eastern Tirisfal Glades that has fallen into blight and ruin.",al={"where to find tomb weed","tomb weed location","balnir farmstead weed"}},{q="Why are the Scourge attracted to tomb weed?",a="Holland has seen the mindless Scourge at Balnir Farmstead drawn to the altered plant, but he does not know why and finds it curious.",al={"why scourge want tomb weed","scourge drawn to tomb weed","scourge reaction"}},{q="How does tomb weed differ from normal doom weed?",a="Doom weed grows naturally near the mass gravesite north of the Brill graveyard. Holland creates tomb weed by altering doom weed through alchemy and replanting it in farmstead soil.",al={"doom weed vs tomb weed","difference doom weed tomb weed"}},{q="Who is Gordo mentioned by Holland?",a="Gordo is a wandering abomination created by the Forsaken who roams Tirisfal Glades' roads. Holland often gives him simple tasks that prove difficult for his sluggish mind.",al={"who is gordo","gordo run in","gordo tirisfal"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see Holland's work in the Forsaken apothecaries' drive to reshape Tirisfal's blighted plants for alchemy.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know alchemical treatment can change a blighted herb such as doom weed and its behavior."},kw={"balnir farmstead","doom weed","gordo","junior apothecary holland","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades","tomb weed"},rel={"quest:5482","subzone:balnir-farmstead","quest:1882","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={level="11",id=99142},src={"In-game quest text: Tomb Weed"},fv=true}
E["quest:99156"] = {t="quest",n="Rear Guard Patrol",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Linnea calls patrollers to defend Tirisfal Glades. She sends them after Riptear, an abomination roaming near Venomweb Vale that should never have passed the Bulwark.",h="Deathguard Linnea calls patrollers to defend Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="The Breach at the Border",b="The Bulwark is the sole fortified barrier between Tirisfal Glades and the horrors of the Western Plaguelands. Forsaken military strategy depends on fighting on one front. If mindless undead slip behind the lines, they can choke the supply routes feeding the front. Stray spirits or ghouls sometimes bypass the barricades, but an abomination roaming the glades signals a grave failure of containment.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Riptear",b="Riptear, a rogue abomination, was sighted near Venomweb Vale. Abominations are massive engines of slaughter, stitched from corpses through dark necromancy. Such a creature cannot pass through fortified chokepoints unseen, and its presence leaves Deathguard Linnea deeply unsettled. She demands Riptear's heart as proof that the creature has been destroyed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the Rear Guard Patrol quest?",a="Deathguard Linnea, a Forsaken Deathguard in Tirisfal Glades, issues the patrol order and reports to Executor Zygand.",al={"who gives rear guard patrol","rear guard patrol questgiver","who gives this quest"}},{q="What is Riptear?",a="Riptear is a rogue abomination found roaming the eastern glades near Venomweb Vale, behind the forward defensive lines.",al={"who is riptear","what is riptear","riptear lore"}},{q="Why is an abomination near Venomweb Vale so alarming?",a="Abominations take dark necromancy and heavy labor to create. One slipping unnoticed through the heavily fortified Bulwark suggests a grave breach or an unseen path behind Forsaken lines.",al={"why is riptear a big deal","why is an abomination dangerous here","bulwark breach"}},{q="Where is the beast usually found?",a="Riptear has been sighted roaming the woods and clearings of eastern Tirisfal Glades near Venomweb Vale.",al={"where is riptear","riptear location","where to find the abomination"}},{q="What proof is required to finish the patrol?",a="Deathguard Linnea requires Riptear's Heart as proof that the massive abomination has been put down for good.",al={"what do i bring linnea","quest turn in item","proof of riptear death"}},{q="Who oversees the defense of the Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark's commander is not named. Deathguard Linnea answers to Executor Zygand in Brill, who receives her commendations for patrols that keep the Scourge at bay.",al={"who is in charge of bulwark","linneas superior","executor zygand"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Securing Tirisfal's eastern border protects the supply lines to the Bulwark and the Undercity from rogue horrors.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Forsaken cannot fight on two fronts. Any Scourge construct roaming behind their barricades threatens the kingdom's survival."},kw={"abomination","bulwark","deathguard linnea","rear guard patrol","riptear","tirisfal glades","venomweb vale"},rel={"npc:deathguard-linnea","subzone:bulwark","subzone:venomweb-vale","npc:executor-zygand","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal","subzone:balnir-farmstead","quest:1882"},m={level="13",id=99156},src={"In-game quest text: Rear Guard Patrol","Rear Guard Patrol"},fv=true}
E["subzone:agamand-family-crypt"] = {t="subzone",n="Agamand Family Crypt",z="tirisfal",s="The Scourge holds the Agamand Family Crypt just north of Agamand Mills. It was the ancient resting ground of one of Tirisfal's wealthiest farming dynasties, but Captain Dargol has opened its tombs and raised the ancestors as mindless terrors.",h="The Scourge holds the Agamand Family Crypt just north of Agamand Mills.",sec={{t="Restless Ancestors",b="The Agamand family once held broad estates across northern Tirisfal Glades, and buried their ancestors in this hillside crypt. The Plague ruined the kingdom, and Captain Dargol, an agent of the Scourge, seized the tombs. Through dark necromancy, he awakened the Agamand dead as vengeful skeletons and apparitions. Their restless forms now make the family burial ground a Scourge foothold beside Forsaken territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Agamand Family Crypt located?",a="You’ll find the crypt carved into a hillside just north of Agamand Mills, in northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"agamand crypt location","where is the crypt","how to find agamand crypt"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls the crypt right now?",a="Captain Dargol controls the crypt for the Scourge and commands the raised dead.",al={"who is in agamand crypt","crypt boss","captain dargol"},it="in_charge"},{q="What will I encounter inside the crypt?",a="Awakened skeletons and vengeful spirits of the Agamand ancestors fill the crypt. Dark magic drives them to attack anyone who enters the tombs.",al={"crypt enemies","what is inside agamand crypt","agamand crypt mobs"},it="threat"},{q="Are the undead inside the crypt allied with the Forsaken?",a="No. The dead in the crypt serve the Scourge under Captain Dargol and are hostile to Forsaken and living travelers alike.",al={"are they forsaken","agamand crypt friendly","why attack undead"},it="side"},{q="What is the Agamand Family Crypt?",a="The Agamand Family Crypt is the ancestral burial vault of the Agamand lineage, situated just north of their expansive mills in Tirisfal Glades. Once a quiet sanctuary meant to grant eternal rest to the noble family, it has fallen into darkness following the Scourge's conquest of Lordaeron.",al={"what is agamand family crypt","agamand crypt info","what is this crypt"},it="place",add="1e347eab"},{q="What happened at the Agamand Family Crypt?",a="When the Scourge swept across northern Lordaeron, the Agamand estate was shattered and its burial grounds defiled. A servant of the Lich King named Captain Dargol claimed the crypt, using necromancy to awaken the corpses and ancestral spirits of the Agamand line into mindless, vengeful servitude.",al={"agamand crypt history","what happened to agamand crypt","history of agamand crypt"},it="history",add="2b90d8b5"},{q="Is the Agamand Family Crypt dangerous?",a="Yes, it is exceptionally perilous. The dusty halls crawl with raised undead and vengeful specters twisted by necromantic magic. Controlled by Captain Dargol, these spirits and walking corpses violently assault anyone foolish enough to breach the tomb unbidden.",al={"is agamand crypt dangerous","agamand crypt danger","how dangerous is agamand crypt"},it="danger",add="1ce0db9b"},{q="Why is it called the Agamand Family Crypt?",a="It bears the name of the Agamands, a prominent human family of Lordaeron who owned and operated the nearby Agamand Mills. The vault was constructed to house the remains of multiple generations of their ancestors before the fall of the kingdom.",al={"why called agamand crypt","agamand family crypt name origin","who are the agamands"},it="name",add="02ac6c6f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you face an intolerable Scourge presence in Tirisfal. Captain Dargol's occupation mocks the dead and threatens the Undercity's northern frontier."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand mills","captain dargol","crypt","mausoleum","scourge","skeletons","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Agamand Family Crypt"}}
E["subzone:agamand-mills"] = {t="subzone",n="Agamand Mills",z="tirisfal",s="Agamand Mills lie in ruin across northern Tirisfal, now the Scourge’s largest stronghold in the region. The wealthy Agamand dynasty once held this farm and milling estate.",h="Agamand Mills lie in ruin across northern Tirisfal, now the Scourge’s largest stronghold in the region.",sec={{t="A House Divided",b="The Agamand family built its estate around a vast milling network across northern Tirisfal. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron during the Third War, patriarch Gregor Agamand refused to flee. He fortified the compound and persuaded his retainers and laborers to stand with him. Their provisions and stone walls might have held, but their youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed them. Devlin slaughtered the estate watchmen and let the walking dead into the sleeping quarters. Crippled from within, the remaining defenders fell, and the family joined the mindless ranks of the undead.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion of Rot",b="Agamand Mills are the Scourge’s strongest hold in Tirisfal Glades, and a direct threat to the Forsaken realm. Rotting windmills turn above fields crawling with wights, zombies, and skeletal horrors. Beneath the estate, Captain Dargol commands the garrison from the Agamand Family Crypt, where he practices necromancy to reanimate generations of Agamand ancestors. From Brill, Magistrate Sevren and the Deathguards fight to clear the mills and purge the Scourge before it can march on the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Agamand Mills overrun with Scourge?",a="When the Scourge ravaged Lordaeron, the Agamand family fortified their estate and tried to hold back the undead. Their youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed them and opened the gates to the Scourge. Everyone within was slaughtered and reanimated.",al={"what happened to agamand mills","why are there undead at the mills","agamand mills lore"},it="ruin"},{q="Who controls the mills right now?",a="Captain Dargol leads the Scourge at Agamand Mills. Deep in the fortified Agamand Family Crypt, he uses dark magic to raise ancestral corpses as new soldiers.",al={"who leads agamand mills","scourge leader tirisfal","who is in charge at the mills"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about this place?",a="Agamand Mills hold the largest concentration of mindless Scourge forces in Tirisfal Glades. If left unchecked, Captain Dargol’s force threatens Brill and could choke off roads south to the Undercity.",al={"why brill attacks agamand","forsaken interest in agamand mills"},it="conflict"},{q="Who was the Agamand family?",a="The Agamands were a wealthy human family of Lordaeron who owned the mills and surrounding farmland in northern Tirisfal. Their reanimated scions, including Gregor, Nissa, Thurman, and Devlin, now wander the grounds as mindless thralls.",al={"who are the agamands","agamand lineage","gregor agamand"},it="people"},{q="What is Agamand Mills?",a="Agamand Mills is a sprawling network of windmills and farmlands situated in the northern highlands of Tirisfal Glades. Before the plague swept through Lordaeron, it was a prosperous agricultural estate owned by the wealthy Agamand noble family. Today, it has fallen into decay and serves as the largest Scourge stronghold remaining in the region.",al={"agamand mills lore","what was agamand mills","what is this place"},it="place",add="9a335608"},{q="What happened at Agamand Mills?",a="When the Scourge swept into Tirisfal, Gregor Agamand chose to fortify the mills and convince his family and workers to make a stand. Their defense was sturdy and well stocked until their youngest son, Devlin, betrayed them to the enemy. Devlin slew the sentries and let a strike force of undead into the encampment, slaughtering a third of the defenders in their sleep. Overwhelmed by subsequent assaults, the survivors succumbed to the plague and rose as mindless minions of the Lich King.",al={"fall of agamand mills","agamand mills history","how did agamand mills fall"},it="history",add="ef38e774"},{q="Is Agamand Mills dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The estate crawls with reanimated farmhands, skeletal guards, and the risen members of the Agamand family themselves. Deep in the family crypt, the Scourge commander Captain Dargol wields dark necromancy to awaken long-dead ancestors, turning the mills into an armed outpost aimed directly at the Forsaken in Tirisfal.",al={"is agamand mills safe","how dangerous is agamand mills","threat at agamand mills"},it="danger",add="513094d3"},{q="Why is it called Agamand Mills?",a="The estate takes its name from the Agamands, a wealthy human family of Lordaeron who owned the mills and the surrounding farmland, and whose name the estate bore until their tragic demise.",al={"why is it called agamand","agamand mills name origin","who named agamand mills"},it="name",add="4d06011e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Agamand Mills means vengeance against the Scourge. Former estate servants like Coleman Farthing also have scores to settle."},kw={"agamand","agamand family crypt","agamand mills","captain dargol","devlin agamand","gregor agamand","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:agamand-family-crypt","quest:426","quest:408","quest:354","subzone:brill","npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:coleman-farthing","topic:scourge"},src={"Agamand Mills"}}
E["subzone:balnir-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Balnir Farmstead",z="tirisfal",s="In eastern Tirisfal, Balnir Farmstead lies ruined just behind the Bulwark. Once worked by the Balnir family, the estate now draws Scourge that slip past the defenses.",h="In eastern Tirisfal, Balnir Farmstead lies ruined just behind the Bulwark.",sec={{t="A Farm Before the Plague",b="Snapdragons still bloom in the garden where the Balnir family worked their homestead for generations. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron during the Third War, the farm was overrun and its people were lost. The buildings now rot among the hills of eastern Tirisfal.",sp=0},{t="Desolation and Scourge Infiltration",b="Mindless Scourge slip past the Bulwark and gather among the farmstead's ruins. Forsaken deathguards watch the farm warily, while Undercity magi gather surviving snapdragons from its garden. They study the flowers to learn how deeply plague corruption has reached into the soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Balnir Farmstead important?",a="Balnir Farmstead lies just behind the Bulwark on Tirisfal's eastern approaches. Scourge that slip past the defenders gather there, and Forsaken mages study the garden's snapdragons to measure how far the plague has spread into Tirisfal.",al={"balnir farm importance","why go to balnir farmstead"},it="fame"},{q="Who lived at the farmstead before the plague?",a="The Balnir family lived and worked at the farm, which bears their name. They were lost when the Scourge swept through Tirisfal during the Third War, and only the undead walk its fields now.",al={"who owned balnir farm","balnir family"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the Forsaken monitoring the farm now?",a="Mindless Scourge slip past the Bulwark from the Plaguelands and gather at the farmstead, threatening Tirisfal's eastern approaches. Undercity scholars also study the resilient snapdragons still growing in the gardens to measure how far plague contamination has spread.",al={"why forsaken care about balnir","rear guard patrol lore","balnir snapdragons"},it="threat"},{q="What is Balnir Farmstead?",a="Balnir Farmstead is a derelict estate in eastern Tirisfal Glades, just northeast of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Before the kingdom fell, it was a peaceful rural homestead of the Balnir family. Today, it lies broken and haunted, overgrown with wild snapdragons and overrun by wandering undead.",al={"what is balnir farmstead","balnir farm","about balnir farmstead"},it="place",add="40268029"},{q="What happened at Balnir Farmstead?",a="When the Scourge swept through Tirisfal during the Third War, the farm was overrun and the Balnirs were lost. Today mindless undead that slip past the Bulwark gather among its ruins.",al={"balnir farmstead history","what happened here","history of balnir farmstead"},it="history",add="decbf492"},{q="Why is Balnir Farmstead ruined?",a="The farmstead was devastated during the Scourging of Lordaeron when the undead overran eastern Tirisfal. The estate's owners, the Balnirs, were lost in the onslaught, leaving the buildings to rot and the grounds to be claimed by roaming spirits and encroaching horrors from the nearby Plaguelands.",al={"why is balnir ruined","why is balnir farm abandoned","what destroyed balnir farmstead"},it="ruin",add="037a698c"},{q="Is Balnir Farmstead dangerous?",a="Yes. It serves as a haven for restless undead and wandering spirits that slip past the Bulwark from the Western Plaguelands. Bleeding horrors and vengeful ghosts stalk the overgrown fields and ruined outbuildings, making it a constant menace to travelers along the eastern road.",al={"is balnir farm dangerous","balnir farmstead danger","threats at balnir farm"},it="danger",add="05134e04"},{q="Why is it called Balnir Farmstead?",a="The land takes its name from the Balnir family, the human farmers who tended the estate for generations until they were lost when the Scourge overran Tirisfal during the Third War.",al={"why is it named balnir","balnir farmstead name origin","who are the balnirs"},it="name",add="55c3446e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Balnir Farmstead recalls the Lordaeron they lost. Scourge from the Plaguelands still slip behind the Bulwark, leaving a breach in their defenses.",["class:Mage"]="Forsaken magi gather surviving Balnir snapdragons from these blighted grounds and study them for the Scourge's lingering magical taint."},kw={"balnir","farmstead","snapdragon","tirisfal"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","quest:1882","quest:356","subzone:bulwark","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Balnir Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:bandarion-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Bandarion Keep",z="tirisfal",s="At Bandarion Keep, defenders face threats from the coast and the woodland. The outpost near the Whispering Forest is named for Garek Bandarion and tied to Tyr's Watch.",h="At Bandarion Keep, defenders face threats from the coast and the woodland.",sec={{t="A Bastion on the Western Border",b="Bandarion Keep stands near the Whispering Forest in western Tirisfal Glades. Named for Garek Bandarion, the stronghold is closely tied to Tyr's Watch. Quartermaster Jorin Croge works to keep the garrison supplied, though the keep lies far from the courtyards of the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Surrounded by Threats",b="Danger reaches Bandarion Keep from several directions. Vile Fin murlocs raid along nearby waters, the Scarlet Crusade probes with skirmishes, and mindless Scourge thralls wander through the gloom. Some paladins have struggled to adjust to their unlife as Forsaken and succumbed to madness. They turn their weapons against their own kindred.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bandarion Keep located?",a="Bandarion Keep lies in western Tirisfal Glades, near the Whispering Forest.",al={"bandarion keep location","where is bandarion keep","how to find bandarion keep"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Bandarion Keep named after?",a="Bandarion Keep is named for Garek Bandarion.",al={"who is bandarion","garek bandarion","bandarion keep name origin"},it="name"},{q="What is Tyr's Watch?",a="Tyr's Watch is tied to Bandarion Keep and the Forsaken paladins who hold it. The keep is counted as one of Tyr's Watch, and the two names are often used interchangeably.",al={"tyrs watch","what is tyrs watch"}},{q="What dangers threaten the keep?",a="Vile Fin murlocs raid nearby waters, Scarlet Crusade zealots skirmish with the defenders, and mindless Scourge wander near the keep. Some unstable Forsaken paladins lose their minds and attack their own allies.",al={"who attacks bandarion keep","threats to bandarion keep","bandarion enemies"},it="danger"},{q="What is Bandarion Keep?",a="Bandarion Keep is a stronghold held by Tyr's Watch, situated near the mysterious Whispering Forest in western Tirisfal Glades. It serves as an outpost in a quiet but perilous corner of the region, housing Forsaken who maintain their vigil far from the heart of the Undercity.",al={"what is bandarion keep","bandarion keep info","about bandarion keep"},it="place",add="a6af85d6"},{q="Who lives in or runs Bandarion Keep?",a="The keep is garrisoned by members of Tyr's Watch. Among those tending to the bastion is Jorin Croge, who oversees the supply efforts and ensures the garrison remains properly provisioned amid the surrounding threats.",al={"who runs bandarion keep","bandarion keep residents","who is at bandarion keep"},it="residents",add="c054e935"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may see Bandarion Keep as a refuge and a warning. Some paladins who cannot reconcile the Light with their unlife have broken and turned their weapons against their Forsaken peers.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the keep on Tirisfal's western rim must stay vigilant against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade, as well as turmoil within its own ranks."},kw={"bandarion","bandarion keep","garek bandarion","jorin croge","tirisfal","tyr's watch","whispering forest"},rel={"subzone:whispering-forest","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","topic:murloc","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Bandarion Keep"},fv=true}
E["subzone:brightwater-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Brightwater Lake",z="tirisfal",s="Across Tirisfal's lowlands, Brightwater Lake lies cold and dark northeast of Brill. Once a retreat for Lordaeron, it now surrounds an island where a lone necromancer conducts forbidden research.",h="Across Tirisfal's lowlands, Brightwater Lake lies cold and dark northeast of Brill.",sec={{t="Waters of the North",b="Brightwater Lake spreads across northern Tirisfal between Brill and the Scarlet Watch Post. Under the Kingdom of Lordaeron, its shores offered a quiet country haven. That peace is gone. The Plaguelands lie to the east, and grey skies hang over the lake's murky, chilled waters. Withered trees line the shore, where murlocs and hostile undead roam.",sp=0},{t="The Hermit's Refuge",b="Gunther Arcanus lives apart from others on the island retreat at the heart of Brightwater Lake. He broke free of the Lich King's control alone, yet believes every other undead remains a Scourge slave. Undead servants guard his retreat. Bethor Iceshard hopes to show his old friend that the Forsaken can choose their own path. When an adventurer proves opposition to the Scourge, Gunther agrees to join the Forsaken.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="Where is Brightwater Lake located?",a="Brightwater Lake lies in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just northeast of Brill. It is south of the jagged North Coast and west of the Scarlet Watch Post, which guards the mountain passes toward the Western Plaguelands.",al={"brightwater lake location","where is brightwater lake","find brightwater lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives on the island in the middle of the lake?",a="Gunther Arcanus lives on the central island, known as Gunther's Retreat, with his undead servants. The Forsaken in Brill and the Undercity have taken an interest in him.",al={"who is on the island","gunther arcanus","brightwater island npc"},it="residents"},{q="What threats are found around the waters?",a="Aggressive vile fins and murlocs scavenge along the shore. Undead servants guard Gunther Arcanus's island against intruders.",al={"lake monsters","brightwater enemies","dangers at brightwater lake"},it="danger"},{q="Why do the guards in Brill talk about a summer camp here?",a="Brill's deathguards joke that the Forsaken tried to run a children's summer camp on Brightwater Lake's shores. They say masked psychos terrorized the grounds until it had to close, a grim local twist on human campfire tales.",al={"summer camp rumor","brill guards lake joke","masked psycho camp"}},{q="What is Brightwater Lake?",a="Brightwater Lake is the largest body of water in Tirisfal Glades, stretching northeast of Brill and bordered to the east by the hills leading toward the Scarlet Watch Post. In the center of its dark waters lies a prominent island known as Gunther's Retreat, along with smaller outcroppings that dot the expanse.",al={"what is brightwater lake","brightwater lake lore","tell me about brightwater lake"},it="place",add="010a8c36"},{q="What is the history of Brightwater Lake?",a="Before the plague, Brightwater Lake was a peaceful country haven of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. Today its chilled waters surround Gunther's Retreat, where the undead mage Gunther Arcanus hides from the world.",al={"brightwater lake history","what happened at brightwater lake","brightwater lake lore past"},it="history",add="5d21e80d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you must secure Brightwater Lake to defend Brill's eastern approaches. You must also learn whether the independent necromancer Gunther Arcanus will be an asset or an enemy.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can find unusual, unguided mastery on the lake's island in the renegade wizard Gunther Arcanus."},kw={"brightwater lake","brill","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","necromancer","scarlet watch post","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"subzone:gunther-s-retreat","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:scarlet-watch-post","subzone:north-coast","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","subzone:crystal-lake"},src={"Brightwater Lake"}}
E["subzone:brill"] = {t="subzone",n="Brill",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Forsaken gather north of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Newly awakened undead travel here from Deathknell, joining a rebuilt human town that now anchors Forsaken rule and arms in tirisfal glades.",h="In Brill, Forsaken gather north of the Ruins of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="From Plague Ground to Bastion",b="Before the Third War, Brill grew under nobles such as the Barov and Agamand families. Then Kel'Thuzad chose the region for the Cult of the Damned's first experiments with the Plague of Undeath. The blight swept through the people so swiftly that the local militia fled. A vast graveyard remained for the dead.\n\nNow Magistrate Sevren leads the Forsaken who have rebuilt Brill. Weathered Lordaeron buildings line its streets. The town coordinates defenses against Scarlet Crusade attacks, Scourge remnants, and native beasts changed by necromantic decay.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of Northern Lordaeron",b="Brill links Tirisfal Glades to the wider Horde. Goblins operate the zeppelin tower, carrying travelers south toward Durotar and deep into Stranglethorn Vale. Gallows' End Tavern offers shelter. Its cellar also holds captured Scarlet zealots for interrogation and apothecarial testing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Brill?",a="Magistrate Sevren oversees Brill's civil administration and local defenses for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",al={"brill leader","who is in charge of brill","magistrate of brill"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is there such a massive graveyard outside Brill?",a="Kel'Thuzad carried out some of his first live experiments with the Plague of Undeath in Brill. The contagion killed the local human population so quickly that a mass graveyard was needed to bury the victims before they rose as Scourge.",al={"brill graveyard","cemetery near brill","why so many graves"},it="history"},{q="What is Gallows' End Tavern used for?",a="Gallows' End Tavern shelters weary travelers. In its cellar, apothecaries test chemicals and poisons on captured Scarlet Crusade zealots.",al={"gallows end","brill inn","what is happening in the brill tavern"},it="place"},{q="Where does the zeppelin tower outside Brill travel to?",a="Goblin crews fly from Brill's zeppelin tower to Kalimdor outside orgrimmar, and south to grom'gol base camp in stranglethorn vale.",al={"brill zeppelin destinations","where do blimps go brill","brill flight paths"},it="place"},{q="What is Brill?",a="Brill is the central settlement of Tirisfal Glades, located just north of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Once a sleepy human hamlet, it now serves as a key military hub and outpost for the Forsaken. Fresh recruits journeying from Deathknell report here to aid Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's forces in securing the surrounding glades against encroaching threats.",al={"what is brill","brill overview","brill town"},it="place",add="0490a2ec"},{q="What happened to Brill in the past?",a="During the Third War, Brill was among the first villages stricken by the Plague of Undeath when the necromancer Kel'Thuzad began his dark trials in Tirisfal Glades. Its defenders were overwhelmed, forcing survivors to flee before Prince Arthas investigated the region. After the Scourge tore through the kingdom, the Forsaken reclaimed the ruined settlement, rebuilding it into their primary fortified hub north of the capital.",al={"history of brill","what happened at brill","brill lore"},it="history",add="3209731c"},{q="Is Brill dangerous?",a="Within its borders, Brill is heavily defended by vigilant Deathguards and Magistrate Sevren's watch. Outside the town, however, danger presses from all directions. Mindless Scourge prowl the countryside, vicious Rot Hide gnolls scour nearby waterways, and fanatical Scarlet Crusaders wage relentless war across the glades, seeking the utter destruction of everyone living within the settlement.",al={"is brill safe","threats to brill","is brill dangerous"},it="danger",add="fbdb53db"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken leaving Deathknell, Brill offers the first glimpse of civilization and a place to prove loyalty to the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Brill's zeppelin dock links the northern Horde with allied strongholds in Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"brill","forsaken","gallows end","lordaeron","magistrate sevren","tirisfal glades","zeppelin"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill-town-hall","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp"},src={"Brill"}}
E["subzone:brill-town-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Brill Town Hall",z="tirisfal",s="Brill Town Hall anchors Forsaken rule in the shattered heart of Lordaeron. From its doors, the undead govern Brill and coordinate the defense of Tirisfal Glades.",h="Brill Town Hall anchors Forsaken rule in the shattered heart of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="Civic Seat of the Forsaken",b="Brill Town Hall remains open under Forsaken rule while much of Lordaeron lies in ruins. Magistrate Sevren directs town affairs from his podium, issuing orders to Forsaken travelers. Beyond the Defiler's Den in the Arathi Highlands, few recognized town halls in the known world remain active under Forsaken control. Brill’s hall carries on Lordaeron’s old civic order beneath undead rule.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Brill Town Hall used for?",a="Brill Town Hall is the local seat of government for Brill. Magistrate Sevren and other Forsaken leaders use it to direct local defense, issue decrees, and assign work to travelers and newly awakened undead.",al={"brill town hall purpose","what is this building","why visit brill town hall"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is in charge here?",a="Magistrate Sevren presides over Brill Town Hall from his podium. He manages town affairs for the Forsaken and directs their operations across central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who runs brill town hall","brill town hall leader","who is the magistrate"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is this town hall notable compared to others?",a="Brill Town Hall is one of the few active civic halls run by the Forsaken. The Defiler's Den in Arathi is another, while most town halls belong to living human kingdoms.",al={"unique forsaken town hall","are there other forsaken town halls"},it="fame"},{q="What is Brill Town Hall?",a="Brill Town Hall stands as the most prominent structure in the settlement of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the civic and administrative heart of the town, where Forsaken leadership organizes local affairs and coordinates efforts across the region.",al={"what is brill town hall","brill town hall place","brill hall"},it="place",add="27f01e5a"},{q="Is Brill Town Hall dangerous?",a="Not if you are an ally of the Forsaken and the Horde. Brill Town Hall is firmly under Forsaken control, functioning safely as their local seat of governance, though any intruders hostile to the Dark Lady will find no mercy within its walls.",al={"is brill town hall dangerous","brill town hall safe","danger in brill town hall"},it="danger",add="0a44eaf1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken setting out from Deathknell, you find your first taste of organized civic rule under Queen Sylvanas here. Local defense and efforts to reclaim the land are formally arranged within Brill Town Hall.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally arriving in Tirisfal, you can visit Brill Town Hall to see how the Forsaken maintain civil authority and military order in their darkened homeland."},kw={"brill","forsaken","lordaeron","magistrate sevren","sevren","tirisfal glades","town hall"},rel={"subzone:brill","npc:magistrate-sevren","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},src={"Brill Town Hall"}}
E["subzone:cold-hearth-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Cold Hearth Manor",z="tirisfal",s="Along Tirisfal’s main road, Cold Hearth Manor offers travelers a Forsaken outpost west of Brill. The farm once fed Lordaeron, but the Plague of Undeath killed its people and left the fields crawling with Scourge.",h="Along Tirisfal’s main road, Cold Hearth Manor offers travelers a Forsaken outpost west of Brill.",sec={{t="A Chilled Hearth",b="Forsaken guards hold the farmhouse at Cold Hearth Manor, west of Brill along Tirisfal’s main road. Before the Third War, the estate was known for warm hospitality and rich harvests in the heart of Lordaeron. When the Plague swept through the kingdom, the family and their laborers died and rose again as husks bound to the Scourge. Feral undead still stumble through the ruined fields, but Forsaken forces drove the mindless dead from the farmhouse. They now use it as a trading post and foothold on the road toward the eastern glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the people who lived here?",a="The family and laborers who tended the estate died when the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron. They rose again as mindless zombies that still haunt the surrounding fields.",al={"who lived at cold hearth","manor backstory","what happened to the family"},it="ruin"},{q="Why is it called Cold Hearth Manor?",a="The estate was once known for its warm welcome and fires. The Forsaken likely gave it the grim name as an ironic nod to its former life and the dead, blighted farm it has become.",al={"cold hearth name meaning","why cold hearth"},it="name"},{q="Who controls the manor right now?",a="The Forsaken hold the main farmhouse as a safe stop for travelers and traders on the road from Brill. Hostile Scourge still infest the surrounding fields and barns.",al={"who owns cold hearth manor","is cold hearth friendly"},it="residents"},{q="Why don't the Forsaken clear out the fields?",a="The Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades are stretched thin, fighting mindless Scourge remnants and Scarlet Crusade crusaders. They secure the farmhouse and main road for immediate use, while scattered dead remain in the fields as a nuisance rather than an immediate threat to Brill.",al={"why are there zombies in the fields","why scourge here"}},{q="What is Cold Hearth Manor?",a="Cold Hearth Manor is a farmstead located in central Tirisfal Glades along the main road. Once celebrated across Lordaeron for its rich crops and inviting atmosphere, the estate fell during the Third War when the Plague of Undeath swept the countryside. Today, Forsaken merchants maintain a fragile roadside presence at the farmhouse, trading with travelers while keeping a watchful eye on the blighted lands around them.",al={"what is cold hearth manor","cold hearth manor overview","cold hearth manor lore"},it="place",add="29a639a2"},{q="What happened at Cold Hearth Manor?",a="During the Third War, the Plague of Undeath devastated the farmstead, killing everyone who lived and worked its soil. Mindless Scourge zombies rose from the fallen to roam the overgrown fields. Following the fall of Lordaeron, the Forsaken reclaimed the farmhouse, turning the grim remnant of human agricultural life into an outpost along the Tirisfal thoroughfare.",al={"cold hearth manor history","what happened here","cold hearth manor story"},it="history",add="673749f2"},{q="Is Cold Hearth Manor dangerous?",a="The farmhouse itself provides a measure of safety alongside Forsaken merchants, but the surrounding fields are perilous. Mindless Scourge zombies still infest the barren grounds, attacking anyone who strays from the road. Travelers must stay on guard, as the Scourge presence remains an ever-present menace right outside the manor doors.",al={"cold hearth manor danger","is it safe here","cold hearth manor threats"},it="danger",add="7e9cca93"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Cold Hearth Manor recalls their lost mortal lives. They turn former human sanctuaries into grim outposts against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",["faction:Horde"]="The manor offers a secure waypoint on the road between Brill and Tirisfal’s eastern reaches, where travelers can pause amid the plagued countryside."},kw={"brill","cold hearth manor","farmstead","forsaken","scourge","tirisfal glades","zombies"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Cold Hearth Manor"}}
E["subzone:crusader-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Crusader Outpost",z="tirisfal",s="Scarlet Crusaders watch the eastern road from the heights of Crusader Outpost. Their tower guards the approaches to the Scarlet Monastery and waits for Forsaken incursions.",h="Scarlet Crusaders watch the eastern road from the heights of Crusader Outpost.",sec={{t="Eyes Over Tirisfal",b="Crusader Outpost watches the eastern road from bluffs above the valley. Scarlet sentries scan the route between Brill and Lordaeron’s eastern reaches, hoping to spot undead and scouting parties before they reach the Monastery gates. The tower also gives the garrison a way to flank forces marching up the valley toward their holy bastion.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in the Dark Lady's Side",b="Captain Vachon and other Scarlet officers keep the garrison on alert. They regard the woods as unhallowed ground stolen from humanity by monsters, not Forsaken territory. Travelers loyal to the Undercity face an ambush point near the bluffs, where crossbow bolts and cleansing steel await anyone who comes too close.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crusader Outpost?",a="The Scarlet Crusade holds this watchtower in eastern Tirisfal Glades. Its sentries monitor the road below and guard the southern approach to the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"what is this tower","crusader outpost tirisfal","scarlet watchtower"},it="place"},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="Captain Vachon commands the Scarlet Crusade zealots who man the outpost. They see all undead as abominations to eradicate on sight.",al={"who owns crusader outpost","who lives here","scarlet crusade outpost"},it="people"},{q="Why is the tower situated in these hills?",a="The tower’s height gives Crusaders a clear view of Tirisfal Glades’ eastern road. From there, they can spot Forsaken troop movements early and flank forces attacking the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"why build here","outpost location","tactical purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Will the guards here attack me?",a="Yes. The Scarlet Crusade sees outsiders, especially the Forsaken and their Horde allies, as corrupt enemies to purge in holy fire.",al={"is crusader outpost hostile","are they aggressive"},it="danger"},{q="Who is in charge of Crusader Outpost?",a="The outpost is commanded by Captain Vachon, a Scarlet Crusade officer stationed here to oversee reconnaissance and hold the line against intruders trespassing on Crusade territory.",al={"who leads crusader outpost","crusader outpost captain","crusader outpost commander"},it="in_charge",add="a83c5de5"},{q="Why is it called Crusader Outpost?",a="The outpost takes its name directly from the Scarlet Crusade, the fanatical human order that built and maintains it as an early warning post and defensive flank for the nearby Scarlet Monastery.",al={"why is it called crusader outpost","crusader outpost name origin","why crusader outpost"},it="name",add="b91596ef"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you pass near a watchtower on the edge of Forsaken territory. Its living crusaders hold a pocket of ground in the glades.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you must travel the eastern trails of Tirisfal with care. Scarlet sentries on the hill attack anyone heading toward the Monastery."},kw={"captain vachon","crusader outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scout tower","tirisfal glades","watchtower"},rel={"topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Crusader Outpost"}}
E["subzone:crusader-s-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Crusader's Outpost",z="tirisfal",s="In western Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Crusaders hold a fortified scout tower beside Solliden Farmstead. It marks the Crusade's westernmost position in all of Lordaeron, far from its main bastions and deep in hostile Forsaken territory.",h="In western Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Crusaders hold a fortified scout tower beside Solliden Farmstead.",sec={{t="A Lonely Watchtower",b="A stone tower rises in the western Tirisfal hills, just north of Deathknell. The Scarlet garrison here marks the farthest reach of the Crusade's power in Lordaeron. Its soldiers work with the surviving human laborers at Solliden Farmstead, trying to hold back the encroaching undead. Lookouts watch the nearby pumpkin fields and forest paths for Scourge fiends and patrols from the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Isolated Behind Enemy Lines",b="The western frontier leaves the crusaders in a perilous position. Their main strongholds lie at the Scarlet Monastery and far to the east at Tyr's Hand, with no swift reinforcements likely if an attack breaches the palisade. Should Forsaken forces massing across Tirisfal lay siege, the garrison must hold the tower alone or face annihilation before help can arrive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade all the way out here in western Tirisfal?",a="The tower is an early warning post and defensive fortification in the western Tirisfal hills. It protects the living human farmers at Solliden Farmstead and watches the western approaches for feral Scourge and Forsaken advance scouts.",al={"why are scarlet here","scarlet crusaders tirisfal west","crusader outpost purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Can reinforcements reach this outpost if it gets attacked?",a="Reinforcements cannot reach the outpost easily. It is the westernmost Scarlet holding in Lordaeron, while the Crusade's main bastions lie far to the east at the Scarlet Monastery and Tyr's Hand. If Forsaken forces surround the garrison, it is cut off.",al={"can scarlet reinforce","outpost help","how far is help"}},{q="What is the relationship between the tower and Solliden Farmstead?",a="The crusaders have allied with the remaining human farmers at Solliden Farmstead. The soldiers protect them from the walking dead in exchange for sustenance and a loyal staging ground on Lordaeron's fringes.",al={"solliden connection","why are crusaders at farm","crusaders and farmers"},it="allies"},{q="Are there other towers like this in the region?",a="Yes. The Scarlet Crusade established four similar Crusader's Outposts across Tirisfal Glades to survey and patrol the surrounding lands.",al={"other crusader outposts","more scarlet towers"}},{q="What is Crusader's Outpost?",a="Crusader's Outpost is a fortified scout tower in western Tirisfal Glades, just north of Deathknell. Standing as the westernmost holding of the Scarlet Crusade in Lordaeron, it serves as a frontline watchpost against the surrounding Forsaken and Scourge threats, keeping vigil over the region alongside the nearby allied farmers of Solliden Farmstead.",al={"what is crusaders outpost","crusader outpost tirisfal","scarlet outpost western tirisfal"},it="place",add="5e123392"},{q="Who controls Crusader's Outpost?",a="The tower is manned and operated by zealous members of the Scarlet Crusade. Far from their strongholds to the east, these sentries and crusaders maintain an isolated garrison, working in close cooperation with the sympathetic human farmers at Solliden Farmstead to protect their small pocket of territory in Tirisfal.",al={"who lives at crusaders outpost","crusaders outpost residents","who runs crusaders outpost"},it="residents",add="74d073f8"},{q="Is Crusader's Outpost dangerous?",a="Yes, exceedingly so if you are an outsider or undead. The Scarlet Crusade views nearly everyone beyond their ranks as tainted or corrupted, and they attack intruders on sight. Isolated deep within hostile lands, the crusaders here remain on hair-trigger alert, making any approach perilous.",al={"is crusaders outpost dangerous","crusader outpost danger","are crusaders hostile here"},it="danger",add="30c5615e"},{q="Why is it called Crusader's Outpost?",a="It takes its name directly from the Scarlet Crusade, the religious military order that constructed and occupies the scout tower. It serves as one of several such outposts erected across Tirisfal Glades to secure their zealot crusade against the Scourge and Forsaken.",al={"why is it named crusaders outpost","crusaders outpost name origin"},it="name",add="52f2bf53"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly risen Forsaken emerging from Deathknell, you find a nearby tower guarded by Scarlet zealots, an immediate threat on your border.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the outpost as a bitter reminder that the Scarlet Crusade refuses to yield Tirisfal to the Forsaken and their allies."},kw={"crusader's outpost","scarlet crusade","scout tower","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:solliden-farmstead","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken","subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge"},src={"Crusader's Outpost"}}
E["subzone:deathknell"] = {t="subzone",n="Deathknell",z="tirisfal",s="Deathknell is where the newly freed dead first wake, in a hidden valley of southwestern Tirisfal. They have broken from the Lich King's grasp, and here they join the Forsaken. But mindless Scourge, zealots and wild beasts beset the village. For anyone who would claim a place in Sylvanas Windrunner's kingdom, it is a harsh first trial.",h="Deathknell is where the newly freed dead first wake, in a hidden valley of southwestern Tirisfal.",sec={{t="Cradle of the Forsaken",b="The valley lies behind jagged hills, just north of the Silverpine border. Elite Deathguards keep the narrow gorge out of the valley sealed. Most towns in Tirisfal kept their human names from fallen Lordaeron. This one did not. The undead who claimed it named it Deathknell.\n\nThe town itself is split in two. Its northern half is still overrun by mindless zombies and feral ghouls, the village forge with it. The Forsaken cling to the southern grounds, around the old church. There the caretakers take in each new arrival, and bring them into the Banshee Queen's service.",sp=0},{t="A Valley Under Siege",b="Survival here is never certain. To the northwest, monstrous spiders have taken Night Web's Hollow, a gold mine the young Forsaken nation needs. To the southeast, the Scarlet Crusade keeps a camp, and watches the valley without rest. Its couriers run to the Crusade's strongholds in the east, and its scouts probe Deathknell's defenses. And in the northern ruins, the caretakers must still fight off the mindless dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was the town renamed Deathknell?",a="The undead who claimed Deathknell renamed it after making it their settlement, unlike most Tirisfal communities, which kept their human names. Why they chose that name is unknown.",al={"deathknell name origin","why is it called deathknell","old name of deathknell"},it="name"},{q="Why is the northern half of the town overrun by undead?",a="Many corpses raised after the Third War did not regain their minds. The northern village square and forge are infested with the Mindless Ones, feral zombies, ghouls, and skeletons still driven by the Scourge’s lingering will. Forsaken defenders clear them out to salvage equipment and guard the church. Caretakers gather scrap metal, tools, and supplies for newly arisen souls setting out on the road ahead.",al={"why are zombies in deathknell","scourge in deathknell","mindless ones deathknell"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Scarlet Crusade doing near Deathknell?",a="A Scarlet Crusade detachment camps in the hills southeast of Deathknell. Its members seek to destroy all undead, watch the pass, ambush newly awakened Forsaken, and exchange scouting intelligence with Scarlet strongholds elsewhere in Lordaeron.",al={"scarlet camp deathknell","crusaders outside deathknell","scarlet crusade tirisfal valley"},it="threat"},{q="Why can't the Forsaken use the local gold mine?",a="Night Web’s Hollow, in the cliffs northwest of Deathknell, is overrun by aggressive spiders. Gold matters to the Forsaken war effort, but the settlement cannot exploit the vein while the spiders remain. Its loss cuts off a resource vital to the Forsaken’s fledgling economy.",al={"deathknell mine","night webs hollow","spider mine tirisfal"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Deathknell?",a="Deathknell is a small Forsaken settlement tucked into a sheltered valley in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Silverpine border. It serves as the awakening ground for newly freed undead, where the freshly risen are received, assessed, and trained. The village is split in two: while the Forsaken hold the southern grounds near the church, the northern half and its old blacksmith forge remain overrun by mindless undead.",al={"what is this place","deathknell village","about deathknell"},it="place",add="1ab0c524"},{q="Was it a normal village once?",a="Yes. Before the Third War ravaged the land, Deathknell was a living human settlement within the Kingdom of Lordaeron. When the Plague of Undeath swept across the countryside, its people succumbed and were raised into the Scourge's thrall. Unlike other towns in Tirisfal that retained their original human names, this village was later renamed Deathknell by the Forsaken.",al={"deathknell past","was deathknell human","old deathknell"},it="history",add="ae63ed0c"},{q="Who lived here before?",a="The original inhabitants were ordinary human subjects of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, including farmers, smiths, and townsfolk. When the kingdom collapsed under the Scourge, many were slaughtered or corrupted by the plague, buried in the graveyard and crypts on the hillside, or turned into mindless thralls who still wander the northern ruins.",al={"who lived here","original inhabitants deathknell","former villagers"},it="people",add="2ffa4d6f"},{q="Why is Deathknell ruined or abandoned?",a="The town fell during the Third War when the Plague of Undeath consumed Lordaeron. The Forsaken have since reclaimed only the southern portion around the church. The northern buildings, including the forge, remain abandoned and infested by hostile undead remnants of the Scourge whom the defenders have yet to fully purge.",al={"why is deathknell destroyed","why is deathknell broken","ruins of deathknell"},it="ruin",add="e9c17660"},{q="Is Deathknell dangerous?",a="Very dangerous beyond the southern perimeter. Mindless undead roam the northern half of the town, while giant Night Web spiders infest the nearby gold mine to the northwest. To make matters worse, a camp of fanatical Scarlet Crusaders sits just to the southeast, launching periodic raids against the village.",al={"is deathknell safe","danger deathknell","threats in deathknell"},it="danger",add="af76d1fc"},{q="Why am I undead? What happened to me?",a="You died during the fall of Lordaeron, victim to the horrific Plague of Undeath unleashed by the Lich King. Your body was raised into the Scourge army and forced to serve the master's iron will. When the Lich King's grip weakened after the Third War, your mind broke free, leaving you with free will in a dead body.",al={"why am i undead","how did i die","what happened to me"},it="arrival",add="9b2c91d1"},{q="Was I alive before this?",a="You were. You lived as a mortal resident of Lordaeron before the Third War brought ruin to the realm. You had a life, a home, and mortal ties before the plague claimed you and unholy magic remade your corpse.",al={"was i alive","was i human","my past life"},it="arrival",add="4fca782c"},{q="Do I remember my old life?",a="Many undead retain fragmented, agonizing memories of their former mortal lives and the horrors they were forced to commit while under the Lich King's thrall. For most Forsaken, those memories are a source of lingering torment and quiet vengeance.",al={"do i remember","past memories undead","forsaken memory"},it="arrival",add="37eab6c0"},{q="Who are the Forsaken?",a="The Forsaken are intelligent, free-willed undead who broke away from the Lich King's control following the Third War. Rallied and led by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, they carved out a home in the ruins of Lordaeron and established their capital in the Undercity.",al={"who are forsaken","forsaken faction","what is the forsaken"},it="other",add="e26c7288"},{q="How are we different from the other undead?",a="The vast majority of undead on Azeroth belong to the Scourge, chained completely to the mental domination of the Lich King. You and the other Forsaken broke those chains and regained your sentience, autonomy, and free will.",al={"difference between forsaken and scourge","are we scourge","free willed undead"},it="other",add="b31080e3"},{q="Why did we join the Horde?",a="Surrounded by hostile living kingdoms and the relentless Scourge, the Forsaken faced total destruction alone. They entered an alliance of convenience with the Horde across the sea, securing necessary military backing and mutual survival in exchange for a northern foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why join horde","forsaken horde alliance","why horde"},it="allies",add="7fbc82e5"},{q="Who is the Dark Lady everyone mentions?",a="She is Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen and sovereign ruler of the Forsaken. Formerly the Ranger-General of Silvermoon, she was slain and raised into banshee form by Prince Arthas during the Scourge invasion of Quel'Thalas. She later broke free of the Lich King's will, gathered the renegade undead, and reclaimed Lordaeron's catacombs.",al={"dark lady","who is dark lady","banshee queen"},it="leader",add="c317a133"},{q="What are the Mindless Zombies? Weren't they Forsaken too?",a="They were never Forsaken. When the plague raised the dead of Lordaeron, many lost all capacity for reason and higher thought, reduced to feral husks driven entirely by basic predatory instincts. Because they lack minds to break free or make choices, they remain hostile Scourge minions.",al={"mindless zombies","who are the mindless zombies","zombies in deathknell"},it="threat",add="1b5563f2"},{q="Could that have happened to me?",a="Yes. Countless corpses raised by the plague suffered total mental degradation, never recovering their sanity or awareness. It was pure fortune or iron will that preserved your intellect and self-command while so many others were lost to mindless savagery.",al={"could i be mindless","why am i not mindless","mindless zombie risk"},it="threat",add="68a4c897"},{q="Who is the Scarlet Crusade and why are they attacking us?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a fanatical order born from the remnants of the Knights of the Silver Hand and Lordaeron's surviving humans. They are consumed by zealous hatred for all undead, refusing to distinguish between the bloodthirsty Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken, and seek total eradication of undeath across Lordaeron.",al={"who is scarlet crusade","why scarlet crusade attacks","scarlet crusade"},it="threat",add="05e3a89b"},{q="Were they once part of the Silver Hand?",a="Yes. When the Knights of the Silver Hand shattered during the Third War after the death of Uther the Lightbringer and the fall of the capital, surviving paladins and priests banded together to fight the undead, eventually twisting into the zealous Crusade you see today.",al={"scarlet crusade silver hand","were scarlets paladins","silver hand origin"},it="history",add="b4877dc1"},{q="What are the Rattlecage Skeletons and why are they hostile to us?",a="Rattlecage Skeletons are Scourge automatons raised through necromancy from the bones of Lordaeron's dead. Lacking independent will or living flesh, they are bound directly to the lingering necromantic compulsion of the Lich King to slaughter any living or renegade undead intruders.",al={"rattlecage skeletons","why rattlecage attack","hostile skeletons"},it="threat",add="56471820"},{q="Aren't they undead like me?",a="They are undead like you, but the hostile Rattlecage Skeletons do not show the free will and self-command that distinguish the Forsaken. They serve the Scourge's destructive purposes.",al={"are rattlecage skeletons undead","aren't skeletons like us","skeletons undead"},it="threat",add="574ed092"},{q="What are the Night Web spiders and where did they come from?",a="The Night Web spiders are venomous arachnids that infested the gold mine and surrounding hollow northwest of Deathknell. As Tirisfal withered under the plague, native vermin mutated and grew aggressive, taking over the valley and driving the Forsaken away from their vital gold deposits.",al={"night web spiders","where did spiders come from","night web mine spiders"},it="threat",add="9d34c29a"},{q="What's next after Deathknell? What's in Brill?",a="Leaving Deathknell's valley leads into Tirisfal Glades toward Brill. Brill is a larger Forsaken town with a town hall, the Gallows' End Tavern, and trainers. From there, the road continues south to the Undercity.",al={"after deathknell","what is in brill","where to go after deathknell"},it="next_step",add="22acb08e"},{q="Where is Undercity from here?",a="Undercity lies to the east of Deathknell. To reach it, you take the northern road out of the valley, pass through Brill, and continue south beneath the ruined palace of Capital City.",al={"where is undercity","how to get to undercity","direction to undercity"},it="next_step",add="969b7b3b"},{q="How did I end up in Deathknell?",a="You died during the Scourge's destruction of Lordaeron and were buried in the crypts of the Shadow Grave above the village. When the Lich King's iron grip on the undead weakened, your mind snapped back to awareness. You pulled yourself free from your tomb and wandered down the slope into Deathknell, where the Forsaken gather freshly awakened corpses to see if they possess the will to serve the Dark Lady.",al={"how did i get here","why am i here","where did i come from"},it="arrival",add="95231242"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Deathknell?",a="You are proving your usefulness to the Forsaken and securing this valley. Newly awakened undead must demonstrate they have not lost their minds to the mindless Scourge lurking around the village. The local leaders need you to put down rogue zombies, clear the spider infestation in the nearby gold mine, and push back Scarlet Crusade zealots seeking to purge the undead from Tirisfal Glades before you can be sent onward to Brill.",al={"what do i do here","what is my goal here","what is my mission"},it="purpose",add="6fb0c436"},{q="Why does a new Undead start here, in Deathknell?",a="Deathknell serves as the Forsaken's recovery grounds for newly reawakened dead. The surrounding hills and crypts, particularly the Shadow Grave, hold thousands of Lordaeron's casualties from the Third War. As the Lich King's mental domination falters, corpses continuously rise here with their free will intact. Deathguard sentries stationed throughout the valley intercept the newly risen, giving survivors shelter and guidance before madness or hostile crusaders destroy them.",al={"why do undead start here","why do i start in deathknell","why deathknell for undead"},it="arrival",rc="Undead",add="3bebe502"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken adventurer, you begin here, rising from the cold earth of the Shadow Grave. Lady Sylvanas offers purpose and shelter after the horror of the Plague.",["faction:Horde"]="Though this valley is isolated and dark, it opens onto the Forsaken kingdom and sends fresh soldiers to strengthen the Horde’s foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken starting area","mindless ones","night web's hollow","shadow grave","sylvanas","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:shadow-grave","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","subzone:night-web-s-hollow","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:silverpine"},src={"Deathknell"}}
E["subzone:faol-s-rest"] = {t="subzone",n="Faol's Rest",z="tirisfal",s="In eastern Tirisfal, Faol's Rest lies neglected southwest of the Scarlet Monastery. The gravesite holds the tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, founder of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Beneath the blighted canopy, it is now a resting place for spirits who perish near the monastery.",h="In eastern Tirisfal, Faol's Rest lies neglected southwest of the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="Tomb of the Archbishop",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, mourners traveled to Faol's Rest to honor Archbishop Alonsus Faol. He led the Church of the Holy Light through the dark days of the Second War and founded the paladins to protect humanity. Faol died peacefully before the Scourge arrived, spared the agony of seeing his kingdom fall. In those years, mourners journeyed up the road from Capital City to leave offerings and pay their respects to the beloved patriarch.",sp=0},{t="Desolation in the Shadow of the Monastery",b="The Plague of Undeath withered Tirisfal, and the pilgrims stopped coming. Now the monument lies abandoned and cracked beneath the Scarlet Monastery's high bluffs. Wild brush has reclaimed the pathways, and the tomb rests amid damp mist. Those who fall near the monastery or elsewhere in Tirisfal find a quiet place here to gather their spirits before returning to the dangers around them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Alonsus Faol?",a="Alonsus Faol led the Church of the Holy Light as Archbishop during the Second War. Revered for his wisdom and compassion, he organized relief for refugees and founded the Knights of the Silver Hand. He united holy priests and pious knights as humanity's first paladins, including Uther the Lightbringer and Turalyon.",al={"who is faol","alonsus faol lore","who is buried here"},it="identity"},{q="Why is this monument located near the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The Church of the Holy Light held religious grounds near the Scarlet Monastery in northern Lordaeron. Faol was laid to rest in this tranquil corner of Tirisfal Glades before the kingdom fell, long before scarlet-clad zealots fortified the nearby monastery.",al={"why near monastery","scarlet monastery connection","location meaning"},it="why_here"},{q="Is anyone maintaining the tomb today?",a="No one tends the tomb. Since the Scourge took Lordaeron, the site has been neglected. The Scarlet Crusade rarely descends into the hollow to care for it, and the Forsaken have little interest in honoring the old church's shrines, leaving the stone markers weathered and overgrown.",al={"who tends faol's rest","is it abandoned","tomb upkeep"},it="today"},{q="What practical purpose does Faol's Rest serve for travelers?",a="Faol's Rest is the local spirit graveyard for the surrounding wilderness and the Scarlet Monastery. Those who perish trying to enter the monastery or traveling through eastern Tirisfal find their spirits returning to the Archbishop's quiet monument.",al={"graveyard run","what is this place in game","monastery graveyard"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is Faol's Rest?",a="Faol's Rest is a secluded, solemn burial ground nestled in the hills of eastern Tirisfal Glades, just southwest of the Scarlet Monastery. Built to honor Archbishop Alonsus Faol, one of the most revered figures of the Holy Light and the founder of the Knights of the Silver Hand, the site once drew faithful pilgrims from across Lordaeron before the kingdom fell.",al={"what is faols rest","faols rest lore","faol rest"},it="place",add="f2893c17",nx={6}},{q="What happened at Faol's Rest?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol passed away before the Third War and was laid to rest here amidst grand mourning. Pilgrims traveled from all corners of the kingdom to pay their respects at his tomb. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, however, the kingdom collapsed into ruin and the dead rose, leaving the sacred hillside desecrated, abandoned, and untended.",al={"faols rest history","what happened to faols rest","history of faols rest"},it="history",add="02f08d97"},{q="Why is Faol's Rest ruined and abandoned?",a="When the Plague of Undeath ravaged Lordaeron, the kingdom that once venerated the Archbishop was destroyed. With the Scarlet Crusade locking themselves inside their nearby fortress and fighting an endless war against the undead, no one remains to care for the memorial, leaving the tomb weathered, overgrown, and largely forgotten by the outside world.",al={"why is faols rest abandoned","why is faols rest ruined","who tends faols rest"},it="ruin",add="7971c9da"},{q="Is Faol's Rest dangerous?",a="While the immediate clearing around the tomb is quiet and solemn, the surrounding slopes are perilous. Zealots of the Scarlet Crusade patrol the nearby monastery approaches, attacking any outsiders on sight, while feral beasts and roaming Scourge wander the mist-shrouded hills of eastern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"is faols rest dangerous","is faols rest safe","faols rest danger"},it="danger",add="3ebb89a0"},{q="Why is this place called Faol's Rest?",a="The site was named in honor of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, who was originally interred here after his passing. Regarded as a saintly patriarch by the Church of the Holy Light, the memorial grounds were dedicated to give the beloved leader his final, peaceful rest.",al={"why is it called faols rest","who is faols rest named after","faols rest name"},it="name",add="bc843590"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, your calling traces back to Archbishop Faol, who first gathered Uther and his peers to unite martial skill with the Holy Light. His untended tomb recalls the order's beginnings.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you follow the faith Faol led as the Church of the Holy Light's supreme leader through the Second War. His ruined monument reflects the church's tragic ruin in northern Lordaeron."},kw={"alonsus faol","church of the holy light","faol's rest","graveyard","scarlet monastery","silver hand","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","topic:lordaeron","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Faol's Rest"}}
E["subzone:gallows-end-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Gallows' End Tavern",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Forsaken gather at Gallows' End Tavern for hospitality and fellowship. The town's principal inn offers shelter and spirits, with class mentors and trade instructors in its halls and covert interrogations below.",h="In Brill, Forsaken gather at Gallows' End Tavern for hospitality and fellowship.",sec={{t="A Gathering Place for the Dead",b="Along Brill's road, Gallows' End Tavern gathers newly awakened Forsaken leaving Deathknell and traveling south toward the Undercity. Though undead, they come for fellowship, trade, and refuge. Class instructors guide young warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks. Vendors and medical practitioners are here as well.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Cellar",b="Beneath the tavern's floorboards, prisoners of war are bound and guarded out of public view. Among them are a captured Scarlet Zealot and a Dwarven Mountaineer. The Forsaken hold them for interrogation and experimentation as they fight to secure their borders against zealous crusaders and Alliance scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gallows' End Tavern located?",a="Gallows' End Tavern stands in the center of Brill, the main Forsaken settlement in Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Undercity.",al={"gallows end location","where is gallows end tavern","brill inn location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the undead need an inn or tavern?",a="The Forsaken need no sleep or mortal sustenance to survive, yet taverns preserve social bonds and habits from their past lives. Gallows' End also provides a secure civic center for training, commerce, and official business.",al={"why do undead drink","why do forsaken need taverns","undead inn lore"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is imprisoned in the basement?",a="In the cellars beneath Gallows' End Tavern, the Forsaken hold a Scarlet Zealot from the hostile Scarlet Crusade and an Alliance Dwarven Mountaineer.",al={"tavern prisoners","who is in the cellar","brill tavern dungeon"},it="target"},{q="What services and trainers can be found here?",a="The tavern has instructors for warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks, as well as first aid and enchanting trainers, general trade vendors, and an innkeeper.",al={"gallows end trainers","who trains in brill inn","tavern vendors"},gp=true},{q="What is the Gallows' End Tavern?",a="Gallows' End Tavern serves as the social heart and vital resting haven of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Standing amidst the blighted ruins of Lordaeron, it is the premier fully functional tavern maintained by the Forsaken. Travelers, apothecary assistants, and passing adventurers congregate beneath its crooked timber beams to rest, seek council, trade supplies, and receive training in the dark and martial arts from resident mentors.",al={"what is gallows end tavern","tell me about gallows end tavern","gallows end tavern"},it="place",add="d83e4303"},{q="Is the Gallows' End Tavern dangerous?",a="For loyal allies of the Forsaken and the Horde, the tavern is a fortified sanctuary protected by the deathguards of Brill. However, danger lingers just beneath the floorboards. The cellars serve as a holding pen for captured enemies—namely an interrogation-bound Scarlet Zealot and an Ironforge mountaineer—reminding all who enter that the war against living zealots and intruders is waged on their very doorstep.",al={"is gallows end dangerous","danger in gallows end tavern","is gallows end safe"},it="danger",add="ae373cb3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a newly awakened Forsaken, you find your first major inn beyond Deathknell at Gallows' End Tavern. It is a crossroads for entering the wider world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Beneath the taproom, the Forsaken hold captured Alliance scouts and Scarlet Crusade zealots for intelligence and interrogation."},kw={"brill","forsaken","gallows end","gallows' end tavern","innkeeper","scarlet zealot","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","npc:captured-scarlet-zealot","topic:forsaken","quest:365"},src={"Gallows' End Tavern"}}
E["subzone:garren-s-haunt"] = {t="subzone",n="Garren's Haunt",z="tirisfal",s="Rot Hide gnolls prowl the ruined fields of Garren's Haunt in northern Tirisfal. The farm once belonged to the Garren family, until the Scourge slaughtered them and left the homestead to decay.",h="Rot Hide gnolls prowl the ruined fields of Garren's Haunt in northern Tirisfal.",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Garren's Haunt once fed a human family under the Kingdom of Lordaeron. Before the Third War, its fields yielded bountiful harvests. When the Plague of Undeath swept across the countryside, the Scourge came to the farm and slaughtered Garren and his kin. Now gray, withered fields surround a farmhouse and barn that decay beneath Tirisfal's perpetual gloom.",sp=0},{t="The Rot Hide Squatters",b="Rot Hide gnolls have claimed Garren's Haunt, led by the vicious Maggot Eye. These undead-tainted scavengers defend the farm fiercely, picking clean what remains and savaging travelers or Forsaken patrols passing through northern Tirisfal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Garren?",a="Garren was a human farmer who lived here with his family before the Third War. They worked the surrounding fields until the Scourge overran Lordaeron and butchered the household as the plague spread.",al={"garren lore","who lived here","garren story"},it="identity"},{q="What creatures occupy the farm now?",a="Rot Hide gnolls led by Maggot Eye occupy the farm. They prowl its fields and buildings, attacking those who come too close.",al={"monsters at garrens haunt","what lives here","who controls the farm"},it="residents"},{q="Why is it called Garren's Haunt?",a="The farm bears the name of its murdered owner, Garren. “Haunt” describes the grim, abandoned land left to rot after his family was slain beneath Tirisfal's pall.",al={"why called haunt","garren name origin"},it="name"},{q="Why haven't the Forsaken reclaimed it?",a="The Forsaken are stretched thin fortifying the Undercity and battling the Scarlet Crusade and active Scourge remnants. Passing mercenaries and adventurers are largely left to deal with scavengers like the Rot Hide gnolls at outlying farms.",al={"why forsaken ignore it","forsaken garrens haunt"},it="today"},{q="What is Garren's Haunt?",a="Garren's Haunt is an expansive, derelict farmstead situated in northern Tirisfal Glades. Before the fall of Lordaeron, it was a productive homestead featuring a large farmhouse, a barn, several silos, and wide fields. Today, blighted by the Plague of Undeath, the crops have withered into gray dust and the farm stands as a grim reminder of the kingdom's agrarian past.",al={"what is garrens haunt","garren's haunt farm","where is garrens haunt"},it="place",add="f7a25cdf"},{q="What happened at Garren's Haunt?",a="During the Scourging of Lordaeron, the Scourge swept across Tirisfal Glades and laid waste to the countryside. Garren and his entire family were brutally murdered when the undead overran their homestead. The blighted earth choked the life from the fields, leaving the land ruined and allowing carrion-seeking monsters to claim the empty structures.",al={"garrens haunt history","what happened here","how was garrens haunt destroyed"},it="history",add="b3ebc210"},{q="Why is Garren's Haunt ruined and abandoned?",a="The farmstead was devastated when the Plague of Undeath swept Lordaeron, killing the resident family and leaving the buildings rotting under a corrupted sky. With its human owners slaughtered and the surrounding soil tainted beyond natural cultivation, no living farmers remain to tend the land, leaving the ruined structures to decay in the mist.",al={"why is garrens haunt ruined","why was garrens haunt abandoned","who ruined garrens haunt"},it="ruin",add="0c808513"},{q="Is Garren's Haunt dangerous?",a="Yes. Rot Hide gnolls and their leader, Maggot Eye, occupy the ruined farm and attack travelers who approach their territory.",al={"is garrens haunt safe","dangers at garrens haunt","how dangerous is garrens haunt"},it="danger",add="41bc539b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The ruined farm recalls the slaughter that preceded the Forsaken. Clearing out the Rot Hide gnolls helps secure northern Tirisfal for the Dark Lady."},kw={"farmstead","garren's haunt","maggot eye","plague","rot hide","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","topic:gnoll","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron","quest:358"},src={"Garren's Haunt"}}
E["subzone:gunther-s-retreat"] = {t="subzone",n="Gunther's Retreat",z="tirisfal",s="On an island in Brightwater Lake, Gunther's Retreat shelters a renegade necromancer. Gunther Arcanus broke free of the Scourge through sheer will, but trusts no outsider and keeps undead minions around his camp.",h="On an island in Brightwater Lake, Gunther's Retreat shelters a renegade necromancer.",sec={{t="A Recluse in Brightwater Lake",b="Mist hangs over the waters around Gunther's Retreat, where undead sentinels guard a lonely camp. Gunther Arcanus was raised in undeath, but his arcane mastery let him tear his soul from the Lich King's grip without help. He mistrusted everyone and believed the undead wandering Lordaeron remained puppets of the Scourge. Gunther withdrew to the island to practice his craft in peace, and his zombie sentinels attack anyone who crosses the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Gunther's Retreat?",a="Gunther Arcanus, a necromancer who broke free of the Lich King's control by his own power, lives on the island. Undead thralls guard his camp.",al={"gunther island","who is on the island","gunther's retreat master"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the undead on the island hostile?",a="Gunther Arcanus believes every other undead in Tirisfal remains enslaved by the Scourge. He prizes his independence, so his minions attack anyone who approaches the island.",al={"why does gunther attack","why hostile","is gunther scourge"},it="hostile"},{q="Is Gunther aligned with the Forsaken?",a="At first, Gunther keeps apart from the Forsaken, though he is also free-willed undead. The authorities in the Undercity seek to prove they too have escaped the Lich King's grasp and to recruit his talents.",al={"is gunther in the horde","gunther forsaken","gunther undercity"},it="side"},{q="What is the small islet southwest of the retreat?",a="A tiny, unnamed islet lies just southwest of Gunther's Retreat. It is known as Lillith's Dinner Table, an eerie landmark in Brightwater Lake.",al={"lillith dinner table","small island near gunther","table island"},it="place"},{q="What is Gunther's Retreat?",a="Gunther's Retreat is an isolated island nestled in Brightwater Lake in central Tirisfal Glades. Sheltered by surrounding waters, the island serves as the secluded sanctuary of Gunther Arcanus, a powerful free-willed lich. Cut off from the rest of Lordaeron, the grounds are patrolled by shambling undead servants guarding their reclusive master.",al={"what is gunthers retreat","gunthers retreat lore","brightwater lake island"},it="place",add="dc3ef5e2"},{q="Is Gunther's Retreat dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very dangerous to approach unprepared. Gunther Arcanus mistakenly believes all other undead in Lordaeron are mindless thralls of the Scourge. To protect his sanctuary, he commands his zombie minions to violently attack any who set foot on the island shores.",al={"is gunthers retreat dangerous","gunther retreat safe","danger gunther retreat"},it="danger",add="2d8f9787"},{q="Why is it called Gunther's Retreat?",a="The island takes its name from Gunther Arcanus, the free-willed lich who made Brightwater Lake his private sanctuary. After breaking away and retaining his independence in death, Gunther retreated here to escape the reach of the Scourge and seclude himself from the wider world.",al={"why called gunthers retreat","gunthers retreat name origin","who named gunthers retreat"},it="name",add="721e4715"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gunther Arcanus shares the Forsaken's fate: free of the Lich King, yet wary of a world he believes remains under the Scourge's thrall.",["class:Mage"]="Arcanists may recognize Gunther's rare feat: his magical will severed the Lich King's mental grip without help."},kw={"brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","lich","lillith's dinner table","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:brightwater-lake","quest:357","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Gunther's Retreat"}}
E["subzone:night-web-s-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Night Web's Hollow",z="tirisfal",s="In Tirisfal Glades, spiders have overrun Night Web's Hollow, an abandoned gold mine northwest of Deathknell. Newly raised Forsaken are sent into its tunnels to cull the vermin and prove their readiness for combat.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, spiders have overrun Night Web's Hollow, an abandoned gold mine northwest of Deathknell.",sec={{t="The Infested Mine",b="Night Web's Hollow lies in the hills northwest of Deathknell. Before the plague swept through Lordaeron, humans worked its gold mine. After the kingdom fell, the shafts stood empty. Now webs cover the rock walls, and aggressive night web spiders fill the vale and tunnels. The Forsaken send their newly raised into the hollow to kill young and adult spiders and regain access to the mine's gold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Night Web's Hollow?",a="Night Web's Hollow is a small ravine and abandoned gold mine northwest of Deathknell. Webs cover the vale, and aggressive spiders swarm through it, making it an early proving ground for new Forsaken recruits.",al={"night webs hollow","spider mine deathknell","spider cave tirisfal"},it="place"},{q="Why are the Forsaken clearing out the spiders?",a="The Forsaken need the mine's gold, but spiders block the tunnels. Executor Arren has few hands to spare, so new recruits help clear the infestation over time.",al={"why kill spiders","deathknell spider quest"},it="purpose"},{q="What lives deep inside the mine shafts?",a="Young spiders skitter through the vale, while full-grown Night Web Spiders prowl the tunnels. Deep in the darkest chamber lives the Night Web Matriarch, broodmother of the infestation.",al={"spider boss mine","night web matriarch location"},it="threat"},{q="Was this always a spider den?",a="No. Before Lordaeron fell, local humans worked the mine for gold. After the Scourge wiped out the region, the shafts fell into disrepair, and spiders took shelter in the dark tunnels.",al={"who dug the mine","deathknell mine history"},it="history"},{q="Who lives in Night Web's Hollow?",a="No civilized folk dwell here. The hollow and its old mine tunnels are overrun entirely by aggressive Night Web Spiders. Outside, younger arachnids skitter through the shaded vale, while fully grown spiders and their massive matriarch nest deep within the dark shafts.",al={"who lives in night web hollow","night webs hollow inhabitants","who is in night webs hollow"},it="residents",add="132bc2d1"},{q="Why is the mine in Night Web's Hollow abandoned?",a="Like much of Tirisfal Glades, the old gold mine fell into ruin during the Third War when the Scourge plague ravaged the kingdom of Lordaeron. With its miners dead or scattered, the shafts were left deserted, allowing the local spiders to claim the hollow and weave their nests throughout the depths.",al={"why is night webs hollow abandoned","why was night web mine abandoned","what happened to the gold mine"},it="ruin",add="3ed77784"},{q="Is Night Web's Hollow dangerous?",a="It poses a genuine threat to newly awakened Forsaken. While lone young spiders along the path are manageable, the mine interior teems with venomous adult arachnids, culminating in their vicious matriarch waiting in the deepest recesses.",al={"is night webs hollow dangerous","how dangerous is night webs hollow","night webs hollow danger"},it="danger",add="8db143d3"},{q="Why is it called Night Web's Hollow?",a="The valley takes its name directly from the Night Web Spiders that blanket the hollow and its abandoned mine in thick, shadowy webs. Their sprawling nests choke the valley, giving the desolate ravine its menacing title.",al={"why is it called night webs hollow","night webs hollow name origin","how did night webs hollow get its name"},it="name",add="2ca4d435"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you, newly risen, Night Web's Hollow is one of your first trials. Slaying the arachnids proves you have the focus and will to serve the Dark Lady.",["profession:Mining"]="The shafts were dug for gold, but lethal spiders have halted mining there."},kw={"deathknell","mine","night web matriarch","night web's hollow","spiders","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},src={"Night Web's Hollow"}}
E["subzone:nightmare-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Nightmare Vale",z="tirisfal",s="Twisted trees and hungry beasts crowd Nightmare Vale in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, west of the Crusader's Outpost. Once a forest haven, it now lies blighted and withered.",h="Twisted trees and hungry beasts crowd Nightmare Vale in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, west of the Crusader's...",sec={{t="A Decayed Wilderness",b="Before the Third War, songbirds and woodland game filled this valley in the Tirisfal countryside. After the Scourge's plague, its plants blackened and rotted. Ravenous darkhounds and massive vampire bats consumed the native wildlife, leaving the hollow to scavengers and beasts of prey.",sp=0},{t="Stalkers of the Hollow",b="Ressan the Needler, an unusually large, pale vampire bat, lurks in Nightmare Vale and is known to local travelers. The vale lies between haunted wilderness and the zealous sentries at the nearby Crusader's Outpost. Unwary travelers crossing this unforgiving expanse can quickly become prey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nightmare Vale located?",a="Nightmare Vale lies in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, just west of the Crusader's Outpost.",al={"nightmare vale location","where is nightmare vale","find nightmare vale"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the valley called Nightmare Vale?",a="The plague that devastated Lordaeron consumed what had been a peaceful, vibrant forest. Withered trees and aggressive predators, including hungry darkhounds and blood-drinking bats, make the valley a waking nightmare for travelers.",al={"why nightmare vale","nightmare vale lore"},it="name"},{q="What creatures roam Nightmare Vale?",a="Savage darkhounds and giant vampire bats roam the vale, driving out or consuming native forest animals. The rare white vampire bat Ressan the Needler also prowls there.",al={"nightmare vale mobs","monsters in nightmare vale","beasts here"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Ressan the Needler?",a="Ressan the Needler is a rare, stark-white vampire bat that stalks Nightmare Vale's dark skies and withered canopy.",al={"ressan","ressan the needler","rare bat tirisfal"},it="identity"},{q="What is Nightmare Vale?",a="Nightmare Vale is a wide, blighted valley nestled in southwestern Tirisfal Glades. Once a lush forest teeming with vibrant woodland creatures, the vale has fallen completely into decay. The trees have withered away, and the once-peaceful glade has become a desolate hunting ground prowled by ravenous darkhounds and monstrous vampire bats.",al={"what is nightmare vale","nightmare vale lore","tell me about nightmare vale"},it="place",add="5ff12c50"},{q="What happened to Nightmare Vale?",a="Like much of Tirisfal Glades, Nightmare Vale succumbed to the devastating plague and corruption that swept through Lordaeron. The verdant canopy withered and died under the blight, and the native wildlife vanished, supplanted or consumed by corrupted predators. Today, it stands as a bleak reminder of the kingdom's fall.",al={"nightmare vale history","how did nightmare vale fall","what happened here"},it="history",add="2fb13922"},{q="Is Nightmare Vale dangerous?",a="Yes, Nightmare Vale poses a serious threat to solitary travelers. The valley is infested with ravenous darkhounds and enormous vampire bats that hunt anything straying through the dead woods. In addition, the notorious and vicious white bat, Ressan the Needler, is known to stalk these shadows.",al={"how dangerous is nightmare vale","is it safe here","threats in nightmare vale"},it="danger",add="9de72d2c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see the plague's lingering mark across Tirisfal in Nightmare Vale's twisted wildlife. Those beasts threaten travelers who venture beyond Brill.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can find vicious darkhounds and vampire bats in the vale, including the rare white bat Ressan the Needler. These fearsome beasts make the vale a notable hunting ground."},kw={"darkhounds","nightmare vale","ressan the needler","tirisfal glades","vampire bats"},rel={"zone:tirisfal"},src={"Nightmare Vale"}}
E["subzone:north-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="North Coast",z="tirisfal",s="Fog shrouds North Coast along the Great Sea, where blight and murlocs shape the shore. Its cold sands lie at Tirisfal Glades' northern edge, littered with rotting marine life.",h="Fog shrouds North Coast along the Great Sea, where blight and murlocs shape the shore.",sec={{t="A Blighted Shoreline",b="Before the Third War, North Coast's waters and stony beaches formed Lordaeron's peaceful northern boundary. The Plague of Undeath swept across the continent, and its blight seeped down the bluffs to poison the coast. The waters grew cold and murky. Now giant sea creatures wash ashore and rot on the sand beneath the lasting coastal fog.",sp=0},{t="The Vile Fin Shore",b="With Lordaeron shattered, the Forsaken focus on Brill and the Capital City, while coastal murlocs claim the desolate sands. The Vile Fin tribe keeps huts along the surf and uses nearby shallows as spawning grounds. Ravenous murlocs gather there, including Deeb and growing tadpoles. They violently guard the tideline against surface-dwellers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures inhabit the North Coast?",a="Aggressive Vile Fin murlocs inhabit the beach, alongside their tadpoles and scavengers picking over rotting sea life washed ashore from the Great Sea.",al={"north coast mobs","what lives on north coast","monsters north coast"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Deeb?",a="Deeb is a murloc found along North Coast, among the shore's huts and shallows.",al={"deeb","murloc deeb","who is deeb"},it="people"},{q="Why is the coast covered in rotting carcasses?",a="The Plague of Undeath devastated Lordaeron and seeped into the coast, poisoning its shallows. Dead marine beasts wash ashore and decay on the blighted sand.",al={"dead sea monsters","beached whales tirisfal","why dead creatures"},it="ruin"},{q="Is the North Coast contested by any major factions?",a="Neither the Forsaken nor remnants of the Alliance actively garrison North Coast. The shore remains untamed, left largely to murlocs and sea vermin.",al={"who owns north coast","forsaken presence north coast"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the North Coast?",a="The North Coast is a desolate strip of shore along the northern boundary of Tirisfal Glades, bordering the Great Sea. Tainted by the Plague of Undeath that ravaged Lordaeron, its chill waters wash ashore decaying sea creatures, and crude huts belonging to hostile coastal murlocs dot the sands.",al={"what is north coast","north coast overview","about north coast"},it="place",add="8e1fe0f4"},{q="What happened to the North Coast?",a="Once a peaceful shoreline of northern Lordaeron, the coast fell victim to the Plague of Undeath alongside the rest of the kingdom. The blight poisoned the waters and marine life, leaving the beaches strewn with dead sea beasts while savage murloc tribes moved in to claim the blighted sands.",al={"north coast history","what happened here","north coast lore"},it="history",add="bb9c4791"},{q="Is the North Coast dangerous?",a="Yes. The beach is overrun by vicious murlocs, including the local Vile Fin tribe and their kin, who fiercely defend their crude settlements and nearby spawning grounds. Between these aggressive amphibious packs and the lingering chill of the plague, unwary travelers will quickly find themselves swarmed and cut down.",al={"is north coast dangerous","threats north coast","north coast hazards"},it="danger",add="5791ac67"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken patrols follow the road through Brill. Clearing North Coast of encroaching murlocs helps keep Tirisfal Glades' northern flank relatively secure."},kw={"beach","deeb","great sea","murloc","north coast","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","topic:murloc","subzone:brill","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"North Coast"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery",z="tirisfal",s="Scarlet Monastery now shelters the fanatical Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades. Once a peaceful center of scholarship and worship for the Church of the Holy Light, it has become a fortified redoubt. Anyone approaching without red colors is treated as a carrier of the plague and executed on sight.",h="Scarlet Monastery now shelters the fanatical Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="From Sanctuary to Stronghold",b="Before the Third War, the Scarlet Monastery was a proud center of Lordaeron's priesthood. Its halls held theological studies and sacred archives, and paladins trained there. When the Scourge brought down the kingdom, surviving defenders held the site against the undead. Those survivors became the zealous Scarlet Crusade and fortified the cloister. Libraries, gardens, and the cathedral became parts of an armed stronghold.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion of Fanaticism",b="Four wings make up the Scarlet Monastery: a defiled graveyard, an expansive library, an armory, and a grand cathedral. Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane command its massive garrison. The Crusaders see every outsider as a plague-bearer, living or undead, Alliance or Horde. The Forsaken seek to destroy the garrison that threatens their doorstep, while Alliance leaders increasingly see the Crusade's violent extremism as a dangerous perversion of the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Monastery here?",a="Lordaeron built the Scarlet Monastery as a peaceful sanctuary for study, sacred scriptures, and paladin training. After the kingdom fell, surviving crusaders seized and fortified it as a military staging ground against the undead in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what is scarlet monastery","why did they build monastery in tirisfal","monastery purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade attack Alliance members?",a="The Scarlet Crusade believes anyone who has traveled beyond its secured compounds could carry the Scourge's plague of undeath. Its zealotry has grown into complete paranoia, and it takes no chances with outsiders, whatever their race or allegiance.",al={"why are scarlet hostile to alliance","are scarlet crusade alliance","why do crusaders attack humans"},it="hostile"},{q="Who leads the forces within the Monastery?",a="Scarlet Commander Mograine directs military operations from the cathedral, while High Inquisitor Whitemane commands the garrison. She is a zealous priestess renowned for her devotion and powers of resurrection.",al={"who is the boss of scarlet monastery","monastery leaders","who runs the scarlet crusade here"},it="leader"},{q="What are the four wings of the complex?",a="The four wings are the Graveyard, with restless dead and torture chambers; the Library, with historical archives and tomes; the Armory, where the Crusade makes weapons and armor; and the Cathedral, the spiritual heart and commander's seat.",al={"monastery sections","what wings are in scarlet monastery","monastery layout"}},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Tucked into the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery was once a peaceful cathedral and center of learning for Lordaeron's priesthood. Following the Third War and the devastation of the kingdom, the Scarlet Crusade seized the ancient sanctuary and transformed it into a heavily fortified stronghold. Its halls, once dedicated to enlightenment and the training of holy paladins, now echo with fanatical zealotry.",al={"what is scarlet monastery","scarlet monastery lore","tell me about scarlet monastery"},it="place",add="b123b1b5"},{q="What happened at the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The monastery was once a proud bastion of Lordaeron's priesthood, a center for learning and enlightenment that also trained paladins. When the Scourge overran Lordaeron during the Third War, surviving zealots of the Scarlet Crusade seized the complex and converted the peaceful holy seat into an armed fortress.",al={"history of scarlet monastery","what happened here","monastery past"},it="history",add="5fcbefd1"},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The complex is garrisoned by hundreds of heavily armed, zealous crusaders who view any outsider as a potential carrier of the plague of undeath. Whether you belong to the Horde or the Alliance, their standing orders are merciless execution. Even beyond their martial soldiers, the inner sanctum is protected by high-ranking inquisitors whose holy powers can resurrect the fallen back into combat.",al={"is scarlet monastery dangerous","how dangerous is the monastery","is it safe to enter"},it="danger",add="73cac1e2"},{q="Why is it called the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The name comes from its masters. When the Scourge overran Lordaeron, the extremist Scarlet Crusade seized the monastery and fortified it as their stronghold, and it now bears the name of their crimson order.",al={"why is it called scarlet monastery","scarlet monastery name origin","where does the name come from"},it="name",add="a14a0fc8"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Monastery sits at the Undercity's doorstep. Its heavily armed crusaders pose an active, existential threat to Forsaken territory.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may find it bitter to see a place that once trained paladins under the Silver Hand corrupted into an intolerant stronghold of fanaticism."},kw={"armory","cathedral","graveyard","library","mograine","old monastery","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral","subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory","subzone:scarlet-monastery-library","subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scarlet Monastery"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-watch-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Watch Post",z="tirisfal",s="In northeastern Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Watch Post guards the rocky hills just north of the Scarlet Monastery. Its garrison watches the monastery’s northern flank for attacks.",h="In northeastern Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Watch Post guards the rocky hills just north of the Scarlet...",sec={{t="Guarding the Northern Approach",b="Scarlet Watch Post watches the northern cliffs behind the Scarlet Monastery. The southern road to the monastery gate is busy and fortified, but the rugged cliffs along Tirisfal’s northern coast offer infiltrators a back route. The Scarlet Crusade built this stone tower to guard that blind spot. It is one of several Crusader outposts scattered across Tirisfal Glades. Captain Melrache commands a mixed, devout force of Neophytes, Vanguards, and Friars. They keep watch over the cliffs so neither the Scourge nor the Forsaken can surprise the order from behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Scarlet Watch Post?",a="Scarlet Watch Post protects the Scarlet Monastery from a northern flanking attack. The monastery’s rear slopes face the northern wilderness, where sentries watch for intruders and intercept anyone attempting a northern bypass.",al={"why is scarlet watch post here","scarlet watch post purpose","crusaders run role"},it="purpose"},{q="Who commands the Scarlet Watch Post?",a="Captain Melrache commands the garrison at the tower. His force includes personal bodyguards, front-line Vanguards, aspiring Neophytes, and spellcasting Friars.",al={"scarlet watch post leader","who leads scarlet watch post","captain melrache"},it="in_charge"},{q="Is the Scarlet Watch Post related to the other towers in Tirisfal?",a="Yes. Scarlet Watch Post is one of four Crusader outposts across the northern and western reaches of Tirisfal Glades. Together, the stone towers form a defensive perimeter to monitor Scourge activity and contain the Forsaken’s expansion from the Undercity.",al={"tirisfal towers","crusader outposts tirisfal","other scarlet towers"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Scarlet Watch Post?",a="The Scarlet Watch Post is an isolated watchtower stationed in the rugged hills of northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Scarlet Monastery. It serves as a fortified scout outpost built to guard the vulnerable northern approach to the Crusade's mighty bastion.",al={"what is scarlet watch post","scarlet watch post lore","what is this tower"},it="place",add="24ad1453"},{q="Is the Scarlet Watch Post dangerous?",a="Yes, exceedingly so for any outsider. The post is garrisoned by zealous Scarlet crusaders, including friars, neophytes, and heavily armed vanguards and bodyguards sworn to butcher any intruder, living or undead, on sight.",al={"is scarlet watch post dangerous","scarlet watch post threat","watch post danger"},it="danger",add="1857b7a1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you face the Scarlet Crusade near the Undercity. Attacking isolated towers like Scarlet Watch Post disrupts the zealots’ communications and helps secure northern Tirisfal.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you’ll find Scarlet Watch Post hostile ground. The Crusaders see outsiders, living or dead, as tainted carriers of undeath."},kw={"captain melrache","crusader outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scarlet watch post","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","subzone:crusader-s-outpost","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Scarlet Watch Post"}}
E["subzone:shadow-grave"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadow Grave",z="tirisfal",s="Newly freed Forsaken awaken in Shadow Grave, above Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades.",h="Newly freed Forsaken awaken in Shadow Grave, above Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Cradle of the Forsaken",b="Shadow Grave sits on the rocky slope above Deathknell, a stone mausoleum where the newly freed Forsaken awaken. Once raised into the Scourge’s mindless service, the dead recover their free will in its vaults. Undertaker Mordo watches over them as they rise from stone slabs and take their first steps into a world that despises them. They follow the footpath down to Deathknell and pledge themselves to the Banshee Queen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shadow Grave used for?",a="Newly awakened Forsaken regain their free will in Shadow Grave, instead of remaining mindless Scourge thralls. From the crypt, they begin a second life serving Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"shadow grave purpose","what is shadow grave","shadow grave crypt"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Shadow Grave located?",a="Shadow Grave sits at the top of the graveyard slope above Deathknell, against Tirisfal Glades’ southern mountains. A dirt trail leads downhill from its entrance to Deathknell.",al={"where is shadow grave","shadow grave location","shadow grave map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who oversees the newly awakened here?",a="Undertaker Mordo attends the newly awakened in the tomb. He judges whether they have recovered their minds and can serve the Forsaken cause.",al={"who is in shadow grave","shadow grave npcs","undertaker mordo location"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Shadow Grave?",a="The Shadow Grave is a secluded stone crypt situated high on the graveyard slope above Deathknell in western Tirisfal Glades. Connected to the settlement of Deathknell by a winding downward path, this solemn tomb serves as the quiet threshold where newly awakened Forsaken first claw their way back into consciousness, sheltered from the threats that roam the surrounding glades.",al={"what is shadow grave","shadow grave lore","tell me about shadow grave"},it="place",add="f1e0774e"},{q="Is the Shadow Grave dangerous?",a="The crypt itself remains relatively safe, functioning under the vigilant care of the Forsaken attendants stationed here to assist the newly awakened. However, just beyond its stone doorway lies the perils of Tirisfal Glades, where mindlessly wandering Scourge undead, scavengers, and the ever-watchful agents of the Scarlet Crusade threaten anyone who strays too far unprepared.",al={"is shadow grave dangerous","shadow grave safe","are there enemies in shadow grave"},it="danger",add="742f7843"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, your journey begins on the crypt’s stone slabs, where you awaken to unlife and free will."},kw={"awakening","crypt","deathknell","shadow grave","starting tomb","tirisfal glades","undertaker mordo"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Shadow Grave"}}
E["subzone:solliden-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Solliden Farmstead",z="tirisfal",s="At Solliden Farmstead, human farmers still tend pumpkins in western Tirisfal Glades, just north of Deathknell. These native Lordaeronians survived the Plague of Undeath, a rare sight in northern Lordaeron, and hold fiercely to their soil beneath the Scarlet Crusade’s shadow.",h="At Solliden Farmstead, human farmers still tend pumpkins in western Tirisfal Glades, just north of Deathknell.",sec={{t="A Defiant Remnant",b="Solliden Farmstead’s fields still yield healthy crops while much of Lordaeron lies in ruin and rot. The surviving human farmers are traumatized and insular, living beneath the watch of Scarlet Crusade patrols from a nearby tower. They defend their home with fierce hostility, striking at outsiders who come near, whether Horde or Alliance.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Undercity",b="Forsaken rising from Deathknell see Solliden Farmstead as both a threat and a resource. The Royal Apothecary Society wants its pristine pumpkins as prime organic material for testing and brewing the New Plague. Forsaken officers such as Deathguard Simmer send fledgling recruits to raid the fields, steal pumpkins for Apothecary Johaan in Brill, and teach the living a lesson.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there living humans farming in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Solliden farmers are native humans of Lordaeron who miraculously escaped infection during the Third War. Scarlet Crusade patrols from a nearby tower shield them, and they keep cultivating their land rather than flee their ancestral home.",al={"why are they alive","who are these farmers","living humans in tirisfal"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the Solliden farmers hostile to Alliance players?",a="The fall of Lordaeron left the farmers paranoid, bitter, and unwilling to trust anyone beyond their circle. Shielded by the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, they see trespassers as threats or infected scavengers and attack Alliance and Horde travelers alike.",al={"why do farmers attack alliance","are they alliance","why red to alliance"},it="hostile"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want pumpkins from Solliden Farmstead?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society needs fresh, uncorrupted organic matter to test and refine its New Plague. Pumpkins growing in Solliden’s soil are untainted hosts for developing toxic strains.",al={"why steal pumpkins","fields of grief pumpkin quest","royal apothecary society pumpkins"},it="item"},{q="Who is Deathguard Simmer, and why does he target the farm?",a="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken officer stationed near Deathknell. He sends fledgling Forsaken to raid the farm, steal ten pumpkins for Apothecary Johaan in Brill, and teach the humans and their Scarlet Crusade protectors a lesson.",al={"why kill the farmers","deathguard simmer quest","reaping the reapers"},it="threat"},{q="What is Solliden Farmstead?",a="Solliden Farmstead is an active pumpkin farm located in western Tirisfal Glades, tucked just north of Deathknell. Remarkably, it stands as one of the very few places in northern Lordaeron where living native humans managed to survive the Plague of Undeath entirely uncorrupted, clinging fiercely to their soil under the shadow of the nearby Scarlet Crusade.",al={"what is solliden farmstead","solliden farm","tell me about solliden farmstead"},it="place",add="cf3d4bd1"},{q="What is the history of Solliden Farmstead?",a="Little is recorded of the farmstead's early history. What is known is that, against all odds, it remained an active agricultural estate right through the Third War, its farmers surviving the Plague of Undeath under the protection of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"solliden farm history","who founded solliden farm","what happened at solliden farmstead"},it="history",add="45cdb17a"},{q="Is Solliden Farmstead dangerous?",a="Yes, if you get too close. The surviving farmers have grown deeply paranoid and aggressive from surviving surrounded by horrors. Rather than welcoming outsiders, they will attack both Horde and Alliance travelers on sight. Furthermore, the farm sits in close proximity to the Scarlet Crusade's defenses at a nearby outpost, making the surrounding area treacherous.",al={"is solliden farm dangerous","are solliden farmers dangerous","solliden farmstead threat"},it="danger",add="7c9ed8e2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For a newly risen Forsaken, Solliden Farmstead is an immediate lesson in realpolitik: living Lordaeronians despise what you have become, while the farm offers raw material for Apothecary toxins and a possible southern beachhead.",["faction:Alliance"]="Seeing living humans till Lordaeron’s soil may bring you hope, but these isolated survivors hate Stormwind’s citizens as they hate the undead."},kw={"deathguard simmer","deathknell","fields of grief","pumpkins","solliden","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:deathknell","quest:365","npc:deathguard-simmer","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Solliden Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:stillwater-pond"] = {t="subzone",n="Stillwater Pond",z="tirisfal",s="At Stillwater Pond, gray water and skeletal fish mark the loss of a place where Lordaeron's children once swam. Dangerous scavengers prowl its western shore, just west of Brill.",h="At Stillwater Pond, gray water and skeletal fish mark the loss of a place where Lordaeron's children once...",sec={{t="A Ruined Respite",b="Stillwater Pond once drew families from nearby hamlets for picnics on its grassy banks. Before the Third War and the Plague of Undeath, its shallows gave children too young to brave Brightwater Lake a place to learn to swim. The water is now lifeless and gray. The living have vanished, leaving skeletal fish beneath the surface and wandering undead in the surrounding woods.",sp=0},{t="Prowlers in the Mist",b="Stillwater Pond is quieter than Tirisfal's besieged roads and contested farms, but danger lingers along its shore. Blighted beasts drink from its murky water, including Bayne, a ferocious darkhound that stalks the banks. Travelers crossing the western meadows toward Brill must watch for predatory beasts and aimless zombies by the water's edge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Stillwater Pond like before the Plague?",a="Before the Plague, Stillwater Pond drew local families for picnics in human Lordaeron. Its shallows were calmer than Brightwater Lake, so parents brought young children there to swim.",al={"stillwater pond history","what was stillwater pond used for","tirisfal swimming spot"},it="history"},{q="Is there anything living in the water now?",a="No normal aquatic life survived Tirisfal's blighting. Only animated, skeletal fish swim beneath the gray surface, left by the Scourge's corruption.",al={"stillwater pond fish","what lives in stillwater pond","stillwater creatures"}},{q="What dangerous creatures wander near the pond?",a="Mindless undead wander the glades, and Bayne is the shore's most notorious threat. The unusually powerful, aggressive darkhound feeds on unwary travelers.",al={"stillwater pond monsters","who is bayne","darkhound near brill"},it="danger"},{q="Where is Stillwater Pond located?",a="Stillwater Pond lies in central Tirisfal Glades, directly west of Brill and southwest of Brightwater Lake.",al={"where is stillwater pond","stillwater pond location","how to find stillwater pond"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Stillwater Pond?",a="Stillwater Pond is a quiet, shadowed lake lying just west of the town of Brill. Once a cherished leisure spot for the living families of Lordaeron, it now rests cold, gray, and still, mirroring the grim desolation that blankets the rest of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what is stillwater pond","stillwater pond lore","tell me about stillwater pond"},it="place",add="fa6e3aa4"},{q="Why is Stillwater Pond ruined and abandoned?",a="The pond fell to ruin alongside the rest of the kingdom during the Third War, when the Scourge unleashed the Plague of Undeath across Tirisfal. The blighted corruptions that swept through Lordaeron snuffed out mortal life around its banks, turning pleasant picnic grounds into a desolate wilderness stalked by wild beasts and the wandering dead.",al={"why is stillwater pond abandoned","what ruined stillwater pond","why is stillwater pond dead"},it="ruin",add="7a8eb54a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken who remembers life in Lordaeron, Stillwater Pond may recall childhood days spent picnicking and swimming along its once-clear banks.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face blighted wildlife around the pond, including feral darkhounds like Bayne. The shore is hazardous hunting ground for scouts patrolling Brill's outskirts."},kw={"bayne","brightwater lake","brill","darkhound","skeletal fish","stillwater pond","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:brightwater-lake","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:forsaken"},src={"Stillwater Pond"}}
E["subzone:undercity"] = {t="subzone",n="Undercity",z="tirisfal",s="Beneath Capital City, the Forsaken hold their underground stronghold, ruled by Sylvanas Windrunner. Its halls began as Scourge work and now shelter the free-willed undead.",h="Beneath Capital City, the Forsaken hold their underground stronghold, ruled by Sylvanas Windrunner.",sec={{t="From Royal Crypts to Scourge Bastion",b="Before the Third War, sewers, royal catacombs, and dungeons lay beneath Capital City. As Lordaeron fell, Prince Arthas Menethil ordered the Scourge to enlarge them into an underground seat of power. The Lich King summoned Arthas to Northrend before the work was finished.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken Capital",b="During the civil war in the Plaguelands, Sylvanas Windrunner rallied undead who had escaped the Lich King's grip. She overthrew the dreadlords and drove out rival forces, and the Forsaken claimed the underground complex. They finished the maze of catacombs the Scourge had begun and fortified it beneath the silent ruins of their former kingdom. Now the Dark Lady rules her people from its poisoned halls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Was Undercity always here before the undead took over?",a="Yes. Ancient royal crypts, dungeons, and the city's sewers lay beneath Lordaeron's palace.",al={"undercity origins","was undercity always there","history of undercity"},it="origin"},{q="Who actually built the modern Undercity?",a="Prince Arthas Menethil began expanding the old tunnels into a seat of power for the Scourge in Lordaeron. After Arthas was recalled to Northrend, Sylvanas Windrunner and her Forsaken seized the unfinished tunnels. They spent years excavating and fortifying them into the fortress city seen today.",al={"who made undercity","who built the undercity","undercity construction"},it="origin"},{q="Why live underground instead of rebuilding the city above?",a="Capital City's surface ruins face attacks from the Scarlet Crusade, Scourge remnants, and the Alliance. The underground catacombs are defensible and hidden from view, and suit undead who need no daylight, warmth, or open air.",al={"why live underground","why not rebuild lordaeron","why undercity"},it="why_here"},{q="Who rules the Undercity?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen and leader of the Forsaken, rules the city from the royal quarters deep inside the complex.",al={"who is the leader of undercity","undercity leader","who rules undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is the Undercity?",a="The Undercity is the subterranean capital of the Forsaken, sprawling directly beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's Capital City. Originally composed of ancient royal crypts, dungeons, and sewers, the vast complex was expanded into a labyrinthine fortress. Today it serves as the heart of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's realm, functioning as a fortified haven, political center, and research bastion for the free-willed undead of the Horde.",al={"what is undercity","undercity overview","undercity lore"},it="place",add="f1849a51"},{q="What happened at the Undercity?",a="Following the fall of Lordaeron, Prince Arthas began carving out a stronghold beneath the capital to serve the Scourge. When the Lich King's power weakened and Arthas fled to Northrend, Sylvanas Windrunner led a rebellion of liberated undead. During the Plaguelands civil war, her forces defeated rival dreadlords and Alliance remnants to seize the subterranean network, claiming it as the bastion of the newly founded Forsaken.",al={"history of undercity","undercity history","what happened here"},it="history",add="88d828cf"},{q="Who lives in the Undercity?",a="The city is populated primarily by the Forsaken—undead who tore themselves free from the Lich King's iron grip. Within its districts, you will encounter the Royal Apothecary Society brewing deadly concoctions, shadowy rogues, dark spellcasters, and deathguards watching the perimeter. Visiting emissaries and warriors from the Orc, Tauren, and Darkspear Troll nations of the Horde also walk the corridors, though rarely comfortably.",al={"who lives in undercity","undercity residents","undercity population"},it="residents",add="9e3a5d6b"},{q="Is the Undercity dangerous?",a="It is exceedingly perilous to outsiders and unwary visitors. For Alliance trespassers, death is swift and assured at the hands of the vigilant deathguards. Even for sworn Horde allies, the city poses hazards: vast open shafts, vats of toxic alchemical sludge, brooding necromancers, and scheming apothecaries conduct experiments where a single misstep can prove fatal.",al={"is undercity dangerous","how dangerous is undercity","undercity dangers"},it="danger",add="a78ac513"},{q="Why is it called the Undercity?",a="The name describes the place itself: a city beneath the ruins of Lordaeron's Capital City. It grew out of the royal crypts, dungeons, and sewers that once lay under the palace: Arthas's Scourge began expanding them, and the Forsaken finished the work and made the vast subterranean warren their home.",al={"why undercity name","undercity name origin","why is it called undercity"},it="name",add="4cec4aa1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Undercity as the heart of Forsaken civilization. Its halls rise among the ruins and crypts of your former lives, sheltering you from the Scourge and the living alike.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find its main military stronghold in the Eastern Kingdoms beneath the ground. Its dim passages, tainted by apothecaries, can unsettle visitors from Kalimdor."},kw={"arthas","capital city","catacombs","crypts","forsaken","lordaeron","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:tirisfal","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:forsaken","topic:arthas-menethil","subzone:sewers"},src={"Undercity"}}
E["subzone:venomweb-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Venomweb Vale",z="tirisfal",s="South of the Scarlet Monastery, Venomweb Vale lies blighted beneath a swarm of venomous spiders. The valley was once a lush woodland where hunters tracked deer and rabbits.",h="South of the Scarlet Monastery, Venomweb Vale lies blighted beneath a swarm of venomous spiders.",sec={{t="A Blighted Refuge",b="Venomweb Vale has fallen from a peaceful hunting ground to a blighted refuge. Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, local hunters followed deer and rabbits through its grass and trees. Now rot and gloom cover the valley, while giant venomous spiders swarm through the trees and hollows. The monstrous arachnid Sri'skulk leads them. To the north, the Scarlet Crusade holds the neighboring territory. Darkhounds prowl near the fortified Scarlet Encampment, where Lieutenant Sanders commands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many spiders in Venomweb Vale?",a="Venomweb Vale was once a hunting ground for deer and rabbits, but the valley is now overrun by poisonous spiders led by Sri'skulk. Their deadly webs and venom gave the vale its name.",al={"venomweb spiders origin","why so many spiders","who made the spiders"},it="why_here"},{q="Who rules the arachnids in the vale?",a="Sri'skulk leads the spider brood in Venomweb Vale, stalking the hollows beneath its blighted canopy.",al={"spider boss venomweb","sri'skulk","spider leader tirisfal"},it="leader"},{q="What is Venomweb Vale?",a="Venomweb Vale is a wide, blighted valley in eastern Tirisfal Glades, sitting just south of the Scarlet Monastery. Once a lush woodland teeming with deer and rabbits, it has decayed into a murky, poisoned hollow overrun by aggressive arachnids and prowling beasts, flanked nearby by vigilant Scarlet Crusade patrols.",al={"what is venomweb vale","venomweb vale info","tell me about venomweb vale"},it="place",add="c3248b05"},{q="What happened at Venomweb Vale in the past?",a="Before the plague tainted Lordaeron, the vale was a peaceful haven of verdant trees and green grass, favored by hunters tracking deer and rabbits. After the kingdom fell, it became a tainted place overrun by poisonous spiders led by Sri'skulk, which gave the vale its new name.",al={"venomweb vale history","what happened at venomweb vale","history of venomweb vale"},it="history",add="a3685aae"},{q="Who lives in Venomweb Vale?",a="No civilized folk dwell in the heart of the vale. It is dominated entirely by poisonous spiders under the broodmother Sri'skulk, alongside wandering darkhounds. Toward the northern edge of the valley, the Scarlet Crusade maintains an armed outpost known as the Scarlet Encampment under Lieutenant Sanders.",al={"who lives in venomweb vale","venomweb vale inhabitants","who controls venomweb vale"},it="residents",add="266d3ee0"},{q="Why is Venomweb Vale ruined?",a="When Lordaeron fell, blight crept across the glades, leaving the trees withered and the grass dead. Poisonous spiders led by the monstrous Sri'skulk overran the valley, and with no one left to check them, the brood now chokes the once-verdant haven.",al={"why is venomweb vale ruined","what ruined venomweb vale","venomweb vale corruption"},it="ruin",add="f69dc1ca"},{q="Is Venomweb Vale dangerous?",a="Yes, it is exceptionally perilous for unwary travelers. Lethal, venomous spiders nest throughout the valley's blighted trees, ambushing prey under the shadow of Sri'skulk. Furthermore, aggressive darkhounds roam the northern perimeter, where zealots of the Scarlet Crusade violently attack anyone approaching their camp.",al={"is venomweb vale dangerous","venomweb vale dangers","threats in venomweb vale"},it="danger",add="f71a1b3a"},{q="Why is it called Venomweb Vale?",a="The valley earned its grim moniker from the dense, toxic webs spun across the trees by the massive spiders that infest the hollow. Once an unnamed woodland haven, travelers and locals began calling it Venomweb Vale after the deadly arachnids claimed the entire basin.",al={"why is it called venomweb vale","venomweb vale name meaning","how did venomweb vale get its name"},it="name",add="7b7f7008"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken traveler heading toward the Scarlet Monastery, you must navigate Sri'skulk's lethal brood and the watchful Crusader patrols led by Lieutenant Sanders to the north."},kw={"lieutenant sanders","scarlet encampment","sri'skulk","tirisfal glades","venomweb vale"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Venomweb Vale"}}
E["subzone:whispering-forest"] = {t="subzone",n="Whispering Forest",z="tirisfal",s="Behind Deathknell, the Whispering Forest lies quiet beneath western Tirisfal’s cliffs. Its lake, giant mushroom ring, and uncanny wildlife break the stillness, while corruption stirs beneath the soil.",h="Behind Deathknell, the Whispering Forest lies quiet beneath western Tirisfal’s cliffs.",sec={{t="The Hidden Glen",b="Beyond Northface Rock and Bandarion Keep, the Whispering Forest feels far removed from plague-touched Tirisfal. Afflicted deer and roaming predators share its woods with a tranquil lake. Nearby, giant mushrooms form a ring beneath a hovering cloud of mist, glowing with uncanny energy. The ghostly Knight of Mourning wanders among them, bound by oath. Natural magic lingers here in a land scarred by the Scourge.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow Beneath the Woods",b="An ancient dread stains the woods beneath their wonder. Centuries ago, high elves tried to settle Tirisfal Glades, but many began to go mad. Some believed an evil slept beneath the land, though no one proved the rumors. Vile Fin murlocs and the undead threshadon Blightsculler prowl the lake, and necromantic remnants blight the ruined settlement of Shadowvale. Across Lordaeron, mad wanderers still mutter fearful warnings of a consuming darkness beneath Tirisfal’s roots.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Whispering Forest located?",a="The Whispering Forest lies in the mountains of western Tirisfal Glades, just west of Deathknell and south of Tyr's Fall. Northface Rock, a steep ridge with Bandarion Keep atop it, walls off the forest.",al={"whispering forest location","where is whispering forest","how to get to whispering forest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens at the giant mushroom circle?",a="Giant mushrooms form a ring beneath a hovering cloud of mist, glowing with strange energy. The ghostly Knight of Mourning wanders there, bound by oath, while the ring’s magic remains unknown.",al={"mushroom circle tirisfal","faerie dragon ring","fairy ring ritual"}},{q="Who watches over the forest?",a="Tyr's Watch, an order of Forsaken paladins, holds the heights of Bandarion Keep. Near the fairy circle, the spectral Knight of Mourning wanders the woods, bound by oath.",al={"who guards whispering forest","bandarion keep whispering forest"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why did the high elves abandon this region long ago?",a="After the high elves first reached Lordaeron’s shores, they tried to build a settlement in Tirisfal. Within a few years, many began to go mad. Some suspected an evil slept beneath the land, but the rumors were never proven. The elves abandoned the glades and traveled north.",al={"high elves tirisfal","why elves left tirisfal","madness beneath tirisfal"},it="history"},{q="What is Shadowvale?",a="Shadowvale is a ruined village southwest of the forest’s lake. The Tarnished dwell there alongside mindless undead afflicted by a necromantic crystal fragment dating back to clashes involving the Undercity.",al={"shadowvale tirisfal","ruined village whispering forest"}},{q="What is the Whispering Forest?",a="The Whispering Forest is a secluded, mist-shrouded woodland tucked beyond the steep western mountains of Tirisfal Glades. Separated from the rest of the region by the heights of Northface Rock, it is an eerie, untamed wilderness harboring diseased wildlife, mysterious fairy rings, forgotten ruins, and secluded mountain lakes cut off from ordinary travel.",al={"what is whispering forest","whispering forest lore","tell me about whispering forest"},it="place",add="d118db82"},{q="Is the Whispering Forest dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so. Beyond its sickly and diseased wildlife, the bluffs and waters are infested with displaced Vile Fin murlocs and the monstrous undead threshadon Blightsculler. Further inland, mindless undead haunt the ruins of Shadowvale around a fallen necromantic crystal fragment, while hostile Tarnished cultists lurk amidst the blighted woods.",al={"whispering forest danger","is whispering forest safe","threats in whispering forest"},it="danger",add="4326a394"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can feel the glowing faerie ring’s natural magic, one of the few such pulses left in blighted Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you find this secluded woodland just beyond Deathknell, under Tyr's Watch at Bandarion Keep. Forgotten dangers lie close to the Undercity."},kw={"bandarion keep","blightsculler","deathknell","faerie ring","shadowvale","tirisfal","whispering forest"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:bandarion-keep","subzone:deathknell","topic:lordaeron","topic:forsaken","npc:nat-pagle","topic:murloc"},src={"Whispering Forest"}}
E["subzone:whispering-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Whispering Shore",z="tirisfal",s="Along Tirisfal Glades' western coast, the Whispering Shore lies north of Solliden Farmstead, its waters claimed by hostile murlocs.",h="Along Tirisfal Glades' western coast, the Whispering Shore lies north of Solliden Farmstead, its waters...",sec={{t="A Ruined Haven",b="Before the Third War, Lordaeron's fishermen came to the Whispering Shore for calm waters and plentiful catches. Now the Great Sea breaks against an empty coast, and the water is cold and dark. Travelers coming down from the hills risk an ambush from the murlocs along the shore.",sp=0},{t="The Murloc Menace",b="A band of hostile murlocs claims the beach and attacks anyone who approaches the surf. Their chieftain, Muad, leads them as they guard the shallows and tidal flats, threatening nearby roads and Solliden Farmstead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Whispering Shore located?",a="The Whispering Shore runs along Tirisfal Glades' western coast, directly north of Solliden Farmstead.",al={"whispering shore location","where is whispering shore","whispering shore map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What used to be at the Whispering Shore before the Scourge?",a="Before the Scourge, local fishermen came to the shore for its calm waters and plentiful catches.",al={"whispering shore history","what was whispering shore used for","whispering shore past"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Whispering Shore now?",a="A hostile tribe of murlocs controls the coastline under the leadership of Muad, their chieftain. They attack anyone who approaches the water.",al={"who lives on whispering shore","whispering shore enemies","whispering shore mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Can you still fish peacefully at the Whispering Shore?",a="No. The shore has lost its peaceful character, and hostile murlocs guard its cold, dark waters, where the catches are no longer plentiful.",al={"fishing at whispering shore","whispering shore fish"},gp=true},{q="What is the Whispering Shore?",a="The Whispering Shore is a cold, dark stretch of coastline along the western reaches of Tirisfal Glades, situated just north of the Solliden Farmstead. Once known as a quiet and bountiful retreat for local fishermen, the blighted coast has since fallen to ruin and chaos, leaving behind little of the peaceful waters that common folk once enjoyed.",al={"whispering shore lore","what is whispering shore","tell me about whispering shore"},it="place",add="a19e4211"},{q="Is the Whispering Shore dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous for unwary travelers. The coast is currently overrun by a hostile band of ravenous murlocs led by the vicious Muad. These creatures aggressively attack anyone who wanders too close to the surf, making the shore uninhabitable for living settlers and a hazard to anyone traveling along western Tirisfal.",al={"is whispering shore safe","whispering shore threats","whispering shore danger"},it="danger",add="84b8417d"},{q="Why was the Whispering Shore abandoned?",a="Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge and the corruption of Tirisfal Glades, the once-bountiful fishing waters turned cold, dark, and barren. Without peaceful settlers to maintain the coast, predatory murlocs moved in and claimed the shoreline, driving away anyone who might have hoped to return.",al={"why is whispering shore ruined","what ruined whispering shore","why was whispering shore deserted"},it="ruin",add="bea21c89"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken securing western Tirisfal Glades, you face an unruly murloc threat along the edge of your holdings at Whispering Shore."},kw={"coast","fishing","muad","murloc","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades","whispering shore"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:murloc"},src={"Whispering Shore"}}
E["zone:tirisfal"] = {t="zone",n="Tirisfal Glades",z="tirisfal",s="Tirisfal Glades, in the north of Lordaeron, is home to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her Forsaken. Under blighted skies, fallen manors and dormant crypts surround their vast capital beneath the earth, the Undercity. The mindless Scourge hem them in, and so do the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade. Here the free-willed dead fight to survive.",h="Tirisfal Glades, in the north of Lordaeron, is home to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Land in Twilight",b="Tirisfal was once the fertile cradle of humanity, before the Lich King's plague withered its people. Now the sun rarely breaks through the gloom, over dying woods and cold coastal hills. Old farmsteads like the Agamand Mills still stand, but most of their masters lie in mass graves or walk as restless dead. Yet a dark resilience holds on in towns like Brill. And in Deathknell, the newly awakened Forsaken learn to endure their second life.",sp=0},{t="A War on Two Fronts",b="Now Lady Sylvanas rules the region from beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron, yet her people are beset on every side. Scourge thralls still infest the hollows, the fields and the crumbling crypts, bound wholly to the Frozen Throne in Northrend. To the east, the Scarlet Crusade holds northern Tirisfal, from its stronghold at the Scarlet Monastery. Sworn to destroy every undead creature, its patrols wage constant guerrilla war on Forsaken scouts and travelers.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Ancient Past",b="Older than any human crown is the story of the Glades. Of old, high elven exiles sought to settle in these woods. But shadowy powers deep beneath the earth began to drive them mad, and they passed on into the north. Centuries later, the secret Council of Tirisfal chose these shadowed groves. Here it empowered its solitary Guardians, who shielded Azeroth from the demons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the sky green and the land rotting?",a="During the Third War, Prince Arthas and the Scourge unleashed the Plague of Undeath across the Kingdom of Lordaeron. The magical blight poisoned not only the populace, but the soil, trees, and water itself, leaving the glades in an eternal state of eerie, sickly decay.",al={"why is tirisfal blighted","what happened to tirisfal","why is tirisfal dying"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the difference between the Forsaken and the Scourge here?",a="The Forsaken are undead who broke free from the Lich King's telepathic domination after the Battle of Mount Hyjal, choosing to follow Lady Sylvanas Windrunner with their own free will. The Scourge roaming the farmsteads and ruins remain mindless slaves bound to the Lich King's commands.",al={"forsaken vs scourge","why are zombies attacking undead","are all undead evil"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the red-armored soldiers attacking travelers?",a="They belong to the Scarlet Crusade, an uncompromising splinter order of former Silver Hand paladins and survivors. Convinced all undead are irredeemable abominations that must be purified by sword and fire, they execute both mindless thralls and free-willed Forsaken with fanatical hatred.",al={"scarlet crusade","red humans","monastery humans"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the name Tirisfal come from?",a="The name is older than any human kingdom, and its true origin has been lost to history. It is best known through the Council of Tirisfal, the secret order of magi that empowered the Guardians to shield Azeroth from demons.",al={"tirisfal meaning","origin of tirisfal"},it="name"},{q="Where do newly awakened Forsaken begin their journey?",a="Newly awakened Forsaken rise from the crypts of the Shadow Grave inside Deathknell, a cloistered town in southwestern Tirisfal. There, administrators and executors judge whether the risen dead have the sanity and loyalty to serve the Dark Lady.",al={"undead starting zone","where is deathknell","forsaken starting area"},it="arrival"},{q="How do travelers leave Tirisfal for other continents?",a="A large goblin-operated zeppelin tower sits on the hillside south of Brill, right outside the Ruins of Lordaeron. These airships provide direct, regular transit across the seas to Orgrimmar in Kalimdor and Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"tirisfal zeppelins","how to get to orgrimmar","how to get to stranglethorn"},it="place"},{q="What is Tirisfal Glades?",a="Tirisfal Glades is the heartland of the Forsaken on the northern coast of Lordaeron. Once the peaceful, fertile core of a proud human kingdom, it was ravaged during the Third War by the Scourge's Plague of Undeath. Today, blighted woods and perpetual green gloom blanket the hills, framed by the ruins of Lordaeron's capital and surrounded by hostile zealots, feral beasts, and lingering undead.",al={"what is tirisfal","tell me about tirisfal glades","tirisfal zone lore"},it="place",add="6c272224",nx={8}},{q="Was this always Undead land?",a="No. For thousands of years, Tirisfal was the cradle of human civilization and the thriving heart of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. Peaceful farmsteads, prosperous mills, and small hamlets flourished under King Terenas Menethil. That era ended violently during the Third War when Prince Arthas and the Cult of the Damned swept through with the plague, turning the inhabitants into undead slaves before Sylvanas broke them free.",al={"was tirisfal always undead","who lived here before","tirisfal before plague"},it="history",add="342b65f9"},{q="Who lives in or runs Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Forsaken claim Tirisfal Glades under the rule of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner from the Undercity. However, their hold is constantly contested. The fanatical Scarlet Crusade commands fortifications and their great Monastery in the northeast, while mindless Scourge prowl derelict farms. On the eastern border at the Bulwark, the Forsaken coordinate alongside the Argent Dawn to keep the horrors of the Plaguelands contained.",al={"who rules tirisfal","who controls tirisfal glades","tirisfal factions"},it="residents",add="4790468d"},{q="Is Tirisfal Glades dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. Beyond the walls of Forsaken outposts, you face mindless Scourge remnants, savage gnolls, giant arachnids, and vicious wildlife tainted by the plague. Worse still are the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade, who execute any undead on sight. To the far east lies the Western Plaguelands, where monsters far deadlier than anything in Tirisfal will tear apart the unwary.",al={"how dangerous is tirisfal","tirisfal threats","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="97ffdb73"},{q="Who's in charge in Brill?",a="Magistrate Sevren oversees the civic administration of Brill, managing the town's rebuilding and daily survival. Military authority and tactical operations, particularly the campaign against the nearby Scarlet Crusade, are commanded by Executor Zygand.",al={"brill leader","who leads brill","in charge of brill"},it="in_charge",add="30e6283a",nx={12,13}},{q="Who does Magistrate Sevren answer to?",a="Sevren serves the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. As magistrate of Brill, he represents the Forsaken crown's civilian authority in the region, operating in direct concert with royal executors and the Royal Apothecary Society based in the Undercity.",al={"sevren boss","who does sevren report to","brill leadership chain"},it="in_charge",add="3fc3649e"},{q="Where is the Banshee Queen?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner resides in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity, deep beneath the ruins of Capital City just south of Brill. From her throne room, she directs the Forsaken in their war against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"where is sylvanas","find sylvanas","banshee queen location"},it="leader",add="381a9b46"},{q="What is Brill?",a="Brill is the primary Forsaken town in central Tirisfal Glades, situated along the crossroads north of Capital City. Once a living settlement under the Barov estate, it was rebuilt after the Third War to provide newly awakened undead a place of rest, trade, and organization before venturing further into the world.",al={"about brill","what kind of town is brill","brill lore"},it="place",add="e7993821",nx={15,16}},{q="Were living people here before?",a="Yes. Brill was once a quiet human community within the Kingdom of Lordaeron. It became ground zero for early plague experiments orchestrated by Kel'Thuzad, resulting in mass casualties and massive communal graves before Prince Arthas ever arrived to investigate.",al={"did humans live in brill","brill living history","who lived in brill"},it="history",add="529e09c8"},{q="What's the Gallows' End Tavern?",a="The Gallows' End Tavern is Brill's central gathering hall and inn. It offers shelter, foul libations, and respite from the grim glades outside. In its darker corners, the Forsaken keep captured enemies—such as Scarlet zealots—for sinister Apothecary concoction trials.",al={"gallows end tavern","brill inn","what is gallows end"},it="place",add="7b7ff5e2"},{q="What's the deal with the Agamand Mills?",a="Agamand Mills was once the wealthiest and most productive farming estate in Tirisfal Glades, famous for flour and grain. When the plague struck, the entire complex was overrun and slaughter ensued. Today, it stands as a rotting, windmill-dotted ruin choked with lingering Scourge undead.",al={"agamand mills lore","what happened to agamand mills","agamand mills"},it="place",add="0d8014ee",nx={18,19}},{q="Who were the Agamands?",a="The Agamands were a noble, wealthy human dynasty who developed the sprawling mills and held property throughout Tirisfal, including Brill. During the Third War, their fortune could not save them; the family fell to the Scourge and their reanimated patriarchs continue to haunt the estate.",al={"agamand family","who lived at agamand mills","the agamands"},it="people",add="001d4abe"},{q="Why are they hostile to us if they're undead too?",a="The undead haunting the Agamand Mills never regained their free will. Unlike the Forsaken, who shook off the Lich King's mental grip, these creatures remain enslaved as mindless Scourge thralls, compelled to destroy any living or rebellious dead who trespass on their domain.",al={"why do agamands attack us","why are agamand undead hostile","why fight other undead"},it="threat",add="eeb96a2c"},{q="Where does all this lead after Tirisfal?",a="Most Forsaken journey south through the mountain pass into Silverpine Forest to assist in securing the southern frontier and battling Dalaran agents and Rot Hide gnolls. Alternatively, zeppelins south of Brill provide passage to Orgrimmar or Grom'gol Base Camp across the sea.",al={"where to go after tirisfal","next zone after tirisfal","after tirisfal glades"},it="next_step",add="a357af07",nx={21,22}},{q="What's Undercity?",a="The Undercity is the sprawling subterranean capital of the Forsaken, built within the ancient sewers, crypts, and catacombs beneath the shattered Ruins of Lordaeron. It serves as Queen Sylvanas's fortress and the command center for Forsaken operations across Azeroth.",al={"what is the undercity","undercity lore","about undercity"},it="place",add="50336b90"},{q="Is the Silverpine border next?",a="Yes. Following the road south out of Tirisfal leads directly into Silverpine Forest. It is the natural continuation of your service to the Forsaken, where you confront the growing threat along the southern borders of Lordaeron.",al={"silverpine next","do i go to silverpine next","silverpine border"},it="next_step",add="ddddba9f"},{q="How did I end up in Tirisfal Glades?",a="If you are newly risen Forsaken, you died during the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge and were buried here. With the Lich King's grip broken, your free will returned, and you clawed your way out of the grave in the secluded valley of Deathknell. If you belong to the other Horde nations, you likely arrived through the zeppelin towers situated between Brill and the Undercity, which connect this blighted realm directly to Orgrimmar and Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to tirisfal glades","how did i arrive here"},it="arrival",add="789ead4d"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Your goal is to help the Forsaken secure their tenuous hold over Lordaeron's blighted heartlands. Moving out from the crypts of Deathknell toward the town of Brill, you must purge the mindless Scourge haunting abandoned farms, eliminate fanatical zealots of the Scarlet Crusade encroaching from the north, and cull plagued beasts roaming the rotting woods. Doing so proves your worth to Lady Sylvanas and prepares you to serve her growing kingdom beneath the ruins of Capital City.",al={"what should i do here","why am i in tirisfal","what is my goal here"},it="purpose",add="89135166"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This is your ancestral homeland twice over: the kingdom you built in life, and the precarious sanctuary you must defend in undeath under Lady Sylvanas.",["faction:Horde"]="Tirisfal is the Horde's vital bastion in the northern Eastern Kingdoms, anchoring diplomatic ties with the Forsaken while warding off human extremists and the Scourge.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the surviving nations of the Alliance, Tirisfal is a tragic monument to Lordaeron's fall, filled with the desecrated tombs of former brothers and sisters in faith.",["class:Priest"]="Historic holy grounds like Faol's Rest—the tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, founder of the Silver Hand—lie here, warped by death and contested between zealots and Shadow priests."},kw={"agamand","balnir","brill","deathknell","forsaken","glades","lordaeron","scarlet crusade","sylvanas","tirisfal","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:scarlet","zone:silverpine","zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","subzone:bulwark"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Tirisfal Glades (Classic)","Tirisfal Glades"}}
